vered your book review with fantastic energy and a very engaging tone. It was a pleasure to hear your voice, and your enthusiasm for the subject was clear from the start. Your volume and overall intonation were excellent, helping to keep the listener's attention throughout the recording.<br><br><b>What You Did Well:</b> You used a very good range of intonation to emphasize important parts of your story. Your volume was consistent and strong, ensuring that your presentation felt professional and confident from the beginning to the end.<br><br><b>What to Watch Out For:</b> Clarity /ɪnˌtel.ɪ.dʒəˈbɪl.ə.ti/ was often affected by the repetitive dropping of final consonant sounds, such as the "d" in "red" /red/, the "t" in "white" /waɪt/, and the "s" in "states" /steɪts/. Additionally, you frequently overstressed the final syllables in words like "camera" /kæm.əˈrɑː/, "kindergarten" /ˌkɪn.də.ɡɑːˈtən/, and "party" /pɑːˈtiː/.<br><br><b>How to Get Even Better:</b><br>1. Focus on fully pronouncing the final sounds of words, especially /d/, /t/, and /s/, to ensure your meaning is clear.<br>2. Practice placing the stress on the correct syllable—usually earlier in the word—to create a more natural English rhythm.<br><br>You have a very engaging presence, Platwo, so keep working on those specific sounds! 🌟	\N	\N	12.0	Platwo, you gave a very lively and engaging review of your book! You used an excellent hook to start your talk and included many specific details about the plot. Your vocabulary is quite strong for B1, especially words like "rival" and "emergency." To improve, remember to mention the author and try to keep your tenses consistent while you tell the story. Reducing the pauses and nervous laughter will also make your speaking sound much smoother and more natural. You clearly enjoyed the book, and that made your presentation very fun to listen to! 🌟	B1	Speaking	CA	PET	\N	\N
