cine. And some people made a cartoon to mocking and joking him, like, uh, people have a part of cow, like cow ears or tails.<br><br><br>But, but then his work was accept and get a award.<br><br><br>Uh, his award, uh... [laughs] he get award but he don't get a Nobel Prize because Nobel Prize came in 1906.<br><br><br>Okay, I will tell you why he is a hero. He recovered vaccination and he saved millions of life. He changed... uh, he changed medicine forever with his work, vaccine.<br><br><br>Edward Jenner, the man who saved a million of life. Thank you.	445	3	<p>Nut, your presentation showed a good control of simple grammatical forms, and you were able to use a range of appropriate vocabulary when talking about Edward Jenner and his work. For example, phrases like "the man who saved a million lives" and "basis his first vaccines" demonstrate effective vocabulary use. You also used some complex forms, such as "Milkmaid who was sick from the cowpox, but when the smallpox come, the milkmaid didn't get sick from the smallpox."</p><br><p>However, there were a few instances where more complex grammatical structures could have been attempted or where simple forms contained errors. For example, "He's born into a large family" should be "He was born into a large family." Another example is "The boy immune to smallpox" which should be "The boy became immune to smallpox." To achieve a score of 5, focus on consistent accuracy with both simple and complex forms and try to incorporate a wider range of vocabulary to express your ideas with more precision and nuance. For example, instead of "tell you about overview," consider "give an overview of."</p>	3	<p>Nut, you produced extended stretches of language throughout your presentation, which is excellent, especially given the expected word count! You effectively structured your talk according to the prompt, moving from the introduction to his early life, his actions, criticisms, and finally, your conclusion. The use of phrases like "Let's start with his early life" and "Now I will tell you about his activity" helped to guide the listener through your points.</p><br><p>Your contributions were mostly relevant, and you managed to develop your ideas clearly. However, there was some hesitation (e.g., "Uh, uh, I probably you don't know who he is," and "And the last important... and... and the last thing is why he is a hero.") and occasional repetition that impacted the overall flow slightly. For example, "Edward Jenner... Edward Jenner born in..." and "local doctor, doctor, and clergymen don't... don't trust he because, uh, because his vaccine." To achieve a score of 5, aim for even smoother transitions between points, reduce hesitation, and strive for more varied phrasing to avoid repetition. Your word count of 445 words comfortably met the minimum requirement of 400 words, demonstrating your ability to sustain a monologue. Well done! 👏</p>	4	<p>Nut, you have a very clear speaking voice and excellent intonation, which makes your presentation easy to understand! Keep up the great work here. 👍</p><br><p>However, there were a few areas for improvement. You sometimes overstressed final syllables in words, for instance, in "ci**ty**," "Jen**ner**," and "fami**ly**." In English, stress usually falls on a different syllable in these words, such as /ˈsɪt.i/, /ˈdʒɛn.ər/, and /ˈfæm.li/.</p><br><p>You also had some issues with the final /s/ sound, as in "cowpox" which was pronounced more like "cow pok." Remember to articulate that final /s/ sound clearly. To improve, try practicing words with final /s/ and focusing on the correct stress patterns of English words. Listening to native speakers and mimicking their pronunciation can be very helpful! 🎧</p>	\N	\N	13.0	<p>Hi Nut! 👋 Overall, you did a great job with your "My Hero" presentation on Edward Jenner. You shared a lot of interesting information clearly and with good flow. You have a very clear speaking voice, which is a big strength! Keep practicing your presentation skills, and focus on expanding your vocabulary and varying your sentence structures to make your speech even more dynamic. You're well on your way to becoming an excellent speaker! 💪</p>	B2	Speaking	CA	FIRST	\N	\N
