nk their parent can teach them.<br><br>NENE: Yeah, I agree with Lookpear because some children in school, I I have see they like to pull the grass and they didn't care environment for more. Like, they or they didn't they use the bottle water and they didn't and they just don't care them. They put on the table and they didn't put in the trash. So if we teach them and they learn how to put in the trash and yeah, I think it will be good.<br><br>NENE: I think is they have to learn and think because because sometimes don't have people or sometimes parents didn't teach them.<br><br>NENE: Uh, for me, sometimes I see posts in social media to to useless about to help world, like go to to to ...<br><br>	501	2	You show a good understanding of simple sentence structures and can talk about familiar topics, which is a great start! 😊 For example, you were able to describe what you like to do in your free time and how you travel to school. However, sometimes basic grammatical errors affect how clearly you communicate. For instance, you said, "because now have a lot of because now people like to cut the tree" (it should be "because there are a lot of trees being cut down") and "tree is have a lot of advantage" (which should be "trees have a lot of advantages"). Also, phrases like "it it useless, it will useless carbon dioxide" would be clearer as "it will reduce carbon dioxide." To improve, try focusing on subject-verb agreement and the correct use of articles (a, an, the). Practise making sure your sentences are complete and grammatically accurate before you speak them, perhaps by thinking for a moment before you answer. This will make your meaning much clearer!	3	You're good at producing longer answers, which is fantastic for showing off your English skills! 👍 You kept your contributions relevant to the topics, such as when you discussed planting trees and cleaning the beach in Part 2. However, there were moments of hesitation, and sometimes you repeated words or phrases, which made your speech slightly less fluent. For example, when talking about cleaning, you said, "cleaning, cleaning cleaning place." To make your speech flow more smoothly, try to expand your use of connecting words beyond just 'and' and 'because.' You could use words like 'however,' 'therefore,' 'in addition,' or 'on the other hand' to link your ideas more effectively. This will help your explanations sound more connected and natural!	2	Your intonation is generally appropriate, and your speech is mostly understandable, which is a big plus! 🎉 However, to make your English even clearer and more natural, we need to work on making your speech less 'staccato' (choppy) and on linking sounds more effectively. You sometimes drop final consonant sounds, for instance, "relax" /rɪˈlæks/ can sound like /rɪˈlæk/, "trees" /triːz/ like /triː/, and "park" /pɑːk/ like /pɑː/. On the other hand, you sometimes overstress the final syllables in words like "picture" /ˈpɪktʃər/ and "electricity" /ɪlɛkˈtrɪsɪti/. Many Thai speakers might experience these challenges because Thai doesn't always place strong emphasis on final consonants or syllables. Try practicing words like "rela**x**" /rɪˈlæks/, "tree**s**" /triːz/, and "par**k**" /pɑːk/ to ensure you articulate those final sounds. Also, listen carefully to how English speakers connect words (e.g., "in the park" rather than "in [pause] the [pause] park") to make your speech more flowing.	2	You did a good job of starting the conversation and responding to your partner, Lookpear! 😊 You contributed your opinions and reasons, such as your ideas about saving electricity at home. However, while you maintained the interaction, your contributions were often quite short, and you didn't always link your ideas directly to what Lookpear had just said. Sometimes, it felt like you were giving your opinion rather than building on the conversation. To improve, try to respond directly to your partner's points, perhaps by saying, "That's a good point, and I also think..." or asking them for more details. This will help you to develop the interaction further and show that you can have a really dynamic conversation! 🗣️	9.0	Hi Nene! 👋 It was a pleasure to hear you speak during your test. You communicated your ideas on various environmental topics clearly, and it’s evident you have a good grasp of English. To help you progress even further, let’s concentrate on making your grammar a bit more precise and your speech flow more smoothly, especially when connecting your thoughts and sounds. Keep working hard, and remember that every little step helps you improve! You're doing well!<br><br>📋 **Action Plan**<br>*   ✔️ Pay close attention to grammatical accuracy, especially subject-verb agreement and article usage.<br>*   ✔️ Practice linking your words and sentences to create a more natural, less 'staccato' rhythm.<br>*   ✔️ Work on building on your partner's ideas more in discussions, rather than just agreeing.	B1	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
