ed well together to reach a decision. To achieve a 5, you could try to consistently link your contributions even more directly to your partner's exact words and try to develop the interaction further by asking for more detailed opinions or even gently challenging an idea. This shows a very natural and advanced level of interaction.	14.0	Kris, you've shown a good command of English in your speaking test, communicating your ideas effectively and engaging well in discussions. While you're already doing many things well, focusing on a few key areas will help you really polish your language and achieve an even higher score. Keep up the great work! 🚀<br><br>📋 **Action Plan**<br>*   ✔️ Pay close attention to your verb tenses and subject-verb agreement.<br>*   ✔️ Practise using a wider variety of vocabulary and more complex sentence structures.<br>*   ✔️ Focus on clearly articulating consonant sounds, especially at the end of words.<br>	B2	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
