ou you clean up and help environment.<br><br>KREWKHEW: This.<br><br>KREWKHEW: is the easiest.<br><br>KREWKHEW: Yeah. But all this is about we need to use more than two people to do it. But this we...<br><br>KREWKHEW: Maybe it's better to first reducing plastic.<br><br>KREWKHEW: Recycling. Yeah, that's awesome. But first, we going to teach our kid to know where the recycle bin is.<br><br>KREWKHEW: Yeah. We all we all throw everything away from the trash.<br><br>KREWKHEW: And saving electric at home is also easiest.<br><br>KREWKHEW: And.<br><br>KREWKHEW: Yeah, of course it's very important to teach. As a fact, nowadays, people are not really knowing much about this kind of lesson. So that would be great because uh our future self might be teaching others too. Yeah.<br><br>KREWKHEW: I think the biggest challenge is to repeat the healthy life in the same day because the healthy life was so boring. Boring at some kids don't don't want to change their habit of being lazy and un-activate. Yeah.<br><br>KREWKHEW: Uh, I I don't know if you know but there are app that help and they can see all the polluted thing in the world and that might help teenager to know that the polluted in the world was so a lot and bad. Yeah.<br><br>KREWKHEW: Oh. Yeah. Of course but I think some some environment in the country is also clean. But as as I see, the river as Rico say the river was so polluted. One one time I ever swim in it and I got eye injury. It was bad.<br><br>KREWKHEW: No, not at all. I think it's better that we take an action to it and care about it. That because the polluted in the world this way was a lot more than our past. That's why we need to care about it more than ever.	641	2	KK, you show a good handle on using simple English sentences effectively, and you're making a great effort to use a variety of words when talking about different subjects. For example, you talked clearly about why you like go-karting and places to visit! 🏎️ However, sometimes little grammatical slips or word choices can make your sentences a bit harder to follow. For instance, you said, "mine is in my area have a lot of store to visit," which would be clearer as "In my area, there are a lot of stores to visit." Another example is "camping are a little boring," where the verb "are" should be "is" to match "camping." 🤔 You also said, "a movie cinema too which just pretty rare for a place to stand." Perhaps you meant "a movie cinema, which is pretty rare for a town of this size." To help tighten up your grammar, try to pay close attention to verb agreement (making sure singular subjects have singular verbs, like "camping *is*") and think about the best word to describe what you mean in context. Thai speakers sometimes find English articles (a, an, the) and plural forms a bit tricky because they aren't used in the same way in Thai, so practicing these can really make a difference! 📚	3	You do a solid job of speaking for extended periods, KK, which is a key skill in English! 🗣️ Your contributions are usually relevant to the discussion, and you rarely repeat yourself, which helps keep your listener engaged. You also use words like "because," "and also," and "that's why" to connect your ideas, making your explanations easier to follow. For example, your explanation about saving electricity was very well organised: "saving electricity at home is also helping the environment. It's really effective, to be honest. Because now a day, we use electric so much. Everything in our life is electric. That's why saving is reduce a lot of oh no, help a lot of environment." To improve further, try to reduce those "uh" and "um" hesitations. Sometimes, a quick, silent mental pause before you start a new sentence can make your speech sound even smoother and more confident. You're well on your way to becoming a very fluent speaker! 👍	3	Your pronunciation is generally clear, KK, and your intonation, the way your voice rises and falls, is very good! 🙌 This helps make your English sound natural and easy to understand. Most of your individual sounds are clear, but you do have a tendency to drop some consonant sounds, especially /s/ and /d/ at the ends of words. For example, "plants" /plɑːnts/ might sound like "plant," and "world" /wɜːld/ might sound a little incomplete. While this doesn't usually cause confusion, being mindful of these final sounds will make your speech even clearer. A great way to practice this is to over-emphasise those final consonants when you're practising alone. Try saying words like "plants-s-s" or "world-d-d" to really feel the sound. Sometimes, in Thai, final consonant sounds are less pronounced than in English, so making a conscious effort to produce them can be a fun challenge! 🗣️	3	You're good at starting conversations and responding appropriately, KK, which is fantastic for keeping the interaction flowing! 😊 You actively participate in discussions, giving your opinions and reasons, just like you did when explaining the importance of saving electricity. You also did well in the collaborative task, working with Rico and suggesting ideas. For example, "So reducing plastic use is also helping because plastic are a major reason why our earth is a lot of waste. That's why reducing is the best way to helping the environment. You agree?" To really take this to the next level, try to build even more on your partner's ideas. Instead of just agreeing, you could say something like, "Yes, I completely agree with that, and to add to your point, we could also..." This shows you're not just listening but actively connecting your thoughts to theirs, making the conversation even richer! 💬	11.0	Fantastic effort in your speaking test, KK! 🎉 You're doing a really good job of speaking at length and keeping the conversation going, which shows you're becoming more and more confident. It's clear you have some wonderful ideas to share, and your ability to connect with the topics is impressive. To help make your communication even clearer and more pre