l you about special places to visit and the nightlife.	\N	4	Arty, you used a good range of vocabulary to describe Pattaya's attractions, such as "great outdoors," "turquoise water," "cultural shows," and "unique design." You showed good control of simple grammatical forms. However, you need to pay closer attention to articles and subject-verb agreement. For example, you said "in the eastern of Thailand" instead of "in the east of Thailand," and "Pattaya have lots of delicious food" instead of "Pattaya has lots of delicious food." Also, "Seafood is a very famous" should be "Seafood is very famous." To achieve a score of 5, you need to minimize these types of errors and demonstrate consistent control over more complex grammatical forms.	3	You produced extended stretches of language, Arty, but there was some hesitation. While your contributions were relevant to the topic, there was some repetition, for instance, "white... white... white sandy beach." You used cohesive devices like "Moving on to the next topic," but the overall organization of ideas could be more consistently clear. To improve, work on reducing hesitation and ensuring a smoother, more coherent flow of ideas. Practice connecting your thoughts more seamlessly to present your information clearly and effectively.	3	Your pronunciation was generally intelligible, Arty, but your voice was a bit flat and quiet. Try to introduce more animation and variation in your intonation. While you made a good effort at pronouncing word endings, focusing on overall sentence stress and intonation will help convey meaning more effectively and make your speech sound more natural.	4	You initiated the presentation appropriately, Arty, and your interaction with the audience, including eye contact, was good. You effectively handed over to your partner Fergie. The breakdown in discourse at times, possibly because you had memorized parts of your speech, might affect the natural flow of interaction. To improve, practice more spontaneous speaking to maintain and develop the interaction without relying heavily on memorized phrases.	14.0	Hello Arty, your presentation on Pattaya was a good effort. You did well in providing detailed descriptions of the places and food, showing a good range of vocabulary. To improve, focus on maintaining consistent fluency and refining your grammatical accuracy, especially with articles and verb forms. Keep up the good work!	B2	Speaking	CA	FIRST	\N	\N
