omething like COVID because they need to protect themselves by eating vitamins and help is very important by cleaning them to teach them about cleaning your their body to keep them clean. I think technology can help us to like we search for how to be healthy and they're going to show us the some people who upload their YouTube to like practice exercise. They can watch and do their exercise with them on the video to be healthy, not just go on Tik Tok or doing nothing. Thank you.	471	2	Kao-Oat, you've shown that you can put together simple sentences pretty well, especially when you're talking about things you know, like where you live or what you do for fun. For instance, you said, "I live in Bangkok near the school." That's a great clear statement! 👍 However, sometimes a few little errors creep in, which can make your message a little less clear. For example, you said, "It's about five kilometer," but when we talk about more than one, we add an 's' to the end, so it should be "five **kilometres**." Another example was "I'm enjoy doing housework," which should be "I **enjoy** doing housework." 🤔 To help you improve, try to pay close attention to the small grammar rules like making sure your verbs agree with "I" (I enjoy, not I'm enjoy) and adding 's' for plural nouns. This will make your English sound much more natural!	2	You're good at giving longer answers, Kao-Oat, which is fantastic because it shows you can talk about a topic in more detail. You kept the conversation going and your contributions were always on topic. 🎉 However, sometimes there were pauses, and you repeated yourself a little, especially when you said, "I think so" several times. To make your speaking even better, try to use different linking words or phrases to connect your ideas more smoothly, like "also," "furthermore," or "in addition." For example, instead of just saying "I think so," you could say, "I think so, and another point is..." or "That's a good point, and I'd also add that..." This will help your ideas flow more clearly and keep your listener interested.	1	You were generally understood, Kao-Oat, which is a great start! However, to make your English even clearer and more pleasant to listen to, we need to work on making your voice more lively. Your voice sometimes sounds a bit flat, and you speak quite slowly, which can make it hard for the listener to stay engaged. 🗣️ Also, you tend to put a lot of stress on the very last part of words, like in "buy**ing**" and "read**ing**." Try to let those final syllables relax a little more. You also sometimes drop consonant sounds at the end of words. For example, in "chance," the /s/ sound wasn't always clear, and in "outside," the /d/ sound was often missing. For "relax," the /ks/ sound was sometimes hard to hear. Try practising making these sounds clearly at the end of words. Many Thai speakers find it tricky to pronounce final consonants as they are less common in Thai, so it's a common area to focus on for improvement!	3	Kao-Oat, you did a good job of responding to questions and starting new parts of the conversation. You were able to keep the discussion moving along, especially when you shared your thoughts and reasons, like when you said, "I think young people need to do some spend outside sometimes outdoor because they like enjoy playing game too much and make their eyes going broken." That's a good way to give your opinion! 👍 To really get to a higher score here, try to build more on what your partner says. Instead of just agreeing with "I think so," you could ask them more questions to get more details or explain *why* you agree, perhaps adding a new point. For instance, you could say, "I agree with you because... and another reason is..." This shows you're not just listening, but you're also adding to the conversation in a deeper way!	8.0	Hi Kao-Oat! It was lovely to hear you speak. You're doing a good job of getting your ideas across, and that's the most important thing in speaking English. Keep working on making your sentences a little more varied and clear, and you'll find your confidence growing even more. You're making progress, and with a bit of focus, you can continue to improve how smoothly and clearly you express yourself! <br><br> 📋 Action Plan: <br>✔️ Practice making your sentences a bit longer by using words like "because," "and," or "but" to connect your ideas. <br>✔️ Pay attention to the endings of your words, especially those 's' sounds for plurals (like "kilometers" instead of "kilometer") and verb endings. <br>✔️ Try to speak a little faster and use a wider range of tones in your voice to make your speech sound more natural and engaging.	B1	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
