auses or sighs to make your speaking smoother. You should also watch your verb patterns and make sure to use 'was' or 'is' where needed. You communicated the main story points very effectively! 🌟	A2+	Speaking	CA	PET	\N	\N
28716	2025-09-21	2025-09-21	2026	Term 1 Finals	AUNNA: My name is Aunna.<br><br><br>AUNNA: Pretty much, but I'm more prefer baking.<br><br><br>AUNNA: I think it's like more fun. I like a bit of like more details.<br><br><br>AUNNA: Like the the normal food. Like some rice and then like some noodles, fried eggs, and omelet. I usually like cook myself.<br><br><br>AUNNA: My mom usually spends things in the hospital and she don't really like she doesn't really have time for me that much.<br><br><br>AUNNA: For me, like my most favorite is probably pad kaprao because it's like the most like not from that traditional, but like most foreigner would know pad kaprao, right? Like the taste is like very flavorful and it's like my favorite of all time.<br><br><br>AUNNA: I think it's like very, very important because it's like all of your like nutrients for like your energy for like the whole day. Like imagine if like you didn't eat any like breakfast and then you just like randomly come in and try to like study, your brain doesn't work like that.<br><br><br>AUNNA: As I can see between these picture, the first one on the top is like in a market, like full of fruits and vegetables, but on the other picture, it was like a supermarket that's like in in the mall or maybe not. And like you can see in the, as I can see in the picture, the first picture is like very crowded, full of people. must be like a lot of conversation happens. But the the lower picture, they're like they were like doing all by themselves. Just only like some groceries. Yeah, I think that's it.<br><br><br>AUNNA: I I agree with that but like more for me, I think organizing a healthy food fair would be more better because like you see if you're good at cooking but you're bad at organizing, it doesn't mean like you would be like completely like best for healthy eating.<br><br><br>AUNNA: That's a pretty good idea, but I also think guest speakers from local farm would be also great because like you can get a lot of information from like your guest. Like if you just only like you know how to like grow a vegetables but like you don't know like the specific thing of it, doesn't like it doesn't matter.<br><br><br>AUNNA: Yeah, mhm.<br><br><br>AUNNA: I think it's like it's also a way to like for people to eat more healthy food, but I don't think it's like the best way because like, you know, it's like only poster and like some of the students or people don't really read poster that much.<br><br><br>AUNNA: I agree, but not really that agree because like I think teacher can like will organize students, so like maybe when the guests come, teacher could be like well organized.<br><br><br>AUNNA: For me, like every students love to do something new. So maybe cooking club or healthy recipes would be good. Like you can you can learn more like about new recipe and also more about healthy food.<br><br><br>AUNNA: Um, maybe a school vegetable garden like, you know, you can like interact with friends more and you can like, you know, grow plants together and I think it would be like more fun instead of just like learning inside.<br><br><br>AUNNA: I think it is like very important because like if you just like randomly eat or like try to like, you know, eat them, like all the nutrients or maybe like some maybe some of the factory just like somehow put some chemicals that just like make your digest system like working hard, a lot more hard. Yeah.<br><br><br>AUNNA: I think they like eat too much often. Like you see, like even though it's like very delicious, I like the taste and everything, but like it's still full of like, you know, like bad things. Mhm.<br><br><br>AUNNA: For like mostly people or like family in Thailand, parents, like kids don't really like, you know, like talk back to their parents that much. So like if their parents told the kids to like do this, do this, it's mean that they're like try to like give something good for you, so like we don't really like talk that much and we just like go along with them.<br><br><br>AUNNA: Absolutely. I think like if it's like full of like, you know, vegetables or like something more healthier, I think like the school fair or like the grade would be a lot more better.	749	3	Aunna, you show a good handle on putting sentences together, especially when you talk about everyday things like your cooking preferences and what you eat for lunch. For instance, you said, "I think it's like more fun" and "Like the taste is like very flavorful," which are both clear and effective! 😊 You've also got a good range of words for familiar topics, using terms like "nutrients" and "flavorful." To push your score higher, you could try to be a bit more precise with some of your grammar, especially when you're trying to express something a little more complex. For example, instead of saying "I'm more prefer baking," you could simply say "I prefer baking more." Another good practice would be to think about the correct verb forms, like changing "My mom usually spends things in the hospital" to "My mom usually *works* in the hospital" and "she don't really like" to "she *doesn't* really like." Taking a moment to double-check these small details will make your sentences even stronger and clearer! 💪	4	You do a fantastic job of speaking for longer periods, Aunna, and you manage to keep your ideas well-organised and relevant without too much repetition. This really helps the listener follow your thoughts easily! 👏 For instance, when you compared the market and the supermarket, you clearly distinguished between the two, using phrases like "the first one on the top is like in a market... but on the other picture, it was like a supermarket." You also use linking words like "because" effectively to explain your points. However, one small thing to be mindful of is your frequent use of the word "like" as a filler. While it doesn't stop us from understanding you, sometimes it can make your speech sound a little less formal or polished. To improve, try