al. Focusing on which part of the word gets the strongest emphasis will make your speech sound more natural. 🔊	3	You did a good job of responding to questions and sharing your opinions, Bona, and you even tried to link your ideas to what your partners were saying, like offering a different view on playing online games! That's excellent! 🎉 To score even higher, try to ask your partners more questions or build more directly on their points to keep the conversation going and make it a real back-and-forth discussion. This shows you're not just speaking your mind but also actively engaging with others' contributions.	9.0	Hello Bona,<br><br>It was good to hear you speak during your English assessment! You shared your ideas and opinions clearly, which is a big step. To help you improve even further, focusing on speaking a little more smoothly and watching how you pronounce the ends of your words will make a real difference. Keep up the good work, Bona!<br><br>📋 **Action Plan** <br><li>Practice speaking at a slightly faster, more consistent pace.</li><br><li>Work on placing stress correctly in words, especially avoiding overstressing final syllables.</li><br><li>Try to expand on your friends' ideas more in conversations.</li>	B1	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
