king sure the first syllable is the strongest and loudest.</li><li><b>Focus on Final /t/:</b> Say words like "point," "rocket," and "it" very clearly, focusing on making the sharp "t" sound heard at the end.</li><li><b>Record and Compare:</b> Record yourself saying these words and compare your rhythm to a native speaker's to hear the difference in where the stress is placed.</li></ul><br>You are a very talented and fluent speaker, Nine—keep focusing on these small details and you will reach even higher results! 🎯	\N	\N	15.0	Nine, your Iron Man review was a strong B1 performance! You used an effective rhetorical question to start and your story followed a logical path that was easy for the audience to follow. You showed good control of your vocabulary and shared a personal opinion that made the talk interesting. To get an even higher score, focus on including the author's name and checking your subject-verb agreement in the past tense. Reducing the use of filler words and varying your connectors will make your speaking sound even smoother! 🌟	B1	Speaking	CA	PET	\N	\N
