in more specific terms related to your topic.</p>	2	<p>You introduced your hero and outlined your talk, which is a good start! However, your presentation was quite short, with only 247 words, which is significantly below the expected minimum of 400 words. This has impacted your score here. To improve, aim to extend your responses beyond short phrases and elaborate more on your points. For example, when discussing "What he did," you could give more specific details about the battle and his strategies. Similarly, under "Why he is a hero," adding more examples of his bravery and sacrifices would make your points stronger. Using a wider range of cohesive devices would also help to link your ideas together more smoothly. For example, instead of just listing points like "first," "second," and "last," you could use phrases like "In addition to this," or "Furthermore," to create a more flowing narrative. To achieve a score of 5, you need to produce extended stretches of language with very little hesitation, ensuring your contributions are consistently relevant and well-organized with a clear structure and a range of cohesive devices.</p>	2	<p>Your pronunciation made it difficult to understand some parts of your presentation. Specifically, there was frequent mispronunciation of sounds that affected comprehension, such as "three" sounding like "tree" (the /θ/ sound being replaced by /t/). You also overstressed auxiliary verbs and repetitively dropped word endings, for example, "worked" (missing /t/), "fight" (missing /t/), "criticise" (missing /z/ or /s/), and "message" (missing /dʒ/). This omission of final consonants (like in "fight" and "worked") is a common pattern for Thai speakers. To improve, focus on clearly articulating final consonants in English words. For the /θ/ sound, remember to place your tongue between your teeth and blow air gently, rather than using a hard /t/ sound. Practicing minimal pairs like 'three' and 'tree' can be really helpful. Also, pay attention to word and sentence stress to ensure important words stand out and the rhythm of your speech is natural.</p>	\N	\N	7.0	<p>Hi Eng! 👋 You chose a very interesting hero, Phunloang Patchu, and it's clear you put thought into presenting his story. You did a good job of introducing your hero and outlining your talk. To make your next presentation even better, try to expand on your ideas with more details and examples, and remember to practice your pronunciation, especially those tricky word endings and the /θ/ sound. Keep up the great effort, and you'll shine! ✨</p>	A2+	Speaking	CA	FIRST	\N	\N
