ment:**<br>*   ✅ **Grammar Focus:** When you're speaking or writing, take a moment to think about your nouns – are they singular or plural? And are you using the correct articles like "a," "an," or "the"? This will make your sentences much clearer!<br>*   ✅ **Connect Your Ideas:** Try using a wider range of linking words and phrases such as "however," "furthermore," or "in addition" to make your speech flow more smoothly and connect your ideas more effectively.<br>*   ✅ **Listen to English Rhythm:** Pay attention to how native English speakers pronounce words, especially the ends of words and the natural rhythm of sentences. Try to imitate this as you practise!	B1	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
