ng people to help the environment?<br><br>I do think is a great choice to do but if I need to select, I would select reducing plastic use and saving electricity at home because it's, it just I don't like when the lights turn on, it's too like sparkles. I just close it all day and reducing plastic use is easy because we can use like other other things to use than the plastic because it's bad for environment.<br><br>Yeah, I also think it's important to teach us about the environment because if you don't care about the environments, we just can't live because there's too much like pollution these days from the factory or even the cars mostly.<br><br>Uh, the most difficult one, uh, I for living a good health? Mostly it's about food and these day we just a lot of fast food, junk food and also the drinks, they drink a lot of like Coca-Cola or Fanta or any of that. And also the they're not playing sports, they just play games all day. Yeah.<br><br>Uh, the technology can reduce pollution by like these day we got a kind of robot, but not just human-like. It's a little, like, a box and it just clean up everywhere. And the air pollution, we can reduce by just take a bicycle or just walk if it don't, if your destination is not far from your home.<br><br>Uh, I don't think so because there's a lot of air pollution, water pollution everywhere by people that take cars everywhere like a motorcycle or a big car or a truck. And also the water pollution, we people just don't care and leave the trash in the river or lake everywhere.<br><br>	643	3	You do a wonderful job of using simple sentences correctly to talk about familiar topics like your school routine or your free-time activities. For example, "I also walk to school because my house is near school" is a perfectly clear and accurate sentence! You're also brave enough to attempt more complex sentence structures when sharing your views and describing situations, which is exactly what we want to see. For instance, you said, "Yeah, I 