e connected and collaborative conversation, showing that you're not just taking turns but genuinely building ideas together.	9.0	Vegas, you clearly have a lot to say, and it's great how you get involved in conversations! Your enthusiasm for expressing your ideas is clear. To really boost your English speaking, let's focus on making sure all the little sounds in your words are clear and that your sentences are grammatically complete and smooth. Keep engaging in those conversations, and you'll find your English becomes even more precise and powerful! 💪<br><br>📋 **Action Plan:** Here are three concrete steps you can take to make your English even better:<br>*   ✅ Practice saying the end of every word clearly, especially consonants like 's', 't', and 'd'. Try recording yourself and listening back to catch any sounds you might be skipping!<br>*   ✅ When you're speaking, pause for a moment to think if your sentences have all the little connecting words, like "a," "the," or "with," in the right places. Reading English out loud can help with this!<br>*   ✅ Work on linking your ideas together with different phrases, not just starting new sentences. Think about phrases like "Another point is..." or "Because of this..." to show how your thoughts connect.	B1	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
