y my presentation because I have told you his early life and what... what have he did and how is he a hero? Thank you.	381	3	You used some great topic-specific vocabulary like "researcher," "vaccine," and "influenza" which shows good word knowledge! 😊 The main issues were with verb tenses - you often said "he have worked/invented" instead of "he has worked/invented" or "he worked/invented." Thai learners often struggle with the present perfect tense because Thai doesn't have this exact structure. Remember that "he/she/it" needs "has" + past participle. Also watch for small errors like "a famous words" (should be "a famous word") and "a lots of money" (should be "a lot of money"). These are common mistakes that are easy to fix with practice!	3	You organized your presentation very well with a clear introduction, body, and conclusion - excellent job! 👏 You followed the expected structure by covering Jonas Salk's early life, achievements, criticisms, and why he's a hero. The flow was good, though you had some hesitation and repetition at times. Your use of transition words like "first," "next," and "lastly" helped guide the listener. To improve, try to make your sentences flow more smoothly without pausing as much between ideas.	3	Your pronunciation was mostly clear and easy to understand! 🎯 The main issues were with word stress - you overstressed small words like "was" (should be weaker /wəz/ with schwa sound) and final syllables in words like "action" /ˈæk.ʃən/ and "virus" /ˈvaɪ.rəs/. You also sometimes dropped final consonants in words like "vaccine" /vækˈsiːn/ and "people" /ˈpiː.pəl/, and past tense endings in words like "gained" /ɡeɪnd/ and "started" /ˈstɑːr.tɪd/. These patterns are common for Thai speakers because Thai has different stress rules and final consonant sounds. Practice listening to how native speakers stress words and try to copy their rhythm.<br><br>📋 <b>Action Plan:</b><br>• Practice present perfect tense with "he/she/it has + past participle" through sentence drills<br>• Work on word stress patterns by listening to and repeating native speaker recordings<br>• Focus on pronouncing final consonants clearly, especially in past tense verbs and plural nouns	\N	\N	12.0	<b>Arty (ID: 33955)</b> - Speaking Assessment: <b>12/20 (B2 Level)</b><br><br>Arty, you delivered a well-structured presentation about Jonas Salk with good organization and clear ideas! 👍 You showed you can talk about complex topics and used some excellent vocabulary. The main area to focus on is improving your grammar accuracy, particularly with verb tenses, to make your speaking even more impressive. Keep up the good work - you're making solid progress toward becoming a confident English speaker!	B2	Speaking	CA	FIRST	\N	\N
