ally, I mean, it's very, uh, I will never traveling by train again and I prefer cars because it's kind of relaxing and you can talk to each other freely, not like the trains, you have to be quiet. Uh, I have to always and in car, you always be with your family, so it's guarantee that you will be safe.\n\nYes, it's, it's very important because, uh, knowing you, uh, before you go somewhere like neighbors, sometimes in your boys, you can be lost or you should know the nearest hospital, uh, in case that something happening, like you broke your leg or some accident happens.\n\nUh, the most interesting place is, uh, actually at Phuket. I have a very good experience at Phuket. Uh, the beach is beautiful, so clear, so, so clear and the food is actually good. There's some seafood, seafoods are really, really good, so fresh. Uh, I have traveled been there for just once because we don't have time much. Uh, it's very interesting because there's a lot of, uh, other, other countries from other countries come to Phuket to, a lot of them come to Phuket to take a vacation or something. Yeah, it's very interesting and friendly place.	586	3	Leo, you have some interesting vocabulary, like when you mentioned your grandma being a 'chef' in Australia. That's great! However, there were a few grammar errors that sometimes made it hard to understand. For example, saying 'she's at Australia' isn't quite right. Instead of 'she's at Australia', it would be better to say 'she's in Australia'. Keep practicing those prepositions!	3	I noticed you tried to give long answers, which is good. You included lots of details, for example saying the beach in Phuket was 'so clear, so, so clear'. But sometimes, your sentences were a bit disjointed and had many 'uhms'. To improve, try to pause and think about what you want to say before you start speaking. Even a short pause is better than lots of 'uhms'.	2	Leo, I noticed that your pronunciation was a little difficult to understand at times. You seemed to mumble a bit, making it hard to hear your sounds clearly. For example, try to speak clearly in the beginning and not mumbling. Try to use 'th' sounds and you will be easily understood.	3	Leo, you responded well to my questions and kept the conversation going. You also agreed with Gatchan's ideas in Part 3, saying 'Yeah, I agree with that'. This shows you're listening and engaging. To take it further, try asking Gatchan follow-up questions to show even more interest and keep the conversation flowing naturally. For example, after agreeing, you could ask: 'Why do you think that would be a good choice?'	11.0	Leo, you have some good ideas and vocabulary, but there are some areas to focus on. Work on speaking more clearly and accurately, and try to plan your sentences a little before you speak. This will help you to be more easily understood. All the best, Ed	A2+	Speaking	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N
