35309	2025-09-07	2025-09-07	2026	My Favourite Photograph	Hi, so my name is Atom, as you guys know. So today I will talk all about this photo I've selected, which is one of my favorite. And this is me, my mom and my sister. As some of you guys may not know, my sister name is Neutron. So I'm gonna give you guys some compelling facts and my personal thoughts. So, I once asked my mom, why did I get this name and why my sister named is Neutron? And she said, because both my dad and my mom names is Lex, which means small, and small than small is Adam. Small than Adam is Neutron, which I, I was like, whoa, my mom's quite smart. But when I ask my dad, it's a whole different story, which is kind of funny about it. He said, when he was younger, there was a cartoon and the main character is a robot named Atom. And he said he really loves it. So he named me that, which I find kind of funny and I love my dad.<br><br>Okay, so let's just not waste some more times. Oh, and I forgot. So, my main message is to give love to our loved ones before it's too late.<br><br>So, I will structure my talk in three different things. So first, I will start things off by telling you all about my photo. And second, why I have chosen this photo. And I will end things with why personal photos are so important.<br><br>Okay, so this photo is about me and my family, but you guys won't be able to see my dad because he took it. And we took it in one of my old school, Kasinthorn Academy, which is pretty near here, actually. It was date back then in 2015. And we took it because it was my first time being a narrator. It was such a huge opportunity to be able to speak in front of huge amount of people, especially the one I don't know.<br><br>And then, I will tell you why I have chosen this photo. So, because it captured a really lovely moment with my family, because, as you can see, everybody was so happy in it. Yeah, both of them were so proud of me, even myself. And then it was such an important day of my life, because it was, as I told you, it was my first time being a narrator, and it really went well, and I'm really proud of myself. And thirdly, my mom told me I look good, and looking back, I think it was really cute, and I totally agree with her.<br><br>So we have reached the end of my presentation. I will talk to you why personal photos are so important. So first, to remember our loved ones because you know, people doesn't last forever, but photo does. So being able to take a picture is quite good.<br><br>And secondly, to capture moments that may not happen again, because as I told you, human, people doesn't last forever, and being able to capture a moment that may not happen again, it's really good. And thirdly, just for a pure entertainment. You know what, when I'm, when I'm bored, I can just look at back at photos and it really gives me motivations.<br><br>Okay, in conclusion, I have told you in three different things, and I want you guys to follow my main message, which is, which is, give love to our loved ones before it's too late. Thank you.	584	4	You used a good range of words and generally expressed yourself well, Atom. You did a great job explaining your family's names and the story behind yours! 😊 Just remember to be careful with comparisons; for example, we say "smaller than" instead of "small than". Also, when you talk about "people" in general, we use "don't" (like "people don't last forever") because "people" is plural, not "doesn't". Thai learners sometimes mix these up because the structure can be different in Thai. Keep practising these little things, and your English will sound even more natural!	5	Your presentation was fantastic! You had a really clear structure from beginning to end, starting with an introduction, giving detailed descriptions of your photo, explaining why you chose it, and then talking about why personal photos are important. You moved smoothly from one point to the next, and it was easy to follow your ideas. You spoke for a good amount of time, too, which shows you can develop your points well. Excellent job! 🌟	4	Your speaking was very easy to understand, Atom, and your intonation sounded natural, which is a big plus! 😊 You convey your enthusiasm really well. Sometimes, when you get excited and speak a little faster, some of the sounds at the ends of words can become less clear. For instance, ensure you clearly pronounce final consonants. Thai speakers sometimes tend to drop or weaken final consonants due to differences in Thai syllable structure. Try to slow down just a little sometimes, and make sure those word endings are crisp – it will make an even bigger difference to your already clear speech!	\N	\N	17.0	\N	B1+	Speaking	CA	PET	\N	\N
