ly like your idea, and for me, I also think that they should go to the market because they will buy like a local fruits, vegetables, or maybe a food, food. So they will enjoy eating, like when they're hungry, they can fulfill it, and just talk about something silly or maybe just whatever.\n\nI prefer to, uh, travel by train because it's, uh, it's more comfortable for me, it's really big. So I just sit and then I can sleep whenever I want, or get a food, just order it, and everything, I also like the atmosphere there because some, sometimes it's loud, but when I'm just listening to music and look out at the window, I think I really, uh, feel relaxed, just, uh, getting by myself.\n\nUh, so my opinion, uh, I think it's really important like Kaowut said, because we will know what we want to do there, and we will know where is it, and what can we do when we go to that place, like the activity or it's just for, uh, relax, just chilling, or it, uh, for like maybe do with, uh, some have serious something with it. Uh, like the place, so if we know, uh, if we know what we should do in that place, we should go and we don't need to plan other things.\n\nUh, the most, uh, interesting for me, it's just a big central, because I think in the central it's like it's a huge, it's a huge central for me to walk, like I can buy a lot of things, clothes, uh, food, or maybe drinks, uh, sleep, and it's already like all I need to have it, I need to buy it.	664	4	Grace, your vocabulary is appropriate for B1 level, and you attempt a wide range of topics. I was especially impressed when you used the word 'architecture'. Using specific words makes your descriptions more interesting for the listener. To improve, pay close attention to your verb tenses. For example, instead of saying 'they looks really exciting', it would be better to say 'they look really excited'.	4	I was impressed with how long you can speak, Grace. You consistently provide extended answers, and your ideas are clearly linked together. The examiner can follow your line of thinking without any problem. To improve your coherence further, try using a wider range of linking words. For example, instead of saying 'I prefer to travel by train because...', you could say 'I prefer to travel by train as...'	4	Grace, your pronunciation is already very good! Your linking and intonation help you sound very natural and easy to understand. However, I noticed that your pronunciation of the /k/ sound (as in 'car' or 'school') could be a little stronger. To improve this, practice saying words with a strong /k/ sound, paying attention to making a clear, distinct sound at the beginning of the word. Also, try to really emphasise the beginning and end of your plosives!	5	Grace, you're a great communicator! You respond directly to my questions and build on your partner's ideas really well. In the collaborative task, you said, 'Wow, your idea is really brilliant, Kaowut', which shows you are actively listening and responding positively to his contributions. To make your interactions even better, try asking more follow-up questions to show genuine interest. For example, you could have asked Kaowut, 'Why do you think riding a rollercoaster would be so fun for a school trip?'	17.0	Overall, Grace, you demonstrated strong communication skills at the B1 level. You speak fluently, use a range of vocabulary, and interact effectively with others. Keep practicing your grammar and expanding your vocabulary, and you'll continue to improve. All the best, Ed	B1+	Speaking	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N
