34926	2025-09-07	2025-09-07	2026	My Favourite Photograph	Hello everyone, my name is Chopin. Today, I'm going to present about my favorite photo. As you can see, a picture is a picture of the falling man. And the main my main message for today is behind every number in history, that's a real human life.<br><br><br>But just started, I'm going to do three things. First, the photo, two, why is it important? Three, why are historical photos are important?<br><br><br>I'm going to talk about the photo. This is a guy that jumped from a building. And this is in World Trade Center in New York City. He decided to jump in 911. It is September 11, 2001. Because he doesn't want to get burned by fire. And he is in jump or fell off after the plane is stuck in the tower.<br><br><br>First, why is it important? First, it's so human's light of tragedy. Two, it makes history feel real and emotional. Three, is teaches the importance of remember it.<br><br><br>My historical important, first, they help me remember historical great. Secondly, they make me feel connected to the past. Lastly, they teach me important lessons.<br><br><br>So in conclusion, I have talk about the photo, why is it important, and why are historical photo important. And I want you guys to remember my main message, which is behind every number in history, there's a, there are human life. Thank you.	226	2	You shared some good ideas, but sometimes your grammar made it a bit tricky to follow. For example, you said "I have talk about the photo" instead of "I have *talked* about the photo." Also, when you mentioned "there's a, there are human life," it was a bit confusing with the articles. English grammar can be quite different from Thai, and sometimes we forget to change the verb form for tenses or to use the correct articles (like 'a' or 'the'). To improve, try to pay close attention to verb endings and practice using 'a', 'an', and 'the' correctly. 😊	2	You had a clear plan for your presentation, which is fantastic! You