29031	2025-09-15	2025-09-15	2026	Term 1 Finals	Uh, my, my name is Nupasorn Vorasitipun. It is spelled N A P A S O R N, and my nickname is Racing.<br><br>I live around Nonthaburi, which is a city that is greatly known for a very good university which is name, which is called Mahidol University. It's all about, uh, the medical things.<br><br>I enjoy drawing and painting a lot. I want to improve my, uh, artistic skills along my language skills, so I love to do them both at the same time, although sometimes I cannot keep up with them.<br><br>I really enjoy alternative rock music, as I feel like it, uh, it captures the feeling very well and it's different from the, uh, pop music that we listen to the radio every day.<br><br>Uh, I like to stretch in my free time, and sometimes I like to do weights instead of cardio because I, I, I don't think cardio is that great for, you know, keeping fit. Like, if you do weight, I think it has a better balance. You don't have to stay in a calorie deficit, so you can do weights. Uh, it's a lot of fun.<br><br>Okay. So, the upper picture, it, it shows a group of people sitting in a cafe or a restaurant drinking a beverage. I notice that most of them they, they seem to put their phones down when a lot of people in comparisons today, they, they like to play on their phones. So this, this shows that this group of people, they are, they like to socialize with others and are very extroverted. While the, the picture below, it shows a guy listening to music on his headphones while he is reading a book alone in the, in his garden or something. And that shows that he enjoys his own company more than anybody else and he prefers to be alone. Yeah. And it also shows about a lot about in today's society about people prefer to be alone more and stay in others' people company nowadays.<br><br>All right. I, I get what you mean. Um, I'm also pretty sure because I realized that I haven't been getting enough sleep, so I think sleep and resting is very important for your health. Not only it helps you to rest throughout and and brings you energy throughout the day, it also helps improve your physical, right? Like your height, your weight, your everything, and your eyes, whatever that stuff.<br><br>Yeah, like team sports, it's, it helps in physical health a lot, right? But I also feel like team sport, it also helps in mental health most of the time. I mean, you have people supporting you and that, and that makes you feel like, "Wow, that's so great. People are very supportive of you." But, you know, um, I also think, I also think that eating healthy food is super essential for for our health nowadays. So what do you think?<br><br>Yes.<br><br>Yeah, I get it. I mean, healthy food is great, but you know what else is great? Sometimes maybe food that isn't healthy also helps me happy. Like, improve my mental health too.<br><br>I feel like learning a new skill is the best for people to take care of the health because not only if the skill is is good for physical activities, it also helps improve your mental health, your mindset, everything. What do you think?<br><br>Yeah, I get what you mean. It also helps like, you know, improve your thinking skills too, right? If it's a, like a math skill like you said.<br><br>Yes, I think it's super important for for schools to teach them about healthy eating, especially, uh, when children, they they're exposed to the cafeteria, sometimes it doesn't have the best food. So they should be teach about how to balance their food correctly, like how they can balance their their sweets and their actually healthy food. Like, for example, I, I was a kid that didn't like eating vegetables at all, so now I have to eat them a lot more nowadays. I think I think it's super important because during schools, they didn't teach so well like recommendations to give about, like what is great, what is a great vegetable for this and that. And I think it would be better if they if they put more depth into their teaching.<br><br>I think technology helps people to stay healthy by, you know, like the applications in their phone. It it helps them to maybe check their calories in the the food that they eat every day and check that how much do they have to increase or decrease. It helps provide an easier way for people to calculate their calories in their meals, like not the usual way that they have to do it themselves. I think it would be a nice way and much easier way for people to stay healthy and try eating the correct calorie they needed.<br><br>I, I strongly agree with this one because I've been to various competitions about sports. I feel like they honestly put too much pressure on me. If I fail, I feel like the rest of the team would would hate me. And maybe people on the bleachers, they wouldn't be pleased with the scores. So I feel like there should be some reassurance for the people that are competing before it starts and slowly make them gain more confidence. It, it's different with adults and kids. I feel like kids and teenagers, they they still, they are still very strong about their confidence, so I think they really need some support.	928	4	Racing, you displayed a very good grasp of English grammar, using a variety of sentences and a strong range of vocabulary to talk about different topics, which is a big achievement! You comfortably used advanced terms like "calorie deficit," "extroverted," and "super essential," showing that you have a solid foundation of words to express your opinions. To reach that top score of a 5, let's focus on a few specific areas. For example, sometimes you said "which is name, which is called" instead of "which is named," and "they should be teach" when "they should be taught" is the correct passive voice. Another instance was "others' people company" which could be more naturally expressed as "other people's company." Thai learners sometimes simplify these kinds of structures or translate directly from Thai, so paying close attention to