ning or omitting final consonants. Practising making those final sounds really clear, perhaps even exaggerating them a little at first, and paying attention to consonant clusters, will help you speak even more precisely and with perfect clarity.	5	Racing, you were brilliant at interacting with your partner! You consistently initiated conversations, responded thoughtfully, and connected your ideas seamlessly with what Ikkyu was saying. You really helped to move the discussion forward, offering suggestions and opinions, and you worked well together to negotiate towards a conclusion in Part 3. You actively participated, asked questions to engage the other candidate, and elaborated on your points, demonstrating a natural ability to keep the conversation flowing and involve your partner. This is a crucial skill in a speaking exam, and you showed an excellent command of it, fulfilling all the requirements for a top score. Keep having those engaging conversations!	17.0	Well done, Racing! You spoke confidently and clearly throughout the exam, showing a real knack for expressing your ideas. You handled all the tasks with a genuine eagerness to communicate and interact. Keep working on fine-tuning those tricky grammar points and making sure every sound in your words is heard, and you'll continue to grow as a speaker and confidently express your well-thought-out ideas.	B2+	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
