ugh, you tended to agree with your partner without adding a lot of new information or a different point of view. For instance, after Nene shared an idea, you might just say "I think so" without expanding much. To improve, try to ask your partner more follow-up questions, or offer a slightly different perspective, even if you generally agree. You could say, "I agree with you, and also, another point is..." This will help you to really develop the interaction and show off your conversation skills! 🗣️	9.0	Hi Lookpear! 👋 I'm here to give you some feedback on your speaking test. Overall, you did a good job of communicating your ideas and engaging in the discussion. Your ability to express yourself on various topics is a definite strong point, and it's clear you're building a solid foundation in English. To really push your speaking to the next level, let's focus on making your speech a bit smoother and clearer, especially with some sounds. Keep up the great effort, and remember that every practice helps you improve! You're doing well!<br><br>📋 **Action Plan**<br>*   ✔️ Practice making your sentences flow more naturally.<br>*   ✔️ Work on clearly pronouncing all the sounds at the ends of words.<br>*   ✔️ Try to extend your ideas in discussions by adding more detail or different perspectives.	B1	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N
