alks for a long time with clear organisation. They connect their ideas with words like 'because', 'however', and 'for example'. The listener can follow easily.\n\nYou're at 1/5 because your speech is very short and has many long pauses. You said *'Gonna skip it. So I try again, please.'* — this shows you stopped and restarted. There are many silences marked by `......` (4-7 seconds) where you could not continue. Your ideas are not connected: you jump from 'technologies' to 'experience' to 'plan our life' without linking them. The listener cannot follow a clear line of thought.\n\nTo reach Band 5, work on these two things:\n\n- Plan before you speak. Take 10 seconds to think of 2-3 points. For example: **'First, Gen Z is better with technology. Second, older people think we lack experience. Third, they try to plan our lives.'** This gives you a clear path.\n\n- Practice speaking for 1 minute without stopping. Use a timer. If you get stuck, say **'Another point is...'** or **'For example...'** to keep going. This will help you avoid long silences.\n\nYou can do this! Start with short, simple plans and build up your speaking time slowly.	3	You're doing a good job, and your voice is clear. Sometimes you pause a lot, and this makes it harder to follow what you say. Try to keep going even if you need a moment — it will help your speech sound smoother.\n\nYou also push too hard on the last part of some words. For example, in older /'əʊldə/, people /'piːpəl/, and traditional /trə'dɪʃənəl/, the ending sounds too strong. Try to make the whole word more even, and don't hit the last sound so hard.\n\nThere are a couple of sounds to practise. The "th" sound in think /θɪŋk/ needs a bit of work — put your tongue between your teeth and blow air out. Also, watch the final consonant sounds in words like that /ðæt/. Make sure the /t/ at the end is clear.\n\nYou're making good progress. Keep practising, and you will get better!	\N	\N	8	Hi Porsch,\n\nYou're working at an A2 level in speaking right now, and I can see you have ideas about Gen Z and older people — that's a good start! You used the word *'technologies'* to talk about what makes Gen Z different, which shows you're thinking about the topic.\n\nTo reach Band 5, focus on two things:\n\n- Plan 2-3 simple points before you speak. For example, think of one idea about technology, one about experience, and one about family.\n\n- Practice speaking for one minute without stopping, even if you make mistakes. Use words like 'first', 'also', and 'because' to connect your ideas.\n\nKeep practicing! Every time you try, you get a little better.	A2	Speaking	CA	PET	120	https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qXyjC9N_eMGjuZOXx9TyPnvZK0OcU7Dh/view
