tence before starting the next. Instead of *'gency is like believe in more cultural traditional'*, try **'Gen Z believes in more cultural traditions'**. Say the subject, then the verb, then the object — in that order.\n\n- Use connecting words like 'because' and 'for example'. You have good ideas but they jump together without links. Try: **'Some people think gender is biological, but I think everyone has rights regardless of gender.'**\n\nYou have a good vocabulary range for B1. Focus on completing your sentences, and your speaking will become much clearer!	3	At Band 3, a speaker produces long, well-organised speech with clear structure and a range of linking words. The listener can follow easily without any effort. You're at 3/5 because your response is short and has many long pauses that break the flow. You said *'I think that's like uh outdated because it's like very old thinking and conservative ... why some people may still think'* — the pause and the word 'why' make the connection unclear. You also repeat the same idea about social media without developing it fully. You did use a good word like *'progressive'* to contrast with traditional ideas — that shows you understand the topic.\n\nTo reach Band 3, work on these two things:\n\n- Reduce your long pauses. You have several silences (marked by `...`) in the middle of your sentences. Try to plan your next words while you finish your current sentence. Practice using short fillers like 'well' or 'let me think' instead of silence.\n\n- Use clearer linking words. You said *'and another reason is because of social media'* — this is a good start. Try adding 'firstly', 'secondly', or 'in addition' to make your structure clearer. Also, your conclusion *'so conclusion is I think'* could be 'in conclusion, I believe'.\n\nYou have good ideas about Gen Z and social media. With better organisation and fewer pauses, your speaking will be much stronger!	3	You're doing a good job with your speaking. Your voice is clear and easy to understand. There are a few things you can work on to sound even better.\n\nFirst, try to speak a little more slowly. When you talk fast, the words don't connect well together. Take your time between words so your speech is smoother.\n\nYou also push too hard on the last part of some words. For example, in breadwinner /'bredwɪnə/, housemaker /'haʊsmeɪkə/, opinions /ə'pɪnjənz/, conclusion /kən'kluːʒən/, and people /'piːpəl/, you make the ending too strong. Try to keep the sound more even across the whole word. Don't push the final syllable.\n\nAnother thing to watch is dropping consonant sounds. In think /θɪŋk/, the /k/ sound at the end is missing. In old /əʊld/, the /d/ sound disappears. Make sure you say every consonant clearly, especially at the end of words.\n\nKeep practicing these small points. You're on the right track!	\N	\N	12	Hi PK,\n\nYou're working at a B1 level in speaking. I really like that you have clear opinions — you talked about *'gender is like biological'* and you tried to explain your view on cultural traditions. You also used good words like *'progressive'* and *'cultural'* — these show you know the right vocabulary for this topic.\n\nTo reach Band 5, focus on two things:\n\n- Slow down and finish one sentence before starting the next. Say the subject, then verb, then object in order.\n\n- Use connecting words like 'because' and 'for example' to link your ideas together.\n\nYour vocabulary is good — keep practicing your sentence structure and you will improve a lot!	B1	Speaking	CA	PET	117	https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nqXXCV0P6s0DcLEuNsnz8JDiBZ05qF-R/view
