k the sentence. You also said *'for no reason'* two times in the first part.\n\nHere are two things to work on:\n\n- Reduce your pauses. Instead of *'I come to her ... to ... invite her'*, try planning the whole sentence first. For example: **'I went to her room to invite her to play a game with me'**. Practice saying the full idea without stopping.\n\n- Use more linking words. You used 'and' and 'then' many times. Try adding words like **'because'** or **'so'** to show why things happened. For example: **'I asked her many times, so she shouted at me'**.\n\nYou have a clear story to tell. Keep practicing to make it flow more smoothly!	3	You have a nice voice and it is easy to understand you. You speak with good energy, which is great. There are two main things to work on.\n\nFirst, you often do not say the last sound of a word. For example, in words like first, mad, at, and shout, the final consonant is missing. This can make your words a little unclear. Try to finish each word fully. Say the last sound, even if it feels strange at first.\n\nSecond, you sometimes push too hard on the last part of a word. Words like sister, reason, answer, and question should have a soft ending. Instead, you make the final syllable too strong. Try to keep the stress more even across the whole word. Let the ending be lighter.\n\nYou are doing well. Keep practising these two points, and your speaking will sound even better.	\N	\N	11	Hi Disney,\n\nYou're working at an A2+ level in speaking. I really like that you told a clear story with a beginning, middle, and end. You said *'my sister is my enemy'* — that's a strong way to finish your story!\n\nTo reach Band 5, focus on two things:\n\n- Check your grammar. Make sure you say 'she is mad' (not 'she mad') and 'she doesn't' (not 'she don't').\n\n- Try to speak without long pauses. Practice saying your whole idea in one smooth sentence.\n\nYou have good ideas. Keep practicing!	A2+	Speaking	CA	PET	59	\N
