ed'* again. At the end, you said *'... Yes. And, and that's make me stressed. And'* — this shows you didn't have more to say.\n\nHere are two things to work on:\n\n- Make your ideas longer by adding examples. Instead of just saying *'my mom make a disappointment face'*, you can say: **'My mom looked sad, and that made me feel bad because I wanted to help her'**. This makes your speech longer and more interesting.\n\n- Use better linking words. Instead of only 'and', try: **'The first reason is... The second reason is...'** or **'Another thing that stresses me is...'**. This helps people follow your ideas.\n\nYou have good ideas about stress. Try to say more about each one next time!	2	Your voice is clear and you speak quite fluently, which is great. You keep going without many pauses, and that helps your listener follow your ideas.\n\nOne area to work on is your intonation. Right now, your voice stays quite flat when you speak. Try to let your voice go up and down a little more, especially on the most important words. This will make your speech sound more lively and easier to listen to.\n\nYou also have some trouble with syllable stress. For example, in the words *example* /ɪɡˈzɑːmpəl/ and *properly* /ˈprɒpəli/, the stress is not in the right place. Listen to where the strong part of the word should be, and practise saying these words slowly.\n\nAnother thing to watch is dropping consonant sounds. You sometimes miss the final /t/ in words like *stressed* /strest/. Also, the /s/ and /z/ sounds are a problem for you in general. Make sure you pronounce these sounds clearly at the end of words.\n\nYou are doing well overall. Keep practising these small points, and your speaking will become even clearer.	\N	\N	8	Hi Pang Pang,\n\nYou're working at an A2 level in speaking. I like that you gave two clear reasons for what makes you stressed: one at home and one at school. That shows you can organise your ideas! You also used some good words like *'responsibility'* and *'disappointment face'*.\n\nTo reach Band 5, focus on two things:\n\n- Check your grammar: make sure your verbs match your subjects (like 'my mom tells me', not 'my mom tell me').\n\n- Try to speak for longer by adding more details to each reason. Use words like 'because' and 'also' to connect your ideas.\n\nYou have good ideas. Keep practicing and you will improve!	A2	Speaking	CA	PET	57	\N
