ng is rather than "far from".</li><li><b>📝 Missing the "BE" Verb (is/am/are)</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"It about history and art."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"It <b>is</b> about history and art."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> In Thai, you can sometimes skip the verb when describing something. However, every English sentence MUST have a verb. When you are describing what something is or where it is, you need to use the verb <b>"is"</b>. You also missed this in your first sentence: "That'<b>s</b> great to see you."</li><li><b>📝 Plural Nouns (-s/-es)</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"It would be fun if you visit that museum, because it have many activity to do like puzzle, in role for that story or draw and gess that history."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"It would be fun if you visited the museum because there are many <b>activities</b> to do, like <b>puzzles</b>, role-playing, or drawing and <b>guessing</b> historical events."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> In Thai, the noun doesn't change if there is more than one. In English, if you use words like "many", you must add <b>-s</b> or <b>-es</b> to the noun (e.g., "activities" and "puzzles").</li><li><b>📝 Sentence Capitalisation</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"that's all. see you at my school."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"<b>T</b>hat's all. <b>S</b>ee you at my school."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> Thai script does not use capital letters, but in English, the first letter of EVERY new sentence must be a <b>Capital Letter</b>.</li></ol><br><br>Keep practising these patterns and you'll improve quickly! 🌟<br><br><hr><b>📊 Your Grammar Analysis</b><br><br>I analysed your grammar using Cambridge University's <b>ERRANT</b> script (ERRor ANnotation Toolkit), which is a tool that compares what you wrote against a corrected version to identify grammatical errors. It shows that you wrote <b>8</b> sentences, and <b>0</b> of them had no errors.<br><br><b>Your error breakdown:</b><br><ol><li><b>Missing Verbs:</b> 3 instances</li><li><b>Verb Form Errors:</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Plural/Singular Noun Errors:</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Capitalisation Errors:</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Spelling Errors:</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Preposition Errors:</b> 1 instance</li><li><b>Article/Determiner Errors:</b> 1 instance</li></ol>	A2+	2026
