to make body heally and strong However child or teenager will refused immediately because it was very exhausted and tired to lost a lot of energy and that why reason game is the common thing but it have mean for teenager.<br><br><br>In conclude all of 3 thing that were cloth, study and game what I choose it was the real situation that happen with between family and child. The last main message to make you go in correct way was "choose correct you have good future but choose wrong it can make you be a prison". That was real thing for everyone.	469	6.0	Hello Ken! 👋 It’s clear you’ve put effort into thinking about the different ways friends and parents influence teenagers, and it's great that you're exploring such an interesting topic. You've brought up some really good points about how friends and parents might have different opinions on things like fashion, studying, and even gaming. However, the most significant area for you to focus on for improvement is making sure your essay directly answers the question and that your sentences are clear and easy to read. Keep up the good work, and remember that with a bit more practice on sentence structure and directly answering the prompt, your writing will become much clearer and more impactful! ✨<br><br>📋 **Action Plan:**<br> *   ✅ When you start writing, make sure your first sentence clearly states your main argument or answer to the essay question.<br> *   ✅ After writing a sentence, read it aloud to yourself. If you find yourself taking a very long breath or getting lost, it's a good sign that you might need to break it into two or three shorter sentences and add some punctuation like full stops or commas.<br> *   ✅ Before you submit your writing, reread the essay question and then reread your essay to check if you have directly answered every part of the question.	You’ve done a good job of identifying three key areas where teenagers make choices: clothes and fashion, studying, and your own idea of gaming style. It's really clever how you've thought about how both friends and parents can influence these areas. 👏 To make your essay even stronger and earn a higher score, remember that the question asked "Who has *more* effect?" Your essay needs to consistently argue whether friends or parents have a stronger influence throughout, not just describe their different roles. For instance, in your paragraphs, try to clearly state who you believe has the greater impact in that specific area and why. Sometimes Thai learners tend to describe situations well but can forget to maintain a clear argument that directly answers the main question.	It's wonderful that you’re exploring complex ideas, but a friendly reminder that essays usually have a more formal tone and a clear introduction where you state your main idea, rather than using a list. 😊 The biggest challenge for your reader here is that some of your sentences are very long and have very little punctuation. This makes it quite difficult to understand your excellent ideas. For example, your first paragraph has some wonderful thoughts, but it runs as one very long sentence. Try to break these down into smaller, more manageable sentences, and use full stops to separate them. This will make your writing much clearer and help your reader follow your arguments more easily. Thai learners sometimes prefer to link many ideas in one long sentence, but in English, shorter, well-punctuated sentences often make your writing more powerful.	You've clearly structured your essay into paragraphs, which is a great start. This helps to group your ideas together. 👍 To improve your organisation further, focus on making sure each paragraph has a clear topic sentence at the beginning that tells the reader what that paragraph will be about. Also, think about using a wider range of linking words and phrases to connect your ideas smoothly between sentences and paragraphs. For instance, instead of starting with "The one of popular," you could say "Regarding clothes and fashion," or "Another area to consider is studying." This helps the reader move from one idea to the next without getting lost. Sometimes, Thai learners might use basic linking words, but expanding this range can really help your ideas flow.	You've used some everyday vocabulary that helps convey your message, and it’s good to see you trying to express your thoughts. To really improve your language score, let's focus on a few key areas. Firstly, pay close attention to choosing the right word for the context. For example, instead of "effect all thing," you might say "affect everything," or "make body heally and strong" could be "make the body healthy and strong." Secondly, punctuation is very important, especially full stops and commas, to make your sentences clear. The long, unpunctuated sentences are the most significant barrier to understanding. Thirdly, work on subject-verb agreement and tense consistency. For instance, "Friend is the person who like play" should be "Friend is the person who *likes* to play." Thai learners sometimes have difficulty with subject-verb agreement because their native language doesn't have the same grammatical structures, and they might also translate directly, which can lead to word choice errors. Practising these areas will make a significant difference to the clarity and accuracy of your writing. ✨	2.0	1.0	2.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
