1946	34289	2025-09-18 20:05:22.445369+00	Term 1 Exam Question 1	I have my friends who are really professional and have knowledge abouts clothes and fashion. First, in my opinion, I think when we're having a good fashion are good for yourself. I have my friends who loves fashion, his name is Khun. When I saw he playing his phone, he just only find a t-shirt and pants for his style. And he can help me to change my fashion style to be look better than before. And of course, I look handsome than before. handsomer clothes and fashion are good for your style looking. In conclusion, find a style or a good fashion are good for yourself and people gonna looking at you because you are handsome/beautiful. Keep going to changing your self.<br><br><br>Second, I will talk about Studying. Studying is so important for your future. We must be good And keep study hard. I also have my friends who study very hard and he are really good at studying. His name is Kris. Everyone may know this guy because he help his classmat to learn study. It's good to help each other who need help or not really good at studying, he's my idol for study hard and improve your score to be better than before and care alot about your grade for your future. But my parents also help me about my homework. Example, I can't do math homework, My mom who can help me to do math fast, she can help me to do homework and can teach me to solve math test.<br><br><br>In conclusion, my parents and my friends are really has more effects on the choices to help me study hard and keep going for my future.<br><br><br>The last thing I will talk about sports. My friends are also the choices that I chose because I play with them every. He's Kris again. I've been playing basketball with him together. I don't really good at basketball but Kris who was played basketball and very professional, he teach me how to shoot, dribbling and everything about basketball. He's good at everything about studying and sports. He's my best friend and he help me everything.<br><br><br>In conclusion, playing sports are good and healthy for your body. Pratice more and workout alot for your good physique. Keep going to workout and go to fitness and play sports.	393	9.0	Well done, Pea, for tackling such an interesting essay question. Your writing shows that you have some good ideas about how friends and family can influence your choices. However, there are a few areas where we can make some improvements, especially with structuring your essay and making your arguments clearer. With a bit of practice, I am sure you will make wonderful progress.<br><br>📋 **Action Plan for Improvement:**<br>*   ✍️ Focus on building a single, strong argument throughout your essay, ensuring every part connects back to your main point.<br>*   🧐 Before you write, plan your paragraphs so each one has a clear topic sentence and only one main idea, avoiding mini-conclusions until the very end.<br>*   📏 After writing, read your work aloud to catch any sentences that sound awkward or unclear, and check for consistent grammar like subject-verb agreement.	You have done a good job including all the points asked for in the question, such as clothes and fashion, studying, and your own idea about sports. That is an excellent start! 🥳 However, to truly excel, try to directly answer the question throughout your essay. For example, instead of just describing how your friends influence your fashion, you could compare that influence to your parents' influence and explicitly state who you think has a greater effect. Think about posing the question at the start of each body paragraph to guide your writing and ensure you're always comparing and contrasting the influences of friends and parents. You also wrote quite a bit more than the suggested word count. While it is good to have lots to say, keeping within the word limit helps you practise being concise and focused.	You have communicated your ideas in a way that is generally easy to understand, which is a big plus. 👍 However, for an academic essay like this one, it is important to use a more formal style. Your writing felt a little like you were chatting with a friend, with phrases like "people gonna looking at you" rather than a more formal "people will look at you". To make your writing more appropriate for a formal essay, try to avoid slang and informal expressions. For instance, instead of starting a sentence with "And of course", you could use a more formal linking phrase like "Furthermore" or "In addition". This will help you present your straightforward ideas in a more academic and persuasive way.	You structured your essay with clear paragraphs for each topic, which is a good foundation. 📚 It shows you are thinking about how to group your ideas. However, you used "In conclusion" several times throughout your essay, not just at the very end. This can be a bit confusing for the reader, as it makes it seem like the essay is finishing multiple times. Imagine an essay as a journey: you only reach the conclusion once, at the very end. To improve, try to have one clear introductory paragraph, a few body paragraphs that each discuss a single main idea, and then one strong concluding paragraph that summarises everything. For example, instead of a mini-conclusion about fashion, simply transition to your next point about studying. Thai learners sometimes use such 'summary' phrases to mark the end of a thought, but in English academic writing, a clear transition is often more effective.	You used a good range of everyday words that suited your topics, which is commendable. 😊 However, there were a few areas where your grammar and spelling could use some attention. For example, you wrote "fashion are good" instead of "fashion *is* good" (this is a subject-verb agreement issue) and "he are really good" instead of "he *is* really good". Also, words like "abouts" should be "about", "classmat" should be "classmate", and "alot" should be "a lot". Try to pay close attention to these small details. A common challenge for Thai learners is sometimes verb agreement or using the correct prepositions, so focusing on those areas will really help your sentences flow more smoothly and clearly for the reader. For instance, when you are proofreading, you could specifically look for all your verbs and make sure they agree with their subjects.	3.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
