cademic setting.	Your essay is well-organised, Gut-Jung, with a clear introduction, separate paragraphs for each of your points, and a concluding paragraph that summarises your argument. This logical flow makes your essay easy to follow, and your use of linking words like "Besides" and "Finally" helps to guide the reader along. 🗺️ Many students, including Thai learners, often use these common linking words effectively. To achieve an even higher score, you could explore a wider variety of cohesive devices to connect your ideas, such as "Furthermore," "Moreover," or "In addition to this." Also, thinking about how sentences within each paragraph build upon each other can create an even more seamless and integrated flow, making your arguments feel very polished.	You’re using a good range of vocabulary and sentence structures in your writing, Gut-Jung, which is wonderful! Keep building on that. However, there are a few areas where precision in grammar and word choice would really elevate your work. For example, I noticed a few instances of incorrect word forms, such as "themselve" instead of "themselves," "effection" instead of "effect" or "influence," and "motivationg" instead of "motivating" or "motivational," and "finacial" instead of "financial." Subject-verb agreement is another area to watch; remember that "parents *do not* understand" rather than "parents *does not* understand." These kinds of errors are quite common among Thai learners because English grammar rules, especially those for word formation and agreement, can be quite different from Thai. To help with this, you could create a personal list of tricky words and their correct forms to study. Also, try reading your sentences aloud; sometimes, a sentence that sounds a little awkward needs a small rephrase to make it sound more natural, such as 'friends have more *influence* on decisions' rather than 'friends have more effection in deciding things.' Focusing on these details will make your writing much clearer and more sophisticated! ✨	4.0	3.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
