", you must add an 's' to the end of the noun (<b>cultures/festivals</b>) to show it is plural.</li><li><b>📝 Vocabulary Choice (Word Confusion)</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"When you come to Thailand, please expect each other, and don't be rude."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"When you come to Thailand, please <b>respect</b> each other, and don't be rude."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> This looks like a simple mix-up between two words that sound similar. "Expect" means you think something will happen (คาดหวัง), but "respect" means to show politeness and honor to someone (เคารพ). You also had a similar mix-up with "being" instead of "bring" (นำมา) in your sentence about sunscreen.</li><li><b>📝 Natural Word Order</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"Hi If you find some aboard trip, Thailand is better for you."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"Hi, if you are looking for a <b>trip abroad</b>, Thailand is <b>the best choice</b> for you."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> There are two things here. First, "aboard" means being on a ship or plane (บนเรือ), while "abroad" means another country (ต่างประเทศ). Second, in English, we usually put the description after "trip" in this context. Using "the best choice" sounds more natural than "better" when you are recommending a single destination from many options.</li></ol><br><br>You've got the right idea with how to structure your advice. Just keep a close eye on those plural 's' endings and double-check words that sound similar but have different meanings.<br><br><b>📊 Your Grammar Analysis</b><br><br>I analysed your grammar using Cambridge University's <b>ERRANT</b> script (ERRor ANnotation Toolkit), which is a tool that compares what you wrote against a corrected version to identify grammatical errors. It shows that you wrote <b>7</b> sentences, and <b>0</b> of them had no errors.<br><br><b>Your error breakdown:</b><br><ol><li><b>Word Choice and Punctuation:</b> 8 instances</li><li><b>Verb Form Errors:</b> 3 instances</li><li><b>Noun Number (Plurals):</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Missing or Unnecessary Articles (a/the):</b> 3 instances</li><li><b>Preposition Errors:</b> 2 instances</li></ol>	A2+	2026
