796	29031	2025-07-18 07:59:25.25331+00	Midterm: Term 1, 2025-6	A place I love is Pattaya which is located around the central south of Thailand. I'm really fonded of this place because of the memories I've made while I was staying there. Pattaya is greatly known for its sandy beach and vivid night life. Furthermore, it's also incredibly popular among tourists who visited Thailand. It's a place that you need to experience yourself at least once.<br><br><br>There are several reasons why Pattaya is packed with tourists almost everyday, and why I personally think that it deserves the hype. Firstly, Pattaya has a great mix of city and nature all together. It's a seaside filled with loads of people enjoying must-do activities, such as skiing, swimming or maybe even go on boat tours. Although it may seem not so relaxing, then I recommend enjoying the sunset at dawn. I have been admiring the scenery ever since, and never got bored of it. Next, the night life is something you can't miss. People never sleeps at night in Pattaya, since they'd be going to the night market to buy the local fresh seafood or they'd be at the bar district that is filled with people everyday. I've been to both of the districts, and I'm sure that you'll regret not visiting both of them.<br><br><br>All in all, Pattaya is a unique and an incredible place to visit during anytime' of the year, especially New Years, since they are extremely precise with the celebration. I've loved going to this place since I was young. Which is why you 'can't miss out.	\N	\N	\N	Racing, you have fully addressed the task by clearly identifying Pattaya as a place you love and providing compelling reasons for your affection, including personal memories, its natural beauty, activities, and vibrant nightlife. You support your points with rich details such as "sandy beach and vivid night life," "skiing, swimming or maybe even go on boat tours," and descriptions of the night market and bar district. All content is relevant, and the target reader is fully informed. Despite exceeding the general word count, the additional details provided enhance the essay's coherence and effectiveness, rather than causing strain or irrelevance.	You effectively use the conventions of an essay to hold the target reader's attention and communicate straightforward ideas, and occasionally complex ones. The introduction clearly sets the stage, and the conclusion provides a strong closing recommendation. You use persuasive language effectively, such as "It's a place that you need to experience yourself at least once" and "it deserves the hype." The tone is consistently engaging and enthusiastic. You also attempt to directly address the reader ("you can't miss," "you'll regret") which enhances engagement. The essay successfully conveys the positive aspects of Pattaya, communicating both its general appeal and specific attractions. To improve to a 5, you would need to demonstrate even greater control and flexibility in using communicative strategies, ensuring a consistent and refined style that communicates all ideas with utmost clarity and impact. For example, you could replace slightly informal phrases like "It's a place that you need to experience yourself at least once" with more formal or impactful phrasing such as "Pattaya offers an unparalleled experience that is not to be missed" to further refine the academic style. Additionally, ensuring all contractions like "can't" and "you'll" are expanded for a consistently formal register would enhance the overall impact.	The text is well organised and coherent. You use clear paragraphs, with each focusing on distinct aspects of Pattaya: an introduction, general reasons for its popularity (mix of city and nature, activities, sunset), and then a detailed description of the nightlife. The conclusion provides a good summary and final recommendation. You use a variety of linking words and cohesive devices, such as "Furthermore," "Firstly," "Although," "Next," and "All in all," to connect your ideas logically and move the essay forward. The internal coherence within paragraphs is strong. To achieve a score of 5, you could use an even wider range of cohesive devices and organisational patterns with greater sophistication, ensuring seamless transitions and a perfectly smooth flow throughout the entire essay. For example, instead of simply starting a new paragraph with "Next," you could use more sophisticated transitions like "Moving on to another key attraction," or "Beyond its daytime charm, Pattaya truly comes alive at night." You could also use more complex sentence structures to link ideas, such as subordinating conjunctions (e.g., "While the daytime offers a plethora of activities, the evening reveals a completely different side of Pattaya").	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Reading	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	80	49	Fantastic work, Racing! You achieved right near the top of all students who took the test this year! You were marked wrong on one or more questions due to misspellings or extra words in your answer. Be careful to write the exact answer.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2+	2026
