ommon two-syllable words; remember that /iː/ endings like in "happy" are usually unstressed /ˈhæp.i/.<br>2. Focus on pronouncing every consonant sound, particularly at the ends of words, to improve your overall clarity.<br><br>With a little more focus on word stress, your speaking will become even clearer, Nine! 🌟	Nine, you provided a clear retelling of a famous story with a very effective rhetorical hook to start! Your storytelling was logical and used helpful connecting words like "at first" and "suddenly" to keep the listener interested. To improve, try to include the author's name and add more specific details about your own opinion to make your talk longer. Pay attention to small grammar points like using "confidence" as a noun and making sure every sentence has a verb. You are a clear communicator and you follow the structure well. 🌟	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/149T-QIza1cCqeNpsUNQzEvHxMwqCJN4X?usp=sharing	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
