uent and easily digestible piece of writing.	You use everyday vocabulary generally appropriately for the topic of describing a city, such as \\"capital city,\\" \\"shopping center,\\" \\"department store,\\" \\"landmark,\\" \\"statue,\\" \\"dish,\\" \\"chef,\\" \\"desserts,\\" and \\"polite.\\" However, there are numerous noticeable errors in grammar and vocabulary that affect the overall clarity and control of the language. Examples include: \\"Japan's country\\" (Japan or Japanese country), \\"Many peoples\\" (Many people), \\"for find\\" (to find), \\"There have more of\\" (There are many), \\"dog that stay\\" (dog that stays), \\"it is be honest\\" (it is honest), \\"mad's cafe have more everywhere\\" (cafes are everywhere), \\"they will has\\" (they will have), and \\"my writting\\" (my writing). These errors are frequent and, while often allowing the meaning to be determined, they significantly impede the overall fluency and accuracy. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to use a range of vocabulary and grammatical forms with control and flexibility, with only occasional errors that do not impede communication.	3.0	2.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
