 become uh associated with the politics, he was the Roman dictator, so he has reformed the politics to um make it better. Well, uh he has done a lot of great things. Although some people may not agree because he was not entirely a good person. He was still a bad person if we think about it today, but at that time he was better than any ruler that can compare.<br><br>And not only that, he also fought for peace. He he brought peace to the Republic and the Empire because uh he just wants the best for his people and yeah. Okay, so now I'm going to be talking about the things you got criticized for and his major flaws. Like I've said, he is not entirely a good person. So, uh the most the more memorable thing horrible thing that he did was he prevent free elections from uh his civilians, which means uh peasants or people those who were not associated with the politics, um they they weren't they didn't have the ability to speak up about how they feel about the the you know, their republic, which means they they don't have the rights to speak up about it.<br><br>And not only that, he also suppressed some uh oppositions from his [laughter] from his associates which some at that time thought it was unfair. And the most importantly, he was accused of being a tyrant. A tyrant is someone who like, you know, um how should I say it? Like he wants the power to corrupt the society and the politics, which um that was obviously not his intention, but he was accused of it and he got brutally assassinated by that specific reason too.<br><br>So now I'm going to specifically talk about how is he a hero for me. Well, first of all, uh not only did he reform the politics, he he helped uh those who were in poverty. He lent lands to them, those who are poor and he he not not only if uh he is good at politics, he is also pretty good at his intelligence. Uh if you know, the modern calendar that we use today is the calendar that he created, which is the Julian calendar which has, you know, a majo