630	29031	2025-07-13 03:11:46.227732+00	Expository Essay	There is a large amount of people who have pets in their home all around in Thailand: my friend adopted a cat few years ago, my aunt used to have a snake and my grand ma has a pack of dogs. Surprinsingly, a common belief among Thai buddhists is that humans are more superior than animals. I hardly agree with the statement.<br><br><br>Sometimes, the said belief could lead to neglect and unhealthy habits towards their pets. I personally think that we should still care about our pets, even if they are lower than us. To illustrate, we are responsible for our pets behaviors. Although the belief may be true, there are better ways of taking care of them instead of neglecting them. The least we can do are the necessities which are feeding them, bathe them or taking them for a simple walk. Try to spend time with them and show your affection towards them. Since animals can gradually develop depression too.<br><br><br>To sum it all up, I strongly believe that we need to take care of our pets due to them being the animals that we adopted, which makes them our responsibility. After all, they are still living things, with feelings and necessities, just like us humans. The way I see it, pets still should be taken care of and loved from us, despite being inferior to us humans.	230	15.0	Hi Racing, your essay effectively argues for the importance of pet care and challenges the idea of human superiority over animals. You present clear arguments and support them with relevant points. To further improve, focus on refining your sentence structure for better flow and ensuring greater control over a wider range of grammatical forms. Keep up the good work!	Racing, your essay is highly relevant to the task and effectively addresses the prompt by arguing against the idea of human superiority leading to neglect of pets. You present a clear stance and provide supporting details about the responsibilities of pet ownership. You also introduce the interesting cultural context of Thai Buddhist beliefs, which adds depth to your argument. All content is relevant, and the target reader is well-informed of your perspective.	You effectively use the conventions of an essay to communicate straightforward ideas, and you make a good attempt at communicating more complex ideas related to cultural beliefs and animal welfare. The essay holds the target reader's attention through its clear argumentative stance and logical progression of ideas. Your personal opinion is clearly expressed, and the tone is appropriate for a persuasive essay.	You have organised your text well, with a clear introduction that sets the context, a body paragraph that develops your argument, and a concise conclusion that reiterates your main point. You use a variety of linking words and cohesive devices to good effect, which help to connect your ideas and maintain coherence throughout the essay. The paragraphing is logical and aids readability.	You use a good range of everyday vocabulary related to pets and care. There are some instances of less common lexis used appropriately. You use a range of simple and some complex grammatical forms with a good degree of control. However, there are occasional errors that impede communication, but they do not consistently impede communication.	4.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2+	\N	\N	\N	B2+	2026
