als	FIRST	Your voice is clear and easy to understand, Kris, which is so important! 🗣️ Your intonation and the way you stress words in a sentence are generally good, and you're making good use of linking sounds. To get to a 5, you could work on making sure all your consonant sounds, especially at the end of words, are super clear. For example, really pronounce the final /k/ sound in words like "think" or the final /t/ sound in "important." Sometimes, Thai speakers tend to soften or drop final consonants due to differences in syllable structure in Thai, so practising these will make your English sound even more precise.	Kris, you've shown a good command of English in your speaking test, communicating your ideas effectively and engaging well in discussions. While you're already doing many things well, focusing on a few key areas will help you really polish your language and achieve an even higher score. Keep up the great work! 🚀<br><br>📋 **Action Plan**<br>*   ✔️ Pay close attention to your verb tenses and subject-verb agreement.<br>*   ✔️ Practise using a wider variety of vocabulary and more complex sentence structures.<br>*   ✔️ Focus on clearly articulating consonant sounds, especially at the end of words.<br>	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1yqGR5ip5XtVuoI2jPIboJbuDxmsnlN7a?usp=drive_link	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
