mma Watson and they... they criticize her in online or in real life, like in X application, there there's hashtag RIP Emma Watson. It is fake... fake die report because just they hate her.<br><br><br>And why she's a real hero, not just a celebrity? Because she fight for pre-prejudice and she... she's challenging, she empower, she is confident to speak up for justice.<br><br><br>And now let me wrap up with... what I have talked today. And I will... my main message that I have... that I want you to know is, if not me, who? If not now, when? It is in Emma Watson quote. Yeah... I it is powerful to Thai people in our age to remember that we can be confident, no matter what gender we are. Thank you.	466	9.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Speaking	CA	FIRST	<p>Your pronunciation sometimes made it difficult to understand your message clearly. You frequently dropped word endings and consonants. For example, you pronounced "isn't" as /ˈɪzən/, "she's" as /ʃiː/, "goodwill" as /ɡʊd wɪ/, and "outline" as /ˈaʊt laɪ/. This can make it challenging for your listener to understand every word. Additionally, you tended to overstress vowel sounds in auxiliaries like "was", which can affect the natural rhythm of English. To improve, practice pronouncing final consonants clearly and consciously. For example, focus on words ending with /t/, /d/, /s/, and /z/. Try to listen to native speakers and imitate their rhythm and stress patterns, paying attention to how unstressed vowels are reduced (the schwa sound /ə/ is very common in unstressed syllables in English).</p>	Hello Lookpear! 👋 You did a fantastic job delivering a comprehensive presentation about Emma Watson! You covered many interesting points about her life and activism, and your main message was very clear. Keep up the great work! ✨ To improve even further, focus on refining your grammar and making sure your ideas flow as smoothly as possible. You're doing great! 💪</p>	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4