xcited to share our own ideas that we forget to cover every single point the task gives us. So, next time, imagine you're ticking off a checklist to make sure you've included everything. ✔️	You've made a great start with your email by beginning with "Hello!" and finishing with "See you, Tonnam." That's exactly how we write to a friend! Your message is also organised into neat paragraphs, which makes it easy for your reader to follow your thoughts. 😄 To make your emails even more engaging, try to think about how you can grab your friend's attention and keep them interested throughout. You've definitely got the right idea about how to structure an email to a pal.	The way you've organised your email into different paragraphs is really helpful and makes your message clear and simple to understand. You've used everyday words like "and" and "but" to connect your sentences, which is a good way to link your thoughts. 👍 To make your writing flow even more beautifully, you could try using a few more varied linking words. For instance, instead of just "And we should bring water too," you could say "Also, bringing water would be a good idea," or "It might also be a good idea to bring water." This helps your ideas join up seamlessly, like stepping stones across a river.	You've used a lot of familiar, everyday words in your email, which is just right for chatting with a friend. Well done! 🗣️ However, there are a few places where your grammar could use a little extra care. For example, when you wrote "I really excited," remember we need a "to be" verb in there, so it should be "I **am** really excited." And "I have ask" should be "I have **asked**" because we use a different form of the verb after "have." Also, with phrases like "pick up me," we usually say "pick **me** up." These little changes in sentence structure and word order are common areas where English learners from Thailand sometimes find things a bit different from their own language. Don't worry, with a bit more practice, you'll get the hang of these tricky bits and your sentences will feel much more natural! Keep practicing, and your writing will become super clear. 🌟	2.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
