 improve your organisation, think about how you can group related ideas together using paragraphs. This makes your writing more coherent and much easier for the reader to understand the flow of your thoughts. For example, your current email presents several ideas in a continuous block. If you were to create a new paragraph when you switch from discussing travel plans to talking about activities, it would guide the reader more effectively through your message. Thai learners sometimes present ideas concisely, and separating these ideas into paragraphs can greatly help in structuring your writing for an English-speaking audience.	You used everyday vocabulary appropriately, which is great for communicating with a friend. For example, phrases like "exited to see you" convey your feeling clearly. However, there are a few areas where your grammar could be more accurate. For instance, instead of "I exited to see you," it would be more grammatically correct to say "I'm excited to see you." Similarly, "I think is better" should be "I think it is better," and "will have to many peple" would be "will be too many people." Finally, "it hard to find" should be "it will be hard to find." Focusing on subject-verb agreement, correct use of pronouns, and auxiliary verbs will help make your writing clearer and more precise. These types of errors are common, and regular practice with sentence structure can lead to significant improvements.	1.0	2.0	2.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
