. Keep up the good work, you're certainly on your way to expressing yourself clearly and effectively! ✨<br><br>📋 **Action Plan for Milan:**<br>*   ✍️ **Plan your paragraphs:** Before you start writing, quickly jot down what you want to say in each paragraph, especially for your "own idea" point and a clear conclusion.<br>*   🧐 **Proofread for common errors:** Take a moment to read through your essay carefully, looking specifically for mistakes with things like plurals and verb endings.<br>*   📏 **Aim for the right length:** Try to keep your essays within the suggested word count, as this helps you to be concise and keep your arguments focused.	You’ve done a good job of tackling the main points of the question, Milan, discussing how friends influence clothes and fashion, and how parents influence studying. That's a solid foundation! However, when you introduced 'hobbies' as your own idea, it would have been really helpful to see that idea explored in its own paragraph, just like you did with the other two points. 🤔 Also, your essay finished a little suddenly, and it's always a good idea to bring all your thoughts together in a nice, clear concluding paragraph. This helps your reader feel like they've understood your full argument. Sometimes, Thai learners might introduce a point but then move on without fully expanding on it, so remembering to develop each idea thoroughly will really help you get those higher marks!	You’ve shown a good understanding of what an essay needs, Milan, by clearly stating your main ideas in the introduction. That’s an excellent way to start! 👍 Your writing is generally easy to understand, which is the most important thing. To make your essays even stronger, think about making sure your formal tone stays consistent throughout. Sometimes, you might use slightly less formal language, and keeping it consistently academic will help your essay feel more polished. Also, a strong conclusion would really tie your whole argument together and make sure your reader feels completely satisfied with your points.	Your essay has a good basic structure, Milan, with a clear introduction and separate paragraphs for clothes and fashion, and studying. This makes your essay easy to follow at first. You've also used some helpful linking words, like "To begin with" and "Beside," which guide the reader. To improve further, try to make sure each paragraph develops one main idea fully, and remember to include that important concluding paragraph to summarise your thoughts. Sometimes, it's easy to write very long paragraphs, but breaking them down into more focused sections can make your ideas even clearer for your reader. Thai learners sometimes prefer longer paragraphs, but in English academic writing, shorter, more focused paragraphs often work best.	Milan, you’ve used a good range of everyday words in your essay, and you’re certainly trying to express some complex ideas, which is commendable! ✨ To make your writing even clearer, let's focus on a few things. Firstly, be mindful of subject-verb agreement; for example, we'd say "teenagers *like*" instead of "teenagers likes." Secondly, pay close attention to verb forms, as sometimes words like "effected" should be "affected." Lastly, a quick spell check can catch common errors like "belive" (should be "believe") or "now days" (should be "nowadays"). These kinds of errors, which are quite common for Thai learners, can sometimes make your meaning a little harder to grasp, but with a bit of practice, you’ll see a big improvement in your accuracy!	3.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
