trating'.<br>2. <b>Spelling!</b> 📖 'Prounded' should be 'proud'. Small errors can distract the reader.<br>3. <b>Clarity!</b> 👓 Some sentences were a bit hard to follow. Try to make them simpler and more direct.	Your story about Megan the robot is relevant and has a clear problem-solution arc. 💡<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Focus!</b> 🎯 Try to concentrate on one main challenge Megan faces. Is it getting lost, or a bad signal? Focusing will make the story stronger.<br>2. <b>Details!</b> 🤖 'Crazy robot' – what makes her crazy? Does she sing? Dance strangely? Show us!	I could follow the main events of your story, showing Sam's journey with his invention. 🛠️<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Clarity!</b> 🗣️ Phrases like 'caused disgusting for his research' are a bit confusing. Perhaps 'caused problems for his research'.<br>2. <b>Engagement!</b> 🤩 Try to use more descriptive language to draw the reader into Sam's struggles and triumphs.	You used linking words like 'Intially', 'Subsequently', and 'Ultimately' to show the sequence of events. 🚧<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Cohesion!</b> 🔗 Some transitions felt abrupt. Try to link your sentences and ideas more smoothly within paragraphs.<br>2. <b>Sentence Structure!</b> ✍️ Varying sentence beginnings will make the story more engaging.	You have a creative imagination! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Intially' -> '<b>Initially</b>'. 'Prounded' -> '<b>Proud</b>'.<br>2. <b>Word Choice!</b> 📖 'Caused disgusting for his research' -> 'Caused <b>frustration</b> for his research'. 'Fastly' -> '<b>Fast</b>'.<br>3. <b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'He born' -> 'He <b>was born</b>'. 'It need' -> 'It <b>needs</b>'.<br>4. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Ran away of a house' -> 'Ran away <b>from a house</b>'.<br>5. <b>Pronouns!</b> 👤 'Many neighbours always suggest him to control it. clearly.' -> 'Many neighbours always suggest him to control it <b>clearly</b>.'	4.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https:/