'd prefer to build a robot because I really enjoy hands-on activities' or 'I think building a robot sounds more exciting than watching a film.' Always make sure your opinion is clear. 👍	You've done well to use an email format, starting with 'Dear Corey' and ending with a closing. However, when writing to a friend, we usually use a more informal closing than 'Yours sincerely.' Something like 'See you soon,' or 'Best wishes,' would be more suitable for an email to a friend. 📧 Think about who you are writing to and choose your greetings carefully.	Your email is generally well-organised, and you've used paragraph breaks to separate your ideas, which is helpful for the reader. Well done. You also used linking phrases like 'This is because' to connect your thoughts. To make your writing flow even better, try to vary these linking words. For example, instead of repeating 'This is because,' you could use 'Also,' 'Moreover,' or 'Another reason is...' This will help your sentences connect more smoothly and make your writing easier to read. 🏞️	You've used everyday words quite well, and your simple sentences are generally clear. However, there are a few places where the grammar could be a little more accurate. For example, you wrote 'Thank for getting the ticket for me' when it should be 'Thanks for getting the ticket for me.' Also, the sentence 'this is because my mom, she enjoys with creating technology such as robot' is a bit long and has some extra words; a clearer way to say this might be 'This is because my mum enjoys creating technology, like robots.' Or even better, provide *your* reason. Lastly, when you said 'I think it would be really nice if we all bring our own bottles,' 'bring' should be 'brought' to match the conditional 'if we all brought.' These kinds of small adjustments will make your writing much clearer and more precise. In Thai, sometimes the subject of a sentence can be left out, or repeated, which can lead to English sentences having an extra pronoun or 