ny bars drink also, but right here, uh, in this place, I recommend like those, uh, barbecue like grill beef, grill pork, something like that. And if you... Yeah, Japan is the country of seafood. There are so many fish there. So, recommend Kuromon Market. If you love seafood, yeah, many like you go try sashimi, many like seafood like hotate, makuro, salmon. Yeah, many a lot of fish there. You should go try also the crab, octopus. Yeah, the maybe it's the best... no, it's the best market, seafood... it's the best market of seafood.	\N	14.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Speaking	CA	FIRST	You have a good loud voice, Mymind, and generally excellent intonation, which makes your speech engaging. However, your intonation degraded when you were under stress, and there were some problems with specific sounds, such as "China" sounding like "Shina." To achieve a score of 5, focus on maintaining consistent intonation even when you are thinking or trying to recall information. Pay close attention to individual consonant sounds, particularly those that are influenced by your first language. Practice minimal pairs for sounds like /tʃ/ and /ʃ/ (e.g., "chair" vs. "share") to improve articulation and ensure clarity.	Hello Mymind, your presentation on Osaka was engaging, delivered with a good loud voice, and you demonstrated excellent knowledge of the material, which helped hold the audience's attention. To further enhance your performance, focus on maintaining consistent intonation when under stress and refining your overall fluency to minimize hesitation and breakdowns in discourse.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
