3098	34924	2026-01-04 05:36:03.473315+00	Midterm Exam Part 1	Hello, Maya<br><br>You will come to my school next month for a Language & Media Day. I can help you about the good place near my school. It has a hostel cost 10 $ / person it not much expensive that hostel it look perfect to stay, the hostel far from my school about 400 m. around the mall. And about Thai communication history it has a museum time open was at 9.00 am - 16.00 pm. In that museum the place you will visited you have to know some body-language to say hello and have a question. If you want to hello just wave you hand, or you have a question you can raid your hand up and ask the question. You have to be polite when you at the museum. Enjoy with you school trip.<br><br>Goodbye Maya.<br><br>PingPing	133	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Use of English	Formative	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	2	2.28	Hi Ping-Ping! 😊 You put a lot of thought into explaining these directions and rules, and it is great to see your ideas! <br><br>You tried really hard with this and I noticed some really positive things about your work:<br><br><ul>  <li>✨ <b>Vocabulary Range</b>: You used good topic-specific words like "communication history," "body-language," and "museum" to make your writing more interesting.</li>  <li>🎯 <b>Grammatical Range</b>: I was very impressed that you attempted to use complex structures like "If" sentences (conditionals) to explain what to do.</li>  <li>💪 <b>Sentence Linking</b>: You successfully used connectors like "and," "or," and "if" to show the relationship between your ideas.</li></ul><br><br>However, there are some grammar patterns we need to work on together. I'll explain WHY you're making these mistakes so you can fix them:<br><br><ol><li><b>📝 "There is" vs "Have"</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"It has a hostel cost 10 $ / person it not much expensive that hostel it look perfect to stay, the hostel far from my school about 400 m. around the mall."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"<b>There is</b> a hostel that <b>costs</b> $10 per person. It is not very expensive."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> In Thai, the word "มี" can be used for both "possession" and "existence." In English, if you want to say something exists in a place, we use <b>"There is"</b> or <b>"There are"</b>. We only use "has" or "have" when something actually owns something else.</li><br><li><b>📝 Missing the "BE" Verb (is/am/are)</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"It has a hostel cost 10 $ / person it not much expensive that hostel it look perfect to stay, the hostel far from my school about 400 m. around the mall."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"It <b>is</b> not very expensive... the hostel <b>is</b> about 400m from my school."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> In Thai, you can say "มันไกล" or "มันไม่แพง" without needing a linking verb. But in English, every sentence needs a verb! When describing distance or cost with an adjective, you must use <b>"is"</b>. Think: <b>Subject + IS + Description.</b></li><br><li><b>📝 Verb Forms after Modals and "to"</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"In that museum the place you will visited you have to know some body-language to say hello and have a question."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"In that museum, the place you will <b>visit</b>, you have to know some body language to say hello and <b>ask</b> a question."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> After the word "will," we always use the base form of the verb (no "-ed"). Also, in English, we don't "have" a question like we use "มีคำถาม"; instead, we usually <b>"ask"</b> a question.</li><br><li><b>📝 Word Choice and Spelling</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"If you want to hello just wave you hand, or you have a question you can raid your hand up and ask the question."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"If you want to <b>say</b> hello just wave <b>your</b> hand, or if you have a question you can <b>raise</b> your hand."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> "Hello" is a greeting, not a verb, so you need to <b>"say"</b> hello. Also, be careful with "raid" vs "raise"! "Raid" means to attack, but "raise" (ยก) is what you do with your hand!</li></ol><br><br>Keep practising these patterns and you'll improve quickly! You have great ideas, and fixing these small things will make your writing much clearer. 🌟<br><br><hr><b>📊 Your Grammar Analysis</b><br><br>I analysed your grammar using Cambridge University's <b>ERRANT</b> script (ERRor ANnotation Toolkit), which is a tool that compares what you wrote against a corrected version to identify grammatical errors. It shows that you wrote <b>8</b> sentences, and <b>2</b> of them had no errors.<br><br><b>Your error breakdown:</b><br><ol><li><b>Verb Form Errors:</b> 3 instances</li><li><b>Punctuation Errors:</b> 3 instances</li><li><b>Missing Verbs:</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Spelling Errors:</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Preposition Errors:</b> 1 instance</li></ol>	A2+	2026
