n moving from fashion to studying, you could say, 'Beyond the realm of fashion, academic pursuits also highlight the influence of friends.' Thai learners sometimes stick to a few familiar linking words, but expanding your range will make your essay flow beautifully, like a well-told story! 📖	Florence, it's good that you're using a range of everyday words in your writing. However, there are quite a few errors in your grammar, spelling, and word choices that can sometimes make it tricky for your reader to fully understand your message. We're going to work on making your sentences clear and precise! For example, take care with spelling words like 'Nowaday' (it should be 'Nowadays'), 'teste' (it should be 'taste'), 'Likly' (it should be 'Likely'), 'socia' (it should be 'society'), 'spened' (it should be 'spend'), and 'effed' (it should be 'effect'). These little slips can sometimes trip up the reader. Also, keep an eye on your subject-verb agreement (making sure your verbs match your subjects) and pronoun usage (like using 'their' instead of 'there' when you mean possession). Thai learners sometimes find these areas tricky because of differences between English and Thai grammar structures. A good way to improve is to read through your work slowly, perhaps even aloud, to catch these common errors. It really helps to hear how your sentences sound! 👂	4.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
