2921	29034	2025-12-14 09:33:36.447643+00	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out the window and couldn't believe my eyes. My name is Sam, just a regular teen in highschool. I was so ordinary that I could be mistaken for an NPC! Untill one day I found a book in the library titled "Blood rains supreme".<br><br>I thought the cover looked suspicious. The grammar was wrong but I still opened the first page. All it said was "Blood from land fall to sky". After saying those words out loud I looked out the window.<br><br>I couldn't believe my eyes! The rainwater was red. I heard girls screaming. Students crying or shouting. Teachers were evacuating students indoors. Some students even called the cops. I was shocked. However it did feel nice that I did something in life.<br><br>It was three months afterwards when we learned the truth. Some protesters had put red dye in to the water reserves 2 days prior to the incident. That's why the water was red. Apparently the book was just a prank by one of the protesters.<br><br>Even if I didn't actually do anything memorable since it was just a prank. I still felt like I was some kind of wizard! Although I learned the lesson, find evidence before you assume something.	206	19.0	Hello Anu! 👋<br><br>This is a brilliant story! 🌟 I absolutely loved the 'NPC' voice you created for your character—it was funny and unique. The plot twist with the red rain and the prank book was clever and well-executed. You have a real talent for writing engaging narratives.<br><br>I have a few tiny tips to make it perfect! 📋<br>1. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Looked out the window' needs an 'of' -> 'looked out <b>of</b> the window'.<br>2. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Untill' only has one 'l' -> '<b>Until</b>'.<br>3. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ For the book title, did you mean 'Blood <b>Reigns</b> Supreme'? (Reigns = rules). That would be a cool pun!	Your story structure is excellent: Setup, Incident, Climax, Resolution, Reflection. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>The Prank!</b> 🧪 The explanation about the red dye is good, but maybe a bit brief. How did they get *so much* dye into the clouds? A magical or sci-fi explanation might fit your 'wizard' feeling better!</li>	Your narrative voice is your super power! 🦸‍♂️ 'Mistaken for an NPC' immediately tells us who this character is.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The jump 'It was three months afterwards' is a bit sudden. You could add a sentence about the mystery lingering for weeks before the truth came out.</li>	Your paragraphing and use of linkers like 'However', 'Apparently', and 'Even if' is top-notch. 🎓<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Nothing!</b> 🌟 You mastered the organization here. Keep using this structure!</li>	Your vocabulary is excellent ('evacuating', 'incident', 'suspicious'). 📖<br><br>Here are some tiny polishes:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Untill' -> '<b>Until</b>'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Into the water' -> '<b>Into</b>' is usually one word here.</li><li><b>Titles!</b> 👑 'Rains supreme' -> '<b>Reigns</b> supreme' (if you meant 'rules'). If you meant literal rain, then 'rains' is correct!</li>	4.0	5.0	5.0	5.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
3105	52572	2026-01-06 15:12:39.74797+00	Politeness	Younger people are less polite than older people<br>\n\nI think older people are less polite than younger people, like my grandmother age. Because they think they always right, they will say that "I am older than you I know more than younger people". And another important resond was ol	49	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Use of English	Formative	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2	2.0	Hi Nono! You did a great job expressing your opinion on this topic and I can see you have a very clear point of view.<br><br>You tried really hard with this and I noticed some really positive things about your work:<br><br><ul>  <li>✨ <b>Grammatical Range</b>: You successfully used comparisons like "less polite than" several times to show the difference between two groups of people.</li>  <li>🎯 <b>Sentence Linking</b>: You used "Because" to start a sentence and explain your reasoning, which shows you are thinking about how to connect your ideas.</li>  <li>💪 <b>Vocabulary Range</b>: You used good topic-specific words like "polite", "grandmother", and "important" to make your meaning clear.</li></ul><br><br>However, there are some grammar patterns we need to work on together. I'll explain WHY you're making these mistakes so you can fix them:<br><br><ol><li><b>📝 Missing the BE Verb (is/am/are)</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"Because they think they always right, they will say that "I am older than you I know more than younger people"."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"Because they think they <b>are</b> always right, they will say, "I am older than you, so I know more than younger people.""</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> In Thai, you can describe a subject with an adjective directly, like "พวกเขาถูก". But in English, you ALWAYS need a "BE" verb (is, am, or are) to connect the subject to the description. So, "they right" must become "they <b>are</b> right".</li><br><li><b>📝 Possessive "'s" and Specific Nouns</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"I think older people are less polite than younger people, like my grandmother age."</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"I think older people are less polite than younger people, like <b>people my grandmother's</b> age."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> In Thai, you can place two nouns together to show ownership, like "อายุย่า". In English, we usually need to add <b>'s</b> to show that the age belongs to your grandmother. Also, we need to repeat the noun "people" to make the comparison clear.</li><br><li><b>📝 Spelling and Sentence Completion</b><br><b>What you wrote:</b> <i>"And another important resond was ol"</i><br><b>Correct version:</b> <i>"And another important <b>reason</b> was <b>[unfinished sentence]</b>."</i><br><b>Why this happens:</b> Be careful with spelling words that sound similar but are written differently. Also, make sure to finish your final thought so the reader knows exactly what your second reason is!</li></ol><br><br>Keep practising these patterns and you'll improve quickly! 🌟<br><br><hr><b>📊 Your Grammar Analysis</b><br><br>I analysed your grammar using Cambridge University's <b>ERRANT</b> script (ERRor ANnotation Toolkit), which is a tool that compares what you wrote against a corrected version to identify grammatical errors. It shows that you wrote <b>4</b> sentences, and <b>0</b> of them had no errors.<br><br><b>Your error breakdown:</b><br><ol><li><b>Punctuation and Connectors:</b> 5 instances</li><li><b>Noun and Possessive Errors:</b> 3 instances</li><li><b>Verb and BE Verb Errors:</b> 2 instances</li><li><b>Spelling Errors:</b> 1 instance</li></ol>	A2+	2026
3002	30105	2025-12-14 15:56:28.934289+00	Term 2 Midterm M3A Task 1	Dear Alex<br><br>Hi, Alex<br><br>I am so happy about going camping too. I waited for a month. I am very exciting to live together. I can't wait.<br><br>About you question I think we will go with your dad because it's no need to hold very heavy bag and in the train have a lot of people so I think go by your dad car is better.<br><br>And about what we cook on the campfire. I disagree with you because sausage are not made us full and at night we will hugry. We go camp we need to use energy so we need to eat carb. At night it will cold we need to bring blanket to stay warm.<br><br>See you soon, Preaw	122	14.0	Hi Preaw! 👋<br><br>You wrote a lovely email! Your excitement is contagious ("I waited for a month"). I also liked your scientific point about needing "carb" for energy! ⚡<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>Word Forms!</b> 📝 "very exciting" -> "very <b>excited</b>".<br>2. <b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ "sausage are not made us full" -> "will not make us full".<br>3. <b>There is/are!</b> 🏘️ "in the train have" -> "in the train <b>there are</b>".\n	You covered all the points excellently. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Relevance!</b> 💭 Mentioning "carb" and "energy" was a smart way to explain your food choice!</li>\n	Your friendly tone is perfect. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Repetition!</b> 🔁 You used "need to" a lot. Try "should", "must", or "have to" to mix it up.</li>\n	Your paragraphs were clear and logical. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linkers!</b> 🔗 "About you question" is okay, but "Regarding your question" is even better!</li>\n	Good use of "crowded" and "energy"! 👏<br><br>Fix these small errors:<br><li><b>Excited/Exciting!</b> 😲 "I am exciting" means YOU are interesting. "I am <b>excited</b>" means you feel happy.</li><li><b>Verbs!</b> ⚙️ "it will cold" -> "it will <b>be</b> cold".</li>\n	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
