908	29720	2025-07-21 14:42:05.727702+00	My favorite Movie/TV series	My favourite movie is Squid Game, the main actor is Gi Hun or known as player 456. I think Gi Hun is main actor because of his acting skills is very good. The main parts of Squid Game that were good are, games, challenge and actar, example like,<br><br><br>First is cutting dalgona candy into exact shape. It's really hard and challenging. Second is the glass bridge part which you have to guess and choose which one is safe. It's really hard because you need to be lucky and If you choose the wrong one it will breaks and you will fall and get eliminated.<br><br><br>So, basically, you need to win the game and If you fails, you will get eliminated and lose a chance to win the big prize. But the catch is, Only one person can win it which makes it more fun, challenging and stressing to the viewers which makes this movie popular, fun to watch and Iconic.<br><br><br>And lastly what could they improved is only a few like adding different games and adding more games that is not same like last time. But in my opinion this movie is quite perfect for me. And that's why Squid Game is my favourite movie.	205	16.0	I am going to give you feedback in two areas: first, for your essay, and second, for your midterm grammar test.\n\nDragon, you have written a very detailed and engaging essay about your favorite movie, "Squid Game." You have successfully covered all the required parts of the task, including details about the main actor, what was good about the series (games, challenge), what happens in the story, and what could be improved. Your explanations are clear and well-developed.\n\nDragon, your score on the grammar test was 6/14. This shows a mixed understanding of the grammar. You did an excellent job in Part 2, getting a perfect score, which shows you know the different relative pronouns. However, you had significant difficulty in Part 3, where you need to use these pronouns to connect sentences. You also had some trouble with the verb tenses in Part 1. Your main focus should be on practicing how to correctly build sentences using relative clauses.	Dragon, all your content is relevant to the task. You clearly identified your favorite movie, provided details about the main actor, explained what was good about the series with specific examples (dalgona candy, glass bridge), described the main idea of the story, and suggested clear improvements. The target reader is fully informed.	You use the rules for writing an essay well to keep the reader interested and communicate your ideas clearly. Your introduction is good, and you explain the details of the games and the story effectively. You manage to communicate straightforward ideas and some more complex ones, like why the game is stressing for viewers, quite well. To get a 5 for Communicative Achievement, you should try to make your writing even more engaging to fully hold the reader\\'s attention from start to finish. For example, you could open with a hook that immediately grabs the reader\\'s interest, such as \\"Have you ever watched a show that made your heart race and your palms sweat? For me, that show is Squid Game!\\" You should also ensure that all your ideas, even the more complex ones, are communicated with perfect clarity and smoothness, without any small parts that might be unclear, for example, making sure sentences like \\"The main parts of Squid Game that were good are, games, challenge and actar, example like,\\" flow perfectly into the next sentence.	Your text is generally well-organised and easy to follow. You use clear paragraphs, starting with an introduction, then details about the games, then the overall goal, and finally improvements. You use a good variety of linking words like \\"First,\\" \\"Second,\\" \\"So, basically,\\" \\"But the catch is,\\" and \\"And lastly\\" to connect your ideas. This helps your text flow smoothly and be coherent. To get a 5 for Organisation, you should continue to make your text very well-organised and easy to follow, ensuring a wider variety of cohesive devices (linking words and phrases) are used perfectly throughout, making the flow of ideas seem very natural and effortless. For example, to make the connection smoother between paragraphs, you could use phrases like \\"Moving on to the storyline...\\" or \\"Regarding the overall plot...\\" instead of just starting a new paragraph. You could also vary your linking words more, using options like \\"therefore,\\" \\"in contrast,\\" or \\"despite this.\\'	You use everyday vocabulary generally well. You also use simple grammar correctly most of the time. While there are some mistakes, the reader can still understand what you mean. To get a 5 for Language, you should work on two main things:\nAccuracy: You need to make very few mistakes in your grammar and spelling. For example, check things like verb forms ("it will breaks" should be "it will break," "If you fails" should be "If you fail"). Also, ensure word choice is perfect, like using "actor" instead of "actar."\nRange and Control: You should use a wider variety of simple and some more complex sentences, and show that you can control them very well. This means your sentences should be smooth and clear, even when you are explaining detailed or complex ideas, so that the reader never has to guess what you mean. For example, instead of combining many ideas with "and" as in "monster, action and zombie show how we escape to the safty places with out the monster, found group to go with," you could use relative clauses or different sentence structures to make it clearer, such as "It's a monster, action, and zombie show *that explores* how players escape to safe places *by finding* groups to go with."	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
