2070	34924	2025-09-23 08:46:50.966159+00	Term 1 Writing Task 2	I see an international English website for young people. Firstly, I think this website it's might be Articles wanted! to telling about a festival that we can go with our family celebrate. this website it was be website find a festival to celebrate with family to give then have time to stay longer. Secondly, It's will find a place, think did you like about it or what happens. website will tell you about the place, thing that will be happen and thing you like about. Lastly, the best articles answering these question will be published next month, it's will answer you question and find a good festival to give you celebrate with you family. This kind of this website might be like chat gpt or life coach.	127	2.0	Hello Ping-Ping,<br><br>It is wonderful to see you engaging with the writing task. You have approached the assignment with enthusiasm, and that is a great starting point for any writer. The most significant area for you to focus on for improvement is ensuring that you answer the specific questions in the task rather than writing about the task itself. If you can focus on writing directly about the topic, your writing will become much clearer and more engaging for your readers. Keep practising, and you will see your writing skills flourish.<br><br>📋 Action Plan for Improvement:<br>✔️ Carefully read the task instructions and underline the key information you need to include in your writing.<br>✔️ Before you start writing, make a quick plan or a list of ideas that directly answer the task questions.<br>✔️ After writing, check if every sentence helps to answer the questions you underlined in the task.	Ping-Ping, it is important in writing tasks to make sure your article directly answers the questions asked in the prompt. In this piece, you wrote about what the website would do or what the "Articles wanted" section was asking for, rather than telling us about a specific festival that you or your family celebrate. For example, the task asked for you to name a festival, say when it happens, what activities take place, and what you like about it. To earn a higher score, you would need to choose a real festival, like Songkran or Christmas, and then describe it in detail. Think of it like this: if someone asked you about your favourite game, you would talk about the game itself, not about how to find a game on the internet. 🧐 Always try to bring your own experiences and knowledge into your writing to make it personal and interesting.	When you write an article, Ping-Ping, the goal is to inform and engage your readers about a specific topic. While you made an attempt to communicate some ideas about the website prompt, your writing didn't quite function as an article about a festival. To improve, imagine you are writing for another young person who knows nothing about the festival you are describing. You would want to grab their attention and keep them interested with a clear introduction, body paragraphs that explain things, and a conclusion. For instance, you could start with a catchy title and an opening sentence that makes the reader want to learn more about the festival. Always think about your target reader and how you can make your writing enjoyable and easy for them to understand. 😊	Organisation is about how you arrange your ideas so they flow smoothly from one to the next, Ping-Ping. In an article, we usually have a clear beginning, middle, and end, with each paragraph introducing a new idea or developing an existing one. For example, you might have one paragraph for when the festival takes place, another for the activities, and a final one for your personal feelings. Although you used words like "Firstly," "Secondly," and "Lastly," these were used to organise your thoughts about the prompt rather than the content of an article about a festival. To get a better score, try to plan out what each paragraph will focus on before you start writing about the festival itself. This will make your writing much clearer and easier for your reader to follow. ✨	Ping-Ping, your writing shows that you are beginning to use some everyday words appropriately, which is a positive start. For example, phrases like "international English website for young people" and "find a festival to celebrate with family" are understandable. However, there are many grammatical errors that make your sentences hard to follow at times. For instance, sentences like "this website it's might be Articles wanted! to telling about a festival" or "it was be website find a festival" are difficult to understand because of the way the words are put together. A common area for Thai learners to focus on is subject-verb agreement and using the correct verb tenses. In English, we usually say "this website is" or "it will be." Keep practising forming complete, grammatically correct sentences, and try to vary your sentence structures to make your writing more interesting. Focus on getting the basic sentence patterns right, and your communication will become much clearer. Practice using pronouns like "it" and "they" carefully to refer to the correct nouns. You are using some linking words, which is a good step towards more complex writing. Keep up the good effort. 🌟	0.0	1.0	0.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A1+	\N	\N	\N	A1	2026
