1790	29031	2025-09-13 15:32:53.996906+00	Term 1 Exam Question 2	Some people agree that pets are a nuisance and a burden most of time, I strongly disagree. Pets can be annoyance for some individuals, but for those who can take care of them properly, It's a different story.<br><br><br>Primarily, pets are amazing companions that help you cure your boredom and sadness. There are several types of pets that fit with anyone's prefrence, such as, adopting cat if you enjoy having a furry friend that minds their own personal space or a dog that helps guard your home.<br><br><br>Not only that, pets also assist on how you handle responsibility. They help train and remind you how they have necessities just like you. Further more, they gradually help you to be less neglectful towards every essential things.<br><br><br>Finally, by simply adopting them, it helps them find their forever home. As long as you adopt those pets who are in need of safety, especially the ones that were abandoned in a shelter. If you provide care and security for them, they will too do the same.<br><br><br>To sum up, pets are great companions until the very end. It helps you to be more responsible over time by providing them with care. There are perfect pets for anyone as long as you treat them rightfully.	215	13.0	Well done, Racing. Your article on having pets is engaging and clearly presents your strong opinion on the subject. You’ve shared some thoughtful reasons why pets can be wonderful companions and a positive influence. However, to truly elevate your writing, you could explore both the good and the not-so-good aspects of having pets a little more evenly, as the task suggested. Overall, your article is a pleasant read, and with a few adjustments, it will be even more polished.<br><br>📋 Action Plan for Racing:<br>• ✔️ When you’re given a topic to discuss, make sure to cover all parts of the question, even if you have a strong opinion one way. Try to dedicate a paragraph or two to the other side of the argument to show a balanced view.<br>• ✔️ Practise using a wider range of linking words and phrases to connect your ideas smoothly between sentences and paragraphs. Words like "furthermore," "however," "in addition," and "consequently" can make your writing flow beautifully.<br>• ✔️ Pay close attention to your grammar, especially subject-verb agreement and the use of articles (a, an, the). Reading your work aloud can often help you spot these kinds of small mistakes.	You've done a really good job, Racing, of addressing the task and informing your reader about the positive aspects of having pets. You've clearly stated your opinion and given some excellent reasons, such as pets being companions and helping with responsibility. That's a solid effort. 😊 However, the question asked for both advantages and disadvantages. While you mentioned that some people find pets a "nuisance and a burden" in your introduction, you didn't really expand on these disadvantages in your article. For instance, you could have added a paragraph discussing the costs, time commitment, or potential damage pets can cause, before circling back to your main argument. This would show a more complete understanding of the topic, aiming for that perfect 5. Thai learners sometimes focus very strongly on one side of an argument, perhaps because they want to make their point very clear, but for a task like this, a balanced discussion is usually what's needed.	Your article successfully communicates your ideas about pets, and it's easy for the reader to understand your point of view. You've used the structure of an article effectively to present your arguments. 👍 To reach a higher score, think about the formality of your language for an article that might appear online. Sometimes, expressions like "amazing companions" or "different story" are a little too casual for this kind of writing. You could try to use slightly more formal or academic vocabulary to make your writing sound even more sophisticated. For example, instead of "amazing," you might consider "beneficial" or "rewarding." This helps hold the reader's attention in a more formal way and communicate more complex ideas.	Your article is generally well-organised, and you have a clear structure with an introduction, body paragraphs, and a conclusion. Each paragraph presents a distinct idea, which is a good start. 👏 You also use some basic linking words like "Primarily," "Not only that," and "Finally" to connect your ideas. To improve, try to introduce a wider variety of these linking words and phrases to create even smoother transitions between your sentences and paragraphs. For example, when you move from talking about companionship to responsibility, you could use a phrase like "Beyond companionship, pets also..." or "In addition to offering friendship..." Thai learners sometimes use simpler linking structures, and expanding your range of these words can make your writing flow more naturally and coherently, showing a stronger command of organisation.	You've used everyday vocabulary appropriately, and your writing is understandable despite a few errors. You have a good handle on simple grammatical forms, which is excellent. However, there are a few areas where you could pay a little more attention to accuracy to really make your language more precise. For example, in your first paragraph, "a burden most of time" would be better as "a burden most of the time," and "Pets can be annoyance" should be "Pets can be an annoyance." Also, in the second paragraph, "anyone's prefrence" should be "anyone's preference," and "adopting cat" should be "adopting a cat." These small mistakes with articles and spelling are quite common for Thai learners, as English articles can be tricky, and consistent spelling takes practice. Focusing on these details will help your writing become even more polished and accurate. 🧐	4.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
