1969	28783	2025-09-20 20:01:43.37003+00	Term 1 Exam Question 2	I think having pets is a good ideas. Because pets can playing with you when you feel lonely or heart broke and also pets can pretect you from dangerous situation. For examples dogs can pretect you from the people who was a badhabit. Dogs will barking when they saw a different people. Secondly cats. Cats can playing with you when you feels lonely like people who stress or heartbroken. That why having pets is a good idea.	77	4.0	Hello Kao! 👋 It's lovely to see your thoughts on pets. You've got some great ideas about why pets are special companions. To help your writing become even clearer and more engaging, let's focus on building out your ideas more fully and making sure your sentences flow smoothly for your readers. You've definitely got the spark of an idea here, and with a few adjustments, your writing will truly become even better! One importat thing to note is that you were asked to answer one question only (the pets article or a letter to Lucy), but you answered both. I delected your response to Lucy, which is why your score is so low. ✨<br><br>📋 **Action Plan for Improvement:**<br>• ✔️ Always aim to write more than 140 words, making sure to develop all parts of the question with examples and explanations. Make sure you answer ONE QUESTION ONLY.<br>• ✔️ After you finish writing, read through your work and listen to how your sentences sound. Check if your verbs match your subjects, like 'pets *can* play' instead of 'pets *can playing*'.<br>• ✔️ Think about using different linking words like 'however' or 'on the other hand' to connect your ideas and make your article flow better.	Kao, you did a great job of sharing your opinion that having pets is a good idea and talking about how they can be good company. 👍 You also touched on how dogs can protect us, which is a fantastic point! However, for an article like this, it’s really important to give lots of details and examples for *both* the good things (advantages) and the not-so-good things (disadvantages) about pets. You mentioned "dangerous situations," which is a start, but try to explain more clearly what these disadvantages are. For example, owning a pet can be expensive, or they need a lot of looking after. Next time, try to expand on each point, maybe by giving a personal story or a more detailed example. Also, remember that a longer response, around 140-190 words, helps you explain your ideas fully and makes sure your reader gets all the information they need. Keep pushing yourself to add more explanation and depth!	You've made a start at writing an article, which is great! To really grab your teenage readers' attention in a magazine, think about making your article more dynamic. For instance, you could start with an exciting question like, "Ever wondered if a furry friend is right for you?" or use an engaging title. Your writing needs to make the reader feel interested and find the text easy to understand from beginning to end. Right now, your ideas are quite simple, so try to develop them with a bit more detail and maybe some slightly more complex thoughts. For example, instead of just saying "pets can play with you," you could elaborate on the emotional benefits, like "the unconditional love from a pet can truly brighten even the toughest days." Getting your reader hooked and making your ideas clear is key! 🤩	Your ideas are connected, which is a good foundation, as you talk about dogs and then cats. However, for an article, we want to make sure your writing is super easy to follow. Imagine your article is a journey for the reader, and clear paragraphs are like signposts helping them along. Try to separate your introduction, advantages, disadvantages, and conclusion into different paragraphs. For instance, you could have one paragraph for your main opinion, one for advantages like companionship, and another for advantages like protection. You used "For examples" and "Secondly," which are good basic linking words! To improve, try adding more variety, such as "in addition," "however," or "on the other hand," to show the connections between your ideas even more clearly. This will make your article flow smoothly and feel more professional. 📝	Kao, you’ve used some everyday words to talk about pets and feelings, which is a great start! To make your writing even clearer and more polished, let’s focus on a few things. Firstly, be careful with your verb forms after words like 'can' or 'will'. For example, you wrote "pets can playing," but after 'can', we use the base form of the verb, so it should be "pets can **play**." Similarly, "Dogs will barking" should be "Dogs will **bark**." 🗣️ Secondly, pay close attention to plural words and correct word forms. You said "good ideas" (when you meant "a good idea") and "For examples" (when it should be "For example"). Also, "heart broke" should be "heartbroken," which is an adjective, and "badhabit" should be "bad habits" when talking about several. Lastly, try to make sure your sentences are complete and correctly joined. For example, "That why having pets is a good idea" would be better as "That**'s** why having pets is a good idea." In Thai, sentence structure can sometimes be more flexible with subjects and verbs, but in English, getting these forms just right helps your writing be much clearer for your readers. Keep practicing these little tweaks, and your sentences will soon be super accurate! ✨	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
