pic, and it's great to see you sharing your ideas! Keep up the good work on developing your opinions and expressing them. Your writing shows a good foundation, and with a bit more focus on the specific question asked, you'll be well on your way to earning top marks! 🚀<br><br>📋 Action Plan for Your Writing:<br>* Make sure you read every part of the question carefully and answer all of it. If it asks you to compare two things, talk about both! 🤔<br>* Take some time to check your grammar and spelling after you finish writing. Reading it aloud can help you spot tricky sentences! 📖<br>* Try to use a variety of linking words to connect your ideas smoothly and make your essay flow even better. ✨	You did a good job of talking about clothes and fashion, studying, and even included a really good "own idea" about real friends, which is clever! 👍 However, the question asked you to compare the effect of *friends* **or** *parents* on teenagers' choices, and your essay focused mostly on friends. To get a higher score, you need to make sure you address every part of the question. For example, you could have discussed how parents might influence choices about clothes, or how they guide studying, and then compared that to how friends influence those same choices. It’s important to remember that if a question asks you to compare, you need to discuss both sides! 😊	Your essay successfully shared your thoughts and made your point clear to the reader, which is a big win! 🎉 You generally kept the reader engaged, and your opinion came through strongly. To improve, try to think about the kind of writing you're doing. For a formal essay like this, using slightly more formal words and sentence structures can make your writing feel more academic. For instance, instead of saying "The most effect on the choices is make friends," you could write "The most significant influence on teenagers' choices comes from their friends." This helps you communicate your ideas with the formality expected at this level. Remember to keep practicing expressing your ideas clearly and appropriately for different tasks! 😉	You organised your essay into clear paragraphs, and it was easy to follow your main points, which is a very good start! 📚 You used some basic linking words like "And beside" and "finally" to move from one idea to the next. To make your essay even stronger and flow more smoothly, try using a wider range of linking words and phrases. For example, instead of starting a new paragraph with "And beside," you could use "Furthermore" or "In addition to this." Also, consider how your paragraphs connect to each other. For instance, when you move from studying to real friends, you could use a phrase that helps the reader understand the transition, such as "Beyond academic pursuits, the quality of friendships also plays a crucial role..." Many Thai learners sometimes stick to simple linking words, but expanding your vocabulary in this area will really help your writing shine! 🌟	You used some everyday words well, which is helpful for getting your message across. However, there were quite a few places where the grammar and word choices could be more accurate, and some spelling mistakes that sometimes made your sentences a little hard to understand. 😅 For example, phrases like "make friends" when you meant "the influence of friends," "care yourself," and "you can't leave alone" could be improved. You also had some spelling errors like "absolutley" and "accesories." Many Thai learners find articles (a/an/the) and prepositions (in/on/at) a bit tricky, and these were areas where your writing could be strengthened. To improve, you could try reading more English texts to see how native speakers use these small but important words. Also, double-checking your work for subject-verb agreement (e.g., "they are" instead of "they're a good friends") and making sure your verbs are in the correct form will make a big difference! Focusing on these areas will help your writing become much clearer and more precise. Keep up the great effort; every mistake is a chance to learn! 💪	2.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	a2e775c4-e795-45e6-b042-7e908b05f577	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
