nform the target reader. The essay is within the expected word count range of 140-190 words.	You communicate straightforward ideas about Tokyo, and the general purpose of the essay is clear. You convey your enthusiasm for the city, for example, \\"Tokyo is really good place to visit\\" and \\"That's so delicious and too cheap.\\" However, the conventions of an essay are not consistently used effectively, which impacts holding the target reader's attention. The language is quite simple, and there isn't much variation in sentence structure to engage the reader. To improve to a 5, you would need to use more sophisticated language and a wider range of sentence structures to communicate ideas, holding the target reader's attention throughout.	You have generally organised the text with a clear introduction, body paragraphs discussing specific attractions and experiences, and a conclusion. You use some basic linking words like \\"for examples\\" (should be \\"for example\\") and \\"So.\\" The text is generally coherent, with ideas following a logical progression. To achieve a score of 5, you should organise your text into well-structured paragraphs, using a wider variety of cohesive devices and organisational patterns to create a more fluent and easily digestible piece of writing. For example, instead of \\"Last 2 year I went to there, there're have a lot of tourists. I didn't go inside because It have many people. So I want to street foods to find something to ate,\\" you could use \\"First, I visited Senso-ji Temple. However, as there were a lot of tourists, I decided not to go inside. Instead, I wanted to explore the street food scene.\\" or \\"My trip began at Senso-ji Temple. Although it was very crowded, I still enjoyed the atmosphere. Afterward, I went to find some delicious street food.\\" For introducing examples, instead of \\"for examples Senso-ji temple, Shibuya, street foods toun,\\" you could use \\"For instance, Senso-ji Temple and Shibuya are popular destinations, along with its vibrant street food areas.\\" or \\"There are numerous special places to explore in Tokyo, such as Senso-ji Temple, Shibuya, and the lively street food districts.\\" For showing cause and effect, instead of \\"I didn't go inside because It have many people,\\" you could use \\"I didn't go inside due to the large number of people.\\" or \\"Because there were so many people, I decided not to go inside.\\" For adding information/elaboration, instead of \\"We surprized about price and taste. That's so delicious and too cheap,\\" you could use \\"We were surprised by both the price and the taste; in fact, it was so delicious and incredibly cheap.\\" or \\"The ramen surprised us with its price and taste. Furthermore, it was both delicious and affordable.\\" For concluding, instead of \\"Tokyo is the best place to visit you should go once on your life. There have good environment beautiful place and delicious foods,\\" you could use \\"In summary, Tokyo is truly the best place to visit. Its excellent environment, beautiful scenery, and delicious food make it a must-see destination.\\" or \\"All in all, Tokyo is an incredible city that everyone should experience at least once in their life. It offers a wonderful environment, beautiful sights, and amazing cuisine.\\" 	You use everyday vocabulary generally appropriately for the topic of travel. However, there's occasional overuse of certain lexis, and some inappropriate word choices, such as \\"capital city at Japan\\" (should be \\"in Japan\\"), \\"There have a lot\\" (should be \\"There are a lot\\"), \\"street foods toun\\" (should be \\"street food town\\"), \\"resterant\\" (should be \\"restaurant\\"), and \\"We surprized\\" (should be \\"We were surprised\\"). You use simple grammatical forms, but there are noticeable errors in verb forms (\\"we're went to ate again\\" should be \\"we would go to eat again\\" or \\"we'll go to eat again\\"), articles (\\"a capital city at Japan\\"), and prepositions. While meaning can mostly be determined, these errors are noticeable and sometimes impede the natural flow of the text. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to use a range of vocabulary and grammatical forms with control and flexibility, with only occasional, non-impeding errors.	3.0	2.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
