s:</b> "There are many type of sports example, if you like playing in team you should try foot ball or basketball, if you like matrial arts Tekwando, Karate or Thai boxxing is great to choose."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "There are many types of sport. If you enjoy team activities, try football or basketball; if you prefer individual activities, martial arts such as Taekwondo, Karate or Muay Thai are good choices."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved version separates ideas into clearer sentences, uses correct plurals and gives a short example for each option, so the reader understands the differences and why each activity might suit different people.<br><br>	Your essay follows an appropriate essay format and communicates straightforward information. However, the tone and formality are inconsistent in places (for example, contractions and casual phrasing), which reduces the formal essay feel.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Use a more formal academic tone in introductions and conclusions—avoid contractions and spoken expressions.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "we're going to talk about sports and games."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "This essay discusses two common free-time activities: sports and gaming."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved sentence uses a formal register suitable for an essay; it states the purpose clearly and avoids the spoken-style contraction "we're".<br><br>	You use the required four-paragraph structure: an introduction, two body paragraphs and a conclusion. Paragraphing is logical and helps the reader follow your ideas. To reach a higher band, improve cohesion within paragraphs and use clearer topic sentences and linking phrases.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Make your thesis sentence clearer in the introduction and begin each body paragraph with a strong topic sentence that links to the thesis.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Introduction/thesis: "we're going to talk about sports and games."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Free-time activities are important for teenagers because they improve physical health and develop teamwork and problem-solving skills; this essay discusses sports and gaming."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved introductory sentence states the main idea and previews both supporting points. This makes the structure clearer and helps the reader know what to expect in each paragraph.<br><br>	You use everyday vocabulary and try different sentence types. The main challenges are with grammar (plural and agreement), word forms and sentence boundaries. Below are the three most important examples to focus on.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Free time activities is important to all of the teenagers,"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free-time activities are important for all teenagers."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, plural marking and verb agreement are often not shown the same way as in English, so learners sometimes use singular verbs with plural subjects. This matches the Thai interference pattern 'plural_s' (Plural -s and count/uncount). In English, plural subjects need plural verbs and some nouns need no article (e.g., 'all teenagers' rather than 'all of the teenagers').<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "There are many type of sports example, if you like playing in team you should try foot ball..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are many types of sport. For example, if you enjoy team activities, try football or basketball."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This shows the Thai-to-English 'word_form' and 'plural_s' patterns: Thai often uses flexible word forms, so English learners may forget plural forms ("types") or correct compound words ("football"). Using correct plural forms and standard spelling helps meaning and formality.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "playing games in team help us to work with other, because we will not win if we play aloo or not listen to team mates playing puzzle game can make you improve your ability to think and solve the problem."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Playing team games helps us cooperate with others because we cannot win if we do not listen to our teammates. Also, playing puzzle games can improve your problem-solving skills."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai allows long clause chains, but English prefers clear clause boundaries and correct verb forms; this matches the Thai interference pattern 'run_ons'. Breaking ideas into clearer sentences and using correct subject–verb agreement makes the meaning easier to follow.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Practice 10 minutes daily: transform three of your original sentences into improved versions (focus on verb agreement and plurals).<br>2. Do targeted spelling checks for 5 common words you misspell (e.g., 'football', 'martial', 'Taekwondo', 'physical', 'teammates') and write each correctly 5 times.<br>3. Rewrite one body paragraph each week to improve cohesion: add a clear topic sentence and one specific example that supports it.<br><br>	4.0	3.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
