999	29076	2025-08-12 00:00:00+00	Thai Food	Food is really crutial for living things. Although there are a lot of delicious foods in every country, they will have their own signature dish. In particular, a lot of Thai vegetables are used to make a lot of foods, that are really unbelievable and incredible. Three of the most successful street foods, that are quite famous, are Krapow, fried rice and Tom yum.<br><br>The most common Thai street food is Krapow, a quite spicy minced pork with Krapow leaves. It's really delicious for Thai people and foreigners. Moreover there are only five ingredients that are used to make this dish which are minced minced pork, chili, seasonings and Krapow leaves. The steps of how you can cook it are also very simple. First, fry minced pork. Then, add Krapow leaves and seasonings. After that fry them together again. Finally, put these ingredients on the rice. Many foreigners are interested in Krapow because it represents the signature culture from these ingredients not as dull as and Kraprw leaves which are actually incredible Thai vegetables.<br><br>Beside Krapow, fried rice is also a really simple street food in Thailand. You're going to see fried rice in any street restaurant because it has a really good taste and it's very simple and easy to cook. First, fry whatever meats you want such as chicken, pork, fish and crabs. When it's cooked, add some eggs, vegetables and seasonings to make your fried rice look better. Finally, add rice and fry them all together. After that you can enjoy eating your perfect fried rice. This menu represents how Thai people look like because we're all enjoy to do something simple, but also have a great effect as well as fried rice.<br><br>The last Thai street food that I want to introduce is Tom yum, a spicy and a little bit of sour soup. This is one of the most delicious example of Thai street food for foreigners. Many ingredients are used to make Tom yum such as water, chili, mushroom, Kaffir lime leaves and other Thai herbs. First, heat water until it boils and add all of your herbs in it. Then, add some shrimps, limes and chillies. Finally, add whatever you want to make the taste better. This menu is full<br><br>In conclusion, all of these street foods that I have presented are full of Thai culture and traditions. Finally, foreigners who want to try some original Thai foods. of Thai foods and traditions. They'll attract many of Thai food.	416	\N	Hi Kris, this is a good essay about Thai street food! You've introduced some popular dishes and explained how to make them, which is very clear. It's great that you also tried to include some ideas about Thai culture in your writing. You have a good handle on writing, and with a bit more focus on accuracy and clearer connections, your writing will become even stronger!	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
