2366	29579	2025-11-26 21:53:49.901149+00	Creative Writing	Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it. Sam, who love to create new invention when he have a free time. At first, Sam thought about the machine that could help his mom to get ingredients for cook. He made it and gave her. After that, mom tried to use it, but it didn't work. She asked the machine for vegatable but it gave her so many eggs. Then, the machine burnt and hurted mom. So, he brought his mom to the hospital. He fell terrible because the result didn't go like he thought. Finally, mom felt better.	101	13.0	Hello Ka-nhom, 👋<br><br>Good job on this story! It's a classic 'invention gone wrong' tale. Trying to help his mom cook was a sweet motivation, and the machine giving eggs instead of vegetables was a funny detail.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you improve. 📋<br>1. <b>Irregular Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Hurt' doesn't change in the past tense (not 'hurted'). 'Feel' becomes 'felt' (not 'fell').<br>2. <b>Details!</b> 🖌️ What happened when it burnt? Was there smoke? Did the fire alarm go off?<br>3. <b>Connecting!</b> 🔗 Use words like 'because' to join sentences together.	You answered the prompt well! 🌟 The story makes sense.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Length!</b> 📝 It is a bit short (100 words). Try to write more details to make it longer.<br>2. <b>Reaction!</b> 😲 How did his mom react? Was she angry or surprised?	Your story is simple and clear. 👍<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Emotions!</b> 🎭 Describe Sam's feelings more. 'He felt terrible' is good, but *show* us (e.g., 'He hung his head').<br>2. <b>Suspense!</b> 😬 Build up the moment before it breaks. 'The machine started to shake...'	You used 'At first', 'Then', and 'Finally' correctly. 📑<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Flow!</b> 🌊 Instead of 'After that, mom tried...', say 'When his mom tried to use it...'.<br>2. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 You could split the story into: The Idea, The Problem, The Result.	You used words like 'ingredients' and 'hospital' correctly. 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br>1. <b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Hurted' -> 'hurt'. 'Fell terrible' -> 'felt terrible'.<br>2. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Vegatable' -> 'vegetable'.<br>3. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Ingredients for cook' -> 'ingredients for *cooking*'.<br>4. <b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'The machine' is correct!<br>5. <b>Pronouns!</b> 👤 'He made it and gave her' -> 'gave *it to* her'.	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
