 city as 'abandon' (abandoned) and 'no living thing' really helped the reader picture the scene.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Emotional Connection!</b> 💓 You said 'I am very shock', but showing *how* the character felt (e.g., 'My hands were shaking', 'I couldn't breathe') makes the story more exciting than just saying the emotion.</li><li><b>Clarity!</b> 💡 Some sentences were a bit hard to follow, like 'that made me founded'. keeping your sentences simple and clear helps the reader stay in the story.</li>	You used some good linking words like 'So', 'When', 'But', and 'After' to move the story forward in time. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 The whole story is one long block of text. Try to start a new paragraph when the scene changes—for example, one paragraph for waking up, one for finding the scientists, and one for the explanation.</li><li><b>Flow!</b> 🌊 Some of your sentences feel a bit disconnected. Using words like 'Suddenly' or 'However' can help connect your exciting events more smoothly.</li>	You used some good specific vocabulary like 'city center', 'safety zone', and 'acid rain'! 🌧️<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you polish your grammar:<br><li><b>Verb Patterns!</b> 🛠️ After 'make' and 'must', we use the base verb without 'to'. So 'must to find' -> 'must <b>find</b>' and 'make me founded' -> 'made me <b>find</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Forms!</b> 🔄 'The city look like abandon' should be 'The city looked <b>abandoned</b>' (adjective).</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Scienetis' should be '<b>scientists</b>'.</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ You mostly used past tense well, but watch out for consistent forms: 'make me know' -> 'made me <b>know</b>'.</li>	2.0	3.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
