ts play under the table and help friends to deceive."<br><b>Correction:</b> "Secondly, some teachers may not notice students using phones, as students often play under the table and help each other deceive. This makes it difficult for teachers to enforce rules."<br><b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, ideas can be connected loosely, but in English, each point should clearly and directly support your main argument to avoid confusing the reader.	Your paragraph has a clear beginning, middle, and end, using basic linking words to connect your ideas.<br><b>Problem:</b> Some of your linking words are basic or a bit repetitive, and could be improved for smoother transitions, such as ". Also chat with other on social. -I agree that it was fun to play."<br><b>Correction:</b> ". They also chat with others on social media, which I agree is fun to do."<br><b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, sentences can often stand alone, but English writing benefits from clearer connections between sentences and ideas to help the reader follow your thoughts.	You use everyday words correctly most of the time. You can control simple sentences well, but there are some noticeable mistakes with grammar and spelling.<br><b>Problem:</b> You often miss the plural '-s' on nouns, even when referring to more than one, for example: "To begin with students don't concentrate and play attention to study."<br><b>Correction:</b> "To begin with, students don't concentrate or pay attention to their studies."<br><b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, you don't usually add an '-s' to show that there's more than one of something, but in English, you need to add '-s' to most nouns when there are many.<br><br><b>Problem:</b> You sometimes use the wrong preposition, like "According from" instead of "According to".<br><b>Correction:</b> "According to my friends, they post stories on Instagram."<br><b>Explanation:</b> Thai prepositions often translate differently to English, so it's important to learn the correct English prepositions for common phrases.<br><br><b>Problem:</b> There are some spelling mistakes that make the text harder to read, such as "instragram" and "Becuase".<br><b>Correction:</b> "Instagram", "Because"<br><b>Explanation:</b> Always double-check your spelling, as correct spelling helps your writing look professional and makes it easier for the reader to understand.<br><br><b>Problem:</b> You sometimes miss articles (a/an/the) or use the wrong form of a word, for example: "They spent a lot of money to send we to get knowlage at school."<br><b>Correction:</b> "They spent a lot of money to send us to gain knowledge at school."<br><b>Explanation:</b> Thai doesn't use articles like 'a', 'an', or 'the', which can make them tricky in English. Also, be careful with word forms (e.g., noun vs. verb vs. adjective).	5.0	2.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
