r each part of the question.<br>❌ Weakness: You explained that Thai teenagers strive to get into good schools, and this is why they spend time studying. This explains why they *need* to study, but not as much why studying is a *popular hobby* in the same way that playing games is. To clarify, study is usually thought of as work not as a leisure activity, so it requires extra explanation.<br>✨ Improved: "Studying can be a challenging activity, but for many Thai teenagers, it also becomes a rewarding hobby. They might enjoy solving complex problems, engaging in academic competitions, or exploring new subjects beyond the classroom, finding personal satisfaction and intellectual stimulation in their learning."<br>💡 Explanation: Expanding on *why* studying is a popular hobby, beyond just the necessity for academic excellence, helps the reader understand its appeal as a free time activity.</p>	<p>You used an appropriate tone for an article and tried to keep the reader interested. However, sometimes you presented dependent clauses as if they were full sentences, or connected them in a way that affected the clarity. This can make your writing a little harder to follow.</p><p>👉 To Improve: Ensure that all your sentences are complete thoughts and that dependent clauses are properly connected to main clauses.<br>❌ Weakness: You wrote: "Due to their lack of free time and the need for academic excellence in their society." as a separate sentence.<br>✨ Improved: "All in all, playing games and studying are extremely popular hobbies in Thai teenagers' world, often chosen due to their lack of free time and the need for academic excellence in their society."<br>💡 Explanation: Connecting the dependent clause ("Due to...") to the main sentence makes the meaning much clearer and improves the flow of your writing.</p>	<p>Your essay was well-organized into four paragraphs, which is great for readability. Your introduction, body, and conclusion were clear. However, some of the connections between your ideas could be a little smoother.</p><p>👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases to show clearer relationships between your ideas, making your writing flow more naturally.<br>❌ Weakness: You wrote: "This is one of the major reasons why video games has deserve its hype on Thai teenagers. As well as playing video games, studying is another popular hobby." The connection between the two sentences could be clearer.<br>✨ Improved: "While video games clearly deserve their hype among Thai teenagers for these reasons, studying is another equally popular hobby."<br>💡 Explanation: Using 'While' and 'equally' creates a stronger contrast and connection, showing how the two hobbies are related but distinct, leading the reader more smoothly from one idea to the next.</p>	<p>You used good vocabulary related to the topic, including 'vividly' and 'strategic' (even with the small spelling error!). However, there are some recurring grammar patterns that affect clarity, especially with verb forms.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Many teenagers all have their hobbies to help them relaxed."<br>✨ Correction: "Many teenagers all have hobbies to help them relax."<br>💡 Explanation: In English, after 'help someone', we usually use the base form of the verb ('relax'), not the past participle ('relaxed'). This is a common word form issue for Thai learners. We also do not need to use "their" to indicate posssession.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Thai teenagers loves to relive their stress by playing games..."<br>✨ Correction: "Thai teenagers love to relive their stress by playing games..."<br>💡 Explanation: In English, verbs change their form depending on the subject. For plural subjects like 'teenagers', we use 'love'. In Thai, verbs do not change for plurals, which is why this can be a challenge.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "This is one of the major reasons why video games has deserve its hype on Thai teenagers."<br>✨ Correction: "This is one of the major reasons why video games deserves their hype."<br>💡 Explanation: The auxiliary verb 'has' needs to be followed by a past participle (e.g., 'deserved'), or the main verb 'deserve' should be in the correct present simple form for a plural subject ('deserve' for 'video games' if it's the subject) or singular ('deserves' if 'video games' is treated as a singular concept, which seems to be the case here). In English, 'has' followed by a bare infinitive like 'deserve' is incorrect, and the simplest fix here is to change 'has deserve' to 'deserves'.</p><p>🎯 YOUR ACTION PLAN<br>1. Complete all parts of writing tasks and develop each point fully.<br>2. Ensure that dependent clauses are properly connected to main clauses to avoid fragments.<br>3. Practice using a wider variety of linking words and phrases for better cohesion.<br>4. Review verb forms, especially after 'help' and for subject-verb agreement.</p>	4.0	3.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
