itten and descriptive essay, Racing. Keep up the good work!	Racing, you have included a lot of relevant information about Koh Saemsan, making the reader well-informed. You describe its physical characteristics (turquoise water, sandy beach), activities (diving), and your personal connection to the place. To achieve a 5, you could perhaps expand on the types of sea life or provide more specific examples of the welcoming nature of the locals.	You generally use the conventions of the task to communicate straightforward ideas. The essay is engaging and maintains the reader's interest. The personal tone is appropriate and effective. To reach a score of 5, you could incorporate more complex ideas or perhaps a more nuanced perspective on why Koh Saemsan is special to you.	You have organised your text into clear paragraphs, and it follows a logical progression. You use a variety of linking words and cohesive devices (e.g., "Although," "therefore," "moreover," "Furthermore," "All in all," "In addition"). While "That said" isn't entirely appropriate, the overall organization is strong. For a 5, ensure that all linking words are used accurately and effectively to enhance the flow of the essay.	Racing, you demonstrate a range of everyday vocabulary and some more descriptive language (e.g., "turquoise water," "sandy beach," "breathtaking scenery"). You also use a range of simple and some complex grammatical forms with a good degree of control. Errors are present, but they do not generally impede communication. For instance, "there are other plenty activities" should be "there are plenty of other activities.".	4.0	3.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
