nd real!</li><li><b>The "Other Thing"!</b> ❓ You said 'another thing I found...'. What was it? Finishing that thought would make the story complete!</li>	Your personal, informal, and excited voice is very effective in drawing the reader in! 🗣️ It felt like I was right there with you in the classroom.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Punctuation for Speech!</b> 💬 When you wanted to shout '[name] is there!!!', remember to put quotation marks around it to show it's direct speech.</li>	Your paragraphing is excellent, creating a clear psychological progression from boredom to discovery to excitement. 🧱 This makes your story very well-structured.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Flow!</b> 🌊 Some sentences are a bit long and complex. Breaking them down into shorter, punchier statements, especially in the moment of excitement, could enhance the impact.</li>	You used ambitious and engaging vocabulary like 'overwhelmed', 'gorgeous', 'accidentally', and 'screamed'. 📚 Your use of slang ('stan', 'face card') adds to the authenticity of your voice.<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'Full of a numbers' -> 'full of <b>numbers</b>'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Noeasy' -> '<b>noisy</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'Bited my hand' -> '<b>bit</b> my hand', 'All I was could is' -> 'All I <b>could do</b> was'.</li><li><b>Conciseness!</b> ✍️ 'Just imagine finding met your artist' -> 'just imagine <b>meeting</b> your artist'.</li>	5.0	4.0	5.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
