u. [applause]	370	16.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Speaking	CA	PET	Your book review was very well-organized and presented with a good level of confidence. You managed to keep a steady pace throughout the recording, which made it easy to follow your ideas. Your volume was perfect, and I could hear every word you said quite clearly.<br><br><b>What You Did Well:</b> You maintained a consistent volume and used syllable stress /ˈsɪl.ə.bəl.stres/ accurately in most words. This gave your speech a stable rhythm and helped me understand which words were the most important in each sentence.<br><br><b>What to Watch Out For:</b> The most noticeable issue was the repetitive dropping of final consonant sounds /ˈkɒn.sə.nənt/. You often missed the "d" in "died" /daɪd/, the "n" in "human" /ˈhjuː.mən/, and the "n" in "town" /taʊn/, which can be intrusive for the listener.<br><br><b>How to Get Even Better:</b><br>1. Practice emphasizing the final consonant of every word to avoid dropping sounds systematically.<br>2. Focus on linking vowel sounds to the following consonants to create a more fluid, connected speech pattern.<br><br>You are making great progress with your clarity, Namo K! 🌟	Namo, this was a great book review of the Ramakien! You managed to explain a very complex story in a way that was easy to follow and very engaging for the listener. Your use of descriptive vocabulary really brought the characters to life, and you used a great range of linking words to move through the plot. To reach the next level, just keep an eye on your past tense endings and try to introduce your characters more clearly at the start. Your confidence in speaking is great to see! 🌟	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/149T-QIza1cCqeNpsUNQzEvHxMwqCJN4X?usp=sharing	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
