2377	29034	2025-11-28 10:04:25.755774+00	Creative Writing	Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it. The apparition of a ghost appeared before him, slowly becoming... Solid or in other words tangible.<br><br><br>Sam was a 16 year old inventor in Texas. There is a saying in Texas "Everything's bigger in Texas", which could be used for Sam's brain. He was a smart person, able to create pretty much anything, like a laser gun or his newest invention "Ghost Detector". An intricate device that allows one to locate THE DEAD... However, there was a massive problem. Sam couldn't see or speak to ghosts, that gave him a brilliant idea. What if he made a machine to make ghosts visible? It initially seemed impossible but everything was at the start.<br><br><br>Three tiring months of work later, he did it. The "Tangibler", he called it was a projector that used electrical waves to turn ghosts into ghouls. All he needed was to test it at a haunted house. Good thing there was a random house down the street. The next day, Sam set off to the haunted house despite his mom's concern (mostly for his sanity).<br><br><br>Sam set up the Tangibler, made a few small adjustments and started it. It actually worked. The ghost now ghoul was strangely aggressive but nevertheless, it was a success. Sam decided to make more ghouls but it was a huge mistake.<br><br><br>The ghouls started to crave blood as they started to chase Sam down the halls, not giving him a chance to hide until Sam found an opportunity to hide in a closet. Unfortunately one of the ghouls found him and played A game where they do sexual stuff for 7 minutes in heaven in a closet. The other ghouls just decided to rip his limbs of one by one. Until he bled out to a slow death.<br><br><br>The lesson was learned the hard way. Leave ghosts alone.	311	18.0	Hello Anu, 👋<br><br>This is a genuinely chilling story! 👻 You did a fantastic job setting the scene with the 'Ghost Detector' and building up the suspense. The description of the ghosts becoming 'tangible' was excellent and very spooky. You clearly have a talent for horror writing.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing even further. 📋<br>1. <b>Audience!</b> 🎭 Remember that for school assessments, we need to keep the content PG-13. Avoid graphic violence or sexual references.<br>2. <b>Tone!</b> ⚖️ The shift from scientific invention to extreme horror was quite sudden. Try to keep the tone consistent.<br>3. <b>Vocabulary!</b> 🌟 You used amazing words like 'intricate' and 'sanity'. Keep building that vocabulary!	You answered the prompt perfectly with a very creative invention! 💡 The background in Texas added nice flavor.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Appropriateness!</b> 🚫 As mentioned, avoid graphic scenes in school writing. Focus more on the *feeling* of fear rather than the gory details.<br>2. <b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The ending felt a bit rushed compared to the detailed beginning. Spend a bit more time resolving the conflict.	You held my attention from the very first line! 😱 The 'Ghost Detector' concept is very engaging.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Consistency!</b> 🎭 The tone shifted from a fun sci-fi story to a dark horror very quickly. Try to hint at the danger earlier.<br>2. <b>Ending!</b> 🎬 'Leave ghosts alone' is a catchy lesson, but maybe show us Sam reacting to this lesson.	Your story is very well organized. 📚 The progression from idea to invention to disaster is logical.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Linking!</b> 🔗 You used 'However' well. Try adding more variety like 'Furthermore' or 'Despite this'.<br>2. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 Your paragraphs are solid. Just ensure the ending isn't too abrupt.	Your vocabulary is fantastic! 'Intricate', 'tangible', 'sanity' - wow! 🌟<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br>1. <b>Capitalization!</b> 🔡 'THE DEAD' doesn't need to be all caps. Italics work better for emphasis.<br>2. <b>Punctuation!</b> 🖊️ 'Sam couldn't see or speak to ghosts, that gave him...' -> This i