hort. You can join them with 'because' or 'although'.	You answered the prompt fully with a very original plot! 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Motivation!</b> 💭 Tell us more about why he missed his grandmother. It would make the ending sweeter.<br>2. <b>The Villain!</b> 🦹‍♂️ Describe the prisoner more. Did he look scary? Was he big?	Your story was exciting to read! 🤩 The chase scene kept me interested.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Dialogue!</b> 🗣️ You could write the actual words the prisoner said when he offered the deal.<br>2. <b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The negotiation happened very fast. You could slow it down to make it more tense.	Your story is well-structured with a clear beginning, middle, and end. 📑<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Transitions!</b> 🔗 Use words like 'Consequently' or 'Moments later' to move between scenes.<br>2. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 The paragraph about the chase is good. Make sure the final resolution stands out.	You used great words like 'prisoner suit' and 'GPS tracker'! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br>1. <b>Infinitives!</b> 🛠️ 'Refused to gave' -> 'refused to *give*'. 'Had to bought' -> 'had to *buy*'.<br>2. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Successfull' -> 'successful'. 'Immedietly' -> 'immediately'.<br>3. <b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'An meal' -> '*a* meal'.<br>4. <b>Adverbs!</b> 🏃‍♂️ 'Ran far away' -> 'run far'.<br>5. <b>Past Perfect!</b> ⏳ 'Grand mother that passed away' -> 'who *had* passed away'.	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
