nd heartwarming story! I particularly enjoyed the unique twist of the 'scary robot' turning out to be Sam's old childhood friend. The emotional depth and action scenes kept me captivated!<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing even further. 📋<br><li><b>Tense Consistency!</b> ⏳ Practice keeping your verbs in the same tense, usually past tense for narratives.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> 🤝 Double-check that your subjects and verbs match correctly (e.g., 'he' with 'shouted', not 'shout').</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Connect sentence fragments to make your ideas flow more smoothly.</li>	You told a complete and engaging story that fully addresses the prompt, with a strong resolution! 🌟 The 'buddy' relationship between Sam and the robot added a lovely, touching dimension.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Clarify Motivation!</b> 🤖 It would be interesting to know *why* the robot initially started destroying things. Was it confused, or acting under a misconception?</li><li><b>Enhance Reactions!</b> 😲 When the robot speaks, describe Sam's immediate reaction. Was he surprised, relieved, scared? Show us his emotions!</li>	You skillfully communicated a strong sense of atmosphere and action when describing the robot attack! 🏙️ The image of 'robots destroying the building, cars' is very clear and powerful.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Narrative Voice!</b> 🔄 Maintain a consistent narrative perspective. Shifting from 'I feel really upset' to 'he was stun' can be a little confusing for the reader.</li><li><b>Sentence Clarity!</b> 👓 While your language is evocative, ensure every sentence conveys its meaning with utmost clarity, especially phrases like 'The rain was raining 2 hours ago, but now, it stops' in context.</li>	Your story is well-organised, using clear paragraph breaks to separate the exposition, rising action, and resolution! 📚 Linking words like 'At first', 'After that', and 'So' effectively guide the reader through the narrative. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Connect Fragments!</b> 🧩 Some phrases, like 'Fly around the city in the sky', are quite descriptive but could be integrated into a full sentence to enhance flow and coherence.</li><li><b>Stronger Connections!</b> ➡️ Phrases like 'But stepped out' would benefit from a clear subject to ensure seamless transitions between actions.</li>	You made a good effort using complex sentences and appropriate vocabulary such as 'massive', 'confront', and 'introverted'! 👏<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Tense Consistency is Key!</b> ⏳ This is an area to focus on. You frequently switch between past and present tenses ('walks', 'lives', 'is' should be 'walked', 'lived', 'was'). Consistent past tense is crucial for storytelling.</li><li><b>Correct Modals!</b> 🛠️ After modal verbs like 'can't', use the base form of the verb. So, 'can't heard' should be 'couldn't <b>hear</b>'.</li><li><b>Adjective/Verb Forms!</b> 🎨 'He was stun' should be 'he was <b>stunned</b>' (an adjective) and 'didn't even protected' should be 'didn't even <b>protect</b>' (base verb after 'didn't').</li><li><b>Preposition Precision!</b> 📍 Instead of 'Walk forward his apartment', use 'walked <b>towards</b> his apartment' for better accuracy.</li><li><b>Avoid Repetition!</b> ✍️ While 'brilliant kid' and 'buddy' are good, try to find synonyms or rephrase sometimes to keep the vocabulary fresh.</li>	5.0	4.0	5.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
