id he was going to 'hit the planet' - I think you meant 'plane'? A tiny spelling change makes a big difference!</li><li><b>Show the Innovation!</b> 🔧 What did the machine look like? Wings? A jetpack? Describing it helps us see it.</li>	Your story held my attention, especially during the flight test. 🛫 The message of perseverance was communicated well.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Length!</b> 📏 Some of your sentences are very long with many commas. Try breaking them into shorter sentences for more impact.</li><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The ending jumps quickly to 'The next day'. Maybe show him landing and people cheering first?</li>	You organised your story well into paragraphs. 📚 Linking words like 'Therefore', 'however', and 'finally' guided the reader perfectly. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Run-on Sentences!</b> 🏃‍♂️ Your second paragraph is one giant sentence! Put a full stop after 'fully completed' and 'young'.</li><li><b>Transitions!</b> ➡️ 'Therefore his invention' - 'So' might be a smoother choice here.</li>	You used some good words like 'potential', 'accepted', and 'viral'. 👏<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Contry' -> 'country'. 'Finnished' -> 'finished'. 'Botton' -> 'button'.</li><li><b>Comparatives!</b> ⚖️ 'More and more closer' -> 'closer and closer'.</li><li><b>Modals!</b> 🛠️ 'Cannot controlled' -> 'cannot <b>control</b>'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Help him everything' -> 'help him <b>with</b> everything'.</li>	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
