hat the paragraph will be about and how it connects to your overall thesis, creating better flow and structure in your essay.<br><br>	You use everyday vocabulary appropriately, and your meaning is generally clear despite some errors. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Free time is really important because it help us relax and have fun."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time is really important because it helps us relax and have fun."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, verbs do not change form depending on the subject. However, in English, for 'he/she/it' and singular nouns, you must add an '-s' to the verb in the present simple tense.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "There are 2 activity people like to do when they have free time..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are 2 activities people like to do when they have free time..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, when you refer to more than one countable noun, you need to add '-s' or '-es' to make it plural. Thai does not have direct plural markers like English, which can lead to this type of error.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: ". it is one of the activity people do to relax..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "It is one of the activities people do to relax..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, every new sentence must begin with a capital letter. This is a common point to remember for clear writing, and will also help you to correct the plural form of 'activity'.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Review and practice subject-verb agreement rules, paying close attention to verbs that follow 'it', 'he', 'she', and singular nouns.<br>2. Focus on using a more formal and academic tone in your writing, especially in essays, by avoiding casual expressions and conversational phrasing.<br>3. Experiment with using relative clauses (e.g., 'who,' 'which,' 'that') to combine sentences and add detail, and try to incorporate passive structures (e.g., 'is done by') to vary your sentence construction.<br><br>	3.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
