3210	29034	2026-01-12 09:40:19.180999+00	Book Review	Um, hello everybody, hi, wow, hi, good morning, good morning. My name is Anu, you probably know me already. So, today I'm going to talk about a very interesting and complex novel called A Good Girl's Guide to Murder, written by Holly Jackson.<br>So, let's start off with a hook, shall we? ... ... Imagine this. Your friend was framed for murder, but he couldn't prove his innocence because he committed suicide before he went to court. So, you decide to use your final school project as an excuse to investigate the murder of his victim, Andie Bell, to uncover the truth because you know, you knew he was innocent, but you don't have proof to prove it.<br>So, the stories takes place in a small, small town called Kilton, in the year 2017. The main character is a girl called Pip, Pippa Fitz-Amobi. That's quite hard to pronounce. Basically, she knew, she knew that her friend Sal Singh did not murder Andie Bell five years ago, but she couldn't prove it. So she's using her final school project as an excuse to investigate the murder of Andie Bell. Of course, along the way she discovers clues and Pip partners up with Sal's little brother, Ravi Singh.<br>Of course, something unexpected happens like in every story. Now, the thing that is most disturbing about Andie Bell is that she was a drug dealer. She used to deal drugs at house parties. So, Pippa actually managed to track her supplier, who apparently was a man called Howie Bowers. Now, Howie actually gave very relevant information about Andie. She had a planner and a secret phone. A secret second phone, that is.<br>Now, let's talk about the most exciting part. The most exciting part on the book is obviously the climax, right? Now, in this case, I would have to say climaxes because there's two. Basically, the first one, I'm going to explain the first one very quickly. The killer actually threatens Andie, and I mean Pippa, there's too many characters... ... Pippa. Basically by kidnapping her dog and threatening Pippa that they will kill her dog if she does not burn all the evidence that she has gathered. So she does that, but later she finds her dog dead. And then the second climax is when she finds out who the killer actually is, Mr. Ward, a history teacher, or in this case, a pedophile. Yes, I said it ladies and gentlemen, a pedophile. He was the one sleeping with Andie Bell and who murdered her, and Sal Singh to cover up evidence. Yes, absolutely disgusting.<br>Now then, let's talk about what I like about the book. I don't think everybody will agree with this, but I really like that not all of the suspects are innocent. I mean, even if they are not the killer, they are still not innocent. There's a drug dealer and a rapist for example. But what I disliked about the book is that there are too many characters because it makes my brain go blank every time I read a page with a character I don't recognize because there's too many.<br>Now, to conclude this, I recommend this book to anybody who likes gore violence and is not bothered by mentions of pedophile, gore violence, kidnapping, and murder. And to conclude this, I hope you enjoy this book and at least watch the movie. Thank you very much. [applause]	574	19.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Speaking	CA	PET	Thank you for such a detailed and well-structured presentation today, Anu. Your preparation really showed, and you did a fantastic job explaining the book. It was a very impressive performance!<br><br><b>What You Did Well:</b><br>Your individual sounds are very clear and accurate, which is a great foundation for your speaking. Your intonation is also excellent and shows that you have a very strong grasp of English rhythm.<br><br><b>What to Watch Out For:</b><br>I noticed that your intonation can sometimes become a bit "sing-songy," which might happen because of nervousness. It is also important to project your voice more, as it was a bit quiet and hard to hear in some parts of the recording.<br><br><b>How to Get Even Better:</b><br><ul><li><b>Project Your Voice:</b> Practice speaking from your chest rather than your throat to give your voice more power and clarity, even when you feel nervous.</li><li><b>Ground Your Intonation:</b> Try to keep your voice a bit more level and steady to avoid the sing-song pattern, which will make you sound more professional and confident.</li><li><b>Breathe and Relax:</b> Take deep breaths before you start speaking to help calm your nerves and keep your volume consistent throughout.</li></ul><br>You have all the right skills, so just focusing on your volume and tone will make you a truly stellar speaker! 🌠	Anu, this was a fantastic book review! You used an excellent "Imagine" hook that really grabbed my attention, and you followed the structure of the task perfectly. Your vocabulary was very advanced for a B1 student, with words like "framed," "investigate," and "evidence." You also used great linking words to connect your ideas smoothly. To get even better, watch out for small grammar slips like subject-verb agreement and prepositions. Your ability to explain such a complex mystery was very impressive! 🌟	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
