mfortable. What problems does the heat cause?<br>2. <b>Show, Don't Tell!</b> 🎭 Instead of saying 'He can fix the big problem', show us *how* he fixes it. What tools does he use?	I could clearly follow the story of the Magic Sweater and Sam's journey to improve it. 👕<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Engagement!</b> 🗣️ Try to add more details about the sweater itself. What does it look like? How does it feel to wear?<br>2. <b>Emotion!</b> 😊 You said 'He very happy'. Describe *why* he's happy. Does he celebrate? Does he tell his friends?	You used paragraphs to separate your ideas, which is great! 🧱<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Opening Sentence!</b> 📝 Your very first sentence has some errors. Make sure it grabs the reader's attention clearly.<br>2. <b>Linking!</b> 🔗 Use transition words like 'Therefore' or 'As a result' to connect your sentences and ideas more smoothly.	You have a fantastic imagination! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Fisrt' -> '<b>First</b>'. 'Parent' -> '<b>Parents</b>'.<br>2. <b>Subject-Verb!</b> 🗣️ 'He is think' -> 'He <b>thinks</b>'. 'It's answer questions' -> 'It <b>answers</b> questions'.<br>3. <b>Tense!</b> 🔙 'Press the button to started' -> 'Press the button to <b>start</b>'. 'Battery is ran out' -> 'Battery has <b>run out</b>'.<br>4. <b>Word Choice!</b> 📖 'He can fix' -> 'He <b>fixed</b>'. 'Everyone interesting of his invention' -> 'Everyone <b>was interested in</b> his invention'.<br>5. <b>Sentence Structure!</b> ✍️ 'He decide to do everything because this sweater' needs to be clearer. Perhaps: 'He decided to do everything *for* this sweater'.	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
