ship pets bring as advantages, and then discuss the financial costs or the time commitment as disadvantages. Adding these details would make your article much richer and more informative for your readers! 🐶🐱	Your article has a clear beginning and end, which is excellent for an article! You’ve communicated your main ideas clearly, and the reader can understand your opinion. To make your article even more engaging for an online magazine for teenagers, try adding some questions for your readers to think about, or use more exciting words and phrases. 🤔 For example, instead of just stating that pets are a "bad idea" for students, you could say something like, "Imagine juggling homework, sports, and then a playful puppy – it can be a real challenge!" This helps to grab and hold your reader's attention throughout the whole piece.	Your article flows quite logically, moving from a general statement to more specific examples about age groups, and then wrapping up with a summary. That's a good structure! To make your writing even clearer and easier to follow, think about using a wider variety of linking words. For example, you could use "on the other hand" when you introduce disadvantages, or "consequently" to show a result. This helps your ideas connect more smoothly, like putting all the pieces of a puzzle together perfectly! 🧩 Sometimes, Thai students might use shorter sentences or link ideas with simpler connectors, which is a good start, but English often benefits from a greater range of these linking words to create a more sophisticated flow.	You’ve used everyday words well, and your sentences are generally easy to understand. Keep up the great work with your grammar! There were just a few small things that, with a little practice, you can easily improve. For example, "aldult" should be "adult," and instead of "their parent's responsible," it would be "their parents' responsibility." Also, "too busy to their work" would be better as "too busy with their work." These little adjustments in spelling and prepositions will make your writing even more polished. Remember to always proofread carefully for these kinds of errors – it makes a big difference! Sometimes in Thai, articles and plural forms are not as strict as in English, which can sometimes lead to these kinds of small mistakes. Keep practicing, and you'll master them! ✏️	3.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
