ise your main points and offer a final thought.<br>❌ Weakness: Your conclusion stopped suddenly: "In short, teens who play games will have more connection with their friends. So, they won't feel depress but..."<br>✨ Improved: "In short, while both gaming and studying are prominent free time activities for Thai teens, it is clear that balancing academic pursuits with social interactions, perhaps through engaging activities like gaming, is essential for their overall well-being and sense of community."<br>💡 Explanation: A complete conclusion, with a transition and a clear summary of your main points, helps to leave a lasting impression on the reader and makes your essay feel well-rounded and complete.</p>	<p>You used good vocabulary related to the topic, but there are some recurring grammar patterns that affect clarity, particularly with articles.<br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "most of teenagers"<br>✨ Correction: "most teenagers" or "most of the teenagers"<br>💡 Explanation: In English, when you use "most of" with a plural countable noun, you often need "the" (e.g., most of the students). However, you can also just use "most" directly before the plural noun (e.g., most students). Thai doesn't have articles like "the" or "a/an," so it's common for Thai learners to omit them or use them incorrectly.<br><br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "most of children"<br>✨ Correction: "most children" or "most of the children"<br>💡 Explanation: Similar to the previous example, "children" is a plural countable noun. You can say "most children" or "most of the children." Thai grammar does not use articles, which often leads to this type of error for Thai speakers learning English.<br><br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "to have connection with their friends"<br>✨ Correction: "to have a connection with their friends" or "to have connections with their friends"<br>💡 Explanation: "Connection" is a countable noun, and in this context, it needs an article ('a') or to be plural ('connections'). In Thai, nouns don't typically change form for countability in the same way, which can make it tricky to know when to use articles in English.</p>	3.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
