lace, It must also be the well - known places in Soeul, As I was walking along, I found tons of best - know food in Korea such as, Teokbokki, Jajangmyeon, Bibimbab and fish cakes. The surrounding was awsome camparing to the food that I have encounterd, When I got back to Thailand I couldn't stopped thinking about it, It was such a memorable moment.<br><br><br>Lastly I conclude that, Korea is a very famous place known for it awsome structures and food. Come along with my expereance Korea is a place where you should go. Once in your life.	451	10.0	Aunna, you did a great job describing a place you love. It's clear that Seoul is a very special city for you. You share many interesting details about your trip and your feelings.\\n\\nTo make your writing even better, you can work on making your ideas flow more smoothly and fixing some small grammar and vocabulary mistakes. Keep practicing, and you'll improve a lot.	Aunna, you shared a lot of details about Seoul, like its traditional side and K-pop, and your personal story about going to Lotte World and the night market. You covered most of the things the question asked for. However, the exam question asked for an article between 150-180 words, and your response was 451 words. You need to keep your writing within the word count.	You wrote in a way that is easy to understand, and your personal story was interesting. You tried to get the reader's attention at the beginning with questions. However, the style sometimes felt more like a personal story than an article for a travel website. For example, you wrote, "Incredibly awesome right?". It would be better to use a more neutral tone, like "It was a terrific experience.".	You used paragraphs, which is good, and you presented your ideas in a sequence, like talking about why you love Seoul and then sharing your trip. However, some of your sentences are very long, and it's sometimes hard to follow the different ideas. For example, you wrote, "When I first stepped there It feels like a time stopped machine every stucture or rider there looks completely unrallistic, without thinking much I ran all the way to a roller coaster. Overall it was very fun and an awesome memorable moment". You could break this into shorter sentences to make it clearer: "When I first stepped there, it felt like a time machine had stopped. Every structure and ride looked completely unreal. Without thinking much, I ran all the way to a roller coaster. Overall, it was a very fun and memorable moment." The second paragraph was also very long and contained many different ideas. It would have been better to divide these ideas into separate paragraphs, espcially as you wrote so many words.	You used a good range of everyday words related to travel and entertainment. You also used different tenses to talk about your past trip and general facts about Korea. However, there are many small errors with spelling, punctuation, and sentence structure that make it hard to read at times. For example, you wrote, "Soeul Korea is located in the centre of Korea, And are known for it's traditional things for example, modern structures, clothing and many other things." It would be better to write, "Seoul, Korea, is located in the center of Korea and is known for its traditional things, such as its modern structures, clothing, and many other things." Another example is "My trip all got canded because of the upcoring examination." This should be "My trip was cancelled because of the upcoming examination." Also, pay attention to capitalization, as you wrote "Come to think" when it should be "come to think" and "k-pop" when it should be "K-pop".	4.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
