ear</b> the pain'.<br>3. <b>Tense Consistency!</b> 🛠️ 'Had to faced' should be 'had to <b>face</b>'.	You crafted a highly original and disturbing story that fully embraced the horror genre. 🌟 The internal monologue and the vivid descriptions of the animatronic suit were very effective. All content was relevant and contributed to the unsettling narrative.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>The Suit's Description!</b> 🎭 You mentioned it was 'stained with the children's blood'. Adding a small detail about its appearance (e.g., 'rusty', 'broken', 'gnarled') would make it even more gruesome.</li><li><b>The Children's Spirits!</b> 👻 What did they look like? Were they transparent, glowing, or did they have empty eyes?</li>	You successfully conveyed a chilling, cynical, and ultimately ironic narrative voice. 💀 The shift in power dynamics from hunter to hunted was very well-managed.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing with Punctuation!</b> 🛑 The story reads very breathlessly because of the lack of paragraph breaks. Strategic breaks would allow the reader to absorb the horror and tension more effectively.</li>	Your story follows a clear chronological sequence of events, from initial panic to the ironic demise. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing is CRITICAL!</b> 🧱 This is the single biggest area for improvement. Splitting your long text into logical paragraphs would dramatically enhance readability, dramatic effect, and overall structure.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Some sentences are very long and contain multiple ideas. Breaking these into shorter, distinct sentences would make your story easier to follow and increase the impact of key moments.</li>	You used strong and evocative vocabulary like 'flickered', 'manically', 'suffocating', 'crushing', 'agony', 'ironic', 'consequence', and 'murderer'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Homophones!</b> 📝 'Bare the pain' -> '<b>bear</b> the pain'.</li><li><b>Tense!</b> ⏳ 'Had to faced' -> 'had to <b>face</b>'.</li><li><b>Punctuation in Dialogue!</b> 💬 'I exclaimed my victory by scaring the children's spirits with the thing I had finished them off with.' needs a comma before the speech: '"How the tables have turned!" I exclaimed my victory...'</li>	5.0	5.0	3.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
