se attention to spelling. Keep refining these areas to elevate your writing!	Kaohom L, your essay is highly relevant to the task and effectively argues that people care deeply about their pets. You use strong personal examples to illustrate your point and clearly challenge the opposing view that pets don't need much attention. All content is relevant, and the target reader is fully informed of your perspective.	You use the conventions of an essay to communicate straightforward ideas, and your personal examples help engage the reader. However, the communication is significantly affected by numerous grammatical errors and awkward phrasing, which make it difficult to hold the target reader's attention consistently.	Your essay has a basic organisational structure. However, the coherence is compromised by very long and dense paragraphs which lack internal divisions and clearer transitions between ideas. This makes the text harder to follow and affects the overall flow.	You use everyday vocabulary related to pets and their care. While you attempt to use a range of grammatical forms, there are frequent and pervasive errors that often impede communication. The errors significantly affect the clarity and control of your language.	4.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
2933	33169	2025-12-14 09:35:15.833248+00	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. In front of my house, their was a giant dragon, stomming its foot and shooted a fire blaze out from its mouth. I was so shocked, its roar made my knees feels weak. I couldn't even move my legs to run away, like my feet glued to the floor. But as I took a deep breath. I just noticed that it wasn't a normal dragon.<br><br>It was a red dragon. It's supposed to be gone million years ago. I could still heard people screaming and loud "Boom!" "Crack!" "Help me!". I didn't know what to do, looking out the window to see a disaster. Wow, what a beautiful way to started the day. Then someone yank me back and drag me out of my house. I couldn't see who it was, but they were strong for sure. When that person stop dragging me, I was outside now, that person turn out to be a wizard who knows why the long lost red dragon was here. He told me that the red dragon came here to find it very own egg.<br><br>Too bad, I wake up.	196	16.0	Hello Milan! 👋<br><br>What an epic dragon encounter! 🐉 Your story had great suspense, from the dragon's fiery breath to your feet being 'glued to the floor'. The sudden appearance of the wizard added an exciting magical twist.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you perfect this adventurous tale! 📋<br>1. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Stomming' should be '<b>stomping</b>'. 'Shooted' should be '<b>shot</b>'.<br>2. <b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'Knees feels weak' should be 'knees <b>felt</b> weak'. 'To started' should be 'to <b>start</b>'.<br>3. <b>Ending!</b> 🎭 'Too bad, I wake up' is a very abrupt ending. Try to think of a more original way to conclude the dream.	You created a very engaging high-stakes scenario with a mythological creature! 🌟 The detail about the dragon being 'long lost' added a nice touch of lore.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Dream Ending!</b> 💤 The 'dream' ending is quite common. Challenge yourself to imagine what would happen if it *wasn't* a dream!</li><li><b>Wizard's Explanation!</b> 🧙‍♂️ The wizard's explanation about the egg is a great plot point. Could you give a tiny bit more detail about *why* the dragon came here for its egg? Was it stolen?</li>	You successfully conveyed the tension and fear of facing a giant dragon. 😱 Your descriptions of physical reactions are very effective.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing the Escape!</b> ⏱️ The moment you were 'yanked back' by the wizard happens very fast. Expanding on that escape or initial interaction would add more drama.</li>	Your two paragraphs clearly separated the initial sighting from the wizard's intervention, which is good. 🧱<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Flow!</b> 🌊 Some sentences within your paragraphs are a bit long and combine many ideas. Breaking them down or using more varied linking words would improve the flow.</li>	You used vivid vocabulary like 'giant', 'blaze', 'glued', and 'disaster'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Stomming' -> '<b>Stomping</b>'.</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'Shooted' -> '<b>shot</b>'. 'Knees feels weak' -> 'knees <b>felt</b> weak'.</li><li><b>Infinitives!</b> 🛠️ 'To started' -> 'to <b>start</b>'.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'Their was a giant dragon' -> '<b>There was</b> a giant dragon'.</li>	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
