ls. And when she came back in 1854, the Simon War start to bit out and she like think like I might help in the war and she go.<br><br><br>And her most important action was like, like I say for, she improved hygiene in hospital and cleanliness in hospital, which saved many lives. And she got an award like the order of merit in 1907. And this was the award who like the highest civilian in England, and gave it to her. And the last one is, uh, Florence Nightingale medal like made in 1912. Uh, this was made by International Committee. Um, and that gave it to her because she like hard working.<br><br><br>And what people call her a hero? Um, people call her hero because she was very kind to others. They they... she gives their her money, uh, to help and save people, not just for herself. They... she didn't expect them to like give them back to her. And she is also the one to lead the nurse, uh, in hospital and dramatically is her... her method reduced death rate from 42% to 2%.<br><br><br>And the last thing I'm going to tell you is the quote, uh, "The very first requirement in hospital is that it should do the sick no harm." This mean Florence Nightingale was believed that important in hygiene and patient in to care for others. Thank you.	605	12.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Speaking	CA	FIRST	<p>Florence, you have a lovely loud voice, and your intonation is great, which makes you very engaging to listen to! However, there's a repetitive pattern of dropping final consonant sounds, which significantly reduces intelligibility. For example, words like "nurse" often sounded like /nɜː/, "world" like /wɜːl/, and "slide" like /slaɪ/.<br><br>This is a common interference pattern for Thai speakers, as Thai syllables often omit or weaken final consonants. To improve, focus on clearly articulating final consonant sounds. Try practicing words with strong final consonants, making sure your tongue or lips complete the sound. For example, consciously say the /s/ in "nurse," the /d/ in "world," and the /d/ in "slide." Regularly recording yourself and listening back can also help you identify and correct these sounds. Keep practicing, and your pronunciation will become even clearer!</p>	<p>Hi Florence! 👋 You delivered a presentation about your hero, Florence Nightingale, and shared some really interesting facts about her life and contributions. You spoke clearly and enthusiastically, which is fantastic! Keep up the great work on your speaking skills, and with a little focus on a couple of areas, you'll be speaking even more confidently! 💪</p>	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1by6UKGd4IRmb0pAHXaTn1cuU1wgGUPUF?usp=drive_link	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
