rrors and the unfinished nature of the story make it difficult for the reader to stay fully engaged. Aim for smoother sentences and a complete plot.</li><li><b>Clarity of Ideas!</b> 💡 Focus on expressing your ideas more clearly to avoid any confusion for the reader.</li>	Your text attempts to connect ideas, but the overall structure could be clearer. You use '<br><br>' to separate some ideas, but not consistently.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 🧱 While you use some paragraph breaks, consider making them more consistent to separate different events or shifts in the story.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 📝 Focus on writing complete sentences with correct punctuation and capitalization to make your writing easier to follow. For example, 'The machine Start spinning. and it create...' could be 'The machine started spinning and created...'</li>	You use some everyday vocabulary appropriately, such as 'spinning', 'Electric Ring', and 'tornado'.<br><br>Here are a few tips to help with your language:<br><li><b>Verb Tenses!</b> ⏳ Pay close attention to verb forms, e.g., 'The machine <b>started</b> spinning' instead of 'Start spinning', and 'He <b>created</b> invention' instead of 'He create invention'.</li><li><b>Capitalization!</b> 🅰️ Be careful with capitalization, especially at the beginning of sentences and for proper nouns like 'Nasa'.</li><li><b>Word Choice/Spelling!</b> 💬 'Riche' should be '<b>rich</b>', and 'millionare' should be '<b>millionaire</b>'. Also, 'depend on the amount' should be '<b>depending</b> on the amount' or '<b>It depends</b> on the amount'.</li><li><b>Sentence Construction!</b> 🛠️ Practice forming complete and grammatically correct sentences to ensure your meaning is clear, e.g., 'The bell skyrocket' could be 'The bells skyrocketed' or 'His wealth skyrocketed'.</li>	3.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
