or your attention. Bye-bye.	361	15.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Speaking	CA	PET	That was a fantastic presentation about your book today, Lookpear. You were very clear and organized in the way you told the story. It was very easy to follow your ideas!<br><br><b>What You Did Well:</b><br>I was extremely impressed by how well you pronounced plural sounds, like in the word "secrets" /ˈsiːkrɪts/. You also have excellent intonation that really brings your speaking to life and shows your confidence.<br><br><b>What to Watch Out For:</b><br>You still have a tendency to drop final consonant sounds, such as in words like "strange" /streɪndʒ/ or "fought" /fɔːt/. I also noticed that some past tense endings, like the /ɪd/ in "unexpected" /ˌʌnɪkˈspektɪd/, were dropped, which can change the meaning of your sentences.<br><br><b>How to Get Even Better:</b><br><ul><li><b>Focus on Past Tense Endings:</b> Pay extra attention to /ɪd/ endings when talking about the past; even if it is just a small /t/ or /d/ sound, it makes a big difference.</li><li><b>Complete Every Word:</b> Practice ending words like "strange" with a clear final sound to ensure your meaning is always 100% clear.</li><li><b>Slow Down for Clarity:</b> When you get to a difficult word or a past tense verb, slow down just a little bit to make sure the ending is pronounced correctly.</li></ul><br>You are already a very strong speaker, so these small adjustments will help you sound even more professional! 🌟	Lookpear, you gave a very clear and interesting review of the manga Gokurakugai! Your vocabulary was impressive, and you used words like "fascinating" and "eliminating" very effectively. You followed the structure well and used a great hook to start your talk. To improve, remember to include all required details like the author's name. You should also work on using past participles correctly and reducing small hesitations to make your speaking even smoother. You have a great ability to explain complex plots! 🌟	\N	\N	\N	\N