2970	33168	2025-12-14 15:55:01.0466+00	Term 2 Midterms 2025-6	Hi,<br><br>I'm glad you are happy to go camping this weekend.<br><br><br>I prefer to take the train on the Saturday morning because I don't want to get traffic jam and I think we should bring barbeque instead because it easier and more delicious. I recommend you to bring a steak, marshmello and chocolate if you want to. I agree with you that it might be cold at night, I suggest that we should bring a warm blanket a fur coat, which is very useful when you are cold, a pillow. I don't know if the campsite has it or not but I think we should bring our own instead, a pair of sock would be good too.	117	14.0	Hi Rome! 👋<br><br>Nice work! I really liked your suggestion of "marshmallow and chocolate" - S'mores are the best part of camping! 🍫 Your idea to bring a "fur coat" sounds very fancy and warm! 🧥<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 "marshmello" -> "marshmallow".<br>2. <b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ "it easier" -> "it <b>is</b> easier".<br>3. <b>Run-ons!</b> 🏃‍♂️ Use full stops to separate your ideas.\n	You covered the points well. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pillow!</b> 💭 You mentioned a pillow. Great idea for comfort!</li>\n	Your tone is friendly. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Closing!</b> 👋 You forgot to sign your name at the end!</li>\n	Your second paragraph was very long and had many ideas. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Structure!</b> 🧱 Put "Food" and "Warmth" in separate paragraphs.</li>\n	"Traffic jam" and "fur coat" are good phrases! 👏<br><br>Fix these:<br><li><b>Articles/Plurals!</b> 🔢 "a pair of sock" -> "a pair of <b>socks</b>" (plural).</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 🔍 "marshmello" -> "marshm<b>a</b>llo<b>w</b>".</li>\n	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
2946	28863	2025-12-14 09:36:22.178373+00	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. It was Saturday latenight and it was rainning heavily outside. I woke up in the dark because of the thunder sound, feeling hungry. So I decided to search some thing to eat in the kitchen downstairs. I closed my room's door quietly trying not to wake my mom in the next room. When I arrived at the fridge I saw the bright light shine throught the curtains so I looked out of the window and I saw my neighbour's house caught on fire then it was a heavy thunder on my neighbour's house roof twice. It caused an awfull noise that woke my mom and dad. They came downstairs and I told them what happened so they called the emergency service. The next morning started in my room and I was on my bed again. I looked out of the window and everything outside was fine like it should on Sunday morning. My neighbour sang peacefully in his garden again so I know what it means.	177	16.0	Hello Namo K! 👋<br><br>This was a very atmospheric and suspenseful story! ⛈️ The thunder, the rain, the fire, and the mysterious twist ending of it all being a dream were very well-handled. You did a great job building up the tension from a simple midnight snack run.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you make your writing even more polished! 📋<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 Watch out for words like 'latenight' (late night), 'rainning' (raining), and 'awfull' (awful).<br>2. <b>Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'It should on Sunday morning' should be 'it should be <b>on</b> Sunday morning'.<br>3. <b>Show, Don't Tell!</b> 🎬 Instead of saying 'I know what it means', describe your character's reaction (a sigh of relief? a smile?) to the peaceful Sunday morning.	You started your story perfectly with the given sentence and developed a very engaging plot about a frightening midnight event turning out to be a dream. 🌟 All content was relevant and contributed to the story's suspense.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>The Fire!</b> 🔥 You mentioned your neighbour's house caught fire. Describing the flames or smoke a little more vividly would increase the drama.</li><li><b>Parent's Reaction!</b> 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 You said your parents called emergency services. Did they look scared? Were they rushing? Adding details to their actions would make the scene more dynamic.</li>	You created a strong sense of atmosphere and successfully built tension throughout your narrative. ⛈️ The dream ending provided a clever resolution.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Smoother Transitions!</b> 🌊 The jump from the middle of the chaotic night to 'The next morning started in my room and I was on my bed again' is a bit abrupt. A sentence bridging these two events could improve the flow.</li>	Your story follows a clear chronological progression, from waking up to discovering the fire and then the dream revelation. 🧱 Your paragraph breaks are generally effective.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Varying Linkers!</b> 🔗 You used 'So' and 'Then' effectively. Try incorporating a wider range of transitional words (e.g., 'Subsequently', 'Meanwhile', 'As a result') to enhance the flow and sophistication of your writing.</li>	You used good everyday vocabulary related to home and emergencies, like 'thunder', 'kitchen', 'curtains', and 'emergency service'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Latenight' -> '<b>late night</b>', 'rainning' -> '<b>raining</b>', 'awfull' -> '<b>awful</b>'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'It should on Sunday morning' -> 'it should be <b>on</b> Sunday morning'.</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'Bright light shine' -> 'bright light <b>shone</b>'. 'Tooked at me' -> '<b>looked</b> at me'.</li>	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
1157	33954	2025-08-30 13:36:51.174328+00	Free time Activities	Activities for teens in Thailand absolutely mostly of them is using their phone or playing game in mobile-phone but they still have their own hobbies which is make a good relax moment in free time without internet or use it less than when just addicted with it. So, the activities teens usually do are hang out with friends and call with friends and talking any topic they like.<br><br><br>In the begining, if there was no any plan to do, hang out with friends is a good choice. To keep a good and fun memories we have to keep each other company going outside together whenever we like. For teenagers, we have to ask for permission from parents to go outside and even planing to friends well enough for a permission. Going outside, having fun, I think that was enough for teenager's life.<br><br><br>As well as calling with friends and talking whatever we want. This can be in real life to, sit then talk but this we can talk even long distance between friends. Calling isn't just for talking, playing games together or playing some challenges and more. All of this is for kill the time that passed.<br><br><br>All in all, all of teen's activities are time for go have a good childhood for life ness with any people they love, friends, parents, sibling or lover if they had a highschool sweetheart. Keeping memory of this life age is the best thing forever in life, keep it as much as we can so, we can remember it until we forgot this life age and wondering how was that life age we've been. Wish we could have a good memories.	278	11.0	<p>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 278 words and achieved B1+. You organized your essay into paragraphs, which is a good way to structure your ideas.</p>	<p>You attempted to address the task by mentioning free time activities, but the essay's ending paragraph becomes quite abstract and less focused on "free time activities" and more on a general reflection on childhood memories, which slightly detracts from fully informing the target reader about the topic. You also have some unclear phrasing in your introduction.<br>👉 To Improve: Make sure to finish your essay and cover all parts of the question clearly. Ensure your introduction clearly states your main points and your conclusion effectively summarizes them, staying focused on the topic.<br>❌ Weakness: Your conclusion talks about "time for go have a good childhood for life ness" and "Keeping memory of this life age is the best thing forever in life," which is a bit general for the topic of "free time activities."<br>✨ Improved: "In conclusion, free time activities like hanging out and calling friends are essential for Thai teenagers. They provide valuable opportunities to build strong friendships, share experiences, and create lasting memories that contribute positively to their social development and overall well-being."<br>💡 Explanation: Completing the essay and developing your ideas fully ensures the reader gets all the information they need and a clear understanding of your points. A strong conclusion summarises your main ideas and directly relates back to the essay topic.</p>	<p>You used an appropriate tone for an article, but the register shifts between formal and informal language, which can confuse the reader about the intended audience. Your grammatical errors also affect clarity and overall impact.<br>👉 To Improve: Maintain a consistent register throughout your writing - either formal for a general audience or consistently informal for peers. For an essay, a semi-formal to formal tone is usually best.<br>❌ Weakness: Phrases like "going outside together whenever we like" lean towards informal language, while other parts of your essay attempt a more formal approach.<br>✨ Improved: "Thai teenagers commonly engage in social activities, such as meeting friends in person or communicating with them by phone, to relax and strengthen their bonds."<br>💡 Explanation: Keeping a consistent formal tone helps establish credibility and makes your writing more professional for a general audience. Clear and accurate grammar also significantly improves how effectively your message is understood.</p>	<p>You organized your ideas into paragraphs, which helps the reader follow your main points, but the connections between ideas could be stronger with better linking words. The thesis statement in your introduction isn't explicitly clear, and your concluding paragraph becomes quite abstract rather than clearly summarizing your points.<br>👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases to show clearer relationships between your ideas (e.g., however, therefore, as a result, in addition). Make sure your introduction has a clear thesis statement, and your conclusion restates it and summarizes your main points.<br>❌ Weakness: Your introduction starts with "Activities for teens in Thailand absolutely mostly of them is using their phone... but they still have their own hobbies which is make a good relax moment..." which makes it difficult to immediately identify your main argument or the essay's focus.<br>✨ Improved: "While many Thai teenagers use their phones for leisure, they also engage in valuable social activities like meeting and calling friends, which are essential for relaxation and personal development."<br>💡 Explanation: Using specific linking words helps show the relationship between ideas more clearly and makes your writing flow better. A clear thesis guides your entire essay, and a strong conclusion brings all your ideas together effectively.</p>	<p>You used some good vocabulary related to the topic, but there are several recurring grammar patterns and sentence structure issues that affect clarity, and there are no error-free sentences.<br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "a good memories"<br>✨ Correction: "good memories"<br>💡 Explanation: In English, the word "memories" is a plural count noun, and you would not use "a" before it when talking about multiple memories. This is similar to how Thai handles plurals without a specific marker like 's' in English, which can be a common challenge for Thai learners.<br><br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "mobile-phone but they still have their own hobbies"<br>✨ Correction: "mobile-phone, but they still have their own hobbies"<br>💡 Explanation: In English, when you connect two complete sentences with a conjunction like "but," you usually need a comma before the conjunction. Thai sentences often connect ideas without these explicit markers, leading to 'run-on' sentences or comma splices in English.<br><br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "All of this is for kill the time"<br>✨ Correction: "All of this is to kill the time"<br>💡 Explanation: The choice of preposition can be tricky in English. In this context, "to" is used to show purpose or intention. Thai learners sometimes choose "for" because it can also indicate purpose, but the grammatical structure required here is "to" + base verb (infinitive).</p>	3.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
