 very evident.<br><br><b>What to Watch Out For:</b><br>Your speech currently feels a bit disjointed and "choppy" because of hesitation and a lack of linking between words. This, combined with a flat intonation, can make it more difficult for a listener to follow the flow of your ideas.<br><br><b>How to Get Even Better:</b><br><ul><li><b>Practice Linking Words:</b> Try to "push" words together rather than speaking one word at a time; for example, practice saying "this is" as if it were one word: /ðɪsɪz/.</li><li><b>Build Fluency with Repetition:</b> Read the same short story aloud several times until you can say it smoothly without many pauses or hesitations.</li><li><b>Add Dynamic Tone:</b> Try to vary the pitch of your voice more so it doesn't sound flat; this will help your listeners stay more engaged with what you are saying.</li></ul><br>Becoming more fluent takes time and practice, so keep going and your confidence will definitely grow! 💪	ThatThat, you gave a very clear and organized review of Demon Slayer! You covered all the required points, including a good hook and a clear recommendation at the end. Your grammar was strong, especially when you described the action scenes. To improve, try to watch out for small mistakes with uncountable nouns like blood and focus on making your speech flow more smoothly by reducing pauses. You are doing a great job expressing your opinions in English. 🌟	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
