1163	28889	2025-08-30 14:23:25.032789+00	Free time Activities	In the freetime people often playing games and play outside. It's pretty normal in Thailand. Although Thai peoples go on trip often then stay at home. There are two most Thai people did in they free time. is go to trip and playing games.<br><br><br>firstly, A trip Thailand have hundred of places to visit. It's very popular in Thailand because It's pretty borading to stay Just at home and do nothing. Most of the captivating place to go is Bankok<br><br><br>Secondly, playing games a basic free time activities mostly teens were did. However teen begin with feeling relaxing when they start to play till it start to get it borading at the end.<br><br><br>all in all, It is important to having a break after a long masive of works. if you haven't, you will gone crazy.	136	8.0	<p>👋 Dear Kao-Oat<br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 136 words and achieved A2+. Your essay started to discuss some relevant points about free time.</p>	<p>You attempted to address the task by mentioning free time activities, but the essay is incomplete, and therefore, the target reader is not fully informed. You only identified one activity in detail, not the two required, and the essay is under the word count.<br>👉 To Improve: Make sure to finish your essay and cover all parts of the question. You need to identify two free time activities and explain them in detail.<br>❌ Weakness: The essay doesn't fully explain the activities or why they are popular in Thailand, for example: "There are two most Thai people did in they free time. is go to trip and playing games." This is not clear.<br>✨ Improved: "Thai people often choose two popular free-time activities: travelling to different places within Thailand and playing online games. Both activities provide a welcome break from daily routines, but they offer different kinds of relaxation and social interaction."<br>💡 Explanation: Completing the essay and developing your ideas fully ensures the reader gets all the information they need and a clear understanding of your points.</p>	<p>You used an appropriate tone for an article in some places, but the register shifts between formal and informal language, which can confuse the reader about the intended audience.<br>👉 To Improve: Maintain a consistent register throughout your writing - either formal for a general audience or consistently informal for peers.<br>❌ Weakness: Phrases like "It's pretty normal" and "mostly teens were did" sound very informal, while "Although Thai peoples go on trip often then stay at home" uses a more formal structure, making the tone inconsistent.<br>✨ Improved: "Thai society often sees people engaging in two main leisure activities: domestic travel and digital gaming."<br>💡 Explanation: Keeping a consistent formal tone helps establish credibility and makes your writing more professional for a general audience, which is usually expected for an essay.</p>	<p>You organized your ideas into paragraphs, which helps the reader follow your main points, but the connections between ideas could be stronger with better linking words. The introduction lacks a clear thesis statement, and the conclusion is very abrupt.<br>👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases to show clearer relationships between your ideas (e.g., however, therefore, as a result). Your introduction should clearly state your main points, and your conclusion should summarize them.<br>❌ Weakness: Your introduction doesn't clearly state what your essay will be about, and sentences are sometimes connected without clear logical flow: "In the freetime people often playing games and play outside. It's pretty normal in Thailand. Although Thai peoples go on trip often then stay at home. There are two most Thai people did in they free time. is go to trip and playing games."<br>✨ Improved: "In Thailand, free time is often spent pursuing two main activities: traveling and playing games. These choices reflect a desire for both exploration and relaxation, offering benefits to those seeking a break from routine."<br>💡 Explanation: A clear introduction helps the reader understand your essay's purpose from the start, and varied linking words improve the flow and coherence of your arguments.</p>	<p>You used some vocabulary related to the topic, but there are several recurring grammar patterns and spelling errors that affect clarity.<br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "There are two most Thai people did in they free time. is go to trip and playing games."<br>✨ Correction: "There are two most common activities Thai people do in their free time: going on trips and playing games."<br>💡 Explanation: This sentence has several issues. Firstly, "is go" should be "are going" or "go". Secondly, "did" should be "do" for general habits. Thai does not always distinguish between verb forms for different tenses or subjects as strictly as English, which can lead to these errors. Also, "they free time" should be "their free time."<br><br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "mostly teens were did."<br>✨ Correction: "mostly teens do" or "mostly teens did."<br>💡 Explanation: This mixes verb tenses and forms. "Were did" is not a correct English construction. In English, you would use "did" for a completed past action or "do" for a general habit. Thai verbal structures are more flexible and often imply tense from context rather than requiring explicit auxiliary verbs and past participles, leading to confusion with English verb forms.<br><br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "It's pretty borading to stay Just at home" and "it start to get it borading at the end."<br>✨ Correction: "It's pretty boring to stay just at home" and "it starts to get boring at the end."<br>💡 Explanation: "Borading" is a common spelling mistake for "boring" (adjective). Also, "Just" should not be capitalized here, and "it start" needs an 's' for third-person singular present tense ("it starts"). Thai spelling is phonetic and does not have the same vowel combinations or silent letters as English, which can make spelling words like "boring" difficult.</p>	2.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
