 healthy Thai foods is well-organized and presents clear information about Larb Gai, Yum Hed Ruam, and Pad Pak Boong. You have effectively used topic sentences and relative clauses, which is commendable. To improve, focus on addressing grammatical errors, particularly with apostrophes in contractions and verb forms. Also, try to expand on the cultural analysis beyond just taste to fully meet the essay requirements.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
1040	33955	2025-08-14 15:41:23.013284+00	Thai Food	Food is essential in every culture. Although all culture need food, each culture develop its own food and styles. In particular, streetfood is very popular. There has been a popular streetfood in Thai. Three of the most important streetfood are moo-ping, kai toad, and look chin toad.<br><br><br>One of the popular streetfood, which is made by pork, moo-ping sauce, and milk. There are three steps to make moo-ping. First, mash the pork, next marinate mashed pork with moo-ping sauce, then grill the pork while spraying the milk on it. Moo-ping strongly represents Thai culture because most of Thai people eat pork. Furthermore, a lot of Thai are half chinese because of that some of them believe in Mother Kuan-Im and one of the rule is you can't eat beef. That's why most of Thai people eat pork.<br><br><br>Besides moo-ping, kai toad is a second major popular streetfood, which is make by chicken, flour, and fish sauce. First, prepare the chicken. Next marinate the chicken with fish sauce. After that, mix marinated chicken with flour. Finally fry the chicken in boiling oil until it's golden. In addition Kai toad symbolize Thai culture because most of Thai people love to eat chicken and you can find chicken everywhere in Thailand. Also fried chicken often serve with sticky rice and chicken sauce that taste sweet and spicy.<br><br><br>Finally, fried meat ball, which is known as look chin, is make by pork meat balls and flour. Fried meat ball is very easy to make, first skewer the meat balls. Then mix it with flour, after that fry it in boiling oil. Look chin toad strongly represents Thai culture because most of Thai people love to eat cheap and delicious food. Furthermore, this fried skewered meat balls are very cheap and it taste very good. It's also serve with sweet and spicy sauce.<br><br><br>In conclusion, there are a lot of popular streetfood in Thailand. However moo-ping, kai toad and look chin toad are the three food that I mentioned. I hope now you have a clearer information about these food.	345	\N	You have written a clear and well-structured essay about Thai street food. You have successfully described three popular street foods and explained why they are important to Thai culture. To improve your writing further, focus on varying your vocabulary and using relative clauses and passive structures more consistently.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
