ne, which keeps the reader engaged in the fast-paced events. 💨<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Vary Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Many sentences start with 'I'. Experiment with different sentence beginnings to create a more dynamic rhythm.</li>	You followed a clear chronological sequence from sighting to rescue to the twist ending. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 The story is currently one long block of text. Breaking it into paragraphs (e.g., one for the sighting, one for the capture, one for the rescue, one for the ending) would greatly improve readability.</li>	You used clear action verbs like 'capture', 'destroy', 'reclaim', and 'fried'. 🍳<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Belive' -> '<b>believe</b>', 'Roster' -> '<b>rooster</b>' (this appears many times!), 'couln't' -> '<b>couldn't</b>', 'imeditly' -> '<b>immediately</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Destroy all of their balls' is very informal. Consider rephrasing for clarity and a more standard tone.</li><li><b>Tense!</b> ⏳ 'I taste it. It taste' -> 'I <b>tasted</b> it. It <b>tasted</b>'.</li>	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
