ables, which can affect the natural rhythm of English. For example, when you said "people," the stress might have been too strong on the second syllable. English often has a more even flow of stress, with some syllables being softer. To improve, pay attention to the natural rhythm and stress patterns of English words and sentences.</p><br><p>You might also find it helpful to practice specific sounds that can be challenging. For example, some Thai speakers tend to drop final consonants, as in "bag" becoming "ba," or they might add extra vowel sounds in consonant clusters like "smoke" becoming "samoke." While these specific errors weren't heavily noted in your comments, focusing on clearly articulating all sounds, especially at the ends of words and within clusters, will help your overall clarity.</p><br><p>To improve your pronunciation, try to:<br>*   Listen carefully to native English speakers and try to imitate their rhythm and intonation.<br>*   Practice linking words together smoothly so that your speech flows more naturally.<br>*   Focus on the correct word stress and sentence stress, rather than overstressing every syllable. For instance, in words like "people," the stress is on the first syllable: /ˈpiː.pəl/.<br>*   You can also try exercises that focus on clearly pronouncing final consonants and consonant clusters. For example, practice words like "friend**s**" or "li**ght**." 🎧</p>	<p>Hello Kao-Oat! 😊 It's great to see your effort in presenting your hero, King Bhumibol Adulyadej. You shared some interesting points about his life and achievements, which shows you have a good understanding of the topic. Keep up the good work! 👍</p><br><p>One of your strengths is being able to produce extended sentences and use basic connectors to link your ideas. However, to improve, try to expand on your ideas more fully and practice using a wider variety of vocabulary and grammatical structures. Also, being mindful of the length of your talk will help you present all your wonderful ideas! You're making progress, and with continued practice, you'll surely shine! ✨</p>	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1by6UKGd4IRmb0pAHXaTn1cuU1wgGUPUF?usp=drive_link	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
