eenagers in the current highly competitive academic environment. Two particularly popular and beneficial activities are listening to music and engaging in creative artwork, both offering unique avenues for self-expression and stress relief."</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: Expanding on why the activities are popular and linking them to a clear thesis in your introduction will give your essay more depth and direction.</p>	<p>You attempted to communicate ideas, but the overall effect on the reader is not entirely successful due to an inconsistent register and a lack of persuasive language. The purpose of an essay (to present a clear argument or explanation) is not fully achieved. For example, your introduction is very direct, and then you use "Morover" as a linking word, which is not typical of a formal essay.</p><br><p>👉 To Improve: Maintain a consistent formal register throughout your writing for an essay, and use more sophisticated language to persuade and inform your reader.</p><br><p>❌ Weakness: Using phrases like "First listen to music" and "Morover creating art work" to introduce main points, which are too informal for an essay.</p><br><p>✨ Improved: "Firstly, music plays a crucial role in the lives of many young Thais. Moreover, artistic endeavors such as painting and drawing offer another significant outlet for self-expression among teenagers."</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: Using formal introductory phrases and appropriate linking words helps maintain a consistent register and makes your essay more professional and engaging for a general audience.</p>	<p>You divided your ideas into paragraphs, which helps the reader follow your main points, but the structure is very basic. Topic sentences are not consistently clear, and linking words are repetitive or used inappropriately. Your introduction does not present a clear thesis, and the conclusion simply restates points without effectively summarizing them.</p><br><p>👉 To Improve: Start your introduction with a clear thesis statement that outlines your main argument. Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases to show clearer relationships between your ideas, and ensure your conclusion effectively summarizes your points and restates your thesis in new words.</p><br><p>❌ Weakness: The introduction "Free time activities make teenager know how to use there free time efficiently, teenager in Thailand like to use there free time listening to music and creating artwork" does not clearly present a thesis. The conclusion simply repeats "In conclusion there alot of activities you can do in your free time. in particular listen to music and creating art is very popular among Thai teen because Thai teen love doing this."</p><br><p>✨ Improved: An effective introduction would state something like: "In contemporary Thai society, free time activities are essential outlets for teenagers to develop improved life skills and express themselves. This essay will explore how listening to music and engaging in creative arts significantly contribute to their holistic development and well-being." A strong conclusion would then tie these ideas together and reinforce the initial thesis.</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: A clear thesis in the introduction sets the stage for your essay, and a strong conclusion provides a satisfying and memorable end by summarizing and reinforcing your main arguments. Using varied linking words improves flow.</p>	<p>You used good vocabulary related to the topic, such as "express their emotion," which is a good effort! However, there are several recurring grammar patterns that affect clarity, and it's helpful to remember that "emotion" should be plural here (emotions) as you are talking about many different feelings.</p><br><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Free time activities make teenager know how to use there free time efficiently, teenager in Thailand like to use there free time listening to music and creating artwork."</p><br><p>✨ Correction: "Free time activities help teenagers know how to use their free time efficiently; teenagers in Thailand like to use their free time listening to music and creating artwork."</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: In English, 'make' can be used for causation, but 'help' is often more natural when describing a beneficial influence. Also, 'teenager' needs to be plural 'teenagers' when referring to the group generally. The possessive 'their' (belonging to them) is often confused with 'there' (a place) or 'they're' (they are) by Thai speakers, as these distinctions don't exist in Thai.</p><br><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "There are a lot of music genra."</p><br><p>✨ Correction: "There are a lot of music genres."</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: This is a common spelling mistake for a word with a foreign origin. Always double-check spellings, especially for less common words.</p><br><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "teen carry alot of stress" and "there alot of activities"</p><br><p>✨ Correction: "teens carry a lot of stress" and "there are a lot of activities"</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: "A lot" is two words, not one. Also, in English, we often pluralize nouns when referring to a general group, so "teens" is more appropriate than "teen" here. Thai learners often struggle with 'a lot' as a single word due to how quantity is expressed in Thai.</p><br><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Morover creating art work"</p><br><p>✨ Correction: "Moreover, creating artwork"</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: "Moreover" is spelled with an 'e'. Also, it is a conjunctive adverb used to link ideas, and typically needs a comma after it when starting a sentence to introduce additional information. "Artwork" is usually treated as an uncountable noun in English.</p><br><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "you can start by skecth your idea on the canvas"</p><br><p>✨ Correction: "you can start by sketching your idea on the canvas"</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: "Sketch" is the correct spelling for the verb meaning to make a rough drawing. Also, when you use "by" + a verb, the verb needs to be in the -ing form (gerund).</p><br><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "it because Thai teenager can express their emotion."</p><br><p>✨ Correction: "it is because Thai teenagers can express their emotions."</p><br><p>💡 Explanation: "It is" (or its contraction "it's") is needed here as a subject and verb before "because". Also, as noted earlier, "teenagers" should be plural, and "emotions" should be plural when referring to multiple feelings. The use of "it" without a verb is a common omission for Thai speakers, as the subject pronoun 'it' is often implied in Thai sentences.</p><br><p>🎯 YOUR ACTION PLAN<br>1. Complete all parts of writing tasks and develop each point fully<br>2. Maintain consistent formal register throughout your writing<br>3. Practice using different linking words to connect ideas<br>4. Review subject-verb agreement rules for present tense and correct use of articles</p>	3.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
