tic inventory of Thai, which might not have a direct equivalent for /v/, leading to substitution with /w/. The flat intonation can be linked to Thai being a tonal language, where pitch changes meaning within words, rather than for emphasis or emotion across sentences as in English.	Leo, your communication skills are really coming along, especially in how well you chat with others! Let's focus on making your grammar super clear and your words easy to hear. With a little practice, you'll be expressing yourself with even greater confidence and accuracy.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1yqGR5ip5XtVuoI2jPIboJbuDxmsnlN7a?usp=drive_link	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
