opriate for a magazine.<br><br>To improve:<br>Check your content! ✍️ You mentioned reading too much makes you 'eppressive'. Try to expand on why you think reading too much is oppressive—does it make you feel tired or trapped? Improving the explanation here would make your argument stronger.	Your text is easy to follow and you used basic linking words like 'because' and 'but' to connect your ideas. 🌊<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 🧱 Your transition from talking about Zita to talking about reading habits is a bit sudden. You could use a linking phrase like 'In my opinion,' or 'Regarding your question,' to start the second paragraph.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> ⛓️ Try to avoid starting sentences with 'But' too often. You can use 'However,' or simply join the two sentences together.</li>	You used some great vocabulary like 'adventure', 'scary aliens', and 'recommended'! 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you improve:<br><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'A story that <b>has</b> pictures' (not 'have').</li><li><b>Infinitives!</b> 🛠️ 'He wanted me to <b>practice</b>' (not 'practicing').</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'It's <b>an</b> interesting comic' (use 'an' before vowel sounds).</li><li><b>Word Forms!</b> 🔄 'Creative and <b>ingenious</b>' (use two adjectives together) or 'it gives us <b>creativity and ingenuity</b>' (use two nouns together).</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Eppressive' should likely be <b>'depressed'</b> or <b>'oppressed'</b>. Also, 'make us' should be '<b>makes</b> us'.</li>	5.0	4.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
