ai learners sometimes write longer paragraphs, but in English, breaking up your text helps the reader understand the different ideas you're presenting. Try to also use a wider variety of linking words, like "furthermore," "in addition," or "consequently," to connect your thoughts more smoothly. 🎀	Tonnam, you use everyday words that are very appropriate for your article, and you generally control your simple sentences well. I understood everything you wanted to communicate, which is really important. To help your language be even more accurate and move towards a score of 5, let's focus on a few things. Firstly, be careful with plurals, for example, "One of festival" should be "one of the *festivals*", and "put some ball" should be "put some *balls*". Secondly, make sure your verbs agree with your subjects, like in "my family *was* excited" it should be "my family *were* excited" because "family" here is thought of as multiple people, or "christmas day *is* come" should be "Christmas Day *comes*." Finally, double-check your spelling for words like "Christmas" and "year" ("Chirstmas," "Someyear"). These little tweaks will make your writing even more precise and impressive. Thai learners sometimes struggle with pluralisation because the concept is handled differently in Thai, where context often indicates quantity rather than specific grammatical endings. Keep practising, and you'll see great improvement. ✨	4.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
