g even clearer and more impactful, focusing on developing a more formal style and ensuring your grammar is as accurate as possible will be a wonderful next step. Keep up the good work on expressing your thoughts.<br><br>📋 **Action Plan for Improvement**<br>*   ✅ Practice writing complete sentences and connecting them smoothly with appropriate linking words.<br>*   ✅ Pay close attention to spelling and common grammatical patterns, especially verb forms and plural nouns.<br>*   ✅ When writing a formal essay, try to avoid very casual language and focus on presenting your ideas in a clear, structured way.	Rico, it is great that you have included all the points from the task, including your own idea about gaming. You have made an effort to give examples, like the "Water elephant pajama" in fashion, which helps to illustrate your points. 👍 To improve, try to make sure each paragraph clearly links back to the main question about who has more effect, friends or parents. For instance, in your section on studying, while you mention parents influence, think about how you can explicitly argue whether this influence is *more* or *less* than friends. Remember, an essay usually requires you to argue a point directly, not just describe a situation.	You have communicated your ideas in a straightforward way, Rico, which is a good start. 😊 However, for a formal essay like this, it is important to use language that is suitable for an academic audience. Starting with "Hello teacher, its me Rico" is very friendly, but it is not what we expect in an essay response. Try to imagine you are writing for someone you do not know personally, and aim for a more objective and formal tone. For example, instead of "its me Rico," you could begin with a general statement about the topic. Focusing on a consistent formal register throughout will help you achieve a higher score in this area.	Your essay has a basic structure with an introduction and separate paragraphs for each point, which is helpful for