on between your hobby and your future career choice is very engaging.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Article Style!</b> 📰 Articles usually benefit from a catchy title at the beginning, like 'Why I Love Science' or 'Reading for the Future'.</li><li><b>Addressing the Reader!</b> 💬 Try to talk directly to the reader. Instead of saying 'There are two reasons', you could say 'Did you know that reading can actually help your health?'.</li>	Your text is connected and coherent. 🌊 You used linking words like 'Firstly' and 'And the last one' to list your points clearly.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Variety in Linking!</b> 🔗 Instead of 'the last one', try using 'Secondly' or 'Furthermore' to sound more professional.</li><li><b>Paragraph Transitions!</b> 🏗️ The jump between the benefits of reading and your favorite book is a bit sudden. You could use a sentence like 'My personal favorite thing to read is...' to connect the two sections smoothly.</li>	You used some good vocabulary like 'knowledge', 'structure', and 'wonderful'. 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you polish your grammar:<br><li><b>The Personal Pronoun!</b> 📝 Always use a capital letter for '<b>I</b>' (e.g., '<b>I</b> read', '<b>I</b> saw').</li><li><b>Missing 'Be'!</b> 🛠️ 'it'll bad for your health' -> 'it'll <b>be</b> bad for your health'.</li><li><b>Verb Tenses!</b> ⏳ When talking about a general fact, use the present tense. 'I like when I <b>see</b> animals' (instead of 'saw').</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> ⚙️ 'if you watching social media too much' -> 'if you <b>watch</b> social media too much'.</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🔍 'I read <b>the</b> biology book' -> 'I read <b>a</b> biology book' (unless you are talking about one specific book the reader already knows).</li>	5.0	4.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
