1151	34059	2025-08-29 15:07:52.941075+00	Free time Activities	Free time activities is make people feel relaxed and reduce stress. Although everyone have a different kinds of activities depend of each personalities and environments. In particular, Thai teenagers also have many activities to do in their free times. The most popular free time activities for teens in Thailand is playing sports and doing handmade.<br><br><br>The most popular free time activities in Thailand is playing sports, which is also supports health and body. Thai teenagers usually playing sports for their connection. It help teenagers to find a good friends thoulgh sport team works. In particular some people can able to become a profesional athlete and make their career jobs even better.<br><br><br>Beside playing sports, handmade activities is the one that very interesting. Handmade activities, which can be both relaxing and creative fullfilling. This include origami, painting, drawing and crafting. Handmade also make you unlock the new skills and stay claim. In Thailand handmade, is the very famous activities for teenagers nowadays. People like to spend time with lovers and friend or family and do handmade to giving to the person that you love and respect.<br><br><br>To summerise, both of these activities is a tiny kind of free time activities in Thailand. Teenagers also use the free time to find their hobbys or made their future better than before.	201	12.0	You did a good job identifying some popular free time activities in Thailand!	You identified two free time activities, but you didn't explain why YOU (the author) chose them, which was part of the task. Also, your conclusion was too short and didn't fully develop your ideas. This means the reader isn't fully informed.👉 To Improve: Make sure to answer all parts of the question, especially when it asks for your personal reasons or choices. Always write a full conclusion that summarizes your main points.❌ Weakness: "The essay ends abruptly without a conclusion or full development of the points."✨ Improved: "To truly unwind, Thai teenagers often turn to digital entertainment. Playing computer games with friends, for instance, not only offers a fun escape but also strengthens their social bonds and communication skills, helping them build empathy rather than becoming isolated."💡 Explanation: Completing the essay and developing your ideas fully ensures the reader gets all the information they need and a clear understanding of your points.	You used an appropriate tone for an article, but sometimes your language changed from being more formal to less formal. This can make it confusing for the reader about who you are writing for.👉 To Improve: Try to keep your language style (register) consistent. Decide if you want to write for a general audience (more formal) or friends (more informal) and stick to that style throughout.❌ Weakness: "Hey guys, let me tell you about this awesome place" followed by more formal language.✨ Improved: "Salem offers visitors a fascinating glimpse into American history through its well-preserved architecture and informative museum exhibits."💡 Explanation: Keeping a consistent formal tone helps establish credibility and makes your writing more professional for a general audience.	You organized your ideas into paragraphs, which is great for helping the reader follow your points. However, the connections between your ideas could be clearer if you used more different linking words. Your conclusion was also very brief.👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases (like "furthermore," "however," "as a result") to show how your ideas are connected. Make sure your conclusion restates your main points and thesis more clearly.❌ Weakness: Using "and" repeatedly to connect ideas instead of showing specific relationships.✨ Improved: "While Salem is famous for its witch trial history, it also offers excellent seafood restaurants; therefore, visitors can enjoy both historical education and culinary experiences."💡 Explanation: Using specific linking words like "while" and "therefore" helps show the relationship between ideas more clearly and makes your writing flow better.	You used good vocabulary related to the topic, but there are several recurring grammar errors that affect clarity, especially with subject-verb agreement and plural forms.❌ Problem: You wrote: "Free time activities is make people feel relaxed..."✨ Correction: "Free time activities make people feel relaxed..."💡 Explanation: In Thai, verbs don't change form for plural subjects, but in English, the verb 'to be' and other verbs must agree with a plural subject (activities - make, not is make). This is a common challenge for Thai learners.❌ Problem: You wrote: "...everyone have a different kinds of activities..."✨ Correction: "...everyone enjoys different kinds of activities..."💡 Explanation: In English, "everyone" is a singular pronoun and takes a singular verb ("enjoys"). Also, "kinds" is plural, so it doesn't take the singular article "a" – you should use "different kinds" or "a different kind." Thai grammar doesn't distinguish singular/plural in this way, which often causes this type of error.❌ Problem: You wrote: "...find a good friends thoulgh sport team works."✨ Correction: "...find good friends through sports teams."💡 Explanation: "Friends" is plural, so you don't need the article "a". Also, "through" is the correct spelling for 'by means of'. In Thai, there isn't a direct equivalent for English articles, leading to their common omission or misuse.❌ Problem: You wrote: "This include origami, painting, drawing and crafting."✨ Correction: "This includes origami, painting, drawing and crafting."💡 Explanation: "This" is a singular subject, so the verb "include" needs an 's' at the end to agree with it in the present simple tense. This is another example of subject-verb agreement which is not present in Thai.🎯 YOUR ACTION PLAN1. Complete all parts of writing tasks, especially personal elements, and develop each point fully.2. Maintain a consistent register (formal or informal) throughout your writing.3. Practice using a wider variety of linking words and phrases to connect ideas.4. Review subject-verb agreement rules for present tense and plural nouns.	3.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
1947	34288	2025-09-18 20:10:48.678958+00	Term 1 Exam Question 1	First of all every generations have their fashion styles. Teenagers in 2025 they are into fashion, some of them start to do a parttime to buy a clothes to make they look cool in social media. To day I going to tell you about teenagers lives firstly clothes and fashion secondly studying finally conversation<br><br><br>In 2025 social media is easy to see there are many contents and the most popular is fashion many content creater start to post their fashion content and that why many teenagers are into fashion, they don't want to be the same with other they want to be unique. My brother who is the co-owner of hoodie brand and goes pretty well.<br><br><br>Secondly is studying, not everyone is love study but it is the way to success in your live. Teenagers to day example my friend Kris who is always got 4 GPA, I ask him why he always get good GPA and he said he didn't like to study that much but he have to do for his good life he want to have. And many teenagers are use technology to studying.<br><br><br>Finally is conversation. To day Teenagers are on screen using social media more than they talk to family because of to day there are more than 1000 games 100 application for them to play, After school when they come back home they just talk with friends in Discord playing Valorant that make a small gap with their family if we stop using social media 1 hour a day talk with real friends eat dinner with family I think that will make a good memory in our life.<br><br><br>In conclusion, social media and smart phone	285	4.0	Hello Nine, it's clear you put effort into writing your essay, and it is a good step to share your ideas about teenagers' lives. However, for this particular essay, there are some important areas where we need to focus our attention to help you improve significantly. Don't worry, with some focused practice, we can definitely work on these together.<br><br>📋 **Action Plan for Improvement:**<br>*   🎯 Always read the essay question carefully and underline the key parts to make sure you answer it directly. For this essay, the main point was about comparing the influence of friends *versus* parents.<br>*   📝 Before you start writing, make a quick plan or outline of your main points and how you will introduce them, develop them, and then conclude your overall argument.<br>*   📖 After writing, take the time to proofread your work slowly, perhaps even reading it aloud, to catch any small errors in grammar or spelling, especially checking if your verbs match your subjects.	You have included ideas related to fashion, studying, and conversation, which is good that you touched on different topics. 👍 However, the most important part of this essay question was to discuss "Who has more effect on the choices teenagers make - friends or parents?". Your essay generally described teenagers' lives but did not directly compare or analyse the influence of friends and parents on these choices. For example, when talking about fashion, you mentioned social media and a brother, but not how *parents* might influence fashion choices compared to friends. To improve, always refer back to the core question throughout your essay. Imagine you are having a debate: you need to clearly state your side or present both sides equally to inform your audience. Also, your essay was quite long, and the conclusion was incomplete, which made it difficult for the reader to fully understand your final thoughts.	You managed to communicate some straightforward ideas, and that is a positive. However, for a formal essay like this one, it is important to use an academic tone and structure, rather than a conversational one. Phrases like "To day I going to tell you" or talking about your brother "who is the co-owner of hoodie brand and goes pretty well" sounded more like a casual chat than a formal piece of writing. To make your writing more effective in a formal context, try to avoid very personal anecdotes and focus on presenting your arguments in a more objective and structured way. Your essay should aim to persuade or inform the reader using clear, formal language, not just share personal stories.	You did separate your essay into different paragraphs using words like "First of all," "Secondly," and "Finally," which shows you are thinking about how to organise your thoughts. That is a good start. However, the connection between your ideas within and between paragraphs needs to be much clearer. For instance, your introductory paragraph didn't really set up a clear argument about friends versus parents, and your concluding sentence was unfinished. Think of each paragraph as a mini-essay with a topic sentence, supporting details, and then a link to the next paragraph or back to your main argument. Using a variety of linking words, not just "first," "second," etc., can help your ideas flow more smoothly. For example, instead of just starting a new paragraph, you could say, "Moving on from fashion, another area where teenagers' choices are influenced is studying."	You used some everyday words, and that is a good foundation. However, there were many noticeable errors in your grammar, spelling, and word choice that often made it difficult to understand your intended meaning. For example, you wrote "every generations **have**" instead of "every generation *has*", and "Teenagers in 2025 they **are** into fashion" instead of "Teenagers in 2025 *are* into fashion". You also frequently missed articles (like 'a' or 'the') and had spelling errors like "To day" (should be "Today") and "live" (should be "life"). For Thai learners, English verb agreement and the use of articles can be particularly tricky, as these concepts are handled differently in Thai. A focused effort on these basic grammatical structures will significantly improve the clarity and accuracy of your writing. Try to review sentences for subject-verb agreement and ensure you are using articles correctly before nouns.	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
