th 'to playing toge'. Make sure you finish your words (together) and your thoughts!</li>	You communicated your ideas clearly enough that I understood your love for <i>Sakura Lovely</i>. 🤩 Using 'Firstly' and 'Secondly' helped me follow your points.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Tone!</b> 🗣️ An article should feel like you are talking to the reader. Instead of just listing facts, try to ask the reader a question, like 'Have you ever read a manga?'</li><li><b>Be more descriptive!</b> 🎨 When you describe the festival in Japan, tell us one thing they did there to make the story come alive!</li>	The text is connected and has a clear beginning, middle, and end. 🌊 You used linking words like 'Firstly', 'Secondly', and 'For example' to organize your thoughts.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Logical Flow!</b> 🔄 You used 'Finally' to describe the book's relationship, but then you continued with 'For example' and a new point about social media. 'Finally' should usually introduce your very last point or a conclusion.</li><li><b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 Try to start a new paragraph when you switch from talking about 'why reading is good' to 'the story of the manga'.</li>	You used good vocabulary like 'relationship', 'information', and 'social media'. 👏 However, there are several grammar mistakes that make it a bit difficult to read at times.<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you:<br><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'I am think it interesting' should be '<b>I think it is interesting</b>'.</li><li><b>Negatives!</b> 🚫 'make your brain don't have to' should be '<b>makes your brain not have to</b>' or '<b>means your brain doesn't have to</b>'.</li><li><b>Possessives!</b> 🧑‍🤝‍🧑 'Sakura and his boyfriend' -> If Sakura is a girl, it should be '<b>her</b> boyfriend'.</li><li><b>Articles and Be-verbs!</b> 🔍 'The manga a romantic story is called' -> '<b>The manga, which is a romantic story, is called...</b>'</li><li><b>Infinitives!</b> 🏃 'time to playing' should be '<b>time to play</b>'.</li><li><b>Social Media Comparison!</b> 📱 'Read more book is make your free more than to allway on social media' -> '<b>Reading books makes you feel more free than always being on social media.</b>'</li>	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
3287	34926	2026-02-05 12:28:23.602792+00	Magazine Article	My favourite commic, a classic, fantasy game as a comic, is 'Minecraft Comic'.<br>'In my view; I think the Minecraft comic isn't good to read a lot. Firstly, if you have read the Minecraft comic once, you'll know the story and it won't be exciting if you read it again. Secondly, Minecraft comic, is an online comic that means you have to pay money to read it and it's an one time read comic. For example, Frame, a friend of mine bought the minecraft comic and he loves it. So, he bought it again, but this time he finds it a bit boring because he already know what's going to happen.	111	14.0	Hello Chopin, 👋<br><br>It was very interesting to read about your passion for the Minecraft Comic! 📖 You did a great job explaining why you enjoy it and providing a real-life example of your friend, Frame, to support your points. Your article feels very honest and personal, which is perfect for this type of task. 🌟<br><br>I have a few tips to help you move to the next level. 🛠️<br>1. <b>Address the General Question!</b> 🎯 While you explained why reading one specific comic many times isn't great, the prompt also wanted to know if you think reading in general is a good habit.<br>2. <b>Punctuation Power!</b> ✍️ Be careful with semicolons and extra commas, as they can break the flow of your sentences.<br>3. <b>Spelling and Grammar!</b> 📝 Watch out for the spelling of 'comic' and making sure your verbs match your subjects (he knows vs. he know).	You answered both parts of the question! 📋 You clearly identified your favorite reading material and gave reasons for your opinion.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Think Big!</b> 🌍 When the prompt asks 'Do you think it's good to read a lot?', it's usually asking about the habit of reading many different books or stories. You focused on reading the *same* comic repeatedly. Try to add a sentence about whether reading many different things is beneficial for your brain or vocabulary!</li>	You communicated your ideas clearly and held my interest with the story about your friend! 🤩 Using a personal anecdote is a great technique for an article.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Article Style!</b> 📰 Articles usually have a catchy title and an engaging introduction. You started right away with your favorite book. Try starting with a question like: 'Do you love gaming and reading? Then I have the perfect story for you!'</li><li><b>Tone Consistency!</b> 💬 Your tone is friendly, which is perfect. Just be careful with phrases like 'In my view; I think' which is a bit repetitive. You can just say 'In my view,' or 'I think...'.</li>	Your article is well-structured with clear linking words like 'Firstly' and 'Secondly'. 🌊 This makes it very easy to follow your argument.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Punctuation Flow!</b> 🛑 Avoid using a semicolon after 'In my view'. A comma is much better: 'In my view, I think...'. Also, check the comma in 'Minecraft comic, is an online comic'. We don't need a comma between the subject and the verb!</li><li><b>Sentence Variety!</b> 🔗 Try to combine some of your shorter sentences. Instead of 'So, he bought it again, but this time...', you could try 'However, when he bought it again, he found it less exciting.'</li>	You used some great descriptive words like 'classic' and 'fantasy'! 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you polish your English:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> ✏️ 'Commic' should be spelled '<b>comic</b>'. You spelled it correctly later, so just be careful with consistency!</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'An one time read' -> '<b>A</b> one-time read'. We use 'a' because 'one' starts with a 'w' sound.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'He already know' -> 'He already <b>knows</b>'. Remember the 's' for he/she/it in the present tense!</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 💡 Instead of 'fantasy game as a comic', you could say 'a <b>comic version</b> of a fantasy game' or 'a comic <b>based on</b> a fantasy game'.</li>	4.0	4.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA