d you included some lovely personal details! To make your writing even more impactful, focus on breaking your long paragraphs into smaller, more focused ones. Also, work on refining your sentence structure and ensuring consistent grammatical accuracy.	Grace, you have successfully identified Tokyo as your favourite place and provided a good amount of relevant information about it, including its landscape, diverse population, famous food (especially Ramen), and the beauty of cherry blossoms (Sakura). You also share a personal experience related to Ramen and a picnic under Sakura trees. However, the essay's significant length (359 words compared to the expected 140-190 words) indicates some minor irrelevances or a lack of conciseness in developing points. For instance, some details could be condensed without losing impact. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to present all content concisely and fully inform the target reader within the appropriate word count, ensuring every detail serves a clear purpose.	You use the conventions of an essay by having an introduction, body, and conclusion. You attempt to engage the reader and communicate your ideas about why Tokyo is special, for example, by directly recommending the city and the cherry blossoms. The tone is enthusiastic and personal. However, the communication of ideas, particularly more complex ones, is sometimes hampered by the lengthy sentences and occasional grammatical inaccuracies, which can make the text slightly difficult to process and reduce its overall effectiveness in consistently holding the target reader's attention. To improve to a 5, you would need to communicate ideas with greater precision and fluency, using a wider range of communicative strategies to engage the reader more consistently and effectively.	The essay has a clear introduction and conclusion. However, the organisation within the main body is limited. The second paragraph is extremely long and attempts to cover too many distinct ideas (l