stion about sharing the price could be phrased more directly to avoid any ambiguity. Also, aim for a consistent friendly tone throughout, without any unexpected phrases like 'If you arrived lol' at the end. Sometimes, learners try to be too informal or use phrases they've seen online, which can sometimes reduce clarity.	Your email is generally well organised into paragraphs, which makes it easier to read and understand. This is a very good habit to have. 👍 You've also used some basic linking words, like 'And what about' and 'For the main activities,' to connect your thoughts. To aim for a higher score, try to use a wider range of linking words and phrases to show the connections between your ideas even more clearly. For instance, when you move from talking about the meeting time to the activities, you could use a phrase like 'Moving on to the activities...' or 'Regarding the main activities...'. This helps your ideas flow more naturally. Thai learners often prefer shorter sentences and direct statements, so expanding on linking phrases can be a helpful step.	You've used everyday vocabulary appropriately, Tata, and your simple sentences are generally correct. This means your message is easy to understand. ✅ However, there are some noticeable errors that, while they don't stop the reader from understanding, do prevent a higher score. For example, you wrote 'Should we met at the enterance' instead of 'Should we meet at the entrance.' Also, 'the enterance open' should be 'the entrance opens.' Pay close attention to verb tenses and common spelling mistakes. Focusing on these specific areas will make your writing much more accurate.	4.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
