<br>Action Plan for Improvement<br>• ✅ Practice writing complete sentences and connecting them smoothly with appropriate linking words.<br>• ✅ Pay close attention to spelling and common grammatical patterns, especially verb forms and plural nouns.<br>• ✅ When writing a formal essay, try to avoid very casual language and focus on presenting your ideas in a clear, structured way.	Rico, it is great that you have included all the points from the task, including your own idea about gaming. You have made an effort to give examples, like the "Water elephant pajama" in fashion, which helps to illustrate your points. 👍 To improve, try to make sure each paragraph clearly links back to the main question about who has more effect, friends or parents. For instance, in your section on studying, while you mention parents influence, think about how you can explicitly argue whether this influence is *more* or *less* than friends. Remember, an essay usually requires you to argue a point directly, not just describe a situation.	You have communicated your ideas in a straightforward way, Rico, which is a good start. 😊 However, for a formal essay like this, it is important to use language that is suitable for an academic audience. Starting with "Hello teacher, its me Rico" is very friendly, but it is not what we expect in an essay response. Try to imagine you are writing for someone you do not know personally, and aim for a more objective and formal tone. For example, instead of "its me Rico," you could begin with a general statement about the topic. Focusing on a consistent formal register throughout will help you achieve a higher score in this area.	Your essay has a basic structure with an introduction and separate paragraphs for each point, which is helpful for the reader to follow your ideas. You have used simple linking words like "Firt," "Move on to studies," and "Lastly." That is a good start. To make your essay even better, try to use a wider range of linking words and phrases to connect your ideas more smoothly. 🤔 For example, instead of just "Firt," you could say "Firstly, regarding fashion and clothes..." Also, make sure each paragraph has a clear topic sentence that tells the reader what that paragraph will be about, making the flow between your ideas much clearer. Thai learners sometimes use very direct transitions, but in English, we often use more varied phrases to guide the reader.	Rico, you have used everyday words to express your thoughts, which is important for getting your message across. However, there are quite a few noticeable errors in spelling, grammar, and sentence structure that sometimes make it a little difficult to understand your exact meaning. For instance, words like "unsterstan," "chouse," "becaus," "on tren," "studiet," and "relation chip" need careful attention. ✍️ Also, there are some issues with subject-verb agreement and plural forms, such as "teenagers usually wear a on tren clothes" instead of "teenagers usually wear trendy clothes." To improve, focus on basic sentence construction and common spelling patterns. Thai learners sometimes struggle with plural 's' and specific verb endings because these concepts are different in their native language. Practising these regularly will truly help your writing become much more accurate and clear.	3.0	2.0	2.0	1.0	writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
