1111	28984	2025-08-27 09:27:24.78052+00	Free time Activities	1 Free time is a time that we can do thing How we wanted. Besides Free time can waste our brain it also know as brainwashing. Some time brain washing also affect people. Free time have mostly in Thailand. You can find tiktok Thailand is the 2th people who which mostly show that in their free time is playing phone it getting more waste time I have suggest for you.<br><br><br>2 First is drawing drawing is a very excellent Free time people should spend more Well some of them do Which is great In my option you could say it called option writer option well my option was drawing is a free time is a free time using brain	88	4.0	Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 88 words and achieved NOT AWARDED. You've started to explore the topic of free time, which is a good first step!	You mentioned free time and drawing, but the essay felt unfinished and didn't fully explain what the activities were or why you chose them. To fully inform your reader, try to elaborate on your ideas more.<br>👉 <b>To reach a 5/5:</b> Make sure to answer all parts of the question, providing clear explanations and specific examples for each activity you choose.<br><br>	Your essay was difficult to understand at times, and the use of numbered paragraphs (like "1 Free time..." and "2 First is drawing...") is not typical for a formal essay. In formal written English, we usually use clear paragraph breaks without numbers to make our ideas flow smoothly.<br><br>	Your essay needs a clearer structure. It was hard to find a main idea (thesis) in the introduction, and the paragraphs didn't always start with clear topic sentences. A well-organized essay guides the reader through your ideas step-by-step.<br><br>	You used some good vocabulary related to free time, which is a great start! The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules, especially those common for Thai speakers learning English.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Free time is a time that we can do thing How we wanted."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time is a time when we can do things as we want."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, we use "when" for time, and "things" needs to be plural. Also, "how we wanted" is a direct translation from Thai; a more natural English phrasing is "as we want" or "as we like."<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Besides Free time can waste our brain it also know as brainwashing."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Besides, free time can *also* be known as 'brainwashing' because it can make our brains feel wasted."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This sentence had several issues. "Besides" needs a comma after it when used as a transition. "It also know as" is a common Thai-to-English interference where the verb "to be" is often omitted, and the past participle is needed for passive voice ("is known as"). Also, "waste our brain" isn't a natural English phrase in this context; rephrasing helps clarify the meaning.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Some time brain washing also affect people."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Sometimes brainwashing also affects people."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> "Sometimes" (one word, plural 's') means "on some occasions." "Brainwashing" is usually one word. "Affects" needs an '-s' for third-person singular present tense, which is a common error for Thai speakers.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "You can find tiktok Thailand is the 2th people who which mostly show that in their free time is playing phone it getting more waste time I have suggest for you."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "You can find that TikTok users in Thailand are the second highest in the world, which mostly shows that people spend their free time playing on their phones. This is becoming a waste of time, so I have a suggestion for you."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This sentence has many issues with clarity and structure. "2th" should be "second." "Who which" is an incorrect use of relative clauses. "Playing phone" should be "playing on their phones." "I have suggest" should be "I have a suggestion" or "I suggest," as "suggest" is a verb. Thai speakers often omit articles and prepositions, leading to phrases like "playing phone."<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Practice writing full paragraphs for an essay, making sure each paragraph has a clear topic sentence and is not numbered.<br>2. Focus on using correct plural forms (e.g., "things," "times") and subject-verb agreement (e.g., "it affects").<br>3. Practice using the verb "to be" correctly in passive voice constructions (e.g., "is known as").<br>4. Work on forming clear and correct complex sentences, paying attention to relative clauses (who/which/that) and transitions.<br><br>	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
2035	33952	2025-09-22 11:07:49.391548+00	Term 1 Exam Question 2	People have own pet better than don't have pet, that was main message of almost people agree with it because sometime when you feel tried for done something and you want the thing that can help you be better and have encourage to do next. Actually, the one thing that was intriguing, it was the same characteristic and stlye. In my perspective about 3 things that adventage were 1. encourage, 2. fun and 3. memory that were a good idea.<br><br><br>The first adventage for have own pet was encourage which can help you more relax from the hard or serious situation. One thing that mostly of people want was the encourage when you feel sad or tire for something. Although you have friend but they don't understand you in sometime then our friend will laugh on you or bully it. On opposite side the pet was the one choice that didn't answer or ask when you have worse situation but you can hug and tell with our pet by you know it will not answer you question.<br><br><br>In addition was a fun that was a simple thing that you can find it easy but it have a special one from pet. Sometime on your freetime, you will find research something that help you to fun with it but it lost your time for the game that you like it. All of teenager agree with it because you alway want a lot of time. Have own pet you can get fun by call the name and you can hug, play and talk with it but the special one was it have a lot of emotion and stlye when you do something.<br><br><br>The last one of three ideas was memory. Memory is essential when you go or do in somewhere, you will take a picture on app. Also when you adopt your pet when it was a little baby then grow be adult that was intriguing because you can see about time and grow up in per month. When you want to find something that help you more relax you can open and see it together with own pet.<br><br><br>To summerize, the three ideas were encourage, fun and memory. That a choice for choose have own pet more than don't have it. It have a lot of advantage but this can conclude that wasn't a disadvantage for have own pet. Finally thing I will you was when you care our pet, the pet will care our back. However that was truth thing for people that have own pet.	422	7.0	Hi Ken! 👋 It’s wonderful to see your enthusiasm for writing about pets and sharing your opinions in an article. You've clearly put effort into thinking about the positive aspects of having animal companions! To make your writing even clearer and more complete, focusing on including all parts of the task and practicing your grammar will be a big step forward. Keep up the great work, and remember that every piece of writing is a chance to learn and improve! 😊<br>\r\n📋 Action Plan for Ken:<br>\r\n☑️ Carefully read the whole exam question and underline every single thing you need to include in your answer before you start writing. For instance, if it asks for advantages and disadvantages, make sure you write about both!<br>\r\n☑️ After writing, read your work aloud to yourself. This helps you catch sentences that sound a little awkward or confusing, and you might spot missing words or grammar mistakes.<br>\r\n☑️ Focus on practicing subject-verb agreement (e.g., "People have" should be "People having" or "People do have") and making sure your sentences flow smoothly. Reading more English articles can help you see how these ideas are connected naturally.	Ken, you did a great job brainstorming and giving us three excellent advantages of having pets – encouragement, fun, and memory! 👍 It’s clear you thought about why pets are special. However, a key part of the task was to also discuss the *disadvantages* of owning pets. Imagine you're writing a guide for someone who's never had a pet before; they'd want to know the tricky parts too, wouldn't they? 🤔 Next time, after you brainstorm the good points, take a moment to think about the challenges as well. For example, you could add a paragraph starting with something like, 'Of course, having a pet isn't always easy, as they need lots of time and money,' and then explain those points. This way, your reader gets a complete picture, and you'll fully meet the task requirements. You also wrote quite a lot, which is fantastic that you have so many ideas, but for exam purposes, try to keep your articles within the suggested word count of 140-190 words to show you can be concise.	You’ve made a good start at writing an article for teenagers, expressing your personal connection and opinions about pets. The most important thing for an article is to keep your reader interested and make sure they understand your main points easily. While your opinion about pets comes through, some of your sentences are a bit long or unclear, which can make it hard for your teenage audience to follow. To make your articles even more engaging, try to use shorter, clearer sentences when you introduce new ideas. For instance, instead of a long sentence, you could break it into two: 'Having pets is a wonderful thing. My dog, Noah, is a good boy.' Also, think about using a friendly, direct style. You could ask a question like, 'Have you ever thought about getting a pet?' to draw your reader in! 🤩	You’ve organised your article into paragraphs, which is a really good start, Ken! Each of your main ideas – encouragement, fun, and memory – gets its own space, and that helps the reader see your structure. To make your writing flow even better, try to use more varied linking words and phrases to connect your ideas smoothly. For example, instead of always starting a new paragraph directly, you could say 'Firstly, one great advantage is...' or 'Another enjoyable aspect is...' or 'Finally, creating lasting memories is truly special.' ✨ Also, make sure that the ideas within each paragraph stick closely to just one topic. This will make your argument much clearer and easier for your readers to follow, helping them move from one point to the next effortlessly.	Ken, you use everyday words to talk about your feelings and experiences with pets, and it’s clear you have many ideas to share! However, to make your writing stronger, we need to focus on accuracy in grammar. I noticed a few areas where we can improve. For example, a common area for improvement is using the correct prepositions and articles (a/an/the). For instance, 'care our pet' should be 'care **for your** pet,' and 'main message of almost people' would be clearer as 'the main message that almost **all** people agree with.' Lastly, watch out for spelling mistakes like 'adventage' (should be **advantage**) and 'stlye' (should be **style**). Sometimes, in Thai, subject-verb agreement is less strict than in English, and articles might not be used in the same way, which can lead to these kinds of errors. Reading your work aloud, as suggested in your action plan, can really help you catch these small but important mistakes! Keep practising, and you'll see a big difference. 🚀	2.0	1.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
