iew, but due to its incompleteness, it was unable to fully communicate its purpose to the reader.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Ensure your writing effectively holds the reader's attention by developing all your points and maintaining a clear purpose throughout the entire essay.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "beside play game, doing a exercise"<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Besides playing games, engaging in regular exercise is another free-time activity that greatly benefits teenagers, offering a different kind of relaxation and positive impact."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Developing your ideas with full sentences and clear explanations helps the reader follow your argument and fully understand your message, rather than leaving them with an unfinished thought.	You attempted to use paragraphs to structure your ideas. However, the essay is incomplete, preventing a clear overall organisation.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Plan your essay to ensure it has a clear introduction with a thesis statement, well-developed body paragraphs with topic sentences, and a concluding paragraph that summarises your main points.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your essay was not completed, so it did not have the required four paragraphs, including a proper introduction, two body paragraphs, and a conclusion.<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In conclusion, free time activities like online gaming and exercise provide essential balance to a busy student's life, offering both mental and physical benefits."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A well-structured conclusion brings your essay to a satisfying close, reinforcing your main ideas and leaving a lasting impression on the reader, which is crucial for overall coherence.	You used some everyday vocabulary and simple sentences effectively. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "In Thailand, we're don't have much free time."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "In Thailand, we don't have much free time."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, we usually use only one auxiliary verb for negation. Thai doesn't have such contractions or complex auxiliary structures, so it's important to use either 'we are not' or 'we do not' but not combine them.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Absolutley all teenager will full of energy if they have some free time."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Absolutely all teenagers will be full of energy if they have some free time."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, when you refer to 'all' or 'many' of something, the noun that follows needs to be plural (e.g., 'teenagers', 'students', 'books'). Thai does not typically add a plural ending like '-s' to nouns, which can lead to this error.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "doing a exercise"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "doing an exercise"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, we use 'an' before words that start with a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u) and 'a' before words that starts with a consonant sound. Thai does not have articles like 'a' or 'an', so choosing the correct one can be tricky.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Complete the next essay task fully, ensuring you address all parts of the prompt.<br>2. Practice using plural '-s' endings correctly on nouns, especially after words like 'all', 'many', and numbers.<br>3. Review the rules for using 'a' and 'an' with different words and practice identifying vowel sounds.<br><br>	1.0	1.0	1.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	a2e775c4-e795-45e6-b042-7e908b05f577	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
2038	28849	2025-09-22 11:31:25.843513+00	Term 1 Exam Question 2	Having pet, every body all over the world know that having pet are great. Although some migth disagree. In my opinions I think having pets are really great thing but also have pet has their evry own flor to which I'm going to explain to you moreover in this article.<br><br><br>Talk about Advantage of having pets first. They lot's of amazing thing you get for being pet ownner. Firstly you will never be lonely sicen your buddy will cover that for you helping your emotion to stay passitive is a second reason why having pet is good, and lastly. They will never ever going to leave you behide if you already make a great relationship with your pet high precent that they will not your pet will just stay beside you.<br><br><br>But we may know that every advantage come with disadvantage to, now the first for flor is you have to be reponsible of takeing care the pets you brougth, the is the major thing you need to having pet. when you have a little buddy you need to be more reponsible becaus you have to take care of another living thing. except You have to let them wake out, hospital check mountly, pay all the meal and that lend to another major reason is price. Price are a big disadvantage same as reponsible because you have to give a hold money section all to your pet as I said a hospital check and meal are all includ money in the procuze to. That to two major disadvantage you get.<br><br><br>I conclusion, is having pet good or bad. I do think it still a good thing to have but you do needs to have more reponsible and make sure you can offer those thing if you have all that. Congrat you will make some memory with them lot's too.<br><br><br>:)	306	9.0	Krewkehw, it's fantastic to see your effort in tackling this article about pets. You clearly have some great ideas about the joys and challenges of having animal companions, and that's a brilliant foundation to build upon! To make your writing even more impactful, we're going to focus on making your points super clear and easy for your readers to follow, especially when it comes to expressing those ideas accurately. Keep up your positive attitude, and you'll see excellent progress! <br><br>📋 Action Plan for Improvement:<br>✅ Proofread Carefully: After writing, always read through your work slowly to catch any spelling or grammar mistakes. Try reading it aloud – sometimes that helps you spot errors!<br>✅ Expand Vocabulary: Look for new words to describe things so you don't use the same words too often. A thesaurus can be a fun tool to discover synonyms!<br>✅ Sentence Structure Practice: Work on building clear, complete sentences with correct subject-verb agreement and punctuation. This makes your ideas much easier to understand.	Krewkehw, you've done a really good job of addressing the main points of the task by discussing both the wonderful advantages and the important disadvantages of owning pets. You mentioned things like companionship and emotional support, which are excellent points! 😊 To reach a score of 5, you could try to develop each point with a bit more detail. For instance, when you talk about pets helping emotions, you could add something like, 'For example, when I feel sad, my pet always cheers me up by cuddling with me.' Also, while it's great to have a lot to say, try to stick closer to the word count (140-190 words). This helps you practice being concise and clear in your writing.	You've made a good attempt to structure your writing as an article for teenagers, and it's clear you want to share your opinions. That's a strong start! However, to really grab and hold your reader's attention and communicate your ideas clearly, focus on refining your sentence structure and word choice. For example, instead of beginning a section with 'Talk about Advantage of having pets first,' you could try a more engaging title or opening sentence like, 'Let's explore the wonderful things about having pets!' or 'One of the biggest pluses of pet ownership is...' This makes your article more inviting and professional. Ensuring your language is clear and appropriate for your audience will help them connect with your message much more effectively.	You've clearly thought about how to organise your article, Krewkehw, with an introduction, sections for advantages and disadvantages, and a conclusion. This logical flow helps your reader follow your arguments. 👍 To make your writing even smoother and more engaging, think about using a wider variety of linking words and phrases. For example, instead of just repeating "and lastly" or "but," you could use phrases like "In addition," "Furthermore," "On the other hand," or "Despite these benefits." This helps connect your ideas more subtly and makes your writing feel more sophisticated. Practising starting new paragraphs when you introduce a completely new idea will also help your article look more organised and professional.	Your enthusiasm for the topic comes through in your writing, Krewkehw, and you use some everyday vocabulary well! However, there are quite a few grammatical and spelling errors that sometimes make it difficult for your reader to fully understand your message. Let's look at three key areas for improvement. First, spelling is very important. Words like "migth" (should be "might"), "opinions" (should be "opinion" or "opinions"), "evry" (should be "every"), "flor" (should be "flaw"), "ownner" (should be "owner"), "sicen" (should be "since"), "passitive" (should be "positive"), "reponsible" (should be "responsible"), "takeing" (should be "taking"), "brougth" (should be "brought"), "mountly" (should be "monthly"), "includ" (should be "include"), and "procuze" (should be "process") appear throughout your text. Regularly checking a dictionary or using a spell checker can really help with this! 📝<br><br>Second, subject-verb agreement and pluralisation need attention. For instance, you wrote "having pet are great" which should be "having pets *is* great" or "having *a* pet *is* great." Similarly, "every body" should be "everybody," and "lot's of amazing thing" should be "lots of amazing *things*." Thai learners sometimes make these kinds of mistakes because the concept of pluralisation and strict subject-verb agreement can be different in Thai. For example, in Thai, a single word can often refer to both singular and plural, and verbs don't change based on the subject in the same way English verbs do. Practising sentences where you focus on matching your verb to your subject will make a big difference! 🧠<br><br>Finally, sentence structure and word choice could be clearer. Phrases like "Talk about Advantage of having pets first" or "you have to give a hold money section all to your pet" are a bit awkward. Try to express your ideas in more direct and natural English sentences. For example, "First, let's discuss the advantages of having pets" or "You have to dedicate a significant portion of your money to your pet." Focusing on forming complete and grammatically correct sentences will make your writing much clearer and more pleasant to read. Keep practising these areas, and your language will become much stronger! 💪	3.0	2.0	3.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
