ds like "firstly," "in addition," or "on the other hand" makes your writing much more coherent. 🔗	Your enthusiasm for the topic comes through, but there are quite a few areas in your grammar and vocabulary that need some attention to make your meaning clearer. For example, you often struggled with making sure your verbs agree with your subjects, like in "Having a pets is" (it should be "Having pets **is**" or "A pet **is**") and "Every pets always have" (it should be "Every pet always **has**"). Also, possessive pronouns like "ours" and "they" were sometimes used incorrectly; for instance, it should be "our friends" and "their dark side," not "ours friends" or "they darkside." Finally, articles (a, an, the) were sometimes missing or incorrect, like "Having a pets" instead of "Having pets" or "a tiger" instead of "tigers" when talking generally. These types of errors, which are common for Thai learners, can make your sentences difficult to understand. Practising these basics will make a big difference in how clearly you express your great ideas! Keep a special notebook for common errors you make and review it often. 📝	3.0	2.0	2.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
