ngs, but making sure these final sounds are always gently pronounced will make your English sound even sharper. Many Thai speakers find these final consonant sounds a bit tricky because Thai doesn't always have strong final consonants in the same way English does. Practising words ending with /d/ and /t/ and trying to blend sounds together a little more will help you speak with even greater clarity! 🎤👂	Atom, you delivered a truly excellent speaking performance in this assessment, showing a strong command of English and communicating your ideas with impressive clarity! Your fluency, organised thoughts, and ability to engage meaningfully in conversations are very good. While your English is already very strong, a little bit of fine-tuning on connecting sounds and making sure those final consonant sounds are always heard will make your speech even smoother and more precise. Keep up the good effort, and your communication skills will continue to develop beautifully! ✨<br><br>📋 **Action Plan for Improvement:**<br>*   Practice smoothly linking words together to make your speech flow even more naturally.<br>*   Work on clearly pronouncing the final /d/ and /t/ sounds in words, even when speaking quickly.<br>*   Listen carefully to native speakers to notice how they connect words and pronounce endings.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1K3bBubutwVYJcfAmMJzMTPdgebO7hnlN?usp=drive_link	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
