2364	34931	2025-11-26 21:53:49.901149+00	Creative Writing	Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it. Sam, who was a nerdy inventor, and also a science teacher. He's not kind a bad person, he just weird and quite random. Whatever he thinks about, he would do it right after he returned home. He loves to invent random things in his garage. And he didn't really care about safety.<br><br><br>One day a little later night. He watched a sci-fi movie, and has been thinking about the teleporter in the movie. Suddenly, Sam has created a teleporter that can travel to everywhere he wants. At first, Sam thought his invention was a brilliant idea. He tested it with a rock. Then, he turned on the machine, and after that the rock has disappeared in front of him.<br><br><br>The machine seem working perfectly. However, he was not happy. He felt dissapointed, because his invention had a huge problem. So, he tried to fixed it. After a while, he thought that his invention was tired so, he tested again. But then, his invention exploded.<br><br><br>Lucky, Sam hadn't cause any damage at all. Consequently, he found out that he was teleported to somewhere. And, he also found out that he has teleported in the past. In the end, Sam was stucked in the past forever and can't find a way back home. He has learned that he had better care about safety that anything.	231	16.0	Hello Frame, 👋<br><br>This is a fantastic sci-fi story! I loved the twist where Sam accidentally creates a teleporter instead of a time machine—and then ends up stuck in the past! The way you described his disappointment before the machine exploded was very funny.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing. 📋<br>1. <b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ Watch out for verbs after 'to'. 'To fixed' should be 'to <b>fix</b>'.<br>2. <b>Past Participles!</b> 🔙 'Stucked' is not a word. It should be 'stuck'.<br>3. <b>Adjectives!</b> 🎨 You said he is 'weird'. Show us *how* he is weird! Does he wear goggles to bed?	You answered the question perfectly! 🌟 The story is imaginative and fits the prompt.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Ending!</b> 🎞️ The ending is a great cliffhanger! You could add one sentence about what the past looked like.<br>2. <b>Safety!</b> ⚠️ You mentioned he didn't care about safety. You could show this by saying he wasn't wearing gloves!	Your story was very exciting to read! 🤩 The pacing was great.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Repetition!</b> 🔄 You used 'Sam' and 'machine' a lot. Try 'the inventor' or 'the device'.<br>2. <b>Feelings!</b> 🎭 Describe his fear when it exploded. Did he jump back? Did he scream?	Your story flows well because you used linking words like 'Suddenly' and 'Consequently'. 🌊<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 📑 Your paragraphs are good, but you could start a new one for the 'explosion' scene.<br>2. <b>Flow!</b> 🔗 'One day a little later night' feels awkward. Try 'Late one night...'.	You used great words like 'teleporter' and 'dissapointed'! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Dissapointed' -> 'disappointed'. 'Stucked' -> 'stuck'.<br>2. <b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Machine seem working' -> 'Machine seemed *to be* working'.<br>3. <b>Past Perfect!</b> ⏳ 'Has created' -> 'had created'.<br>4. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Care about safety that anything' -> 'care about safety *more than* anything'.<br>5. <b>Auxiliary!</b> 🆘 'Hadn't cause' -> 'hadn't *caused*'.	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
