ets! 👍 For example, you mentioned how pets can help with stress and mental health, which is a really important advantage. You also thought about the downsides, like when pets misbehave, which shows you're thinking carefully about the topic. To get an even higher score, remember to give specific examples for *each* point you make. Instead of just saying pets 'ruin couch, sofa eat,' you could write, 'for example, some dogs might chew on furniture, or cats might scratch the sofa, which can be expensive to repair.' Adding these small details helps your reader understand your points much better and makes your article more convincing!	You've made an effort to write an article that shares your opinions, which is exactly what the task asked for! However, sometimes the way your ideas are presented makes it a little difficult for the reader to fully grasp your message, which is really important for an article in an international magazine for teenagers. For example, your opening sentence 'Pets & cat, dogs, hamster is a conom pets' could be clearer and more engaging to grab the reader's attention right away. Think about using a strong opening statement or a question to draw your audience in, like 'Have you ever wondered why we love our pets so much?' 🤔 To improve here, try to use more varied sentence structures and make sure your main point in each section is really easy for your reader to follow from start to finish.	You have a good structure for your article, Platwo, as you move from introducing pets to discussing their benefits and then some challenges. You also use some linking words like 'But I would say' to transition between ideas, which is a great start! To make your writing even more organised and flow smoothly, try to use clear paragraph breaks for each new main idea. For example, you could have one paragraph introducing pets and your general opinion, another dedicated to all the advantages, and a third for the disadvantages. 📝 This way, your reader can easily follow the journey of your thoughts without getting lost. Using more varied linking words such as 'Firstly,' 'In addition,' 'On the other hand,' or 'To conclude' can also really help your ideas connect together beautifully!	Platwo, you're using everyday words to talk about a topic you care about, which is fantastic! However, there are quite a few grammatical errors and choices of words that make your sentences hard to understand sometimes. This means your reader has to work a bit harder to get your message, and it might even impede the meaning occasionally. For example:<br><br>1. Your sentence 'Pets & cat, dogs, hamster **is** a **conom** pets' has a few things we can fix. 'Is' should be 'are' because you're talking about more than one type of animal (cats, dogs, hamsters). Also, 'conom' should be 'common.' So, it should be: 'Cats, dogs, and hamsters **are common** pets.' Remember, for many nouns, we add an 's' to make them plural, like 'pet' becomes 'pets.'<br>2. Another example is 'Pet might be bad when **their** are having animal **spirt** for example dog ruining couch, sofa eat.' Here, 'their' should be 'they' because you're talking about the animals themselves. 'Spirt' should be 'spirit' or, more likely, 'instinct' or 'temperament' in this context. And 'sofa eat' should be 'eating things.' A clearer sentence would be: 'Pets might be challenging when **they** are acting on their animal **instincts**, for example, a dog **ruining** the couch or **eating** the sofa.'<br>3. Also, the sentence 'Nowa days people having less pets' is missing a verb. It should be 'Nowadays, people **are having** fewer pets.' Keep an eye out for these small words like 'are' and 'is' and make sure they match the number of nouns you're talking about!<br><br>Many Thai learners sometimes find articles (`a`, `an`, `the`) and plural forms tricky because these concepts work differently or don't exist in the same way in Thai. Practising these small grammatical points will make a big difference in how clearly you communicate your ideas! Keep a list of these common errors and try to check for them when you review your writing. You're making progress, and focusing on these areas will really help your English get stronger. 💪	3.0	2.0	3.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
590	28836	2025-07-11 03:35:03.959777+00	My Special Place	The town that I like the most is Kanjanaburi, which is one of the 71 town in Thailand. It's located on the left side of Thailand. On the left side of Kanjanaburi is connected to Myanrmar. Do you want to know why it's my favourite? Because Kanjanaburi has a fablous nature. It's nature is so beutiful that no words can explain. It's precious, beutiful, fablous. So beutiful I can't explain. If you haven't been there. I suggest you should go visit it once in your life. But that doesn't mean nature is the only thing about it. Dam, a place that hold about millions liters of water. Kanjanaburi have it too. The dam I'm talking about is Kuan Bhumiphor, one of the most famous dam in Thailand. If you don't know what to there let me give you some advice. You can go see the dam or you can go to see nature example like the mountain, the waterfall, and much more.	151	9.0	Hello Namo, this is a nice description of Kanchanaburi as your special place, highlighting its nature and the dam. To improve, focus on adding more personal details about your connection to this place. Explain *why* the nature is fabulous to you, and what specific experiences you've had there. Also, make sure you write at least 190 words in your essay.	Namo, your response is relevant to the topic "My Special Place," as you identify Kanchanaburi as a place you like. However, the reader is not fully informed about *why* this place is special to *you*. You mention the nature and the dam, but you don't provide personal experiences or feelings. To reach a score of 5, you would need to explain in detail *why* the nature is so beautiful to you, what specific aspects of the dam you find interesting, and how these experiences contribute to your connection with Kanchanaburi. For example, you could describe a specific hike you took, a particular waterfall you saw, or how you felt when you visited the dam.	You use the conventions of writing to communicate your ideas, Namo. The tone is enthusiastic and inviting, and you attempt to engage the reader with questions like "Do you want to know why it's my favourite?" However, the repetitive use of "beautiful" and "fabulous," and some grammatical errors, weaken the overall impact. To improve, focus on using a wider range of descriptive language, adding more personal details, and ensuring that your grammar is accurate.	Namo, your text is not very well-organised. The introduction is a bit abrupt, and the transition between the nature and the dam feels somewhat disjointed. The ending is also a bit weak. To improve, you should aim to organise your ideas into clear paragraphs, with each paragraph focusing on a specific aspect of your experience. Use linking words (like "because," "and," "but," "so") to connect your ideas and create a smooth flow. You also need to ensure that your text has a clear beginning, middle, and end.	Namo, your vocabulary is limited, and there are noticeable errors in grammar and spelling. For example, you've misspelled "Kanchanaburi" as "Kanjanaburi" multiple times, "fabulous" as "fablous," "beautiful" as "beutiful," and "Myanmar" as "Myanrmar." You also have issues with verb tense and word choice, such as "town" instead of "province," "Dam, a place that hold about millions liters of water," and "If you don't know what to there." These errors impede communication. To improve, you need to focus on correcting basic grammar and spelling errors, use a wider range of vocabulary, and practice constructing complete and grammatically correct sentences.	3.0	3.0	2.0	1.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
1127	31545	2025-08-28 13:38:20.57215+00	Free time Activities	Free time is benefit for teenages. Each country has many activities to do, Thailand has different activities. Games and Art work done by teenages in Thailand<br><br><br>First of free time activities is play games. Thier are many game that teenages usally play, but the most famouse is Roblox. Roblox is a platform to play many games. You can design your outfit in this game. Thier many unige games. for example, Brook Haven which is a role play game, 99 night in the forest which is a surviver game. It become famous by many YouTuber play this game.<br><br><br>As well as play game is art work. Art work is the best to relax and spend time with yourself. You can do many art work, but the simple art work is Doodle Art. Doodle Art is the easy one to do. You can draw anything that you want. It become famouse by many artist to Doodle Art and sold it which many money.<br><br><br>In conclusion famouse activities in Thailand are play game and do art work. All of this are made teenages be calm and relax. It help teenages to communicate each other and have time with yourself. In my opinnion, these activities are important for teenages if they use it in correct way.	212	11.0	<b>📝 Dear Mew</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 212 words and achieved B1+. You clearly chose two free-time activities and explained why you like them — that is a good start: you give specific examples (Roblox and Doodle Art) which make your ideas clear.<br><br>	You identified the two required activities (playing games — Roblox — and doing Doodle Art) and gave basic reasons why you like them (relaxation, creativity, socialising, and selling artwork). To improve, develop one clear specific example in each body paragraph (for example, one short detail of how Roblox helps you connect with friends, and one sentence describing a Doodle Art project you made or saw).<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Add one short, specific example or a short reason in each body paragraph (who, what, or how).<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "You can design your outfit in this game. Thier many unige games."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "There are many unique games where you can design an outfit, such as Brookhaven."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved sentence combines the idea into one clear statement and gives a short example, which makes your point stronger and easier for the reader to follow.<br><br>	You generally use an appropriate essay style and you try to explain your reasons, but the register and phrasing are sometimes informal or unclear. Use more formal, complete sentences in an essay and avoid short fragments.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Use full sentences and a slightly more formal tone (avoid fragments and short notes). Start body paragraphs with a topic sentence that links to your thesis (e.g., "The first activity I enjoy is playing games because...").<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "Games and Art work done by teenages in Thailand"<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Games and artwork are popular among teenagers in Thailand."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved version is a full sentence with a clear subject and verb, which fits the formal writing style of an essay and helps the reader immediately understand your point.<br><br>	You used four paragraphs, but the thesis and the topic sentences are not clear or grammatical, so the reader cannot easily see the structure you intended. The introduction should end with one clear thesis sentence; each body paragraph should start with a topic sentence that links to that thesis.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Rewrite your introduction so it ends with a clear thesis (one sentence stating both activities and why you like them). Begin each body paragraph with a topic sentence that refers to the thesis (e.g., "Firstly, I enjoy playing online games because...").<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Introduction lacking a clear thesis: "Free time is benefit for teenages. Each country has many activities to do, Thailand has different activities. Games and Art work done by teenages in Thailand"<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Free time is beneficial for teenagers. In Thailand, two popular activities are playing online games and doing artwork; I enjoy them because they help me relax and connect with others."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved introduction ends with a clear thesis that names both activities and gives the reader the reason you will explain, so each paragraph can clearly relate back to this thesis.<br><br>	You use everyday vocabulary and you try to explain ideas, which is good. The main challenges are frequent spelling, agreement and form errors, and some sentence-structure problems. Below are examples from your essay with corrections and simple explanations that relate to common Thai-to-English interference patterns.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "Free time is benefit for teenages."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time is beneficial for teenagers."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (word form / plural) In Thai learners often use the base form of words where English needs a different form (adjective "beneficial" rather than noun "benefit") and plural marking. From the patterns: "Word form (noun/verb/adjective) — Thai uses flexible forms; English requires precise morphology." Using the correct form and plural makes the meaning grammatical and natural.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "Each country has many activities to do, Thailand has different activities."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Each country has many activities to do. Thailand has different activities."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (run-on / clause boundary) Thai often allows long clauses separated differently; English requires clear sentence boundaries or connectives. The run_ons pattern: "Thai allows long clauses; English needs clear clause boundaries." Use a full stop or a linking word (e.g., "and", "however") to join ideas correctly.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "Games and Art work done by teenages in Thailand"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Games and artwork are popular among teenagers in Thailand."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (passive/word form) The original is a fragment and misses a correct verb form. Thai often omits small grammatical words that English needs. Using "are popular" makes the sentence complete and natural in English.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "First of free time activities is play games."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "The first free-time activity is playing games."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (word form) English frequently uses gerunds (playing) after "activity is". Thai-to-English transfer can produce noun/verb mismatches; check common collocations ("activity is + -ing").<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "Thier are many game that teenages usally play, but the most famouse is Roblox."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are many games that teenagers usually play, but the most famous is Roblox."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (plural / spelling) Multiple issues here: plural nouns ("games"), spelling ("teenagers", "usually", "famous"), and the word "There" (not "Thier"). Thai does not mark plural with -s in the same way, so learners sometimes forget it. See the plural_s and word_form patterns.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "Thier many unige games."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are many unique games."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (spelling / word order) Spelling and the required verb "are" are missing. Thai sentence patterns allow subjects and verbs in different orders; English needs "There are ..." for this meaning.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "for example, Brook Haven which is a role play game, 99 night in the forest which is a surviver game."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "For example, Brookhaven, which is a role-play game, and 99 Night in the Forest, which is a survival game."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (relative clauses / word form) Use commas and "which" correctly for non-defining clauses; correct word forms ("role-play", "survival"). The relative_clauses pattern shows Thai learners may omit or misuse who/which/that and punctuation — add them for clarity.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "It become famous by many YouTuber play this game."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "It becomes famous because many YouTubers play this game."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (verb agreement / plural / clause linkers) English verbs need -s with third person singular ("becomes") and plural nouns ("YouTubers"). Also English prefers "because" or "when" to explain cause. Thai does not always mark third-person -s, so learners forget this ending (related to plural_s/word_form patterns).<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "As well as play game is art work."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "In addition to playing games, artwork is another activity."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (structure / word form) English prefers "In addition to + -ing" for linking ideas. Thai sentence connectors differ, so students may produce sentences that are literal and ungrammatical in English; use standard linking phrases.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "Doodle Art is the easy one to do."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Doodle Art is easy to do."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (word form) English omits "the" in this structure and uses the adjective "easy" directly: "is easy to do". Thai learners sometimes keep extra determiners that English does not need (word_form pattern).<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "It become famouse by many artist to Doodle Art and sold it which many money."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "It became famous because many artists created Doodle Art and sold it for a lot of money."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (tense / plural / preposition / word form) Multiple issues: past tense "became", plural "artists", and correct preposition "for". Thai does not always mark tense or plural the same way; this causes common errors (see word_form and plural_s patterns). Use simple past for completed past events and "sold it for a lot of money" for natural phrasing.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "All of this are made teenages be calm and relax."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "All of these help teenagers feel calm and relaxed."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (plural / verb choice / adjective form) "these" agrees with plural, "help ... feel" is the natural English pattern, and "relaxed" is the correct adjective. Thai speakers sometimes translate word-by-word and miss these collocations (plural_s and word_form patterns).<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "It help teenages to communicate each other and have time with yourself."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "They help teenagers communicate with each other and have time for themselves."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (agreement / reflexive pronoun / preposition) Use plural agreement ("They help"), "communicate with each other", and "for themselves". Thai does not use these exact pronoun or preposition patterns, so they are often mistranslated into English (prepositions_time_place and plural_s patterns).<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> "In my opinnion, these activities are important for teenages if they use it in correct way."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "In my opinion, these activities are important for teenagers if they are used in the correct way."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (spelling / passive structure / pronoun) "opinion" spelling, plural "teenagers", and passive "are used" make the sentence correct and clear. Thai often uses active short forms and omits articles, so using the passive here is clearer and matches English conventions (relative_clauses / word_form patterns).<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Focus on 10 minutes/day of spelling and form drills: correct common words you miss (teenagers, famous, usually, opinion, unique). Make a short list and test yourself twice this week.<br>2. Practice 5 model sentences using passive and relative clauses (e.g., "which is...", "that was...") — write one paragraph using at least one relative clause and one passive sentence.<br>3. Rewrite the essay: make the introduction end in one clear thesis sentence; start each body paragraph with a topic sentence and add one short specific example in each. Compare your rewritten sentences with the corrections above.<br><br>	4.0	3.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
