2964	28997	2025-12-14 15:55:00.514799+00	Term 2 Midterms 2025-6	Hi, Alex<br><br>I am also happy as well. I very miss go on a vacation with you. Last time, we went to the beach and it was so much fun!!<br><br><br>I think I prefer your dad drive us to the campsite. Because we will have more time to spend together so we can do activities we want! And I also really lazy to wake up early. So, this is the best option for us.<br><br><br>I wouldn't recommend you to cook that. We are at campsite. We should cook something that represent about go camping. My opinion is, we should cook a BBQ. Isn't it sound more much fun to cook that? And it really tasty too.<br><br><br>Absolutely! We should bring a blanket that looks fluffy and not too thin like a paper. Also, bring a pair of socks too. It will make your feel feel warm all the time. I really like to do that.<br><br><br>See you there, Mymind	159	14.0	Hi Grace! 👋<br><br>Wait a minute... you signed off as "Mymind"! 😮 Did you borrow a template? Be careful to use your own name! Apart from that, your email was lovely. "Not too thin like a paper" was a great description! 📄<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>Verbs!</b> ⚙️ "I very miss go" -> "I really <b>miss going</b>".<br>2. <b>Questions!</b> ❓ "Isn't it sound" -> "Doesn't it sound".<br>3. <b>Adjectives!</b> 🎨 "really lazy" -> "really <b>lazy</b>" (used correctly! I meant "I am really lazy").\n	You answered everything well. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Activities!</b> 💭 You mentioned "do activities we want". Give examples! "Like hiking or swimming" makes it more real.</li>\n	Your tone was super friendly. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Consistency!</b> 🕵️‍♀️ Signing the wrong name is a big confusion for the reader. Always double-check!</li>\n	Your paragraphing was excellent. Very clear structure. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Flow!</b> 🌊 "Absolutely!" at the start of the last paragraph was a bit sudden. Maybe "About the weather, absolutely we need blankets!"</li>\n	"Fluffy" is a fantastic word! 🧸<br><br>Fix these:<br><li><b>Auxiliary Verbs!</b> 🆘 "Isn't it sound" -> "<b>Doesn't</b> it sound" (Use 'do' for verbs like sound).</li><li><b>Feeling!</b> 💓 "make your feel feel warm" -> "make you feel warm".</li>\n	5.0	3.0	4.0	2.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
2982	28858	2025-12-14 15:55:06.675076+00	Camping trip	I think we should go with your dad because it is easier and we don't have to worry about making it in time and we have alot of stuff to bring if we go by train it will be crowded and its gonna be hard to carry those stuff there.<br><br>Sausages is too expensive. I think we should bring something cheaper and can keep us full for the rest of the trip. I suggest we bring sandwiches because its cheap and can keep us full.<br><br>I suggest we bring a small heater and some heat tech so we can stay warm for the rest of the night.	107	14.0	Hi Gunner! 👋<br><br>You wrote a very practical email! Thinking about carrying stuff ("hard to carry those stuff") is a very smart reason to choose the car. 🚗 And "heat tech" is a great modern suggestion for warmth! 🌡️<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>Agreement!</b> 🤝 "Sausages is" -> "Sausages <b>are</b>".<br>2. <b>Spelling/Grammar!</b> 📝 "its" -> "it's" (it is).<br>3. <b>Plurals!</b> 🔢 "carry those stuff" -> "carry that stuff" (stuff is uncountable) or "those things".\n	You answered well. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Logic!</b> 💭 You said sausages are "too expensive". Usually they are cheap! A sandwich might cost more. But it's your opinion!</li>\n	Your tone was functional. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Greeting!</b> 👋 You forgot to say "Hi Alex" and "Bye Gunner". Don't forget the sandwich structure (Hello + Body + Bye)!</li>\n	Your paragraphs were clear. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Run-ons!</b> 🏃‍♂️ Your first sentence was very long ("because... and... and..."). Break it up!</li>\n	"Crowded" is a good word! 👏<br><br>Watch these errors:<br><li><b>It's vs Its!</b> 🆚 "its cheap" -> "<b>it's</b> cheap" (it is). "Its" means belonging to it.</li><li><b>Plurals!</b> 🔢 "Sausages is" -> "are".</li>\n	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
