2469	28863	2025-12-02 09:53:40.087331+00	Creative Writing	Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it. This was Sam, who's a middle class guy whos not poor and not rich. His normal life is driving a truck. He had some knowledge about how to fix a truck, and he lived in a small country side house. One day Sam decided to make a machine that could make his truck untouchable but visible, so he could pass through the traffic jam easily. Although the machine worked, he was unhappy. Things went wrong when he started to tow a trailer and drive. The problem got bigger because the trailer sweep all the traffic cars. Because the machine only worked with his truck but not the trailer. Suddenly people in their cars were mad at Sam for causes<br><br><br>damages to their cars. As a result, Sam had to pay a lot for the damaged cars. After that Sam became a poor guy and his driving lisence got banned. In the end Sam was a truck mechanic and was saving up to build his new garage. After the bad days passed Sam tried to forget about the machine project and he has learned to test multiple times when make a project.	201	16.0	Hello Namo T, 👋<br><br>This is a very creative story! 🚛 I loved the idea of an 'untouchable' truck to beat traffic jams—we all wish we had one of those! The consequences of the trailer not being untouchable were funny but also a serious lesson for Sam. It was a great read.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you improve. 📋<br><br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 Watch out for 'lisence' (license) and 'whos' (who's).<br>2. <b>Verb Tenses!</b> ⏳ Make sure all your verbs are in the past tense (e.g., 'sweep' should be 'swept').<br>3. <b>Punctuation!</b> ✒️ Be careful not to split sentences in the wrong place (like the break after 'causes').	You have a clear and complete story structure! 🌟 The problem (the trailer wasn't invisible) was a clever twist.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Show the Accident!</b> 💥 You said the trailer 'sweep all the traffic cars'. A little more description here (crunching metal, honking horns) would make the scene more exciting.</li><li><b>Sam's Reaction!</b> 😲 How did Sam feel when he realized what was happening? Was he panicked? Embarrassed? Adding feelings makes the character more real.</li>	Your story is easy to follow and the main idea is very clear. 👏<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Flow!</b> 🌊 'Suddenly people in their cars were mad at Sam for causes... damages'. This sentence is split awkwardly. Try: 'Suddenly, people were mad at Sam for causing damage to their cars.'</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Untouchable' is a cool word, but maybe 'Intangible' or 'Ghost Mode' would be more scientifically accurate for an invention?</li>	You used paragraphs to separate the beginning, middle, and end. Good job! 📚<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linking Words!</b> 🔗 You used 'Although' and 'As a result'. Try adding words like 'Unfortunately', 'Consequently', or 'However' to make your writing sound more advanced.</li><li><b>Sentence Breaks!</b> 🛑 You have a paragraph break in the middle of a sentence ('causes... damages'). Make sure you finish the sentence before starting a new line!</li>	You used some good vocabulary like 'traffic jam', 'mechanic', and 'damages'. 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Lisence' -> '<b>license</b>'. 'Whos' -> '<b>who was</b>' or '<b>who's</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> ⚙️ 'Trailer sweep' -> 'Trailer <b>swept</b>' (past tense). 'He has learned' -> 'He <b>had</b> learned' or just 'He learned'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Mad at Sam for causes' -> 'Mad at Sam for <b>causing</b>'.</li>	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
