 classic article convention that holds attention well.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Fact Check!</b> 🔍 Be careful with names. The author is J.K. <b>Rowling</b>. Getting these details right builds trust with your reader.</li><li><b>Direct Recommendations!</b> 💬 Instead of 'I hope you give it a try', you could use more persuasive language like 'You definitely shouldn't miss it!' to sound more like a magazine writer.</li>	Your article is connected and flows in a logical way with clear paragraphing. 🌊 You move from a specific book recommendation to a general opinion on reading smoothly.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Punctuation!</b> 🛑 Watch out for short, 'choppy' sentences. Instead of 'I think it's good to read a lot. Because reading...', you should combine them: 'I think it's good to read a lot <b>because</b> reading...'</li>	You used some great vocabulary like 'thought-provoking', 'volumes', and 'dark fantasy'! 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you improve:<br><li><b>Articles and Plurals!</b> 🛠️ 'a books written by' -> 'a <b>book</b> written by'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'consist with' -> '<b>consists of</b>'.</li><li><b>Grammar Control!</b> ⚙️ 'reading help' -> 'reading <b>helps</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Forms!</b> 🔄 'difference type of books' -> '<b>different types</b> of books'.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ 'a boy who was attended to magic school' -> 'a boy who <b>attended</b> magic school'.</li><li><b>Word Order!</b> 🔃 'more spend time for reading' -> '<b>spend more time</b> reading'.</li>	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
