3344	28859	2026-02-05 21:33:09.836409+00	Magazine Article	Are you provocative movies? I will recommend this movie. My favorite movie, an action and dramatic, is Weak hero. This movie is telling about school bullying. I love this movie because the actors were very re-nowned and they have a lot of attention to play in this movie.<br><br>I really like it when they are fighting. The school is super bustling.<br><br>Prize, a comedy's lover, is very like this action movie. Weak hero, a best movie for me, is a example case for someone still bullying your friends. I love watching weak hero with my family before we go to bed.	101	10.0	Hello Prize, 👋<br><br>Thank you for your submission! You've written a very passionate article about your favorite story, 'Weak Hero.' I found your description of the school environment and the actors' performances very interesting! 🌟 It’s clear you have a strong interest in action-packed and meaningful stories. <br><br>However, there were two main issues with the task requirements. First, the question asked about things you <b>read</b> (books, manga, or comics), but you wrote about a <b>movie</b> you watch. Second, you forgot to answer if you think it is <b>good to read a lot</b>. <br><br>I have some tips below to help you improve your writing and reach a higher score next time! 📋	The most important part of the exam is answering all parts of the question! 🎯<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Stick to the Topic!</b> 📖 The prompt specifically asked about reading (books/manga). Even if 'Weak Hero' is based on a webtoon (manga), you should mention that you <b>read</b> it rather than watch it.</li><li><b>Answer Every Prompt!</b> 📝 You missed the question: 'Do you think it's good to read a lot? Why?'. Always check the list of questions before you finish to make sure everything is addressed.</li>	You did a good job using a rhetorical question at the start to grab the reader's attention! 🤩<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Tone and Logic!</b> 💡 In your first sentence, 'Are you provocative movies?' doesn't quite make sense. You probably meant 'Do you like provocative movies?' or 'Are you looking for...'. Make sure your opening clearly relates to the reader.</li><li><b>Purpose!</b> 💬 Since this is for a magazine, try to explain <i>why</i> other people should read/watch your recommendation more clearly.</li>	Your article is well-organised with clear paragraphing, and I liked how you used your name and interests to personalize the article. 🌊<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linking Ideas!</b> 🔗 Use more connectors like 'Furthermore' or 'On the other hand' to connect your thoughts.</li>	You used some interesting vocabulary like 'bustling' and 'renowned'! 👏 However, there are some grammar points to work on:<br><br><li><b>Vocabulary Choice!</b> 🛠️ You used 'provocative', which usually describes something that makes people angry. A better word for an exciting action movie might be 'thrilling' or 'intense'.</li><li><b>Verb Patterns!</b> 📝 You wrote 'Prize... is very like this action movie.' To express a hobby, say '<b>really likes</b>' or '<b>is very fond of</b>'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> ✏️ 'Re-nowned' should be one word: <b>renowned</b>.</li><li><b>Articles and Nouns!</b> 📍 'is a example case' should be 'is <b>an</b> example' or 'is a <b>good</b> example'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 💬 'telling about' -> 'The movie <b>is about</b> school bullying' or 'The movie <b>tells a story</b> about...'.</li>	2.0	2.0	4.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
3345	28900	2026-02-05 21:33:09.836409+00	Magazine Article	Do you like to read a Manga? My favorite manga, a fantasy comedy, is Demon Slyer. Demon slyer have many episodes. This manga show about people, live in Japan, fight with demon, Muzan. The story "Rapunzel", the most I like forever wrote by Brothers Grimm. One day a young girl with long golden hair, want to have a freedom and plan to escape from the witch.<br>I think it's good to read a lot of book. because you'll know about "how people live, even in difficult situation. You can choose what you want to read, like romance, love story, dark fantasy. I hope you'll read a lot of book like me!	111	13.0	Hello Bona, 👋<br><br>It was a pleasure to read your article about your favorite stories! 📖 You did a great job of explaining your interest in both modern manga like <i>Demon Slayer</i> and classic fairy tales like <i>Rapunzel</i>. Your explanation of why reading is important—to understand how people live in difficult situations—was very thoughtful and shows a good understanding of the task. 🌟<br><br>I have a few tips to help you move your writing to the next level. 📋<br>1. <b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ Remember that singular subjects (like 'Demon Slayer') need singular verbs ('has').<br>2. <b>Plural Nouns!</b> 📚 When we talk about things in general, we usually use the plural form, like 'a lot of books'.<br>3. <b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🛠️ Some of your sentences are a bit long or missing verbs. Breaking them down can make your writing clearer.	You answered the question perfectly! 🎯 You told the reader exactly what you like to read and gave a clear reason why reading is beneficial. Target reader is fully informed.<br><br>To make it even better:<br><li><b>Explain the 'Why'!</b> 💡 You mentioned <i>Demon Slayer</i> is a fantasy comedy. What makes it funny? Adding one small detail about a character's personality would make the article even more engaging.</li><li><b>Genre Connections!</b> 🔗 You mentioned different genres at the end (romance, dark fantasy). You could briefly say which one <i>Rapunzel</i> belongs to!</li>	You used the conventions of an article well by starting with a question to grab the reader's attention! 🤩 The tone is friendly and personal.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Descriptive Language!</b> 🎨 Instead of saying 'many episodes', you could say 'an exciting series' or 'many chapters' to sound more like a book reviewer.</li><li><b>Clarify the Plot!</b> 📝 When describing <i>Rapunzel</i>, ensure the connection between the girl and the witch is clear so a reader who doesn't know the story can follow along.</li>	The text is connected and follows a logical order. 🌊 You moved from manga to books and then to your general opinion on reading.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Transitions!</b> 🔗 The jump from <i>Demon Slayer</i> to <i>Rapunzel</i> is very sudden. You could use a linking phrase like 'In addition to manga, I also love classic stories' to bridge the two ideas.</li><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 📋 Try to start a new paragraph for each main idea. You started the second paragraph well, but make sure the first part isn't too crowded with different topics.</li>	You used some good vocabulary like 'fantasy comedy' and 'difficult situation'. 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you improve:<br><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'Demon slyer have' should be 'Demon Slayer <b>has</b>'. 'This manga show' should be 'This manga <b>shows</b>'.</li><li><b>Plurals!</b> 📚 'a lot of book' should be 'a lot of <b>books</b>'.</li><li><b>Punctuation and Capitalization!</b> 📍 Keep an eye on your capital letters for titles: 'Demon <b>Slayer</b>'. Also, check your sentences: 'I think it's good to read a lot of book. because...' should be one sentence: '...a lot of books <b>because</b> you'll know...'</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'read a Manga' is usually just 'read manga' (uncountable) or 'read a manga series'.</li><li><b>Passive Voice/Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'The most I like forever wrote by' ->