on like 'Do you love to read the shojou style?' is a fantastic way to grab the reader's attention.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Add a Title!</b> 📋 Articles usually have a catchy title at the top to tell the reader what to expect, such as 'The Magic of Manga'.</li><li><b>Tone Consistency!</b> 💬 You used the phrase 'From me to you', which sounds very friendly. Try to keep that personal 'recommendation' tone throughout the whole piece.</li>	Your text is connected and easy to follow! 🌊 You used linking words like 'But' and 'So' to show how your ideas relate to each other.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 🧱 You could split your text into two paragraphs: one for the manga recommendation and one for your general thoughts on reading. This makes it easier to read.</li><li><b>Linking Sentences!</b> 🔗 Instead of starting a sentence with 'Also reading too', you could use 'Furthermore' or 'In addition' to sound more professional.</li>	You used some great vocabulary like 'dress-code' and 'limit'! 👏 However, there are some grammar mistakes that we can fix to make your writing clearer.<br><br>Here are some corrections:<br><li><b>Gerunds as Subjects!</b> 📝 'Read a lot is a good way' -> '<b>Reading</b> a lot is a good way'.</li><li><b>Word Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'helps your minded' -> 'helps your <b>mind</b>'.</li><li><b>Modals!</b> 🚫 'You also can learning' -> 'You can also <b>learn</b>' (after 'can', use the base verb).</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'The story show you' -> 'The story <b>shows</b> you'.</li><li><b>Adjectives!</b> 😴 'you will tired' -> 'you will <b>be</b> tired'.</li><li><b>Vocabulary!</b> 🐶 'poppy love' -> '<b>puppy</b> love' (this is the common English idiom for young love!).</li>	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
