inions. 💬 The reader understands exactly what you like and why you think reading is important.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Engage the Reader!</b> 🤝 Articles usually talk directly to the reader. Try asking a question at the start, like 'Do you love reading as much as I do?'</li><li><b>Tone!</b> 🎭 Your tone is good, but phrases like 'That is definitely going to garantee your language skill' are a bit strong. Maybe try 'This will definitely help you improve your skills.'</li>	Your text is connected and coherent! 🌊 You used some good linking words like 'Moreover' and 'For instance' to help the flow of your ideas.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Transitions!</b> 🔗 The jump from your favorite books to the importance of English skills is a bit sudden. You could use a bridge like: 'Aside from being fun, I believe reading is also a vital tool for learning.'</li><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 🧱 While you have two sections, make sure each paragraph has a clear focus. The first on 'what' you read, and the second on 'why' it is good.</li>	You used some good vocabulary like 'genre', 'documentary', and 'especially'. 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you polish your language:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> ✍️ 'Garantee' should be spelled <b>'guarantee'</b>.</li><li><b>Relative Clauses!</b> 🧐 'especially the one which Is fantasy genre' -> 'especially <b>those in the</b> fantasy genre' or 'especially <b>fantasy manga</b>'.</li><li><b>Determiners!</b> 🚫 'practice your any language skills' -> 'practice <b>any of your</b> language skills' or just 'practice your language skills'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🔄 'whatever reading you like' -> '<b>whatever type of</b> reading you like' or 'whatever you enjoy reading'.</li><li><b>Capitalization!</b> 🔠 Be careful with 'Is' in the middle of a sentence—it should be lowercase <b>'is'</b>.</li>	4.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
