riety in Recommendation!</b> 💬 Instead of saying 'The reason why I recommend this book because...', you could try 'I highly recommend this book because...' to make it sound more natural.</li><li><b>Polishing Phrases!</b> ✨ Make sure your sentences are complete. 'later become one of the most successful show' needs a helper verb like 'which later <b>became</b>'.</li>	Your article is well-organised into two clear sections: the book recommendation and your general opinion on reading. 🌊 This structure helps the reader follow your points effectively.<br><br>To improve:<br>Linking Words! 🔗 While you used 'In my opinion' and 'because', try to use more variety. Words like 'Furthermore' or 'Consequently' can help link your ideas about education more smoothly.Transitions! 🧱 You can make the transition between the story and your opinion even more polished by using a bridge sentence like 'Beyond the excitement of the story, I believe reading also has many practical benefits.'	You used some good vocabulary like 'addicting', 'habit', and 'education'. 👏 However, there are some grammar points to work on:<br><br>Gerunds! 🛠️ When the action is the subject, use '-ing'. For example: 'Reading a lot can become a really good habit' (not 'read a lot').Apostrophes! ✍️ 'it' so addicting' should be 'it's so addicting' (short for 'it is').Noun count! 🧮 'one of the most important skill' should be 'one of the most important skills' because you are choosing one from many.Verb Tense! ⏳ 'later become' should be 'later became' because it happened in the past.Articles! 📖 'before test' sounds better as 'before a test' or 'before tests'.	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
