o inform the target reader more comprehensively. For example, while you mention \\"high technology,\\" you don't elaborate on it. The connection between \\"mala\\" being a sauce and \\"people always ate\\" it with hot pot is a bit unclear. To achieve a score of 5, you should ensure all aspects are thoroughly described and explained, providing a richer and more complete picture for the reader.	You communicate straightforward ideas about Shanghai and your personal experience there. The essay has a generally informal and personal tone, which is suitable for expressing a favorite place. However, the conventions of an essay are not used effectively to consistently hold the target reader's attention. The opening sentence is a bit awkward (\\"my favorite that I would love to go again is...\\") and some ideas are presented abruptly, affecting the flow. The concluding section feels somewhat disconnected. To improve to a 5, you would need to use essay conventions more effectively, employing clear paragraphing, varying sentence structures, and using more sophisticated language to communicate ideas clearly and keep the reader fully engaged.	The essay has a basic attempt at organisation with an introduction, a body discussing characteristics (culture, technology, food, trains), and a concluding section. You use some basic linking words and phrases such as \\"In addition,\\" \\"For example,\\" and \\"Overall.\\" However, the text is not generally well-organised or coherent. Paragraph breaks are inconsistent or lead to very short paragraphs that disrupt the flow. For instance, the final paragraph begins with \\"Overall this wha I like,\\" which feels abrupt and doesn't clearly transition from the previous point. The shift to \\"weird things\\" could be integrated more smoothly. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to structure your essay into distinct, well-linked paragraphs, using a wider variety of cohesive devices and organisational patterns to create a more fluid and logically structured piece.	Leo, you use some everyday vocabulary appropriate for describing a city and personal experiences, such as \\"culture,\\" \\"technology,\\" \\"food,\\" \\"train,\\" \\"spicy,\\" and \\"disturbing.\\" However, there are frequent and fundamental errors in basic grammatical forms, which are quite noticeable and often hinder clear communication. Examples include: \\"In my opinnion my favorite that I would love to go again is \\\\\\"Shang hai\\\\\\"". (should be \\"In my opinion, my favorite place that I would love to visit again is Shanghai.\\"), \\"it's first country that I ever been too\\" (should be \\"it was the first country I had ever been to\\"), \\"Shang hai is a city... that makes Shang hai is unique\\" (should be \\"makes Shanghai unique\\"), \\"The famouse food\\" (spelling), \\"it's like a suace\\" (spelling), \\"The is advace than Thai a little\\" (should be \\"It is more advanced than Thailand\\"), \\"our trian in Thai land\\" (spelling, capitalization), \\"this wha I like\\" (should be \\"this is what I like\\"), and \\"experince that ever have\\" (should be \\"experience that I have ever had\\"). The consistent errors in spelling, subject-verb agreement, articles, and verb forms demonstrate a limited control over simple grammatical forms, and some errors impede meaning. To achieve a score of 5, you need to significantly improve your accuracy in fundamental grammar, use a wider range of vocabulary with more precision, and demonstrate flexibility with more complex grammatical forms.	3.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
