1119	35239	2025-08-27 21:37:03.859551+00	Free time Activities	Freetime is a nessesity that everyone needs. Most people in Thailand don't primarily have lots of freetime. Thailand has a very demanding schedule, people in Thailand have a longer work and study schedule than other countries. Although there are many things you can do during your limited amount of freetime to help you relax.<br><br><br>One enjoyable activity is reading. Many people like spending their freetime reading comics, novels or magazines. Reading allows you to escape in stories, aquire new knowledge and to expand your imagination. It's also a way to reduce stress, since focusing on the story can help reduce daily worries. For others reading isn't just for entertainment, but it's a source of comfort.<br><br><br>A second enjoyable activity is playing video games. They allow us to escape reality by immersing ourselves in virtual adventures where we can reduce stress. They also allow us to meet new people, where we can create life-long friends. Which makes them both fun and social. Video games help us relax while building connections.<br><br><br>In conclusion, free time is vital to everyone. They offer people valuable ways to relax and reset. Reading and playing games can help us recharge and enjoy our freetime.	221	13.0	<b>📝 Dear Ana</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 221 words and achieved B2. You've clearly identified two popular free-time activities and explained their benefits, which is a great start!<br><br>	You successfully introduced two free-time activities, reading and playing video games, and gave clear reasons why they are chosen, helping the reader understand their appeal.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> While your essay clearly explains your chosen activities, ensure your introduction directly sets the stage for *your* personal choices, rather than broader generalisations.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your introduction started with general statements about free time in Thailand, rather than immediately focusing on the activities you would discuss: "Most people in Thailand don't primarily have lots of freetime. Thailand has a very demanding schedule..."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "For me, free time is a precious opportunity to engage in activities that offer both relaxation and enrichment. I find two particularly rewarding activities are reading and playing video games."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A focused introduction immediately guides the reader to *your* specific topic, making your essay more directly relevant to the task and engaging.<br><br>	You generally communicated your ideas well, and your tone was appropriate for an essay.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> To fully engage your reader and clearly convey your essay's purpose, ensure your introduction concludes with a clear and complete thesis statement that explicitly outlines your main points.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your introduction ended with a fragmented sentence that did not fully present your essay's argument: "Although there are many things you can do during your limited amount of freetime to help you relax."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "This essay will explore how two specific activities, reading and playing video games, offer valuable ways to relax, learn, and connect during one's free time."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A strong, explicit thesis statement acts as a roadmap for your reader, making your essay's intentions and structure immediately clear, which is crucial for effective communication in academic writing.<br><br>	You used a clear four-paragraph structure, and your body paragraphs had good topic sentences.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Focus on strengthening your concluding paragraph with a smoother transition and a more comprehensive summary of your essay's main ideas.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your concluding paragraph began with a simple transition and offered a brief restatement of ideas, without fully synthesising your points: "In conclusion, free time is vital to everyone. They offer people valuable ways to relax and reset."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "To conclude, the importance of free time cannot be overstated. As demonstrated through the engaging experiences of reading and the interactive world of gaming, these activities provide essential avenues for mental rejuvenation, personal growth, and social connection, reinforcing their vital role in our lives."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A more developed conclusion, with a strong transitional phrase and a thorough synthesis of your main points, provides a satisfying sense of closure and reinforces the overall message of your essay.<br><br>	Your writing is generally clear, and the meaning is easy to understand, which is excellent. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Freetime is a nessesity that everyone needs."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time is a necessity that everyone needs."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, compound nouns like 'free time' are often written as two separate words, unlike in Thai where words are often combined without spaces. 'Necessity' is also a common spelling error; practicing words you use often will help.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Reading allows you to escape in stories, aquire new knowledge and to expand your imagination."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Reading allows you to escape into stories, acquire new knowledge and expand your imagination."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> 'Acquire' is a commonly misspelled word in English. Paying close attention to the vowel sequence can help you remember it.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Practice writing clear and complete thesis statements that explicitly outline the main arguments of your essays.<br>2. Focus on developing your concluding paragraphs by using effective transitions and thoroughly synthesising your main points.<br>3. Create a personal spelling list of words you frequently misspell, such as 'free time' and 'necessity', and practice them regularly.<br>