casionally affect clarity ("I ever struggled," "head to speak," "alot of," "might thought," "very struggled," "anything to worried"). You use simple grammatical forms, but errors are present. To improve, focus on practicing sentence construction to reduce grammatical errors.	3.0	3.0	2.5	2.5	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
1121	29929	2025-08-27 21:55:11.289376+00	Free time Activities	Free time is make ppl calm and relax, so there are weny activities to do in free time. but for teens they are need the good activities for their body and wind because in this age all of teens need to grow up to helthy in the future so they need to do an. activities that will make them helthy on body and wind in the future, so this essay will told you two activities that will make teens grow up to be helthy and good.<br><br><br>The first activity is cadio. Cadio is the activity that will make teens have body helthy. for cadio there are activity that it will make teens helthy such as running push-up sit-up and prank pose it all will make teens not to fat but not skinny too. This activity will make teens are helthy and look cool fore weny people.<br><br><br>Beside of cadio is drawing. Drawing is the really good activity one. Because drawing will make teens have weny focus and it will make them creatively. so when you drawing you need to have the picture that you gonna in your mind and focus on paper then you draw it into the great picture. This activity will make teens have weny focus and upgrade their mind so it really important for teens that only play their phone all time that mean drawing is not the bad activity for teens ony.<br><br><br>In my conclusion there are weny activities that good and usefull but there are some activities that useless for teens because teens is the ages that will become adult in the future and there weeny problem that make them ill or the worst is dead so teens have to get ready for it by have some good activities for body helth and wind so their are better than let teens play phone or do something bad like smoke so teens in Thai are do 90% bad thing in their life so they are all need a change.	330	9.0	<b>📝 Dear Tiw</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 330 words. Your writing is at a B1 level. You've made a good effort to identify two free time activities for teenagers.<br><br>	You wrote about two free time activities, cardio and drawing, and you explained what they are. To make your essay stronger, you need to explain more clearly *why* you chose these activities and *how* they help teenagers.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> When you explain an idea, give more details and examples. Make sure your conclusion only talks about ideas from the main part of your essay.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> You wrote: "Free time is make ppl calm and relax, so there are meny activities to do in free time. but for teens they are need the good activities for their body and wind because in this age all of teens need to grow up to helthy in the future..." This introduction is quite long but doesn't clearly tell the reader what your essay will be about or which activities you will talk about.<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Many teenagers today look for activities that help them become healthy adults. This essay will talk about two good free time activities: cardio exercise for the body, and drawing for a healthy mind and creativity."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A good introduction tells the reader *right away* what your essay is about. This makes your writing easier to understand.<br><br>	You used paragraphs, which is a good step for an essay. However, sometimes your writing sounds too much like speaking, not writing. Words like "ppl" and "weny" are not good for an essay.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Try to use more formal language and make sure your introduction clearly tells the reader what your essay is about.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> You wrote: "Free time is make ppl calm and relax, so there are meny activities to do in free time." The word "ppl" is too informal for an essay.<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Free time allows individuals to unwind and relax, offering numerous activities. However, for teenagers, it is important to choose activities that foster both physical and mental well-being."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English essays, use full words like "people" instead of short forms like "ppl". This makes your writing more suitable for school work.<br><br>	You used four paragraphs, which helps organize your writing. But your ideas need to connect better. Sometimes it is hard to follow what you are saying because the paragraphs don't link together smoothly.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Start each new paragraph with a clear sentence that tells the reader the main idea of that paragraph. Also, make sure your conclusion reviews what you already said, not new ideas.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your first body paragraph begins: "The first activity is cadio. Cadio is the activity that will make teens have body helthy." This is a bit repetitive and doesn't clearly introduce the paragraph's main point.<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Firstly, doing cardio exercises can make teenagers' bodies very healthy."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A good opening sentence for a paragraph tells the reader exactly what that paragraph will be about. This helps your essay flow better.<br><br>	You used some common vocabulary in your essay, which is a good foundation. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Free time is make ppl calm and relax..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time <b>makes</b> people feel calm and relaxed..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, when you talk about "Free time" (one thing), the verb "make" needs an '-s' to become "makes." In Thai, verbs don't change like this, so it's a common mistake for Thai speakers.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "but for teens they are need the good activities..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "but teens <b>need</b> good activities..." <br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, we say "teens need" not "teens are need" for a simple action. "Are" is used with verbs ending in -ing (e.g., "are needing" for a continuous action, which is not what you mean here). This is different from how verbs work in Thai.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "...all of teens need to grow up..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "...<b>all teens</b> need to grow up..." or "...<b>all of the teens</b> need to grow up..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> When you say "all" before a general group like "teens," you can just say "all teens." If you want to use "all of," you usually need "the" like "all of the teens." Thai doesn't use words like "the" in the same way, which makes this tricky.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "...this essay will told you two activities..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "...this essay will <b>tell</b> you two activities..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> After words like "will," "can," or "should," the next verb must be in its basic form (like "tell," not "told"). This is a rule for English that is different from Thai.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "...there are meny activities..." and "...grow up to be helthy..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "...there are <b>many</b> activities..." and "...grow up to be <b>healthy</b>..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> These are common words, and making sure you spell them correctly ("many" instead of "meny," "healthy" instead of "helthy") will make your writing much clearer and easier to read.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Review the structure of a B1 essay, focusing on how to write a clear main idea and good topic sentences for each paragraph.<br>2. Practice using more formal language instead of words you would use when speaking to friends, especially for school writing.<br>3. Pay close attention to basic grammar rules like making sure your verb matches your subject, using the correct form of verbs after "will," and spelling common words correctly.<br><br>	3.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
