raphs, or use "Therefore" to show the result of something. For instance, you could say, "The main significance of Makha Bucha lies on three core ideas, reflecting a moral living til this day. Therefore, Buddhists engage in merit-making activities."	Dragon, you use everyday vocabulary generally appropriately, but there are errors in spelling (e.g., "budhhists" should be "Buddhists," "Febuary" should be "February," "Camboadia" should be "Cambodia") and capitalization. There are also some grammatical errors. While errors are noticeable, meaning can still be determined. To improve, focus on learning basic spelling and grammar rules. For example, remember to capitalize the first letter of sentences and proper nouns. Practice using correct verb tenses and subject-verb agreement.	2.0	2.0	2.0	3.0	Writing	Formative	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
