ntions of a story by beginning with the given sentence. To make your writing more engaging for someone reading your story, think about the journey you want to take them on. For instance, when you introduce something "incredible," try to follow through with what makes it incredible and how the characters react. Were you and your friend excited, confused, or amazed? ✨ Sharing these feelings will make your story much more lively and connect with your audience. Remember, a good story has a clear beginning, middle, and end, helping the reader enjoy every part.	Mathew, your story has a beginning, but to help your reader follow your wonderful ideas, it's good to organise them into clear sections. Imagine your story is like a train journey, and each new idea is a new station. You could use new paragraphs for different parts of your story: one for the initial incredible sight, another for what happened because of it, and a final one for how it ended. 🚂 Right now, your ideas are quite close together. Using linking words like "then," "after that," or "because of this" can also help your sentences connect smoothly and make your story much easier to understand.	Mathew, you've used some everyday words to share your thoughts, which is a good foundation. To make your writing even clearer and more accurate, let's focus on a few things. Firstly, pay attention to spelling, like "in credible" should be "incredible" and "alot" should be "a lot." Secondly, checking your grammar, especially when you use "there is" or "there are," will help. For instance, instead of "there alot of shop," you could say "there were a lot of shops" if you are talking about the past and many shops. 🛍️ Finally, remember to use "s" for plurals when you are talking about more than one thing, so "shop" becomes "shops" and "kid" becomes "kids" or "children." Sometimes, in Thai, nouns don't change for plural, but in English, it's an important detail. Focusing on these small but important details will help your words be precise and your meaning really clear for anyone reading your fantastic stories. 🎯	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A1+	\N	\N	\N	A1	2026
