lly important because because there are many student at school who doesn't know how how and why we have to save environment. So if we know why we have to save and how would we save it, it will make our environment better and can help us protecting.<br><br>LOOKPEAR: I think it is about smartphone. Yeah, because not just other student, me too. I we always stuck with smartphone and we we didn't we didn't attack or see like what happened around us. And it is challenge to have healthy lifestyle because we always sit and sleep and eating. Yeah. We didn't go to save and go and do something to protecting our environment or make us healthy.<br><br>LOOKPEAR: Technology, I I because in technology help us to reduce pollution by some some thing that through because what do you think, Nene?<br><br>	475	9.0	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Speaking	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	Your speech is generally understandable, which is the most important thing! 🥳 However, to make your English sound even more natural and clear, we need to focus on a couple of areas. Firstly, try to avoid overemphasizing the final consonant sounds in words like "bicycle" (which sounded a bit like /baɪˈkjuːsaɪkəl/ instead of /ˈbaɪsɪkl/), "together" (where the final /r/ was very strong), "activity" (with heavy stress on the final /iː/), and "picture" (with an overly strong final /r/). Secondly, be careful not to drop the final consonant sounds in words like "muscles" (which sounded like /ˈmʌsəl/ instead of /ˈmʌsl̩z/), "friends" (sounding like /frɛn/ instead of /frɛndz/), and "think" (sounding like /θɪn/ instead of /θɪŋk/). Many Thai learners sometimes make these kinds of mistakes because Thai doesn't always have strong final consonants, or the rhythm is different. Practise saying words like "friend**s**" /frɛndz/, "mu**scl**e**s**" /ˈmʌsl̩z/, and "thi**nk**" /θɪŋk/ clearly, making sure all the sounds are there at the end. Try to listen carefully to native speakers and imitate the way they blend sounds and stress words. This will really help your pronunciation become more accurate! 🎧	Hi Lookpear! 👋 I'm here to give you some feedback on your speaking test. Overall, you did a good job of communicating your ideas and engaging in the discussion. Your ability to express yourself on various topics is a definite strong point, and it's clear you're building a solid foundation in English. To really push your speaking to the next level, let's focus on making your speech a bit smoother and clearer, especially with some sounds. Keep up the great effort, and remember that every practice helps you improve! You're doing well!<br><br>📋 **Action Plan**<br>*   ✔️ Practice making your sentences flow more naturally.<br>*   ✔️ Work on clearly pronouncing all the sounds at the ends of words.<br>*   ✔️ Try to extend your ideas in discussions by adding more detail or different perspectives.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1yqGR5ip5XtVuoI2jPIboJbuDxmsnlN7a?usp=drive_link	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
