e of paragraphing and inconsistent capitalization hinder the overall coherence. To score higher, organize your writing into clear paragraphs, each focusing on a specific aspect of why the paragraph is interesting. You could, for example, have one paragraph explaining the communication aspect and another detailing the mating behavior. Using cohesive devices like "Furthermore" or "In addition" would also help.	Pipe, you use everyday vocabulary appropriately (e.g., "communicate," "attract," "scientists"). However, the frequent lack of capitalization and some grammatical errors affect the clarity of your writing. Examples include "i think" (should be "I think"), inconsistent capitalization of "whales," and some run-on sentences. While meaning can generally be determined, these errors are noticeable. To improve, focus on accurate capitalization and punctuation, and try to vary your sentence structure. For example, use a mix of simple and compound sentences to add complexity to your writing.	3.0	2.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Formative	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
