 essay has a beginning and an end, and you told the story of your trip in order. You used some basic connecting words like \\"First,\\" \\"After that,\\" and \\"At the night.\\" However, the biggest problem is that you didn't use paragraphs. Your whole essay is one big block of text. This makes it hard for the reader to see your different points, like when you are talking about food, or when you are talking about stadiums. To get a higher score, you should divide your writing into clear paragraphs. Also, use more different connecting words to link your sentences and ideas more smoothly.	You used everyday words about travel, football, and food correctly, like \\"stadium,\\" \\"football teams,\\" \\"restaurant,\\" \\"pizza,\\" and \\"spicy.\\" But you used some words too many times, like \\"famous,\\" \\"really,\\" and \\"very.\\" You mostly used simple sentences, and sometimes your grammar has errors that make it hard to understand. For example, you wrote \\"My favourite that I really love it is 'Manchester',\\" instead of \\"My favorite place that I really love is Manchester.\\" Other mistakes include \\"In England, there are the most popular in football premier leauge\\" (should be \\"there is the most popular football premier league\\"), \\"last year, I want to Manchester\\" (should be \\"I went\\"), \\"my familys\\" (should be \\"my family\\"), \\"we're really love\\" (should be \\"we really love\\"), \\"pizza are really hot\\" (should be \\"pizzas are\\"), \\"it's can held people\\" (should be \\"it can hold people\\"), \\"The stadium are very looked very modern\\" (should be \\"The stadium looks very modern\\"), and \\"take a phuto of her\\" (should be \\"take a photo\\"). These mistakes happen often and make your English less clear. To get a higher score, you need to use words more exactly, including some less common ones, and use different kinds of sentences correctly. This way, your writing will have fewer mistakes and be easier to understand.	3.0	2.0	2.0	2.