er variety of cohesive devices and organisational patterns to create a more fluent and easily digestible piece of writing.	You use a very limited range of everyday vocabulary, which is generally appropriate but often repeated or misused. For example, \\"Pattaya\\" and \\"beach\\" are used frequently. While you attempt simple grammatical forms, there is a lack of control, and errors are frequent and often impede communication. Examples include: \\"I have gone Pattaya\\" (should be \\"I went to Pattaya\\"), \\"my friend who is name Paotan appoach to go Pattaya\\" (should be \\"my friend named Paotan suggested going to Pattaya\\"), \\"have more activitiyies to do together like play banana boat in the sea or together\\" (very unclear and repetitive), \\"I feel wow amazing\\" (should be \\"I felt amazing\\"), \\"seafood in this market very cheap for examples, The shrimp and fish\\" (should be \\"seafood in this market is very cheap, for example, shrimp and fish\\"), \\"I havn't seen\\" (should be \\"I haven't seen\\"), \\"some girl wear a sexy costumer\\" (should be \\"some girls wearing sexy costumes\\"), \\"Pattaya it like alert city I think people in this city doesn't sleep at night\\" (very awkward and difficult to understand), and \\"It alot activity to try\\" (should be \\"It has a lot of activities to try\\"). These pervasive errors make it difficult for the reader to understand the meaning clearly and consistently. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to use a wider range of vocabulary more precisely, including less common lexis, and demonstrate control and flexibility over a range of simple and complex grammatical forms, with only occasional errors that do not impede communication.	3.0	2.0	2.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
