ason felt a little less clear in its connection to the main argument: 'Lastly, it\\'s our decision to use mobile phone or not. I know that someone will not pay attention but if we have strong rules, students will scared of teachers and don\\'t use mobile phone before teacher allowed to use it.'<br><b>Correction:</b> 'Lastly, it is good for us to decide whether to use mobile phones or not. While I understand some students may not pay attention, excessively strong rules could reduce students\\' ability to make good decisions.'<br><b>Explanation:</b> Ensure each supporting point is clearly and directly linked to your main opinion. Sometimes, adding a more explicit linking phrase or rephrasing can strengthen the connection and clarity for the reader.	You used everyday vocabulary well and tried to use more complex grammar forms, with good control overall.<br><b>Problem:</b> You had some errors with basic verb forms: 'mobile phones aren\\'t use to play games or post pictures only.'<br><b>Correction:</b> 'mobile phones aren\\'t used to play games or post pictures only.'<br><b>Explanation:</b> In English, when you talk about the purpose or function of something, you often use \\'used to\\' (past participle) for things that are intended for a specific purpose. Thai grammar doesn\\'t always distinguish these verb forms in the same way, which can lead to mistakes in English.	5.0	3.0	3.0	4.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
