a' before 'something'. Problem: You wrote: "To play this game it have a 2 people to catch anther people" Correction: "To play this game, there need to be 2 people to catch other people" Explanation: 👉 In Thai, we use 'it have' but in English we use 'there is/are' to talk about existence, and we say 'other people' not 'anther people'.	1.0	2.0	2.0	1.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
