1133	28835	2025-08-28 14:36:03.200564+00	Free time Activities	Nowadays, Many teenagers usually do some activity in their freetime. Because, it can make them relax and joyful for doing some exercise. More people argue that they do something relax is good for themself but some people don't argue.<br><br><br>First, most people always playing the game on freetime. For instance, playing the game when they finished an assignment. Playing the game with close friend on holiday and more. It can help Teens to have an use full skills in real life.<br><br><br>	81	7.0	<b>📝 Dear Tatar</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 81 words and achieved A2+. You show a clear idea that free-time activities can help people relax, which is a good start. Keep going — you have the basic ideas, now you need to develop them more clearly and follow the essay structure required for First. Make sure you donlt copy from LLMs.<br><br>	You give a relevant idea (playing games) and a basic reason (relaxation), but the task asks for two different free-time activities with explanations and you only describe one. Also your essay is under the minimum required length, so the reader cannot be fully informed.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Add a second activity and give one clear reason and one short example for each activity. Aim for 140–190 words and make sure you fully answer the task.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "More people argue that they do something relax is good for themself but some people don't argue."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Many people believe that doing relaxing activities, such as playing games or going for a run, is good for them, but others disagree."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved sentence names two types of activity (playing games, running) and gives a clear contrast. Adding specific examples and a clearer connection between ideas makes your message more informative for the reader.<br><br>	Your tone is mostly appropriate for a short informal essay, but the development is uneven and the essay does not follow the expected formal structure for a First essay. The reader cannot follow a clear argument because ideas are underdeveloped.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Use a more formal, neutral tone and develop each idea in one short paragraph: state the activity, explain why you choose it, and give a brief example or result.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "Because, it can make them relax and joyful for doing some exercise."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "It can help them relax and feel happier, especially when they do exercise regularly."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved version removes the sentence fragment "Because," and uses a complete, formal sentence that explains the effect and links to the idea of exercise — this suits written English better than the shorter, spoken-style fragment often used in Thai conversation.<br><br>	You used paragraphs but the essay does not meet the required four-paragraph structure (introduction with a clear thesis, two body paragraphs with topic sentences, and a conclusion). This makes the essay hard to follow.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Write four paragraphs: (1) short introduction finishing with your thesis (what two activities you will describe), (2) body paragraph about activity A (topic sentence + reason + example), (3) body paragraph about activity B (topic sentence + reason + example), (4) conclusion that restates your thesis and main reasons.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "Nowadays, Many teenagers usually do some activity in their freetime."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Nowadays, many teenagers spend their free time on activities such as playing games and exercising; both help them relax and learn useful skills."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved introduction ends with a clear thesis that previews the two activities you will discuss. A clear thesis helps the reader know what to expect and makes it easier to structure the rest of the essay.<br><br>	You use some correct simple language, but there are repeated mistakes with word choice, spacing, and prepositions. The main challenges are with a few key grammar and spelling points.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "freetime"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "free time"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, "free time" is written as two words. Thai learners sometimes run words together or separate them differently because Thai script and word boundaries work differently; this can cause confusion when writing English words that are actually two separate words.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "an use full skills in real life."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "useful skills in real life."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The correct form is the adjective "useful" (one word). Thai learners often transfer flexible word-formation from Thai (where one root can be used in different positions) and so they may separate or change word forms incorrectly in English. Remember to use the correct English word form (useful).<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Because, it can make them relax and joyful for doing some exercise."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "It can help them relax and feel happier when they do some exercise."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai learners often use sentence fragments starting with "Because" or omit prepositions. In English, we avoid starting a sentence with "Because" when it creates a fragment, and we use verbs and prepositions differently (e.g., "help someone to relax" or "help someone relax"). This is a common Thai → English interference pattern about sentence connectors and prepositions.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Rewrite the essay to 140–190 words with four paragraphs: intro (thesis), two body paragraphs (one activity each), conclusion. Aim for ~40 words per body paragraph for clear development.<br>2. Focus on three language targets: (a) write "free time" as two words, (b) use correct adjective forms (useful, relaxed), (c) avoid sentence fragments with "Because" — write full sentences and check prepositions. Create 5 example sentences for each target and practice them.<br>3. After revising, read your essay aloud or ask a partner to check paragraph structure and the two required activities and reasons.<br><br>	2.0	2.0	1.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
