ding specific details and reasons for why surfing the internet is a pleasure for teenagers makes your explanation much clearer and more convincing, fully addressing the prompt.<br><br>	You made a good attempt at using an appropriate essay style, but the incomplete nature of your response means your ideas are not fully communicated to the reader.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Ensure your essay is complete and all ideas are fully developed to effectively hold the reader's attention and convey your message.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> The unfinished nature of your essay means the reader does not receive all the information or a complete argument, which reduces the overall impact.<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "To effectively communicate your ideas, make sure to complete all paragraphs and fully explain each point. For example, after introducing surfing the internet, expand on its benefits and why teenagers enjoy it, similar to how you discussed playing sport."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In academic writing, it is crucial to present a complete argument. An unfinished essay leaves the reader with unanswered questions and an incomplete understanding of your points.<br><br>	You used paragraphs to structure your ideas, which is a good start for essay organisation.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Work on creating a clear thesis statement in your introduction and ensuring all body paragraphs are fully developed with clear topic sentences and linking words to create better flow.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your introduction clearly states the topic but does not end with a specific thesis statement that outlines the main points of your essay. Additionally, the second body paragraph is not fully developed due to the essay's incompleteness.<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Freetime is essential for teenagers, especially in Thailand where they face significant academic pressure. Engaging in relaxing activities like playing sports and surfing the internet can effectively help them to refresh their minds and develop important life skills."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A clear thesis statement at the end of your introduction tells the reader exactly what your essay will discuss, making your argument easier to follow and your essay more coherent from the start.<br><br>	You use everyday vocabulary in your essay. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "All teenager need their freetime..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "All <b>teenagers</b> need their freetime..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, the word "all" is a plural determiner and must be followed by a plural noun (e.g., "all students," "all books"). In Thai, nouns do not change form for plural, so it's a common interference to forget the '-s' for plural nouns in English.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "study for 8 hours per day make them weakly..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "study for 8 hours per day make them <b>weak</b>..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> "Weakly" is an adverb describing how an action is performed. Here, you need an adjective ("weak") to describe the state of the teenagers (how they *are*). Thai often uses flexible word forms where a single word can function as an adjective or adverb, leading to confusion in English where these forms are distinct.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "...from different school."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "...from a different school." or "...from different schools."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, singular countable nouns often require an article (a/an/the) or a determiner before them. When referring to one of many schools, "a different school" is correct. If you mean multiple schools, "different schools" (plural) is needed. Thai does not use articles, so it's common for learners to omit them or use them incorrectly.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Complete a full essay following the word count and paragraph structure guidelines, focusing on developing all points of the prompt.<br>2. Review subject-verb agreement and plural noun forms, ensuring nouns match their determiners (e.g., "all students" not "all student").<br>3. Practice distinguishing between adjectives and adverbs to ensure you use the correct word form to describe nouns and verbs.<br><br>	3.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
