 disjointed. For example, the transition to Now is event time is abrupt. You could improve the flow by adding a sentence like Today, we celebrate this event with many activities.	Elle, you use basic vocabulary reasonably appropriately. However, there are noticeable errors in grammar and punctuation that sometimes impede meaning. There is also a tendency to use full stops instead of commas, resulting in short, choppy sentences. For example, you write When he find the line. He didn't eat or drink anything. This could be improved to: When he found the path, he didn't eat or drink anything.	2.0	2.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Formative	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
