ers to express themselves. Thai art, in particular, is unique and often reflects our rich culture and history, making it a source of national pride. Drawing a superior piece of work demands patience and attention to detail, which are valuable skills for young people to develop."<br>💡 Explanation: Completing the essay and developing your ideas fully ensures the reader gets all the information they need and a clear understanding of your points. By adding more detail, you provide a more convincing reason for the popularity of drawing among Thai teenagers.</p>	<p>You used an appropriate tone for an article, but the limited development of ideas and some awkward phrasing mean it doesn't fully hold the target reader's attention or communicate ideas with sufficient depth for a B2 level. The register also has some informal elements which can slightly affect the overall impression.</p><p>👉 To Improve: Maintain a consistent register throughout your writing - either formal for a general audience or consistently informal for peers. Focus on developing your ideas more thoroughly to better engage the reader.<br>❌ Weakness: You wrote: "Althought every one know that people need to have their free time..." which mixes a formal approach with a slightly informal phrase ("every one know").<br>✨ Improved: "Although it is widely recognized that individuals require leisure time, insufficient free time for teenagers can lead to negative emotional states. Conversely, adequate free time allows them to relax and rejuvenate before their responsibilities."<br>💡 Explanation: Keeping a consistent formal tone helps establish credibility and makes your writing more professional for a general audience. Developing your points more clearly helps the reader stay interested and understand your message better.</p>	<p>You organized your ideas into paragraphs, which helps the reader follow your main points, but the connections between ideas could be stronger with better linking words and clearer transitions, especially between paragraphs and into the conclusion. The introduction and conclusion also need more specific thesis and restatement of ideas.</p><p>👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases to show clearer relationships between your ideas (e.g., however, therefore, as a result, in addition). Ensure your introduction has a clear thesis and your conclusion effectively summarizes your main points.<br>❌ Weakness: You began a paragraph with "I will begin with drawing..." and used simple connections like "Beside people need to have much time..." which makes the flow less smooth.<br>✨ Improved: "To begin, drawing is a popular pastime; Thai art, specifically, is renowned for its unique style, offering an insight into the artist's personal expression, which contributes to its broad acceptance. Furthermore, creating a refined piece of art requires considerable time and dedication."<br>💡 Explanation: Using specific linking words like "To begin," "specifically," and "Furthermore" helps show the relationship between ideas more clearly and makes your writing flow better. A clear thesis and strong topic sentences guide the reader through your essay.</p>	<p>You used some good vocabulary related to the topic, but there are several recurring grammar patterns that affect clarity, including issues with subject-verb agreement, word form, and complex sentence structure.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Does free time activities is important to Thai teenager?"<br>✨ Correction: "Are free time activities important to Thai teenagers?"<br>💡 Explanation: In Thai, verbs don't change form based on the subject (e.g., singular or plural nouns). In English, we use 'is' for singular subjects and 'are' for plural subjects. 'Activities' is plural, so it needs 'are'. This is a common challenge for Thai learners.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "...if teenager don't have free time much as much they need they can deprase..."<br>✨ Correction: "...if teenagers don't have as much free time as they need, they can become depressed..."<br>💡 Explanation: This sentence has a few issues. Firstly, 'teenager' needs to be plural 'teenagers' to match 'they'. Secondly, 'deprase' is not the correct word form; you need the adjective 'depressed' to describe someone's emotional state. In Thai, words often have flexible forms, but in English, we need to be precise about whether we use a noun, verb, or adjective. Also, the phrase "much as much" is a direct translation; in English, we say "as much... as they need."</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Althought every one know that people need to have their free time, if teenager don't have free time much as much they need they can deprase, But, if they have free time it will make them relax before work."<br>✨ Correction: "Although everyone knows that people need their free time, if teenagers don't have enough, they can become depressed. However, if they do have free time, it will help them relax before school or work."<br>💡 Explanation: This is a very long sentence that combines many ideas without clear separation, known as a run-on sentence or comma splice. In Thai, it's common to connect many clauses without strong punctuation. In English, we need clearer sentence boundaries and stronger linking words (like "Although" at the start and "However" to introduce a contrasting idea) to make the text easier to read and understand.</p>	3.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
