rstly" and "Finally" to guide the reader through your ideas. This makes your writing coherent and easy to follow. 👏 To reach a higher score, try to use a wider range of linking words and phrases. Instead of just "After you have behavior," you could say "Once this initial training is established," or "Building on this foundation of care." This creates a more sophisticated flow between your points. Also, consider how each paragraph's opening sentence clearly signals what the paragraph will be about. Sometimes Thai learners use basic linking words effectively but could benefit from expanding their repertoire to create a more integrated text.	You use everyday vocabulary well, and your meaning is generally clear despite some small errors. For instance, your description of pets making you happy is easy to understand. To improve your language score and aim for a 5, concentrate on accuracy in grammar. I noticed a few areas where we could make some adjustments. For example, "pets is what you needed" should be "pets are what you need." Also, "theirselves" should be "themselves," and "make you more behavior" could be rephrased for clarity, perhaps as "help you develop more discipline" or "teach you responsibility." Thai learners often make these types of grammatical errors, particularly with subject-verb agreement and pronoun usage, because English grammar rules can be quite different from Thai. A good strategy is to read your sentences aloud to catch these kinds of small but important mistakes.	3.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
