levant and imaginative.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Show the Chaos!</b> 💥 You mentioned 'havoc', but what exactly happened? Did people scream? Did secrets get revealed? Details make it funnier!<br>2. <b>Character Motivation!</b> 👤 Why did Sam want to read minds? Was he lonely? Adding a reason makes us care more.	Your story was very engaging! 🤩 The pacing was excellent, especially when the thoughts started reading out loud.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Transitions!</b> ➡️ The jump to finding the remote is a bit fast. How did they know where to look?<br>2. <b>Narrative Voice!</b> 🗣️ Keep the voice steady. The switch to 'some say reverser' at the end felt a bit different from the rest.	Your story flows well because you used good linking words. 🌊 'At first' and 'In the end' guided me through the plot.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Internal Linking!</b> 🔗 Try to use more words like 'meanwhile' or 'because of this' to link sentences inside the paragraphs.<br>2. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 You could split the long middle paragraph when they start searching for the remote.	You used some amazing words like 'intrusive', 'havoc', and 'comrade'! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br>1. <b>Infinitives!</b> 🛠️ Remember: 'pressed the button *to start* it' (not started).<br>2. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Achived' should be 'achieved'. 'Determainted' is 'determined'.<br>3. <b>Word Forms!</b> 🔄 'Judgy' is slang; 'judgmental' is better for a story like this.<br>4. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'In one of the world's famous school' -> 'At one of the...'.<br>5. <b>Pronouns!</b> 👤 'Sam not knowing what to do' is a fragment. 'Sam *did* not know what to do'.	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
