Instead of 'she was shocked', say 'her mouth fell open'.<br>2. <b>Dialogue!</b> 🗣️ Let us hear the wife talking *before* the machine works to show she is talkative.	Your story is easy to follow with a clear beginning, middle, and end. 📑<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Combining!</b> 🔗 'He decided to work... so he decided' -> 'He decided to work... *because* he needed money'.<br>2. <b>Reference!</b> 🔄 Use 'this project' or 'it' instead of repeating the full name.	You used great words like 'introvert' and 'extrovert'! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br>1. <b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Didn't had' -> 'didn't *have*'.<br>2. <b>Word Forms!</b> 📝 'Being a less talkative' -> 'she became less talkative'.<br>3. <b>Pronouns!</b> 👤 'By his self' -> 'by *himself*'.<br>4. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Interested about' -> 'interested *in*'.<br>5. <b>Infinitive!</b> 🏃‍♂️ 'Went to presented' -> 'went to *present*'.	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
