g the cause and effect of Sam's invention.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Elaborate!</b> 🌍 You mentioned 'people needed to leave the city'. What did the city look like? How did the people react? Adding more detail makes the story more immersive.<br>2. <b>Motivation!</b> 🤔 Why did Sam love volcanoes so much? Knowing his motivation can add depth to his character.	I could clearly follow the events of your story, from Sam's invention to the dramatic eruption. 💥<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Awkward Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ Some sentences like 'drone was explosion' make it a bit harder to read. Rephrasing for smoother flow helps.<br>2. <b>Emotional Impact!</b> 😢 You mentioned 'terrible moment'. How did Sam *feel* during this? Showing emotions helps the reader connect.	You used good linking words like 'At first', 'After he created', and 'Finally' to guide the reader through the story. 🚧<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Variety!</b> 🔗 Try using a wider range of linking words. Instead of 'After that', you could use 'Subsequently' or 'Following this'.<br>2. <b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The ending felt a bit rushed. Try to slow down and describe Sam talking with the police more.	You used some good specific vocabulary related to volcanoes! 🌋<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br>1. <b>Word Forms!</b> 📝 'Drone was explosion' -> 'Drone <b>exploded</b>'. 'Volcano can eruption' -> 'Volcano can <b>erupt</b>'.<br>2. <b>Subject-Verb!</b> 🗣️ 'That make the police' -> 'That <b>made</b> the police'.<br>3. <b>Pronoun Agreement!</b> 👤 'People who consequences' -> 'People who <b>faced the</b> consequences'.<br>4. <b>Articles!</b> 🐜 'Professional photograph' -> 'Professional <b>photographer</b>'.<br>5. <b>Punctuation!</b> 🖊️ 'Sam, who is a professional photograph in Thailand' should be set off with commas.	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
