ammar and spelling errors that affect clarity. For example:\n\n- "it make his hair gone fluffy" 12; Corrected: "It makes his hair fluffy." or "His hair becomes fluffy."\n- "they approched him" 12; Corrected: "They approached him."\n\nWork on subject-verb agreement (e.g., "it makes" not "it make"), verb forms, plural/singular agreement, and spelling. Also, try to vary sentence structures by combining simple sentences with words like "although," "because," or "when" to show relationships between ideas.	4.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
