ll parts of the task!	Your email has a friendly tone and uses appropriate greetings and goodbyes for writing to a friend, which is wonderful! You've communicated your ideas in a way that is easy to understand. One small suggestion to make your communication even stronger is to explicitly refer back to Corey's specific ideas when you're responding to them. For example, instead of just "I don't think so, Corey," you could say something like, "About your idea to watch the film, I don't think so, Corey." This makes your response even clearer and more direct for the reader.	Your email is incredibly well-organised, Pheem! You've used paragraphs effectively to separate your different ideas, which makes your email very easy to follow and read 🤩. The way you've linked your thoughts together with words like "So" and by contrasting ideas shows a really strong grasp of how to structure your writing logically. It flows beautifully!	You've used a good range of everyday vocabulary accurately in your email, which helps you express your ideas clearly and naturally 💬. Words like "can't wait," "bother," and "kind of boring" fit the informal tone perfectly. You also generally show good control over your grammar. There were just a couple of small grammatical points that, if refined, would make your writing even more precise. For instance, when talking about batteries running out, "in case it runs out of battery" or "in case it has run out of battery" would be more grammatically accurate than "in case it's ran out of battery." Also, when talking about the film, "the film is" sounds a little more complete than just "film is." These are minor points, and they certainly don't prevent your friend from understanding your message. Keep up the great work with your vocabulary and grammar!	5.0	4.0	5.0	4.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
