effort to organise your ideas into paragraphs, Best, with one for advantages and one for disadvantages. This is a super important step in making your writing clear! 😊 However, within these paragraphs, some of your sentences feel a little disconnected, which can make it a bit tricky for your reader to follow your thoughts. To improve this, try to use more varied linking words and phrases. For example, instead of just starting a new sentence, you could use phrases like 'In addition,' 'On the other hand,' or 'Because of this' to show how your ideas are related. This will help your article flow more smoothly, and everything will connect together beautifully, making it much easier for your reader to understand your great ideas. 🌟	You’ve used some everyday words that are very appropriate for talking about pets, Best, and that’s fantastic! We can certainly understand what you mean. However, to help your writing become clearer and more accurate, let’s focus on a few key areas. For example, watch out for subject-verb agreement. You wrote 'Mostly every familly are have pets,' but it should be 'Almost every family *has* pets.' Also, pay close attention to your verb forms and tenses, like 'My sister cat was have accident' should be 'My sister's cat *had an* accident.' Similarly, 'She don't have fogus with study' should be 'She *doesn't have focus* on her studies.' Spelling is another area to check, like 'familly' should be 'family,' 'fogus' should be 'focus,' and 'chating' should be 'chatting.' These small changes will make a big difference in how easily your reader can understand your message and will show off your excellent ideas even more! Keep practicing, and you'll see great improvement. 💪	3.0	3.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
