ed a good range of everyday words that are appropriate for the topic, Eri, and your grammar was mostly very good. Words like "Science festival," "pick me up," "build a robot," and "pocket money" were all used correctly. There were a few small errors, such as "cousic" instead of "cousin," "it fix it and clean it" instead of "to fix and clean it," and "activite" instead of "activity." These are minor points, and despite them, your message was perfectly clear. No one would struggle to understand what you meant, which is the most important thing. Focusing on careful proofreading for these small spelling and grammar points will truly elevate your writing. Thai speakers sometimes omit articles or have slight difficulties with verb agreement in English; being aware of these common areas can help you fine-tune your accuracy. ✨	5.0	4.0	4.0	4.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
