ed in the task, which is excellent.	You communicate your ideas clearly, Ka-nhom, and your enthusiasm for Songkran definitely comes through. You manage to hold the reader's attention with your straightforward descriptions. To make your article even more engaging for an international audience, think about how you can use different paragraph breaks to separate your introduction, main activities, and your personal feelings about the festival. For example, you could start a new paragraph when you switch from describing what happens to explaining why you love it. This helps your readers follow your ideas more easily and makes your article look more like what people expect to see on a website. Try to imagine someone reading your article online – clear paragraphs really help them enjoy it more.	Your ideas about Songkran are certainly connected, Ka-nhom, and your article flows in a way that is easy to understand. You use simple linking words like "so" and "and" effectively to join your thoughts. To make your writing even more polished and coherent, try breaking your text into paragraphs. For instance, you could have one paragraph introducing Songkran and its dates, another describing the activities, and a third for your personal feelings and a concluding thought. This will help to visually organise your writing and give each main idea its own space. Adding a wider variety of linking words, such as "in addition," "furthermore," or "consequently," could also make your connections between sentences even smoother and more sophisticated. Remember, good organisation makes your article much more appealing and easier to read for your audience.	You use everyday words well, Ka-nhom, and your meaning is always clear, which is great. However, there are a few areas in your grammar that we can work on to make your sentences even stronger. For example, when you wrote "I and my family," it's more natural in English to say "my family and I." Also, be careful with plurals, as "every years" should be "every year" or "all years," and "many activity" should be "many activities." Similarly, "others people" would be "other people," and "beautiful natures" should typically be "beautiful nature" when talking about nature in general, or "beautiful natural places" for specific spots. Finally, "show loves" should be "show love" when speaking generally about the emotion. These small adjustments will help your writing become much more accurate and fluent. In Thai, sometimes pluralisation works differently, which can be a tricky adjustment when learning English. Practising these plural forms and pronoun order will make a significant difference to your writing.	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
