t should be "we **celebrated** and **had** dinner together." The past tense "celebrated" and "had" helps the reader understand that this happened in the past. Another sentence, "we are very so much fun but when, I was in this school on detember it has a big christmas tree," is a little confusing. Perhaps you meant, "We **had** so much fun. However, when I was in this school, in **December**, it **had** a big Christmas tree." Thinking about when things happened (past or present) will help you choose the right word form. Keep practising your sentences, and you'll find they become much clearer. Don't worry, many Thai learners sometimes mix up verb tenses because Thai language doesn't always show tense in the same way English does, but with practice, you'll get the hang of it. 👍	1.0	1.0	1.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A1+	\N	\N	\N	A1	2026
