1034	34059	2025-08-14 13:59:24.517571+00	Thai Food	Food is represent all cultures. Although each culture develop their food by following each environment. In particular, street food is the most accessible kind of food for all generation. Especially Thai street food, which has the top delicious food in the world. Three of the most famous Thai street food are Mhoo Satay, Khao Jee, grilled pork neck with sticky rice.<br><br><br>One of the representative Thai street food is Mhoo Satay. A simple meal featuring a pork shoulder in bite-sized pieces and lemon grass. In addition, some reipe will add the coconut milk to make the taste more sweet. Mhoo Satay is very general breakfast for Thai workers because it's a common street food and easy to find out.<br><br><br>Beside Mhoo Satay, Khao Jee also very symbolic of Thailand, which is a stick rice coast in an egg. In addition, golden mountain sauce and pepper. Khao Jee is strongly show the Thai culture. In northeastern, which is call "Isan", people often offered Khao Jee to monks during Boon Khao Jee festival. This festival are inspired by a story of Buddha. They believe that it's a way of offering food to ancester spirit. Khao Jee also became a beloved comfort food, enjoyed by people of all ages.<br><br><br>Finally, grilled pork neck with sticky rice is a Thai street food that you shouldn't miss, which is a pork neck marinating and grilling with soy sauce, palm sugar and various spices. It's a very stable cuisin in Thailand. In particular, people appreciated for its taste and texture that reflects the Thai culture. Grilled pork neck had been known as "Kor Moo Yang" in Thailand. It's often serve with spicy dipping sauce, which call "Jaew". That's why its became a popular cusine for traveller around the world.<br><br><br>Overall, food is really represent all cultures in the world involve these three beloved comfort food in Thailand, which is Mhoo Satay Khao Jee and grilled pork neck with sticky rice. However, food represent more than just culture, it also represent traditional society and history.	338	\N	Your essay on Thai street food is well-organized and presents clear ideas about different dishes. You have successfully included cultural aspects, especially in your discussion of Khao Jee, and your use of relative clauses and passive structures adds some variety to your writing. To improve, focus on correcting consistent grammatical errors related to subject-verb agreement and verb forms, and be careful with your spelling.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
