stly' (not Fristy) and 'Ultimately' (not Ultimatly).<br>3. <b>Clarity!</b> 👓 Some parts were a bit hard to follow. Make sure your sentences are always clear and to the point.	Your content is relevant as it focuses on an invention story, but it tries to cover too many events from Sam's life. 📖<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Conciseness!</b> 🎯 With a 100-word essay, it's best to focus on one event or a shorter period in the character's life. This will help you elaborate more effectively.<br>2. <b>Plot Development!</b> 🤔 The 'springer' invention felt a bit vague. What does it do? How does it relate to 'high-harvest'?	The story had some interesting ideas, but it was sometimes hard to follow the plot and character motivations. 😅<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Clarity!</b> 🗣️ Phrases like 'George is Sam frist love' are confusing. Is George a person? Is Sam in love with George? Clarify relationships.<br>2. <b>Flow!</b> 🌊 The shifts in time and focus (from uncle to school to France) were abrupt. Guide the reader more clearly through the sequence of events.	You used linking words like 'Initially', 'Subsequently', and 'Finally' to structure your essay. 🚧<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Cohesion!</b> 🔗 Ensure that the connection between your ideas is always clear. Sometimes the information felt disconnected.<br>2. <b>Paragraph Purpose!</b> 🧱 Each paragraph should have a clear main idea. Check if some paragraphs are trying to do too much at once.	You attempted to use some descriptive language! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Fristy' -> '<b>Firstly</b>'. 'Ultimatly' -> '<b>Ultimately</b>'.<br>2. <b>Word Choice!</b> 📖 'High-harvest' and 'springer' are unclear. What do they mean in this context? Choose words precisely.<br>3. <b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ 'Sam who's my uncle' -> 'Sam, who <b>is</b> my uncle'. 'He live' -> 'He <b>lives</b>'.<br>4. <b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🗣️ 'Sam start there relationship' -> 'Sam <b>started his</b> relationship'.<br>5. <b>Tense!</b> 🔙 'I have been visiting there before' -> 'I <b>had visited</b> there before' (past perfect for action before another past event).	4.0	2.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
