. <b>Sensory Details!</b> 👂 What did this new universe sound like? Smell like? Make us feel like we're there!	Your story about the parallel universe was original and very relevant to the prompt. 💡<br>The theme of acceptance was explored thoughtfully.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Elaborate!</b> 🌍 You described the universe as wonderful. What made it wonderful? Adding more details would make it more vivid.<br>2. <b>Opening!</b> 📖 While the opening sets the scene, try to ensure the prompt's exact starting line is used for future assessments.	I could clearly follow Sam's journey and his feelings in the new universe. 😊<br>The ending where he accepts his reality was well-conveyed.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Engagement!</b> 🗣️ Try to make the reader feel more directly connected to Sam's emotions throughout the story.<br>2. <b>Clarity!</b> 👓 Some phrases like 'he didn't saying goodbye' can be rephrased for smoother reading.	You had a clear progression from the real world to the universe and back again. 🔄<br>The use of 'In the end' and 'Finally' helped guide the reader.<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Variety!</b> 🔗 While your organisation is good, try to use a wider range of linking words and phrases to show more complex relationships between ideas.<br>2. <b>Sentence Flow!</b> 🌊 Ensure each sentence flows smoothly into the next, especially when describing events in the new universe.	You have some great ideas in your writing! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br>1. <b>Irregular Verbs!</b> 📝 'Taked care' -> '<b>Took</b> care'. 'Founded the guy' -> '<b>Found</b> the guy'.<br>2. <b>Gerunds!</b> 🛠️ 'Didn't saying goodbye' -> 'Didn't <b>say</b> goodbye'.<br>3. <b>Tense!</b> 🔙 'When I'm grow up' -> 'When I <b>grew</b> up'.<br>4. <b>Articles!</b> 🐜 'Go in other universe' -> 'Go in <b>another</b> universe'.<br>5. <b>Punctuation!</b> 🖊️ 'High - school' -> 'High-school' (no space).	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/f