ddle-aged' fits the character better?</li>	All content is relevant to the task. The target reader is fully informed about Sam's invention and the consequences ('The robot decided to destroy humanity'). The narrative arc is complete.	The student uses story conventions effectively to hold the reader's attention ('One day, the robot created its own feelings'). The shift from creator to victim is handled well.	The text is well organised into clear paragraphs. A variety of cohesive devices are used to good effect ('On the other hand', 'As a result', 'However', 'Finally').	A range of vocabulary is used appropriately ('introverted', 'aggressive', 'stunned'). Grammatical forms are generally controlled, though some errors appear ('didn't knew', 'would apologized', 'stoped'). To improve, focus on correcting basic verb forms after 'didn't' and with modal verbs.	5.0	5.0	5.0	4.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
