ust commas, like in '...decided to go left, Jo is a new police officer...'. 🚦 This makes the story feel like it is moving very fast without any breaks. Using a full stop there would help the person reading your story understand that one idea has finished and a new one is starting. 🛑	You used some great words like 'nervous' and 'weirdo,' but I noticed some trouble with your action words. 🧠 For example, you wrote 'Jo have to go they' instead of 'Jo had to go there.' Because these types of mistakes with past and present words happen quite often, it can be a little bit confusing to know exactly when the story is taking place. ⏳	5.0	3.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
