rning everything to gold and the tragic accident with the girlfriend was like a scene from a movie. The ending where Sam sacrifices himself is very heroic.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you organize your writing. 📋<br><br>1. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 This is the most important thing for you. Breaking the story into chunks will make it much easier to read.<br>2. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 Watch out for 'arraganited' (arrogant) and 'machien' (machine).<br>3. <b>Verb Tenses!</b> ⏳ Try to keep the story in the past tense ('The engine revved', not 'The engine reved up... laser appear').	You have a wonderful imagination! 🌟 The story has a very clear beginning, a shocking climax (the girlfriend turning to gold), and a sad but strong resolution.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The part where he finds the gunpowder happens very fast. You could describe him searching frantically for a way to stop the machine to build more tension.</li><li><b>The Ending!</b> 💭 'No innovation can change love' is a beautiful line! You could explain slightly more what Sam was thinking right before the explosion to emphasize this lesson.</li>	You communicated the emotions of fear and sadness very well. 😢 The reader really feels Sam's regret.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Clarity!</b> 💡 Some sentences are a bit hard to follow because of the grammar. e.g., 'Sam is a gunpowder on his table'. It should be 'Sam <b>saw</b> gunpowder...'.</li><li><b>Sentence Length!</b> 📏 You have some very long sentences. Try splitting them up. Short sentences can make action scenes feel faster and more exciting!</li>	You linked your ideas together with words like 'Then', 'after that', and 'In the end'. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Use Paragraphs!</b> 📑 You must use `<br><br>` to separate the introduction, the accident, and the ending. It is very hard to read one big block of text.</li><li><b>Pronouns!</b> 👤 'The machine the in front of his eyes.' -> 'The machine <b>was</b> in front...'. Make sure you don't miss small words that connect the sentence.</li>	You tried to use some very ambitious vocabulary like 'generating', 'restless', and 'arrogant'. That is great! 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Arraganited' -> '<b>arrogant</b>'. 'Machien' -> '<b>machine</b>'. 'Spreded' -> '<b>spread</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> ⚙️ 'Sam was tried' -> 'Sam <b>tried</b>'. 'She touch' -> 'She <b>touched</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Swallowing across the room' -> '<b>Swallowing</b> the room' or 'Spreading across the room'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Depression of lost' -> 'Depression of <b>loss</b>'.</li>	5.0	4.0	2.0	3.0	Writing	CA	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
