 limits the score.	4.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
3712	28763	2026-02-23 09:08:53.941124+00	Question 1	Dear Mrs Hallam\n\nIn my point of view. It is a good idea to organise a school talent competition. However, the topic of competition may be about musical, such as, sing dance or play a musical instrument because it can make students relax and make student to show there performace. It better than academic competition.\n\nI think students could be for students of all ages because sing or dance everyone can do it.\n\nThat was a great idea for some parents should judge the competition. It will make a good experence to studends and there parents.\n\nFinally, you should receire money for prizes. It will help students so much.	109	14.0	Hi Best! You did a wonderful job of answering all of Mrs Hallam's questions, which is the most important part of the task. 🌟 Your ideas about including all ages and having parents as judges were very clear. For your next email, my 'homework' for you is to focus on adding a warm closing and checking your spelling of everyday words like 'their' and 'receive'. Keep up the great effort! 🚀 All the best, Ed	It was great to see you include a clear response to every point, especially when you wrote 'It is a good idea to organise a school talent competition' and suggested money for prizes. This ensures Mrs Hallam has all the information she needs to move forward with her planning. To make your response even stronger, you could try to expand slightly on why money is a good prize compared to other options like trophies or certificates.	I noticed that you started with a polite 'Dear Mrs Hallam' but didn't include a closing phrase at the end of your email. This makes the message feel a bit like a conversation that was cut off suddenly, leaving the reader waiting for a proper goodbye. Next time, try adding a friendly sign-off like 'Best wishes' or 'Sincerely' followed by your name to make the email feel complete and professional.	I really liked how you used separate paragraphs for each of your ideas! 📝 However, your email felt a little bit like a list of answers rather than a smooth message. To make it flow even better, try using more 'connecting' words between your sentences, like 'I also think...' or 'Regarding the judges...', to help your reader follow along more easily. 🌟	When you wrote 'make student to show there performace', I could understand your meaning, but the small errors in grammar and spelling make the reader work a little harder. The sentence lacks the correct possessive 'their' and the verb 'make' doesn't need 'to' after it. A good tip is to practice using 'make + object + verb' (e.g., 'make students show') and double-check your spelling of common words like 'experience' before finishing.	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
