928	31545	2025-07-22 11:10:12.704742+00	A Place I Love	Hi guys, to day I'm going to talk about Chiang Rai, which is a massive and northern most city, is in Thailand. Chiang Rai have many natures and rich cultures. I'm going to focus on 3 topic: history, foods and natures. Let's talk about history of Chiang Rai.<br><br><br>Chiang Rai was founded by king Mangrai. He choses this place because it full of enviroment and easy to defense from enemy. Chiang Rai used to be capital city in Lanna kingdom, was a huge kingdom in the past, is controll by king Mangrai, after that capital city moved to Chiang Mai. Let's move on to foods. Foods in Chiang Rai are spicy and delicuse. You can find it in Chaing Rai Night Bazaar, is a central of treading in Chiang Rai. For example, Nam Sao is a spicy soup eating with noodles. Hanlay Carry is a spicy curry with pork or chicken. And then I'm going to talk about natures. Natures in Chiang Rai are really beautiful. You can find it around Chiang Rai. Last two years ago. I went to Chiang Rai with my family, I lived there for three days. First day, I was so tired to go to enywhere, so I still in hotel. Days two, I was excited to go to Mae Fah Roung Garden, which is made by grandmother of king Rama 9 and 9, is a big hill that have many flowers, I taked many pictures on there. Then I went to Phu Chi Fah, I found a really beautiful point view. Days three I went to Doi Tung and saw sunrise. Then I go to Singha park to picnic with my family. That all of topic<br><br><br>In concultion, Chiang Rai was a massive city and have a lot of natures. You can go there on winter, it a few cold, but it good for take a picture. I hope you enjoy in Chiang Rai.	320	10.0	Mew, you've shared a very comprehensive overview of Chiang Rai, touching upon its history, food, and natural beauty. You've clearly put a lot of thought into detailing your personal experiences. To elevate your writing, focus on maintaining a consistent and appropriate tone for an essay and refine your grammar and vocabulary for greater precision. Keep up the enthusiasm for your topics!	Mew, you have presented a good amount of relevant information about Chiang Rai, covering its history, food, and natural attractions. You've included specific examples like King Mangrai, Chiang Rai Night Bazaar, Nam Sao, Hanlay Curry, Mae Fah Roung Garden, Phu Chi Fah, Doi Tung, and Singha Park. However, the essay is quite long at 320 words, while the expected word count is 140-190 words. This might lead to some aspects being over-detailed or less focused than necessary for the task, suggesting minor irrelevances or an imbalance in content development. For example, the historical details are quite extensive for an essay about \\"A Place I Love\\" unless directly linked to your personal affection for the place. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to be more selective with details, ensuring all content directly contributes to informing the target reader within the typical word count for this task, making the essay fully relevant and comprehensive.	You communicate straightforward ideas about Chiang Rai, and your enthusiasm for the city is evident. However, the register is inconsistent and often inappropriate for an essay, particularly with phrases like \\"Hi guys\\" and \\"Let's talk about history of Chiang Rai\\" or \\"Let's move on to foods.\\" This informal tone detracts from the essay's overall communicative impact and may not effectively hold the target reader's attention as expected for a formal written task. To improve to a 5, you would need to consistently use the conventions of an essay effectively, maintaining an appropriate formal register throughout, and employ a wider range of linguistic resources to communicate both straightforward and more complex ideas, thus fully engaging the target reader.	You have a clear attempt at structuring the essay with an introduction, sections on history, food, and nature, and a conclusion. You use some basic linking words and phrases like \\"Let's talk about,\\" \\"Let's move on to,\\" \\"For example,\\" and \\"And then.\\" The chronological account of your trip within the \\"natures\\" section helps in coherence. However, the overall organisation could be improved with clearer paragraphing and more varied cohesive devices to smoothly link ideas between and within sections. For example, the history section feels a bit disjointed from the personal connection to the place. To achieve a score of 5, you should organise your text into well-structured paragraphs, using a wider variety of cohesive devices and organisational patterns to create a more fluent and easily digestible piece of writing.	You use everyday vocabulary generally appropriately for the topics discussed, such as \\"massive,\\" \\"cultures,\\" \\"spicy,\\" \\"delicious,\\" \\"beautiful,\\" and \\"tourists.\\" However, there are numerous noticeable errors in vocabulary and grammar that impede the clarity and fluency of the text. Examples include: \\"to day\\" (today), \\"northern most city\\" (northernmost city), \\"Chiang Rai have many natures\\" (Chiang Rai has many natural attractions/areas of natural beauty), \\"choses\\" (chose), \\"enviroment\\" (environment), \\"is controll\\" (is controlled), \\"delicuse\\" (delicious), \\"treading\\" (trading), \\"Last two years ago\\" (Two years ago), \\"enywhere\\" (anywhere), \\"I still in hotel\\" (I stayed in the hotel), \\"Days two\\" (On the second day), \\"Mae Fah Roung Garden, which is made by grandmother of king Rama 9 and 9\\" (unclear meaning, likely \\"granddaughter of King Rama IX\\"), \\"I taked many pictures\\" (I took many pictures), \\"point view\\" (viewpoint), \\"Then I go to Singha park\\" (Then I went to Singha park), and \\"In concultion\\" (In conclusion). These errors, while generally not making the meaning impossible to determine, are frequent and affect the overall control of language. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to use a range of vocabulary and grammatic