ite about all the parts of the question, which is good! You said the story was 'fun and exciting' and had a 'super dog' that was 'very funny.' These are good points about the movie. You also tried to say what happens, like 'they fingt and some moster.' For things that could be better, you mentioned 'the story about famliy, love and good bet evil.' And about the actors, you said 'I exsuly don konw it becas I wacht it but I don't cars how play how.'\n\nHowever, you needed to clearly say three different good things, three clear parts of the story, and three clear things that could be better. Also, you needed to talk about two things about the actors. For example, you only said 'fun and exciting' and 'super dog' for the good things. You didn't give more details or other good things. For 'what happens in the story,' it was a bit hard to understand.\n\nTo get a score of 5, Richter, you need to:\n* Clearly list **three different good things** about the movie and explain them a little. For example, you could say: 'The special effects were amazing,' 'The super dog made me laugh a lot,' and 'The main characters were very interesting.'\n* Clearly say **three things that happen in the story**. For example, 'Superman saves the city from a monster,' 'He meets a new friend,' and 'He learns an important lesson.'\n* Clearly list **three specific things that could be better** in the movie. For example, 'The ending was too fast,' 'Some parts of the story were confusing,' or 'The bad guy was not very scary.'\n* Talk about **two things about the actors**, even if you don't know their names. For example, 'The actor who played Superman was very strong,' or 'The actress who played his friend was very good at showing emotions.'	You wrote some simple ideas, but sometimes it was hard for the reader to understand everything. The way you wrote was friendly, like for an article. But because some sentences were unclear, it made it harder to understand your main points. For example, sentences like 'I sapir some thing it have a poolto or super dog' and 'I sill angre with my mom which she is seelping wayer in the moive' are a bit confusing.\n\nTo get a score of 5, you need to make sure your writing holds the reader's attention and that your ideas are clear. You can do this by making sure your sentences are easy to read and that your ideas connect well from one sentence to the next. This way, the reader can follow your story and ideas without getting confused.	You tried to put your writing into different paragraphs, which is good! You also used some basic connecting words like 'And' and 'but' to join your ideas. However, sometimes the ideas didn't flow very smoothly. For example, when you talked about your mom at the end, it felt a little sudden after talking about the actors.\n\nTo get a score of 5, you need to make your writing very well-organized and easy to follow. You can use different connecting words (like 'also,' 'however,' 'first,' 'next,' 'finally') to show how your ideas are linked. This will make your paragraphs and sentences flow better, like a smooth story.	Richter, you used everyday words that fit the topic, like 'fun and exciting,' 'funny,' 'great,' and 'amazing.' You also used simple grammar quite well. But there are some clear mistakes in spelling (like 'sapir' instead of 'spoil,' 'poolto' instead of 'Pluto,' 'grat' instead of 'great,' 'garci' instead of 'graphics,' 'soud' instead of 'sound,' 'fingt' instead of 'fight,' 'moster' instead of 'monster,' 'Aills' instead of 'aliens,' 'detis' instead of 'defeat us,' 'dack gord' instead of 'dark god,' 'duatful' instead of 'doubtful,' 'famliy' instead of 'family,' 'bet' instead of 'between,' 'exsuly' instead of 'actually,' 'konw' instead of 'know,' 'becas' instead of 'because,' 'wacht' instead of 'watched,' 'cars' instead of 'care,' 'sill angre' instead of 'still angry,' 'seelping wayer' instead of 'sleeping right there' or similar). There are also some grammar mistakes (like 'Will I see in english my mom sad to me that The Thai vios is not good,' 'it have a poolto or super dog,' 'I can say the emotion it a lot,' 'I meat the garci and the soud are gart'). Even with these mistakes, most of your meaning can still be understood.\n\nTo get a score of 5, Richter, you need to use more different everyday words correctly. Also, you need to use simple and some more complex grammar very well, so that there are no mistakes that make it hard for people to understand what you mean. For example, always try to check your spelling and make sure your verbs are in the correct tense.	3.0	2.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	A2+	2026
