ort email, repeating your main points can make the writing feel like it is going in circles rather than moving forward. A great tip is to state your opinion once clearly and then move on to the next topic to keep the flow smooth and interesting! 🌟	I see that you included the phrase 'everyone who join this competition can won it', which uses good everyday vocabulary for the topic. 🧐 However, using 'won' instead of 'win' and missing plurals like 'ages' and 'skills' are small hurdles that make the reader slow down to understand your meaning. A helpful rule to remember is that after 'can' or 'should', we always use the base form of the verb, so 'can win' would be the perfect way to jump over that hurdle next time! 📚	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
