tence with 'Because' in the second paragraph makes the text feel a bit like a broken puzzle rather than a complete picture. Try connecting that sentence to the previous one with a comma to help your thoughts flow more naturally.	When you wrote 'The prizes that you should recieve to winners is instrument ticket', it was a bit confusing because 'receive' usually means to get something, while 'give' is for when you provide a prize. This mix-up acts like a small speed bump for the reader, making them pause to understand your meaning. A helpful tip is to double-check your 'subject-verb' matches, such as saying 'prizes are' instead of 'prizes is'.	5.0	3.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
