 it clear the email is from you! 🌟	Your choice of 'Secondly' and 'Finally' to start your paragraphs really helps the reader follow your arguments like a clear map. 📝 However, this structure makes your email feel a bit like a numbered list of answers rather than a smooth, connected message. To make your writing flow even better, try using more conversational transitions like 'Regarding the judges...' or 'Also, I think...' to help the transition between your ideas. 🚀	I noticed you used some really impressive vocabulary like 'excellent' and 'experienced', which shows a high level of English. 🌟 However, when you wrote 'the results will also clean and clear', the sentence lacks a heartbeat because it is missing the verb 'be'. My tip for you is to keep an eye out for missing 'be' verbs when you are describing things in the future tense to ensure your great ideas are grammatically complete. ✍️	5.0	3.0	3.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
