e story! 🧙‍♂️ The plot progression from waking up to joining a party is clear and satisfying.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Focus on the Narrative!</b> 🎬 The comment about the 'isekai plot' breaks the immersion slightly. Try to show his surprise through his actions instead of telling the reader it's a genre trope.</li><li><b>Character Detail!</b> 👤 You introduced Kei and Aden quickly at the end. Giving them a bit more description earlier or slowing down their introduction would make the ending feel less rushed.</li>	Your story is very engaging and fun to read! 🤩 The dialogue at the end really brings the characters to life.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Tone Consistency!</b> 🎼 The shift from narrative description to internal monologue ('On my god...') is a bit jarring. Try to weave thoughts in more naturally.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Some sentences are a bit long and complex. Breaking them down can make the action clearer.</li>	Your paragraphing is excellent! 🧱 You clearly separated the different stages of the story, which made it very easy to follow.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Smoother Transitions!</b> 🔗 You used 'Suddenly' and 'After', which are good. Try adding words like 'Meanwhile' or 'Consequently' to show how events are connected.</li>	You used some great fantasy vocabulary like 'guild', 'mage', 'brewer', and 'haphazardly'! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Irregular Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Shut' is irregular—the past tense is just '<b>shut</b>', not 'shutted'.</li><li><b>Adjectives vs. Nouns!</b> 🔄 'The placed seems difference' -> 'The place seemed <b>different</b>'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Haird' -> '<b>haired</b>', 'Help full' -> '<b>helpful</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'The party need three people' -> 'The party <b>needs</b>' or '<b>needed</b>'.</li>	3.0	5.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
