h acts like a helpful map for the reader to follow your thoughts. However, writing 'Because the teachers need to know...' as a separate sentence makes the text feel a bit broken, like a puzzle piece that hasn't been clicked into place. A simple tip is to connect your 'Because' reason directly to the previous sentence using a comma instead of a full stop.	When you wrote 'what the students need to knew', I could still understand your meaning, but the grammar choice was a little 'bumpy'. Using the past tense 'knew' instead of the present 'know' makes the reader pause to figure out the timing of your idea. My advice is to double-check your verb forms, especially after the word 'to', where we almost always use the base form of the verb!	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
