s to read your work out loud once you finish writing; this will help you catch repeated words like 'the The' which can make a sentence feel a bit bumpy for the reader.	I see that you included clear paragraph breaks and used signposts like 'About the judge' to move from one topic to the next. This structure acts like a map for the reader, making it very easy to follow your different suggestions without getting lost. To reach the next level, you could try using a few more 'connecting' words like 'However' or 'Furthermore' to help your sentences flow together even more naturally.	When you wrote words like 'unprofitionnal' and 'proficaint', it showed me that you have a great range of vocabulary and are trying to use advanced B1-level descriptions. While these spelling errors are noticeable and might slow the reader down slightly, your meaning is still 100% clear throughout the email. For your next assignment, I recommend focusing on the spelling of common words with 'i' and 'e' to make your writing look much more polished and professional.	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
2914	33957	2025-12-14 09:33:35.428931+00	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of window and couldn't believe my eyes. I was tried from a work because my manager gave me many works to do, but I realized that the next was my birthday.<br><br>After a work, I went to the cake shop to buy my birthday cake. I saw a strange cake, which sold for only 10$, was on top by smile clown. It looked scary but it's cheap, so I bought it.<br><br>I went back to my room and took a shower. After that, I opened the windows and I saw that many people were in front of my condominium and I saw a clown that looked like my cake. I felt stressed and looked my door. After a few minute, my door had knocked by someone.<br><br>I didn't know how to do next and I was embarrassing. I decided to open the door slowly with a nervous feeling.<br><br>The man in front of the door surprised me. He showed that I bought a special cake which was making by a famous influencer called Mr. Shan. I was surprised and they gave me 10000 $. I was happy with that.	192	15.0	Hello Peptine! 👋<br><br>What a fantastic plot twist! 🎁 I went from feeling scared for you (scary clown!) to feeling happy (prize money!). You did a great job manipulating the reader's emotions. The 'strange cake' was a very creative clue.<br><br>I have a few tips to make it perfect! 📋<br>1. <b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ Don't forget 'the'. 'I looked out of window' -> 'out of <b>the</b> window'.<br>2. <b>Passive Voice!</b> 🛠️ When describing who made the cake, say 'made by', not 'making by'.<br>3. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'I was embarrassing' means *you* were embarrassing people! You meant 'I was <b>embarrassed</b>'.	You created a very engaging story with a satisfying surprise ending. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>The Door Scene!</b> 🚪 You said you 'looked my door'. Did you lock it? Peek through it? clarifying this action would build more suspense.</li>	You held my attention really well! I wanted to know what the clown would do. 🤡<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>