. Could you give one specific example of something they destroyed? (e.g., 'crushed the school gate').</li>	Your story has a very interesting concept, but the events can be a bit confusing. 🧩<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing the Attack!</b> ⏱️ The robot attack happens very quickly. Slowing down to describe the initial chaos and Ava's reaction more would build suspense.</li>	Your use of paragraphs helps to separate different stages of the story. 🧱<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Flow!</b> 🌊 Some sentences are very long and contain many ideas. Breaking them down into shorter, clearer sentences would make your story easier to follow. For example, 'no one came to school even the teacher, but I didn't noticed any things, I had been film this movie since 6 am. till 8 pm. last scene, I was very proud of my project.' is a lot to take in!</li>	You used relevant vocabulary like 'obsessed', 'robot', and 'project'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Infinitives!</b> 🛠️ 'Decided to made' -> 'decided to <b>make</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Huge of robot' -> '<b>huge robot</b>'. 'Terrify' -> '<b>terrified</b>'.</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'I had to stayed' -> 'I had to <b>stay</b>'. 'No one came... but I didn't noticed' -> 'I didn't <b>notice</b>'.</li>	4.0	3.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
