up to that reveal with a bit more interaction or hints before he shows up could make it even more impactful.</li>	You clearly conveyed the wonder and mystery of seeing a dragon. 🤩<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Emotional Arc!</b> 🎢 The quick shifts between confusion ('weird looking living thing'), determination (internet café), and the final dream/coma twist could be smoothed out for a more impactful emotional journey.</li>	You presented a clear sequence of events in your story. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing is Key!</b> 🧱 The story is currently one long block of text. Breaking it into paragraphs (e.g., one for the initial sighting, one for internet research, one for the park encounter, and one for the twist) would greatly improve readability.</li><li><b>Sentence Flow!</b> 🌊 Some sentences are very long and contain multiple ideas. Breaking them into shorter, distinct sentences would make your story easier to follow.</li>	You used good descriptive words like 'weird', 'internet café', and 'similar'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'Flied pass' -> '<b>flew past</b>'. 'I seen' -> 'I <b>saw</b>'.</li><li><b>Contractions!</b> 🛠️ 'It's was there' -> 'It <b>was</b> there'.</li><li><b>Conditional!</b> ⚙️ 'It if fly to me' -> 'It <b>flew</b> to me'.</li><li><b>Homophones!</b> 📝 'Ran outside to see what it was but it was gone' -> 'Ran outside to see what it was, but it <b>had gone</b>'.</li>	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
