al conversation and don't forget to add a friendly sign-off like 'Best wishes' at the end. 🌟	I see that you used paragraphs for each of your points, which helps the reader navigate your suggestions! 📝 However, many of your paragraphs are only a single sentence, which makes the email feel a bit like a list of separate ideas. To help your writing flow even better, try using more 'internal' connectors between your sentences, like 'Furthermore' or 'In addition to that', to bridge your ideas together more naturally. 🌟	When you wrote 'there's many student', I noticed a small hurdle with subject-verb agreement and plural nouns. 🌟 While your meaning is 100% clear, these little slips act like tiny speed bumps for the reader. A great tip for your next piece is to double-check that words like 'many' or 'some' are always followed by plural nouns, like 'many students'. ✍️	5.0	4.0	3.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
