 of notes. For your next task, try including these polite 'bookends' to make your email feel more professional. 🌟	When you wrote 'About the prizes, we should give a snacks...', you used a great signposting phrase that acts like a roadmap for the reader. 📝 However, each paragraph feels a little bit like an answer to a list of questions rather than a smooth, connected message. To help your writing flow even better next time, try using more 'internal' connectors between and within your paragraphs, like 'Additionally' or 'In my opinion...', to make the flow even more natural. 🌟	It was great to see you use 'perform their abilities' and 'participate,' as this shows you have a strong range of B1 vocabulary! 🌟 However, some small 'hiccups' like 'a snacks' and 'a medals' act like tiny speed bumps for the reader because they mix up singular and plural forms. For your next piece, try to double-check that your articles (like 'a') match the nouns (like 'snacks') to make your sentences flow perfectly! 💡	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
