on focused on your helpful suggestions throughout the email. To reach an even higher level, try to use slightly different phrases for your opinions so you aren't repeating 'In my opinion' quite so often. 🚀	I see that you used clear paragraphs to separate your different ideas, such as when you transitioned from the age of the participants to the topic of the judges. This logical structure makes your email very easy to navigate, much like a well-marked path through a garden. You can make the flow even smoother by using a variety of linking words like 'However' or 'Furthermore' to connect those paragraphs together. 📝	Your choice of words like 'suitable', 'professional', and 'participate' shows you have a wonderful range of vocabulary for this level. When you wrote 'the winner should be award', the sentence lost its 'heartbeat' slightly because it requires the passive form 'awarded' to be grammatically complete. Paying close attention to verb endings like '-ed' when something is being done to someone will make your writing much stronger! 🚀	5.0	5.0	4.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
2966	34061	2025-12-14 15:55:00.716666+00	Term 2 Midterms 2025-6	Me too! I really happy that we are going camping this weekend! I'm looking for it.<br><br>First, about how should we go to campsite. In my view, I prefer to take the train on Saturday morning. because I think the train is way faster than a car. And I don't like to sit in the car for a long time. So I think we should take the train.<br><br>Then, about what will we be going to cook. I Disagree about cook sausages because I don't like a sausage. So can We cook the food form eggs. I think it easy too.<br><br>Last, about what should we bring to stay warm I think we should bring a jacket or a heater that we can bring with.<br><br><br>See you soon, Vegas	129	14.0	Hi Vegas! 👋<br><br>Good clear email! I understood all your preferences easily. "Cook the food form eggs" is a creative idea - omelettes on a campfire? Yum! 🍳<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>To Be!</b> 🐝 "I really happy" -> "I <b>am</b> really happy".<br>2. <b>Phrasal Verbs!</b> 🆙 "looking for it" -> "looking <b>forward to</b> it".<br>3. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 "food form eggs" -> "food <b>from</b> eggs".\n	You answered all the questions. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Logic!</b> 💭 "The train is way faster than a car" - Is it? Usually trains stop a lot! But it's your opinion, so it's okay.</li>\n	Your tone is polite but a bit formal. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Register!</b> ⚖️ You used "First", "Then", "Last". This sounds a bit like an essay! For a friend, try "To start with", "About the food", "Finally".</li>\n	Your structure is very clear because of the sequencing words. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linking!</b> 🔗 Try more natural linkers like "By the way" or "On another note".</li>\n	"Heater" is a good word choice! 👏<br><br>Fix these:<br><li><b>Structure!</b> 🏗️ "I really happy" -> "I <b>am</b> really happy".</li><li><b>Verbs!</b> ⚙️ "bring with" -> "bring with <b>us</b>" (bring needs an object usually).</li>\n	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writin