ke a direct conversation. This, along with a bit more focus on grammar, will make your communicative style even stronger! 🚀	It was great to see you use 'Then' and 'Finally' to move between your different points about the judges and the prizes. These signposts act like a map for the reader, helping me follow your thoughts from one paragraph to the next without getting lost. For an even smoother flow, you could try using introductory phrases like 'Regarding the prizes...' to transition into a new topic even more naturally. 🚀	Ken, I really liked some of the words you chose, like 'professional'! 🌟 However, I noticed there were quite a few small mistakes throughout your writing, such as 'students are agree' and 'they can able.' These errors happen quite often and can make it a little tricky for the reader to understand exactly what you mean. For your next piece, I'd like you to focus on the basics—making sure your subjects and verbs work together and that every sentence is complete. You have great ideas, and better grammar will help them shine! 💡	5.0	3.0	4.0	2.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
