ad of 'I'm not really agree.' 🚀	I see that you used clear paragraphs for each point, such as starting a new section with 'In my opinion...', which acts like a roadmap for your teacher. This structure makes it very easy for Mrs Hallam to follow your logic without getting lost in the text. To make your writing flow even more smoothly, try adding a closing phrase like 'Best regards' or 'Sincerely' before your name to finish the email professionally. 📝	Your use of words like 'talented', 'bias', and 'portfolio' shows a great range of vocabulary, but the phrase 'Our school have' shows a little slip in subject-verb agreement. This is like a small 'hiccup' in the rhythm of your writing because the subject (school) is singular and needs a singular verb (has). Try to double-check your 's' endings on verbs and plurals when you finish writing to ensure everything matches up perfectly!	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
