udges' to move from one topic to the next acts like a clear signpost for the reader. It helps the email flow logically from the idea of age limits to the judging process without any confusion. To make your writing even smoother, you could try using a 'linking sentence' that connects two paragraphs together, like 'While the students are important, we also need to think about the judges'.	You used some very sophisticated vocabulary like 'biased' and 'beneficial' to express complex thoughts—that's fantastic! 🌟 One thing to watch out for is your sentence structure. Sometimes, you wrote fragments like 'Not just people over 15' and 'Since parents can be biased' as separate sentences. These actually belong with the sentence before them. By connecting these pieces with a comma, your writing will flow even more perfectly! 💡	5.0	5.0	5.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
