3765	34931	2026-02-23 11:08:00.48494+00	Article	In my opinion, laughing is extremely beneficial for both physical and mental health. When I was going to do an exam, my mind went blank and I was really stressed. Instead of relaxed myself, I laughed without nothing. Inspite of some people may think laughter is just a simple reaction to something hilarious. But it actually plays an important role in enhancing our overall well-being. When we laugh, our body releases positive chemicals that make us feel relaxed and help us reduce stressed. As a result, we can handle pressure more effectively.\n\nFuthermore, laughter strengthens relationship and sharpen our presence. People who laugh often usually seem friendly, kindly and more positive. For instance, sharing a jokes with friends can bring people closer together. In addition, laughing may even support better health in a long terms.\n\nFor these reasons, I strongly believe that laughing often is very good for us. It not only makes life more enjoyable, but also makes us healthier and build stronger connections with others. Therefore, we should try to find happiness in everyday situations and not takes life too seriously.	183	19.0	Hi Frame! Your article was a joy to read, especially the way you connected laughter to both mental health and friendship. You have a wonderful ability to use high-level vocabulary to express your thoughts. My main 'homework' for you is to keep an eye on your sentence structures when using linking phrases like 'in spite of' or 'instead of'—mastering those will make your writing feel incredibly smooth. All the best, Ed	Your inclusion of the personal story 'When I was going to do an exam, my mind went blank' was a wonderful choice because it gives the reader a concrete example of stress. This makes your argument about the benefits of laughter feel much more authentic and convincing. To make your article even more complete, you could name one specific thing that makes you laugh, such as a favorite sitcom or a specific type of joke.	It was great to see you use phrases like 'laughter strengthens relationship and sharpen our presence' to explain complex social ideas so clearly. This sophisticated approach really holds the reader's attention and makes the article feel like it belongs in a real magazine. One small way to make it even more engaging would be to add a catchy title at the top to hook your audience right away! 🌟	The way you used 'Furthermore' and 'For these reasons' to connect your paragraphs acts like a clear map for the reader. This logical flow ensures that your ideas about health and social connections are tied together perfectly. To reach even higher, you might try starting your next article with a question to the reader, which can make your well-organized points feel even more interactive.	Your choice of 'positive chemicals' and 'enhancing our overall well-being' shows a fantastic range of vocabulary that really impressed me. While your meaning is always clear, some small 'hurdles' like 'Inspite of some people may think' can make the reader slow down for a second. A great tip is to remember that 'in spite of' usually needs a noun or an '-ing' verb after it, so you could try 'In spite of what people think' next time! 🚀	5.0	5.0	5.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
