ntal health became one of the	337	11.0	Overall, Aunna, you've done a good job of tackling an interesting and relevant topic for teenagers. There are some excellent ideas in your writing, and you clearly have a point of view on whether friends or parents have more influence. To help your writing become even clearer and more persuasive, we'll focus on making sure your ideas flow smoothly and that your grammar and word choices are as precise as possible. Keep up the great effort, as improving these areas will truly help your thoughts stand out!	You've made a really solid start by addressing the question about who influences teenagers more – friends or parents – and you've included "clothes and fashion" and "studying" as the prompt asked. You even thought of your own idea, "mental healthress," which is fantastic! That shows you're thinking deeply about the topic. To get a higher score, like a 5, try to expand on your points more fully. For example, when you talk about clothes, you could explain *why* friends' opinions are more persuasive than parents' instructions, giving specific examples of situations and peer pressure, not just different types of clothing. Sometimes, the end of your essay felt a little rushed, so ensure all your ideas are fully developed and explained, giving the reader a complete picture of your thoughts.	You've tried to write in a formal style, which is exactly what's needed for an essay like this, and you've definitely aimed to inform the reader about your perspective. That's a great approach! However, sometimes the way you've expressed your ideas makes the essay feel a little less formal or clear. For instance, phrases like "Start of with" could be replaced with more academic alternatives such as "Firstly," or "To begin with." To really impress and achieve a score of 5, focus on consistently using language that is precise and appropriate for an academic audience throughout your entire essay. This will help your arguments come across with greater 