1026	33961	2025-08-14 10:32:09.583872+00	Thai Food	An incredibly wonderful dishes always come from a well developing country. Although, every single culture has their own tradional food in each. In Thailand we are famous for streetfood. Three of the most representative Their streetfood are Moo-Ping, Fried Insect and Luk-Chin (Their meatballs).<br><br><br>Moo-Ping is one of the most representative Thai streetfood. It's a grilled pork with a wooden stick in it, Moo-Ping usually come with a sticky rice. First, you have to stick a wooden stick in a pork, then cover it with sweet souce, heat it on the stove. It's symbotize their working culture because Thai peo eat Moo-Ping in the rush hour on the way to work.<br><br><br>Besides Moo-Ping, another representative Thai streetfood is Fried Insect or Malang-Tod. Malang-Tod is a different type of fried insect with a salty sauce and served in plastic bag and spoon. The recipe are to try any eatible insect that you prefer alive in the pan with lots of oil, hang them on a towel paper to remove oil from frying and spray salt's sauce in to the insect. Malang-Tod represent how abundant Thai natural cycle in insect and nature.<br><br><br>Finally, one of the most representative Thai streetfood is Their culture, which is Luk-Chin. It's a Thai meatball which contain flour and pork, sometimes maybe beef. You have to blend the flour and pork, then boiled it in round shape with heat it on a stove. Luk-Chin symbotize Thai working culture as well as Moo-Ping because everything in Bangkokc are in a hurry such as a traffic in the morning and the evening when the work is done.<br><br><br>In conclusion, streetfood like Moo-ping, Fried Insect or Luk-Chin represents Thai culture and spread it around the world. It's a soft power that embrace the interest towards Thai gargantuatic culture.	298	\N	Overall, your essay effectively introduces three examples of Thai street food and attempts to explain their cultural significance. You have a good grasp of organizing your ideas into paragraphs, and you use some good vocabulary. To improve, focus on refining your sentence structure, especially using relative clauses and passive structures, and pay close attention to common spelling errors.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
