ail to explain what the 'tickets' were for at the very beginning—was it for the same competition where she met Eve? This would make the link even stronger for the reader. 📝	The way you captured Lois's inspiration—'deep in her heart, she wanted to be that girl's accompanist'—was truly moving! 🚀 Using emotional stakes like this makes your story stand out and holds the reader's attention from beginning to end. For your next piece, try to keep your characters' 'voice' in the past tense during dialogue tags (e.g., 'she gasped' instead of 'Lois gasped') to keep the storytelling conventions consistent.	I really liked how you used '5 years later' to mark a big jump in time. It worked like a 'fast-forward' button in a movie, helping the reader follow Lois's growth into a pianist. 📝 To make your paragraphs even smoother, try to use a few more 'Action' connectors like 'Eventually' or 'Without warning' to show the reader exactly when the next important event is about to happen.	You used some fantastic B1-level words like 'accompanist' and 'impression', which showed you have a great range of vocabulary for this topic! 🌟 While your meaning was always 100% clear, there were some 'tense jumps' where you moved from the past to the present (like 'she practice' and 'she plays'). My best tip for next time is to read your work back and make sure every verb stays in the past tense to keep your story's timeline steady. 💡	5.0	4.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
997	28763	2025-08-12 13:00:00+00	Thai Food	Food is the most important thing for everyone. If you don't eat food many days can have an affect on yours. We need food can help us happy when you eat it. Although every cultures in the world don't have same environment. So this make every cultures develops it own from their ingredients that have in their environment. In Thailand, Wherein have perfect environment for growing plants or hunting food. So this make Thai food interesting. But I think the northern Thai food are the most amazing, such as, Khao sai, Gaang hong lay and Gaang Ha<br><br><br>One of the best northern Thai food is Khao sai Which is a Thai curry noodle soup with Burmese and Chinese influences. It has egg noodles in a rich, flavorfal curry broth and is topped with crispy fried noodles. Ingredients of Khao sai are egg noodles, chicken drumsticks, coconut milk, red onion and fried egg noodles for crispy topping. To make Khao sai, first deep-fry some egg noodles until crispy and set them aside. Then cook the curry in oil until fragrant, add chicken and stir to coat. Next pour in coconut milk and chicken broth. Then season with fish sauce, sugar. Simmer until the chicken is tender and boil the noodles. Then put them in a bowl, pour the curry and the chicken on top and add crispy noodles.<br><br><br>A second interesting northern Thai food is Gaang hong lay, which is pork curry with Burmese roots. Ingredients of Gaang hong lay are pork, garlic and red chilli. To make Gaang hong lay, first fry garlic, shallots and ginger until fragrant. Then add spices. Add cinnamon, cloves and dried chilli. Then put in pork and stir until coated with spices. Add water and simmer until pork is tender. Season with fish sauce and sugar. Finally cook until the sauce thicken.<br><br><br>A third amazing northern Thai food is Gaang Ha. which is stir - fried mixed carry and made by combining leftovers curries, glass noodles and some vegetables such as, Kaffir lime leaves , galangal. To make Gaang Ha, first stir - fry curry paste add pork and vegetables Then mix in noodles and herbs with everything is cooked and flavor full.<br><br><br>In conclusion, Thai food are very amazing. I think it's the best option for almost that have spicy taste. That the taste that they tell their live style. They are very good and can keep us happy to eat spicy food to live.	411	\N	You've made a good start on this essay about Thai food, Best! Your writing is generally clear, and you've provided some interesting details about specific northern Thai dishes. You clearly enjoy the topic, which makes your essay engaging. To improve, focus on strengthening your introduction with a clear main idea, varying your vocabulary to avoid repetition, and paying close attention to common grammar and spelling mistakes.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
