sier for the reader to follow.	I noticed that you used sequencing words like 'So', 'On the way', and 'In the evening' to guide the reader through the events of your story. This shows you have a very logical mind and know how to connect ideas in a way that is easy for the reader to follow! For your next story, try to use some 'Action' linkers like 'Suddenly' or 'Without warning' to make the moment they find the tickets feel even more exciting. 🚀	When you wrote 'on the way' and 'so she and her friends' with lowercase letters at the start of your sentences, it made the writing look a bit unfinished. 📝 Always remember that every new sentence needs a big capital letter to give it a strong start! Also, try to practice using 'were' instead of 'was' for plural groups (like Lois and her friends) to make your grammar sound even more natural and polished. 🌟	5.0	2.0	3.0	2.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A2+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
