📋<br>1. <b>Past Tense Consistency!</b> 🛠️ 'Try to figured out' should be 'try to <b>figure</b> out' or 'tried to figure out'.<br>2. <b>Tense Agreement!</b> ⏳ 'Making sure that I have locked' should be 'making sure that I <b>had</b> locked'.<br>3. <b>Punctuation!</b> 🛑 Sometimes your dialogue is a little hard to follow. Make sure each person's speech starts a new line and uses quotation marks.	You nailed the story prompt with a very creative and detailed narrative! 🌟 The escalating tension from the creature sighting to the safety room and the final dream reveal was excellently executed. All content was highly relevant and engaging.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sensory Details!</b> 👁️ You used great visual descriptions. Adding more sounds (the creature's growl, the shattering door) or smells (dust, fear) would make the experience even more immersive.</li><li><b>Dialogue Clarity!</b> 💬 Your dialogue with your mom and dad at the end is very funny. Ensuring each person's speech is on a new line makes it easier to read.</li>	This is a truly engaging narrative! 🤩 You skillfully built suspense and then delivered a satisfying, humorous twist. The pacing and emotional journey were very well managed.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Show, Don't Tell!</b> 🎬 Instead of saying 'I was terrified', you showed it through your actions ('I quickly hide', 'I was making sure I locked all the windows'). Continue this excellent practice!</li>	Your paragraphing is exceptional! 🧱 You used clear breaks to separate each stage of the terrifying experience, which greatly enhanced the readability and pacing of your story.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Cohesive Devices!</b> 🔗 While your paragraphs are well-separated, sometimes the sentences within them could be linked more smoothly. Words like 'As a result', 'Meanwhile', or 'Despite this' can help create a stronger flow.</li>	Your vocabulary is rich and ambitious, using words like 'disgusting-looking', 'terrified', 'shattered', and 'realized'. 📚<br><br>Here are some fixes:<br><li><b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Try to figured out' -> 'try to <b>figure</b> out' or 'tried to <b>figure</b> out'.</li><li><b>Tense Consistency!</b> ⏳ 'Making sure that I have locked' -> 'making sure that I <b>had</b> locked'.</li><li><b>Punctuation in Dialogue!</b> 💬 For example, for 'My mom shouted "look what happend"', remember to put a comma before the speech: 'My mom shouted, "Look what happened!"'</li>	5.0	5.0	5.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
