se is a great skill to master for exams! 🚀	Using vivid descriptions like 'adrenaline that coursed through her body' really helped me feel Lois's excitement as if I were there with her. This kind of emotional language acts like a magnet, holding the reader's attention from the first sentence to the last. Keep looking for these 'feeling words' in your future writing to keep your stories engaging and professional. 🌟	I noticed how you used the phrase 'The rest of the night was a blur' to move the story from the concert to the next morning. This works like a smooth 'fade-to-black' in a movie, helping the reader travel through time without feeling confused. For your next piece, continue using these time-marker phrases to guide your reader through the different scenes of your narrative. 📝	Your use of the past perfect in 'the singer had photobombed her' was a brilliant way to describe an action that happened before she looked at the phone. Using complex tenses like this adds 'layers' to your writing and shows you have great control over English grammar. Just be careful with small 'tense jumps' like 'she walks in'—try to keep everything in the past tense to keep the story's heartbeat steady! ✨	5.0	5.0	5.0	5.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
