<b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The invention and its success happen quite quickly. You could expand on the challenges of building it or the excitement of testing it.</li>	Your paragraphing is good, clearly separating the problem, the solution, and the result. 🧱 This makes your story easy to follow.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Connecting Ideas!</b> 🔗 You used 'So' and 'And finally'. Try to add more varied linking words like 'As a result', 'Consequently', or 'Afterwards' to create a smoother flow.</li>	You used good vocabulary like 'invention' and 'prototype' (even if misspelled). 📚<br><br>Here are some corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Desing' -> '<b>Design</b>', 'buit' -> '<b>built</b>', 'atmosfear' -> '<b>atmosphere</b>', 'literly' -> '<b>literally</b>', 'ture' -> '<b>true</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Couldn't wanted to live' -> '<b>didn't want to live</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'I feel' (past tense) -> 'I <b>felt</b>'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Cold air for the sky' -> 'cold air <b>from</b> the sky'.</li>	5.0	3.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
2932	33961	2025-12-14 09:35:14.904879+00	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. It was snowing! People from other country wouldn't be surprise at all but it's snowing in Thailand.<br><br>As soon as I saw the snow falling down from the sky, I rushed to open the door while shouting loudly to get others attention. I was always. That one person who hates winter, it felt like living in another type of hell and the only good thing about winter is Christmas. Now that it was snowing, I became the most happy person on Earth. Two days passed by, I went outside and it was all covered by snow. Me and my little sister was trying to build a snowman, we looked just like Elsa and Anna! I never experienced this before, never knew it would felt this amazing.<br><br>Sometimes the weather can be different, just like people that are both hot and cold. If you hated something, try to be more open mind about it first, or else you might loose it forever.	172	19.0	Hello Gut-Jung! 👋<br><br>What an uplifting story! ❄️ Your excitement about snow in Thailand was infectious. I loved your journey from hating winter to becoming 'the most happy person on Earth' because of this unique experience. The comparison to Elsa and Anna was a lovely touch!<br><br>I have a few tips to make your writing even more enchanting! 📋<br>1. <b>Word Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'Wouldn't be surprise' should be 'wouldn't be <b>surprised</b>'. 'Would felt' should be 'would <b>feel</b>'.<br>2. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'I was always' is a bit incomplete. 'I was always <b>that one person</b>...'.<br>3. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Loose it forever' should be '<b>lose</b> it forever'.	You fulfilled the prompt perfectly, starting with the given sentence and crafting a delightful, personal story about snow in Thailand. 🌟 Your philosophical reflection at the end adds a wonderful layer of depth.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Describe the Snow!</b> 🎨 You said it was snowing. What did it look like? Was it soft, powdery, glistening? Adding more sensory details would make the scene even more magical.</li><li><b>Shouting!</b> 🗣️ You shouted loudly 'to get others attention'. What did you shout? Adding a line of direct speech would make that moment even more dramatic!</li>	Your strong personal voice and the clear progression of your feelings make this story very engaging. 🤩 The concluding reflection is a powerful way to end.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The jump from seeing the snow to two days later could be bridged with a short phrase like 'After a joyous day...' or 'For the next two days...'.</li>	Your paragraphing is excellent, guiding the reader smoothly from the initial surprise to the joyful experience and finally to the reflective conclusion. 🧱 This is very well-structured.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Variety!</b> 🎼 You have a good mix of simple and complex sentences. Continue to experiment with varying sentence lengths to control the rhythm and emphasis of your writing.</li>	You used strong vocabulary like 'rushed', 'experienced', 'philosophical', and 'open mind'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Word Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'Wouldn't be surprise' -> 'wouldn't be <b>surprised</b>'.</li><li><b>Verbs!</b> ⏳ 'It felt like living' -> 'it <b>felt like I was living</b>'. 'Would felt' -> 'would <b>feel</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'I was always' -> 'I was always <b>that one person</b>'.</li><li><b>Homophones!</b> 📝 'Loose it forever' -> '<b>lose</b> it forever'.</li>	5.0	5.0	5.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
