ed out of despair', describe your tears or the lump in your throat.</li><li><b>Bigfoot's Appearance!</b> 🦍 You said it was 'tall so tall'. Could you add one more detail about its fur, eyes, or sound to make it even scarier?</li>	You successfully conveyed a powerful sense of fear and urgency throughout the story. 😱 The dialogue with Liam added to the realism of the situation.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing with Punctuation!</b> 🛑 The story reads very breathlessly because of the lack of full stops and paragraph breaks. Breaking it into shorter sentences and paragraphs would allow the reader to pause and feel the tension more.</li>	You presented a clear chronological sequence of events, which is great. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing is Key!</b> 🧱 This is the single biggest area for improvement. Splitting your long text into logical paragraphs would dramatically enhance readability and structure.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Some sentences are very long and contain multiple ideas. Breaking these into shorter, distinct sentences would make your story easier to follow.</li>	You used strong vocabulary related to fear and the outdoors, like 'despair', 'hiking', and 'flare gun'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Belive' -> '<b>believe</b>', 'coverd' -> '<b>covered</b>', 'thoregh' -> '<b>through</b>'.</li><li><b>Irregular Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Founded us' -> '<b>found</b> us'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Dengerous animal' -> '<b>dangerous animals</b>'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🔄 'Crying won't me and my boyfriend' -> 'crying won't <b>help</b> me and my boyfriend'.</li>	5.0	4.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
