ext time, try to add a catchy title at the top to make it look even more like a professional website article!	I noticed that you used 'so' and 'because' effectively to link your thoughts together within the text. 📝 However, your article was written as one long single paragraph. For your next piece, try to divide your work into sections—one for your introduction, one for the local area, and one for your advice. This 'breathing space' makes your writing much easier for the reader to navigate and follow! 💡	When you wrote 'there has only one park', I understood that you were describing the location, but using 'has' instead of 'is' makes the sentence feel a bit 'bumpy'. 💡 Using the 'there is/there are' structure correctly is a great way to make your writing sound more natural. A helpful tip is to check your spelling of words like 'Despite' and 'government' to make your writing look even more polished! 🌟	5.0	4.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
