 a professional article.	I noticed you used 'Because of that' to start your final section, which acts like a clear signpost for the reader. This choice helps the text flow logically from your local examples to your general advice about health. To make your writing even more sophisticated, try using 'connecting' words like 'Furthermore' or 'However' to link your ideas within the paragraphs themselves.	When you wrote 'It make your body more healthy', the meaning was perfectly clear, but the missing 's' on the verb creates a small hurdle for the reader. You have a good range of everyday vocabulary like 'essential' and 'healthy,' but there are frequent slips with basic grammar like subject-verb agreement. A great tip for your next draft is to double-check that singular subjects like 'it' or 'the sport' always take a verb with an 's' in the present tense.	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
