 know exactly what they are about to dive into!	I noticed that you used excellent structures like 'not only... but also' to connect your ideas. 📝 However, your article was written as one long single paragraph. For your next piece, try to divide your work into sections—one for your introduction, one for the local area, and one for your advice. This 'breathing space' makes your writing much easier for the reader to navigate! 💡	When you wrote 'every people' and 'reduce stressful', I could still understand your meaning perfectly, but these small errors with word forms act like little speed bumps. 💡 In English, 'people' is already plural, so we usually say 'every person' or 'all people', and 'stressful' is an adjective, so we 'reduce stress'. Keep practicing these noun and adjective forms, and your sentences will have a much smoother heartbeat!	5.0	4.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
