 informal way, and the many mistakes make it harder for the reader to fully follow your ideas.	You connect your ideas using basic linking words like "and" and "because." There's a general flow of ideas, starting with the movie, then its story, and then its importance. However, the text is not well-organised into clear paragraphs, and the long, run-on sentences make it difficult to read. This means the text is connected in a basic way, but it lacks overall structure.	You use basic vocabulary reasonably well, such as "movie," "story," "man," "helped," "award," "actor." However, there are many grammar mistakes and spelling errors that often make it hard to understand what you mean.\n\n**To help you improve, here are some things to practice:**\n\n*   **Capital Letters:** This is very important! Remember to use a capital letter for the start of *every new sentence*. Also, always use a capital letter for names of specific things (called "proper nouns") like:\n    *   **Names of people:** such as "Ray Milland" (your text: "ray milland")\n    *   **Specific events/titles:** such as "The Lost Weekend" (your text: "The lost weekend"), "World War 2" (your text: "world war 2"), "Academy Award" (your text: "academy award")\n    *   **The first word of a sentence:**\n        *   *Your text says:* "A movie I liked is..." -> *Should be:* "**A** movie I liked is..."\n        *   *Your text says:* "IT's have a story about a man who are alqoholism and get helped." -> *Should be:* "**It's** a story about a man **who is an alcoholic** and **gets** help."\n        *   *Your text says:* "and This a best movies in 1945..." -> *Should be:* "**And this** was one of the best **movies** in 1945..."\n\n*   **Grammar (Verbs and Sentence Structure):** You have many errors with verbs (doing words) and how you build your sentences.\n    *   From "IT's have a story about a man who are alqoholism and get helped.":\n        *   Instead of "IT's have," say "**It's** about a man" or "The movie **is** about a man."\n        *   Instead of "who are alqoholism and get helped," say "who **is an alcoholic** and **gets** help."\n    *   From "and This a best movies in 1945 because It's a last year of world war 2 and it why the movies is hardly to make.":\n        *   Instead of "This a best movies," say "This **was one of the best movies**."\n        *   Instead of "It's a last year," say "**It was** the last year."\n        *   Instead of "it why the movies is hardly to make," say "This is why the **movie was** hard to make."\n    *   From "And it's was good because people in this year is sadly for a worldwar2 damage and the movies helped people have a better emotions and this good for their future.":\n        *   Instead of "it's was good," say "it **was** good."\n        *   Instead of "people in this year is sadly," say "people in this year **were sad**."\n        *   Instead of "worldwar2 damage," say "World War 2 **damage**."\n        *   Instead of "have a better emotions," say "have better **feelings**" or "feel better."\n    *   From "and the movies get many award. They get academy award and the actor ray milland has a best actor in 1945.":\n        *   Instead of "the movies get many award," say "the **movie got** many **awards**."\n        *   Instead of "has a best actor," say "**was** a best actor."\n\n*   **Spelling:** Be careful with words like "alqoholism" (should be "alcoholism").\n\nFocus on these basic grammar, spelling, and capitalization rules to make your writing much clearer.	4.0	2.0	2.0	1.0	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	A2	2026
