d to catch any missing words or places where the verb doesn't quite match the subject.<br>*   ✅ Try to use a variety of linking words and phrases to show how your ideas connect, instead of repeating the same ones.<br>*   ✅ Practice using articles (a, an, the) and choose words carefully to make your meaning super clear and exact.	Kris, you did a fantastic job here! 🎉 You understood the question perfectly and talked about clothes, studying, and even came up with your own idea about food. You gave clear reasons why you think friends have more influence than parents in these areas. It's really impressive how you covered all parts of the question so thoroughly and supported your opinions well. Thai students often shine when they understand the task clearly, and you certainly did!	You did a good job of getting your message across to the reader, Kris, and your ideas were generally easy to follow. 😊 To score a 5 in this area, you could work on making your writing sound a little more formal and academic throughout, especially in an essay. For example, instead of starting a paragraph with "First things that friends have more effect," you could try something like "Firstly, when considering the influence of friends, clothes and fashion are a key area." Thai learners sometimes find it tricky to consistently use formal language because in everyday spoken English, we use a mix of styles. Practising different ways to introduce your points will help your essay sound even more sophisticated.	Your essay was quite well-organised, Kris! Each paragraph had a clear main idea, which makes it easy to read. 👍 However, to reach a higher score, you could try using a wider variety of linking words and phrases to connect your sentences and paragraphs. For instance, instead of often using "Moreover" or simple phrases like "The second topic," you could explore words like "furthermore," "in addition," "consequently," or "on the other hand." This helps your essay flow more smoothly and shows a more 