1065	34289	2025-08-17 10:04:20.947411+00	Thai Food	Food is an essential need for all people. Although, most people don't eat more food. People should eat more food, it was really important things to do. One successful type of popular food is street food, which is easy to eat and delicious. The three most important or the best greatest in street food are Som Tum, Lamb and Tom yum.<br><br><br>A first really amazing street food in Thailand is Tom Tum, which is a kind of a spicy papaya salad. Ingredients of Som Tum is lime, fish sauce, chili, papaya, crab and a small shrimp. A taste and flavor of papaya salad are really spicy and salt. Although Som Tum are spicy, but people still eat them because it's was really delicious.<br><br><br>Example, yesterday I ate Som Tum with my family and we're ordered many type of street food. There are many people in the cities, who eat street food like Som Tum. And here is a way to make Som Tum. First, put a garlic and chilies in a motor and pound it until them crushed and add fish sauce, lime, sugar and papaya salad. Mix everything together and you will got a delicious Som Tum.<br><br><br>Besides Som Tum, Tom Yum is also one of the best street foods in Thailand. It has a spicy and sour taste, and many people are enjoy eating with some rice or noodles. Ingredients of 1 stalk of lemongrass and cut into pieces, 3 slices of galangal, 3-5 lime leaves, 2-3 thai chilies, 4 mushrooms or more, 1 table spoon of lime, 1 teaspoon of chili paste. Here is a way to make Tom Yum, boil water with lemongrass, lime leaves, galangal add fish sauce, lime, and chili.<br><br><br>A third famous street food is Laab. Laab is a popular thai dish. It's made from pork, lime, fish sauce, chili, and toasted rice powder. The taste is spicy, sour and a little salty. People usually eat with sticky rice and a fresh vegetables.<br><br><br>In conclusion, street food is a delicious and easy thai dish. You don't need many ingredients and it doesn't take along time to make and very easty to eat it. Most people are really loves it	356	\N	Overall, you have written a clear essay about Thai street food, covering three different dishes. You have a good understanding of the structure of an essay, with an introduction, body paragraphs, and a conclusion. Your writing is easy to follow, and you use some good vocabulary. To improve, you need to work on your grammar, especially with verb forms and subject-verb agreement. Also, remember to include comments on the cultural value of the food, as this was a key part of the task.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026
3793	29031	2026-02-23 13:32:08.183797+00	Question 3 (Story)	Lois smiled as she put the tickets in her pocket and walked out of her house. She walked her way to the nearest train station and quickly got on when it arrived. As the time passed, she finally reached the newly opened museum. Her eyes wandered around until she met her friend, Evan. They exchanged glances and smiles. "I can't wait! Thank you for the tickets!" she said sincerely. He nodded and they both headed into the huge building.\n\nBoth of their faces lit up brightly. The museum was filled with all sorts of taxidermy of animals and ancient fossils. "Look at that lion, Lois. It looks eerily real, doesn't it?" Evan exclaimed with a wide grin. "We should check it out!" She firmly grabbed his wrist and ran to the showcase. As they both admire it, the lights suddenly flickered.\n\nWhen the lights turned back on, the taxidermy disappeared. "Where did it go?" she asked before she heard a distinct roar from behind. Evan took her hand and ran for the exit before the lights flickered again. This time it was back to where it was before. They both let out a sigh of relief, not until it flickered again. "Where can it be now?" Lois turned around to be met with a Lion staring into her eyes.	224	20.0	Hi Racing! 🌟 I was absolutely gripped by your story—you have a wonderful talent for building suspense and using very descriptive language like 'eerily real.' Your vocabulary is excellent! My main advice for your next writing task is to keep an eye on your word count; while your story was fantastic, practicing how to tell a great tale in fewer words will help you stay sharp for the exam. All the best, Ed	Your story began perfectly with 'Lois smiled as she put the tickets in her pocket and walked out of her house,' and you did a wonderful job of building a complete narrative with a clear beginning, middle, and a very exciting ending. This keeps the reader fully informed and invested in Lois's adventure at the museum. For your next piece, try to stay closer to the 100-word target to help you manage your time effectively during a real exam.	Including dialogue such as '“Look at that lion, Lois. It looks eerily real, doesn't it?”' was a brilliant choice because it makes the characters feel alive and pulls the reader right into the scene. This creates an engaging, suspenseful atmosphere that is exactly what a good story needs. To take this even further, you could describe a physical reaction, like Lois's heart racing, to make the reader feel her fear even more.	I see that you used 'When the lights turned back on' to signal a shift in the action, which acts like a clear road map for the reader to follow the sequence of events. This logical flow makes the spooky disappearance of the lion very easy to visualize and follow. You might try using a few more short, punchy sentences during the scary parts to make the pace feel even faster and more exciting.	Your choice of words like 'taxidermy' and 'eerily real' really shows off a sophisticated vocabulary that is well above the average level. When you wrote 'As they both admire it,' the switch to the present tense felt a little bit like a skip in a record because the rest of the story is in the past. Try to keep all your verbs in the past tense, like 'admired,' to keep the 'heartbeat' of your story consistent.	5.0	5.0	5.0	5.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
