1114	28841	2025-08-27 10:01:30.809759+00	Free time Activities	Free time activities are things that we can do during our free time such as drawing a picture, listening to music, playing sport, and more. These activities help us to relax and reduce our stress after working. In Thailand, Thai students study for almost 12 hours per day which caused many to become depressed from pressure. However free time activities help them a lot with their mental health making these activities are seen as very important things foward them. There are two free time activities which are the most famous choices for Thai teenagers; playing games and travelling.<br><br><br>The most popular choice among Thai teens is playing games. Games can be on anything or in any forms like computer games, board games, and more which makes them close to teens. Games also have many genres too, giving Thai teens a lot of choices for them to choose and relax themselves. They can play games with their friends, family, alone, or with their pets, leading to become the most first-choice for Thai teens.<br><br><br>Besides playing games, there are travelling too which is as famous as the frist one.	164	9.0	Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 164 words and achieved B1. You have a clear understanding of the essay topic and present your ideas well in the introduction.	You successfully identified two free time activities and explained the first one (playing games) in good detail. However, your essay is incomplete, as the explanation for the second activity (travelling) is very brief, and you did not include a concluding paragraph. <br>👉 <b>To reach a 5/5:</b> Make sure to develop all points fully and complete all sections of the essay, including a strong conclusion with a restatement of your main points.<br><br>	You communicate your ideas clearly, and the tone is generally appropriate for an essay. However, the incompleteness of the essay means that it doesn't fully achieve its communicative purpose of presenting a well-rounded discussion of your chosen activities.<br><br>	Your introduction is clear, and you started the first body paragraph well with a topic sentence. However, the essay is incomplete, lacking a fully developed second body paragraph and a conclusion. This significantly affects the overall coherence and flow of your writing.<br>👉 <b>To reach a 5/5:</b> Focus on ensuring your essay has a complete structure with all paragraphs fully developed. Remember to start body paragraphs with clear topic sentences and include a strong concluding paragraph that summarizes your main points.<br><br>	You use good everyday vocabulary and are trying to use more complex sentences, which is great! The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules and spelling.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "making these activities are seen as very important things foward them."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "making these activities are seen as very important things for them."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Always double-check your spelling, especially for common words. Sometimes in Thai, we don't focus as much on precise spelling in every context, but in English, it's very important. A small spelling error can sometimes change the meaning of your sentence.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Besides playing games, there are travelling too which is as famous as the frist one."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Besides playing games, there is also travelling, which is as famous as the first one."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> When talking about a general activity like 'travelling' (a gerund), it's treated as a singular noun in English, so we use 'there is' instead of 'there are'. Also, be careful with letter order in English words; 'frist' should be 'first'.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "However free time activities help them a lot..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "However, free time activities help them a lot..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, when you start a sentence with a transition word or phrase like 'However' or 'Besides', you almost always need a comma after it. This helps the reader pause and understand the connection between sentences, which is a key difference from how ideas are often linked in Thai sentence structure.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Complete the essay by adding a detailed explanation for your second activity (travelling) and a clear, well-developed concluding paragraph.<br>2. Review your essays carefully for spelling errors and practice checking unfamiliar words in a dictionary.<br>3. Practice using commas correctly after transition words and phrases at the beginning of sentences (e.g., 'However,', 'Therefore,', 'In addition,').<br><br>	2.0	2.0	2.0	3.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
