 hobbies. Team sports like basketball help teenagers build friendships, while creative hobbies like painting allow self-expression."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved version directly answers the question by naming specific activities and explaining their benefits, rather than focusing on why teenagers can't do activities.	Your writing shows you understand academic topics, but needs to stay focused on the task.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Keep your writing focused on the exact question being asked throughout the entire essay.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Writing about parental pressure instead of free time activities<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> Stay focused on describing and explaining the two chosen free time activities in each paragraph<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Academic writing requires staying precisely on topic. When the question asks about free time activities, every paragraph should develop that specific theme.	You used paragraph breaks well to separate your ideas.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Create a clear thesis statement and use topic sentences that connect to your main argument.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your introduction doesn't clearly state what two activities you will discuss<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Free time activities are essential for teenagers' development, with team sports and creative hobbies being particularly valuable for building social skills and self-expression."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A clear thesis statement tells the reader exactly what your essay will be about and helps you stay organized throughout your writing.	You used some good vocabulary like "investment" correctly. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "I think freetime is the most important for kid and teenagers."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "I think free time is very important for children and teenagers."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, compound words like "freetime" are common, but in English we write "free time" as two separate words. Also, we need to use plural forms: "children" ("kids" is too informal) not "kid" when talking about groups.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "they parents give a lot of pressure to them"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "their parents give them a lot of pressure"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, the same word "they" can be used for possession, but in English we need to use "their" for possessive form. This is a common challenge for Thai learners.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "That make teenagers get stress"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "That makes teenagers feel stressed"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, subject-verb agreement is different. In English, "that" (singular) needs "makes" (singular verb), not "make." Also, we say "feel stressed" rather than "get stress."<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Practice identifying the exact question requirements before writing - underline key words like "two activities" and "explain why"<br>2. Work on subject-verb agreement with singular/plural nouns<br>3. Study possessive pronouns (my/your/his/her/our/their) and when to use them<br><br>	2.0	2.0	2.0	2.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
3798	33169	2026-02-23 13:32:08.183797+00	Question 2 (Article)	Sport is one of the best activities you can do to stay healthy and strong. It is for everyone. Do any kind of sport or exercise once a week can keep you away from doctors, which is one of the several reasons of why we should exercise and play sports.\n\nIn my hometown, there's a park for people to run and play football together. They also have a play ground for kids. But when I moved to Bangkok, I rarely see them around in my area. There's not enough sports activities for people in my area, which left me with nothing to do at the weekends.\n\nFirst year in my school, at that time I was very fat because I don't exercise enough. This make me run slowly and get tired easily. Untill when I start playing sports with my friends. Playing sports not only make you healthy, it also teach you team work and sportmanship. So for young people, do sport and exercise are important and beneficial for yourself.	178	19.0	Hi Milan! 🌟 You've written a very engaging article that really captures the reader's interest with your personal story and honest reflections. Your range of vocabulary and your ability to use complex sentences with 'which' are very impressive! My main 'homework' for your next piece is to watch out for subject-verb agreement (like saying 'this makes' instead of 'this make') and to practice using 'ing' forms when you start a sentence with an activity. You're doing a fantastic job! 🚀 All the best, Ed.	When you wrote 'But when I moved to Bangkok, I rarely see them around in my area', you perfectly contrasted two different locations to answer if there are enough activities. This gives the reader a clear picture of your current situation and makes your article feel very authentic. Try to keep using these personal comparisons in future articles to add depth and personality to your writing.	It was great to see you share a personal story by writing 'First year in my school, at that time I was very fat because I don't exercise enough'. By being honest about your own journey, you build a strong connection with your readers and make your arguments about health much more persuasive. To make it even better, you could add a catchy title at the start to grab the reader's attention immediately.	Your use of the word 'which' in sentences like 'which left me with nothing to do at the weekends' acts like a strong bridge between your ideas. This helps the reader follow your logic effortlessly because the result of the lack of activities is directly connected to your feelings. One small tip: you could use more specific sequencing words like 'Firstly' or 'In addition' to make your different reasons for exercising stand out even more clearly.	I see that you used some sophisticated vocabulary like 'sportsmanship' and 'beneficial', which really shows off your high-level word bank. However, when you wrote 'Do any kind of sport... can keep', it makes the sentence feel a bit unstable because the subject of your sentence needs to be an action. Using a gerund like 'Doing' instead of 'Do' at the start of a sentence will make your grammar much smoother and more professional.	5.0	5.0	5.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
1131	29034	2025-08-28 14:19:40.711563+00	Free time Activities	Freetime activities are the pinicle of relaxation. Every teenager has freetime activites even in countries that give little to no freetime like Thailand, Thai teenagers have many freetime activites but the most popular one is playing videogames. Some of the most played video games are Roblox, Minecraft and ROV.<br><br><br>The first popular game, Roblox is a platform that includes thousands of games "called "maps" that people can choose to play. Some of the more popular maps are Grow a garden, Brookhaven and Dress to Impress. Grow a garden which is a game about growing a garden, has become very popular in the last few months. Other than that Brookhaven a role play game, has become a roblox classic. Lastly Dress to impress is a dressing game, which became popular due to it's creativity. You can find anything on roblox whether it's fan games, a knock off or maybe something original.<br><br><br>Second well known game, Minecraft a sand box game. It is the most downloaded game in the world. The game allows you to build anything you can imagine with cubes called "blocks". There are also "mobs" which can be used on animals or monsters. Minecraft is also a survival game. Monsters appear or spawn at night and most of them burn in the day. Minecraft is a game full of freedom and creativity.<br><br><br>_ The last popular game, ROV or Arena of valor is a team tactic game where you get put on a team and in order to win you have to destroy the other team's base. The game includes charecters in different classes. Your team has to choose which classes go well to gather and stratagize where to go. They also need to defend their base or else it's game over.<br><br><br>In conclusion, Thai teenagers choose to play video games in their free time. Some of the most popular are Roblox, Minecraft and ROV which are chosen due to it's creativity.	323	16.0	<b>📝 Dear Anu</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 323 words and achieved B2+. You give very clear, detailed descriptions of three popular video games and show good knowledge and enthusiasm for the topic — this makes your essay interesting and informative for the reader.<br><br>	Your essay fully fulfils the task by describing free-time activities within the category of computer/video games and giving clear reasons why these games are chosen. You provide concrete details and examples for Roblox, Minecraft and ROV which fully inform the reader. <br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Consider briefly acknowledging an alternative type of free-time activity (for example, a sport or a creative hobby) in one sentence to show a slightly broader perspective. This is optional at B2 but can increase variety. <br><br>	You use the conventions of an essay well and generally keep an appropriate informative tone. Your examples and descriptions hold the reader’s interest. <br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Make the register a little more formal and precise in places (avoid conversational phrases). This will strengthen the essay’s academic tone. <br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> “You get put on a team and in order to win you have to destroy the other team's base.”<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Players are assigned to teams and must cooperate to destroy the opposing team's base."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved version uses a more formal phrasing (passive “are assigned” and “must cooperate”) which is more suitable for an academic essay and makes the sentence clearer and more concise.<br><br>	You use paragraphs and there is a clear introduction and conclusion, which helps the reader follow the text. However, some paragraph topic sentences are weak or run-on, which reduces clarity about each paragraph’s main function. <br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Make each paragraph start with a clear topic sentence that directly links to your thesis. Also aim for four distinct paragraphs: introduction (thesis), body paragraph 1 (activity/category 1), body paragraph 2 (activity/category 2 or subcategory), conclusion (restate thesis + summary).<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> “The first popular game, Roblox is a platform that includes thousands of games "called "maps" that people can choose to play.”<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "One popular choice is Roblox, which is a platform offering thousands of user-created games, known as 'maps'"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved sentence gives a clear topic statement (one popular choice) that links to the thesis and uses a relative clause ("which is...") to add essential information without creating a long or confusing clause.<br><br>	You use a good range of everyday vocabulary and attempt complex structures. The main challenges are with a few key grammar and spelling points. <br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Freetime activities are the pinicle of relaxation."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free-time activities are the pinnacle of relaxation."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (Thai interference — word form/word choice) Thai learners often transfer word forms directly from Thai where word endings and derivational changes are not marked the same way as in English. This can lead to incorrect word forms or spellings such as *pinicle* instead of *pinnacle*. Focusing on common noun spellings and word endings in English helps reduce this error. <br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Some of the most played video games are Roblox, Minecraft and ROV which are chosen due to it's creativity."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Some of the most played video games are Roblox, Minecraft and ROV, which are chosen for their creativity."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (Thai interference — possessive/grammar and relative clause punctuation) Thai has no articles or the same possessive spelling distinctions as English, so learners often confuse "it's" (it is) with the possessive "its." Also, relative clauses in English often need commas and clearer linking words. Putting a comma before "which" and using "their" for plural possession makes the sentence grammatically correct and clearer. <br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Every teenager has freetime activites even in countries that give little to no freetime like Thailand, Thai teenagers have many freetime activites but the most popular one is playing videogames."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Every teenager has free-time activities, even in countries that give little leisure time such as Thailand. Thai teenagers, however, often enjoy playing video games the most."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> (Thai interference — run-ons and clause boundary use) Thai allows long connected clauses without the same punctuation or linking conventions used in English. This can lead to comma splices and run-on sentences in English. Breaking the idea into two sentences and using linking words (however) gives clearer clause boundaries and improves readability. <br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Weekly task: Choose two short model paragraphs (one per week) and rewrite them, focusing on clear topic sentences and correct clause boundaries (15–20 minutes each).<br>2. Grammar focus: Spend 3 sessions practicing relative clauses and possessive forms (its vs it's) with 10 example sentences each; check and correct them.<br>3. Spelling drills: Keep a personal error log for 2 weeks of your frequent misspellings (e.g., pinnacle, activities, characters, strategize) and practice them with flashcards until you can spell them correctly 10/10.<br><br>	5.0	4.0	3.0	4.0	Writing	CA	FIRST	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1cFmq4K2oHYkE4yIkPRNskT3opJFRSJ--?usp=sharing	\N	\N	\N	\N	B2+	2026
