s a consistent, slightly more formal tone suitable for an essay.\n❌ Weakness: "teens will don't individualism too much and empathy people." This sentence is a bit informal and unclear.\n✨ Improved: "Teenagers will not become too individualistic and will develop a stronger sense of empathy."\n💡 Explanation: In an essay, it's better to use more formal language and avoid contractions like 'don't'. Also, making the phrasing clearer helps the reader understand your message easily.	📋 ORGANISATION: 1/5\nYou attempted to use paragraphs, but the essay is incomplete and lacks a clear structure for the two body paragraphs and a conclusion.\n👉 To Improve: Plan your essay before you start writing to ensure you have four complete paragraphs with clear topic sentences and a proper conclusion.\n❌ Weakness: Your essay is incomplete, so it lacks a proper conclusion and full development of all paragraphs.\n✨ Improved: "In conclusion, while academic pressures are significant, engaging in activities like online gaming provides valuable opportunities for teenagers to relax, develop social skills, and build empathy."\n💡 Explanation: A clear concluding paragraph helps to summarise your main points and leaves the reader with a strong final impression, making your essay feel complete and well-structured.	🔤 LANGUAGE: 3/5\nYou use everyday vocabulary generally appropriately, and your simple grammatical forms are mostly under control. The main challenge is with a few key grammar rules.\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Three of the most interesting activities in free time is listen to music, Watching movies, and play computer games."\n✨ Correction: "Three of the most interesting activities in free time are listening to music, watching movies, and playing computer games."\n💡 Explanation: When you list several things, you need to use the plural form of 'to be', which is 'are', not 'is'. Also, when talking about activities that are nouns (like 'music', 'movies', 'computer games'), you should use the '-ing' 