actly what the article is about before they start reading. 🚀	I see that you used 'Beside helping me grow stroger' to start your final paragraph, which acts like a strong bridge between your different ideas. This helps the reader follow your logic easily because they can see how your points are connected. One tip for the future is to check the spelling of key words like 'stronger' and 'trust' to make sure your great structure isn't distracted by small typing slips. 📝	When you wrote that exercise 'made me more healthier,' I could see you were trying to use a more complex comparison to show improvement. While the meaning is 100% clear, using 'more' and '-er' together is like wearing two hats at once; usually, we just need the '-er' for short words. Try to remember that for short adjectives, 'healthier' or 'stronger' is all you need to make your point perfectly! 💪	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
