lly immersed in the characters' world. 📝	I see that you included time markers like 'At the moment' and 'finally' to help move the story forward logically. These words act like road signs that tell the reader where the story is going, making it very easy to follow your sequence of events. One way to improve even further is to break your story into two small paragraphs to visually show the shift from the problem at the cinema to the strange solution. 🗺️	Your choice of 'unexpected thing happen' shows you are trying to use more interesting vocabulary to build suspense, which is wonderful to see. Even though some verbs need a little more control in the past tense, your meaning was always 100% clear to me. A great tip for your next story is to remember that after 'to', we use the base form of the verb, so 'want to saw' should become 'want to see'. 🌟	5.0	4.0	4.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1	\N	\N	\N	B1+	2026
