ht away! 🚀	When you wrote 'This became a major problem because...', it acted as a strong logical bridge that helped me follow your thoughts from the lack of space to the health of the children. The text has a clear internal flow, but because it is written as one large block, it can be a little tiring for the reader's eyes. For your next writing task, try to use separate paragraphs for each main point to give your reader a little 'breathing room' between ideas. 📝	I see that you included sophisticated vocabulary like 'carbohydrates', 'proteins', and 'hormones', which shows you have a fantastic range of topic-specific words. However, small slips like 'Many area' and 'are design' act like tiny speed bumps that slow the reader down because they miss the plural 's' or the 'ed' ending. A helpful tip is to always check your 'countability'—if you use the word 'many', make sure the noun that follows it has an 's' on the end! ✨	5.0	3.0	3.0	3.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B1	2026
