00-word guide, as this helps you keep your story tight and punchy! 🌟	When you wrote that the cold gave 'a chill down her spine,' it really helped me feel the spooky atmosphere of the dark alley and showed a great understanding of how to set a mood. Using such descriptive imagery holds the reader's attention well beyond a basic B1 level. Just keep an eye on some of your word choices like 'bending home,' which might confuse a reader; try using more common phrases like 'heading home' to keep the story flowing smoothly. 🚀	I see that you included helpful phrases like 'The next day' and 'when she arrived' to move the story along, which acts like a map for the reader so we never feel lost. These time markers create a very logical sequence of events from the house to the mysterious alley. For your next piece, try using a few more varied connectors like 'Despite the cold' or 'Eventually' to link your sentences even more naturally. 📝	I was very impressed by your ambitious use of language, especially phrases like 'chill down her spine' and 'case still mysterious'. Even though there are some spelling and grammar slips, you used a wide range of vocabulary to tell a complex and scary story that I could follow easily. ✨ For next time, try to double-check your past continuous forms (e.g., 'she was trying') to make your writing even more polished! 💡	5.0	4.0	4.0	4.0	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	B1+	\N	\N	\N	B2	2026
