t is generally well organised and coherent. Each paragraph focuses on a single topic: excitement, concert preference, climbing refusal, and questions. Linking words like 'because' and 'too' are used, and the sequence is logical. However, the final paragraph runs multiple questions together without clear separation, which slightly reduces coherence.	4.0	A range of everyday vocabulary is used appropriately ('excited'; 'rock concert'; 'good memories'; 'dangerous'; 'experience'; 'scare of height'; 'accident'; 'blankets'; 'snacks'). Simple and some complex grammatical forms are used with good control ('I think I would go to the rock concert because I like rock music'; 'I don't want to climb a mountains because it is dangerous if we don't have an experience before'). Errors are minor and do not impede communication ('climb a mountains'; 'I am scare of height'; 'do I need to bring blankets or where do I sleep in living room or in your bedroom').	0.00	[]	2026-07-10
