29034	2025-08-17 09:59:17.911907+00	2026	Thai Food	Food is a staple for everyone. It is important to every culture but they all have their own unique varieties. Many eastern food cultures have been recognised internationally like Thai. Thai foods have multiple famous and well-known styles although streetfood in particular is considered as the most famous. The three of the more iconic streetfoods are: Padthai, Somtum and Larb.<br><br><br>An iconic street food is Pad thai, which is a stir-fried noodle dish that is relatively easy to find especially in places known for the in street food. The main ingrediants of any Pad thai are Prawns, noodles, lime, chilli and sauce. As for how to make it, first boil the prawns and noodles then second stir fry them with the sauce and chilies once finished plate and serve with a wedge or half a lime. The dish represents the rebellion between Thailand and China in the 1940s. Even though it is not true in the present Pad thai still represents an important part of cultural change in Thailand.<br><br><br>Besides Pad thai, Somtum also known as papaya salad is a flavorful variety of tum. It is also the national food of Thailand. There are five key ingrediants that are needed to make this dish. Which are papaya, chilles, prara, peanuts and tomatoes. First shred the papaya and second pound it with chillies and prara then Third plate it with the tomatoes and peanuts. Somtum represents an important part of Thai cuisines as Thai people used to preserve food. This method works because chillie peppers inhibit the growth of certain bacteria.<br><br><br>The last example is Larb which is a meat-salad dish is very popular for its flavour. Larb also has some key ingrediants minced-meat, lime, chillis, red onions and basil leaves. First lightly stir-fry the minced-meat. Secondly remove from the pan and mix in some chopped chillis and red onions. Lastly squeeze in lime juice and mix for flavour. Larb is traditionally served at important events like festivals and ceremonies, as it represents good fortune.<br><br><br>In conclusion, Thai street foods can represent culture, tradition and history. The three that are well known internationally are Pad thai, Somtum and Larb. Foods are an important representation of culture.	365	\N	You have written a well-structured essay that clearly addresses the prompt. You successfully identify different Thai street foods and effectively connect them to Thai culture and history, which was a specific requirement for this essay. Your vocabulary is generally appropriate for the B2 level, and you use good linking words to connect your ideas. To improve further, focus on correcting consistent spelling errors and ensuring all your sentences are grammatically complete. You have also used some relative clauses and passive structures which adds variety to your writing.	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	Part 2	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-08-17
