," or "for example" to guide your reader through your thoughts.	1.0	Sun, you've used some good everyday words to talk about pets, which is a great foundation. 📚 However, there are quite a few mistakes with your grammar and spelling that make your meaning a bit unclear at times. For example, you wrote "Most people has an question" instead of "Most people have a question." Remember that "people" is plural, so it needs a plural verb like "have." Another common mistake was with spelling, like "belief" for "believe," "fell" for "feel," and "forniture" for "furniture." These small errors can add up and distract the reader from your message. Thai learners often mix up singular and plural verb forms, and also struggle with spelling words that sound similar or have silent letters. A good way to improve is to double-check your subject and verb agreement in every sentence, and to keep a personal list of words you often misspell so you can review them. Also, a complex sentence like "some if you not pay attention to them enough they can be agressive and not listen to you to weeck to have a lot of responbilitie and too feed them and play with it will make them respect and rayalty to you" is difficult to follow. Try to break down long sentences like this into smaller, clearer ones, for instance: "Some pets can become aggressive if you don't give them enough attention. You also need to feed them and play with them regularly to earn their respect and loyalty." Focusing on these areas will make your writing much clearer and more professional.	\N	\N	2025-09-13
