d the conventions of the task to communicate straightforward ideas. The writing is mostly clear, and you have attempted to engage the reader by describing the attractions of Ayuttaya. To improve to a score of 5, you could use more descriptive and vivid language to hold the reader's attention more effectively. For instance, instead of saying it is a "serene meadium town," you could use stronger adjectives and imagery to paint a more compelling picture. Additionally, ensure that your tone and register are consistent throughout the essay.	3.0	You have organized your text into paragraphs, and the ideas generally follow a logical sequence, moving from a general introduction to specific details about the city. You've also used some cohesive devices, such as "This also attractive lots of tourist to vist it once". To reach a higher score of 5, Venice, you should aim for more sophisticated linking words and cohesive devices to improve the flow and coherence of the essay. For instance, using transitions like "Furthermore," "Moreover," or "In addition" could help connect your ideas more smoothly. Also, check to ensure clear paragraphing and avoid sentences that seem disconnected from the main flow.	2.0	Venice, you have used some everyday vocabulary appropriately, but there are several noticeable errors in your language that sometimes impede communication. Examples include spelling errors ("meadium" instead of "medium," "tourist" instead of "tourists," "vist" instead of "visit," "fill" instead of "filled," "hundeard" instead of "hundred," "maillous" instead of "marvelous," "beaitful" instead of "beautiful") and grammatical errors ("one of popular and famous place" instead of "one of the most popular and famous places," "This also attractive lots of tourist" instead of "This also attracts many tourists," "Ayuttaya can know as" instead of "Ayuttaya is known as"). To improve to a score of 5, you need to improve both the range and accuracy of your language. While some of the vocabu