m the exhaustion that school gives them you need to Gives yourself some free times if you can	346	14.0	<p>You did a great job identifying two popular free time activities and explaining why Thai teenagers enjoy them!</p>	B2	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	5.0	<p>All content is relevant to the task. You clearly identified two free time activities and explained what they are, and why they are particularly popular in Thailand. The reader is fully informed.</p>	3.0	<p>You used an appropriate tone for an article, but the register shifts between formal and informal language, which can confuse the reader about the intended audience.<br>👉 To Improve: Maintain a consistent register throughout your writing - either formal for a general audience or consistently informal for peers.<br>❌ Weakness: "But Thai's teenagers are different they doesn't just loves it They are obsessed with it what made Thai's teenager so obsessed With free time? You may be wonder this is two of the popular Activities during free times those are playing video games and listen to the music which help them ease their free time problem" (starts informal, then tries to be more formal).<br>✨ Improved: "Free time is a cherished period for everyone, but for Thai teenagers, it's a source of profound engagement. Many turn to activities like playing video games and listening to music, which offer a refreshing escape from daily pressures."<br>💡 Explanation: Keeping a consistent formal tone helps establish credibility and makes your writing more professional for a general audience. The improved sentence maintains a consistent formal tone suitable for an article, providing a clear and engaging introduction without register shifts.</p>	3.0	<p>You organized your ideas into paragraphs, which helps the reader follow your main points, but the connections between ideas could be stronger with better linking words. Also, you have many run-on sentences, which makes your writing hard to follow.<br>👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases to show clearer relationships between your ideas (e.g., however, therefore, as a result). Pay close attention to sentence boundaries and avoid run-on sentences.<br>❌ Weakness: "Free time is a very special period of time that everyone loves But Thai's teenagers are different they doesn't just loves it They are obsessed with it what made Thai's teenager so obsessed With free time? You may be wonder this is two of the popular Activities during free times those are playing video games and listen to the music which help them ease their free time problem" (This is a very long run-on sentence).<br>✨ Improved: "Free time is a very special period that everyone loves. However, Thai teenagers are different; they don't just love it, they are obsessed with it. You might wonder what makes Thai teenagers so captivated by free time. Two of the most popular activities during these periods are playing video games and listening to music, which help them alleviate their free time concerns."<br>💡 Explanation: Using specific linking words and proper punctuation helps show the relationship between ideas more clearly and makes your writing flow better. Breaking up long sentences into shorter, grammatically correct ones makes your writing much easier for the reader to understand.</p>	3.0	<p>You used good vocabulary related to the topic, including 'sophisticated,' 'depression,' and 'obsessed.' However, there are several recurring grammar patterns that affect clarity.<br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "they doesn't just loves it"<br>✨ Correction: "they don't just love it"<br>💡 Explanation: In English, the verb form changes depending on the subject. For "they," "do not" (don't) is used, and the main verb "love" should be in its base form. Thai verbs do not change for different subjects or for negation, which is why this is a common challenge for Thai learners.<br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "they loves Playing video games"<br>✨ Correction: "they love playing video games"<br>💡 Explanation: Similar to the previous example, in English, the verb "love" should be in its base form when used with the subject "they" in the present simple tense. Thai grammar does not require these changes, leading to common errors for Thai speakers learning English.<br>❌ Problem: You wrote: "They would likely brought something to keep them entertain"<br>✨ Correction: "They would likely bring something to keep them entertained"<br>💡 Explanation: After modal verbs like 'would,' the main verb should always be in its base form ('bring'). Also, 'entertain' should be 'entertained' when used as an adjective to describe someone who is kept happy. This is a common error for Thai speakers as verb forms and past participles used as adjectives can be tricky.</p>	\N	\N	2025-08-30
