ple is "that great," which should be "that's great." Also, when you mentioned the film, "was look bored" should be "looked boring." Finally, "we doesn't need to use" should be "we don't need to use." These types of errors are common for Thai learners as English verb tenses and subject-verb agreement can be quite different from Thai. A good way to improve is to double-check your sentences for correct verb forms and make sure your verbs agree with your subjects. Focusing on these common errors will make your writing much more accurate and fluent.	\N	\N	2025-09-16
