as and makes your writing much easier to read and enjoy.	2.0	You've used everyday vocabulary appropriately to describe the festival and your experiences, which is a great start 👍. However, to improve your score in language, it would be really helpful to focus on accuracy in both spelling and grammar. For example, remember to spell "festival" correctly and pay attention to verb forms, such as saying "I'm telling you" instead of "I'll telling you" or "I went" instead of "I have go to". Another important area is ensuring subject-verb agreement and correct prepositions, for instance, "many people *are* there" instead of "many people *it* there". Thai speakers sometimes face challenges with pluralisation in English because the concept is handled differently in Thai, which might lead to phrases like "fastival" instead of "festivals" or "ever years" instead of "every year". Also, paying attention to the articles "a" and "the" is important, as these are often not used in the same way in Thai. Focusing on these areas will make your writing much clearer and more professional. Keep practising, and your language will certainly become more controlled and precise.	\N	\N	2025-09-21
