nd you'll see your writing grow stronger! 📋<br><br>#### Action Plan<br>* Make sure you understand *all* parts of the question, especially the main point, and refer back to it as you write. ✅<br>* Read your essay aloud after you finish. This can help you spot awkward sentences or missing words. ✅<br>* Pay close attention to verb tenses, especially when talking about past events, and how pronouns like 'themself' should be 'themselves'. ✅	B2	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	Part 2	3.0	You've done a good job, Grace, of including the points about clothes and fashion, and studying, and even adding your own interesting idea about how friends influence "society" – which is a great way to talk about social groups and how we behave. 👍 However, the main question asked whether friends or parents have *more* influence, and your essay focused mostly on friends. Next time, try to remember the core question as you write each part of your essay. For instance, after discussing how friends influence clothing choices, you could add a sentence or two about how parents might also play a role, or how a teenager might balance both influences. This helps show that you're directly answering *all* parts of the prompt, making your argument even more persuasive. 😊	3.0	You've managed to get your message across quite well, Grace, which is the most important thing! Your writing is generally easy to follow. To make your essays even stronger, especially for a more formal piece like this, try to make your opening and closing paragraphs sound a bit more serious and academic. For example, instead of "These are three choices that teenagers get effect by their friends," you could try something like, "Teenagers' choices are often significantly shaped by their friends, particularly in three key areas." Also, keeping your language a little more formal throughout, rather than conversational, will really help your essays shine. ⭐ Thai learners sometimes find it tricky to switch between informal everyday English and more formal academic writing, so it's a super important skill to keep working on!	4.0	Your essay is well-structured, Grace, with clear paragraphs for each of your ideas, which makes it easy for your reader to follow your thoughts. You've also used connecting words like "First of all," "Besides," and "To summarize" to guide the reader, which is excellent. Perhaps next time, you could try to vary these linking phrases a little more to make your writing even more sophisticated and natural. Instead of always starting with "The last one is," you might consider phrases like "Finally," or "In addition to these points..." Good organisation is a fantastic foundation for any piece of writing, and you're doing a great job here! ✨	2.0	This is an area where a little extra practice will make a big difference, Grace. You've got some good vocabulary, but there are a few places where the grammar could be tightened up to make your meaning clearer and more precise. For example, in your first paragraph, "many teenagers did not choose the choices by themself" could be "many teenagers do not make their own choices," and "they get effect by their friends" should be "they are affected by their friends." Also, in the second paragraph, "like to following trends" should be "like to follow trends." Another common area to watch out for is spelling; for example, "gorgous" should be "gorgeous" and "fasinating" should be "fascinating." Many Thai learners find English verb tenses and pronoun agreement a bit tricky because their own language works differently. Don't worry, with consistent practice, especially focusing on these common mistakes, your language accuracy will improve heaps! Keep a notebook of common errors and try to correct them as you write. 📝	\N	\N	2025-09-12
