ould be 'The machine <b>didn't</b> work'.	A2+	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	3.0	Your story is funny and has a clear plot! 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Opening!</b> 🏁 You lost marks because you didn't use the required opening sentence. Always check this first!<br>2. <b>Details!</b> 🖌️ What did the flying cat look like? Was it scared? Happy?	3.0	Your story was fun to read! 🤩<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Clarity!</b> 💭 'Glow the machine' is confusing. Did you mean 'grow'? Or 'show'?<br>2. <b>Consistency!</b> 🔄 Stick to one idea. First it's a cat machine, then a generic machine. Keep it clear.	3.0	You used 'Secondly' and 'Suddenly' to order the events. 📑<br><br>To improve:<br>1. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 Put all the 'testing' parts in one paragraph and the 'success' parts in another.<br>2. <b>Flow!</b> 🌊 'After that he started...' connects well.	2.0	You used 'brilliant' and 'creativity' correctly! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br>1. <b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'He was create' -> 'He *created*'. 'Machine don't work' -> 'didn't work'.<br>2. <b>Modals!</b> 🧱 'Can't working' -> 'couldn't work'.<br>3. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Exacly' -> 'exactly'.<br>4. <b>Adjectives!</b> 🎨 'He thinks a machine was perfect' -> 'He *thought* the machine was perfect'.<br>5. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Interested his idea' -> 'interested *in* his idea'.	\N	\N	2025-11-26
