 make it clearer, you could say something like, \\"Seoul was once called Hun-ou, but after World War 2, its name was changed to Seoul.\\" Also, the task asked you to describe what you love and why, with reasons and examples. You gave some reasons, but developing your examples more would help the reader.	2.0	You tried to share your ideas about Seoul, but sometimes the way you wrote made it hard for the reader to stay interested. For example, you wrote, \\"I will draw it so you can see how it look like.\\" In an article for a travel website, readers expect to learn from the words, not from a drawing you might add later. You could try describing the \\"honey river\\" more vividly with words instead. This will help you hold the reader's attention and communicate your ideas in a way that fits a written article.	2.0	You used paragraphs to separate your ideas, which is good. You started with an introduction and then moved to history, food, and K-pop. However, the connections between your paragraphs and sentences could be stronger. For example, when you move from history to food, you simply start a new paragraph with \\"food that you must try when you visit seoul.\\" It would be helpful to use linking words to make the transition smoother, like \\"Moving on to another reason I love Seoul, the food is amazing.\\" Also, the task asked for a conclusion, but your essay ends abruptly. Adding a concluding sentence or paragraph would help to summarize your points and give the reader a sense of completeness.	2.0	You used everyday words to talk about Seoul, but there are some mistakes in grammar and spelling that make your writing hard to read at times. For example, you wrote \\"seoul\\" instead of \\"Seoul.\\" Remember to always capitalize proper nouns like city names. Also, sentences like \\"seoul use to call Hun-ou\\" and \\"they changing Hun-ou to seoul\\" have grammatical errors. You could say, \\"Seoul used to be called Hun-ou, but they changed the name to Seoul after World War 2.\\" Improving your capitalization and grammar will make your writing much clearer and more professional.	\N	\N	2025-07-23
