erline the key parts before you start writing to make sure you address everything asked.<br>*   ✅ Practice writing topic sentences that clearly state the main idea of each paragraph and link back to your overall argument.<br>*   ✅ Focus on making sure your sentences are complete and grammatically correct, especially with subject-verb agreement and using the right words in the right places.	B1+	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	Part 2	3.0	Gunner, you've done a good job of covering the points given in the question – clothes and fashion, and studying – and you even added your own idea about free time, which is excellent. 👍 However, to get an even better score, it’s really important to directly answer the main question. The prompt asked, "Who has more effect on the choices teenagers make - friends or parents?", but your essay talked more about what teenagers are "forced to do" in general. For example, when discussing clothes, you focused on the pressure to follow friends, but didn't directly compare that to parental influence on fashion choices. Next time, try to explicitly weigh up both sides: how much do friends influence, and how much do parents influence? Then, make sure your conclusion clearly states which group you think has a stronger effect, based on what you've written in your body paragraphs. Thai learners sometimes focus broadly on a topic rather than directly addressing the specific nuances of the question.	2.0	Your essay communicates your ideas, but for a B2 First exam, it needs to adopt a more academic and formal tone. It felt a little like you were chatting with a friend rather than writing for an exam assessor. For instance, phrases like "Nowsaday people don't really believe on their self" could be rephrased to sound more formal, like "In contemporary society, individuals often lack self-belief." To improve, try to use more formal vocabulary and avoid overly simple or conversational language. Think about your opening and closing sentences for each paragraph an