at were suitable for your email, Satang. Most of your sentences were easy to understand, and you controlled your grammar well for many of your ideas. However, there were a few spots where the grammar could be tightened up. For example, instead of "thank a lot," it would be "thanks a lot" or "thank you a lot." Also, when you said "build a robot sound good," it should be "building a robot sounds good" because "building a robot" acts as a single idea, and the verb "sound" needs an 's' for agreement. Another example is "it really bad too," which should be "it's really bad too." These sorts of errors, especially with verb forms and missing words like 'is' or 'are,' are common for Thai learners as the grammatical structures in Thai can be quite different. Focusing on these small but important details will really help your sentences become more accurate and polished.	\N	\N	2025-09-19
