ife back'). To improve, ensure clarity in word choice and avoid potentially confusing phrases.	4.0	The text is generally well organised. Linking words are used effectively ('However', 'Initially', 'So', 'but'). To improve, consider breaking longer paragraphs to enhance readability, especially the second paragraph.	3.0	Everyday vocabulary is used appropriately. There are some errors in spelling and grammar ('ether' for others/either?, 'house were empthy', 'got erase', 'happend') but meaning is clear. To improve, focus on correcting common spelling mistakes and ensuring correct passive voice usage.	\N	\N	2025-12-01
