tion. 🚀 Try to use more full stops to help the reader understand when one idea ends and a new one begins! 💡	2.0	Writing your entire story in one big block of text acts like a marathon for the reader's eyes! 🏁 For your next task, try to use separate paragraphs for each main part of your story (like the setup and the climax). This gives your reader a 'breathing space' and makes your story much easier to follow. 📓	2.0	You used some great vocabulary like 'investigate' and 'suspicious'. However, I noticed that you often forgot to use capital letters for names (like 'lois' and 'peter') and at the start of sentences. ✍️ Also, focusing on your past tense endings (like 'hired' and 'followed') will make your writing much more polished and professional! ✨	\N	\N	2026-02-23
