ld get bullied... when people are children, there is often a group..."<br><b>Explanation:</b>\n*   **Spelling:** Double-check common words like "believe" and "themselves".\n*   **Plural -s:** In English, we add '-s' to most nouns to show there is more than one (e.g., "children" is already plural, not "childrens"). Accordingly, Thai writers often forget to use plurals in English, or use them the wrong way.\n*   **Verb agreement:** Make sure your verbs agree with their subjects (e.g., "it makes" instead of "it make"). This is also a common L1 interference point.<br>	\N	\N	2025-08-22
