29031	2025-08-30 14:11:38.283781+00	2026	Free time Activities	Many teenagers all have their hobbies to help them relaxed. While there are hobbies all around the world and varies in different ways, as for Thai teenagers' hobby vividly reflects their lives. Two of the most popular among Thai teenagers are playing games and studying.<br><br><br>Primarily, Thai teenagers loves to relive their stress by playing games in their free' time. There are several different kinds of games that are greatly known, such as, statergic games like "RoV and Valorant. Some people may say that it's a waste of time but it helps teenagers to improve their critical thinking skills, if it's done the right way. This is one of the major reasons why video games has deserve its hype on Thai teenagers.<br><br><br>As well as playing video games, studying is another popular hobby. Although it has a big contrast to playing games, Thai teenagers are able to balance their free time excellently. Nowadays, Thai teenagers strive to get into their dream school, particularly Triamudom and Mahidol Wittyanusorn School, one of the most difficult schools to enroll in. It's the main reason why a majority of Thai teenagers spend most of their time studying.<br><br><br>All in all, playing games and studying are extremely popular hobbies in Thai teenager's world. Due to their lack of free time and the need for academic excellence in their society. They mostly have hobbies that revolve around their everyday lives, but they all have the goal of succeding in knowledge.	244	14.0	You used some great vocabulary like 'vividly' and 'strategic', which helps make your writing engaging!	B2	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	4.0	<p>You identified two free time activities, playing games and studying, and explained their popularity in Thailand. However, your explanation for 'studying' as a hobby felt a little less developed than 'playing games'. Make sure to fully explain both points.</p><p>👉 To Improve: Develop all your ideas completely and provide sufficient detail for each part of the question.<br>❌ Weakness: You explained that Thai teenagers strive to get into good schools, and this is why they spend time studying. This explains why they *need* to study, but not as much why studying is a *popular hobby* in the same way that playing games is. To clarify, study is usually thought of as work not as a leisure activity, so it requires extra explanation.<br>✨ Improved: "Studying can be a challenging activity, but for many Thai teenagers, it also becomes a rewarding hobby. They might enjoy solving complex problems, engaging in academic competitions, or exploring new subjects beyond the classroom, finding personal satisfaction and intellectual stimulation in their learning."<br>💡 Explanation: Expanding on *why* studying is a popular hobby, beyond just the necessity for academic excellence, helps the reader understand its appeal as a free time activity.</p>	3.0	<p>You used an appropriate tone for an article and tried to keep the reader interested. However, sometimes you presented dependent clauses as if they were full sentences, or connected them in a way that affected the clarity. This can make your writing a little harder to follow.</p><p>👉 To Improve: Ensure that all your sentences are complete thoughts and that dependent clauses are properly connected to main clauses.<br>❌ Weakness: You wrote: "Due to their lack of free time and the need for academic excellence in their society." as a separate sentence.<br>✨ Improved: "All in all, playing games and studying are extremely popular hobbies in Thai teenagers' world, often chosen due to their lack of free time and the need for academic excellence in their society."<br>💡 Explanation: Connecting the dependent clause ("Due to...") to the main sentence makes the meaning much clearer and improves the flow of your writing.</p>	4.0	<p>Your essay was well-organized into four paragraphs, which is great for readability. Your introduction, body, and conclusion were clear. However, some of the connections between your ideas could be a little smoother.</p><p>👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases to show clearer relationships between your ideas, making your writing flow more naturally.<br>❌ Weakness: You wrote: "This is one of the major reasons why video games has deserve its hype on Thai teenagers. As well as playing video games, studying is another popular hobby." The connection between the two sentences could be clearer.<br>✨ Improved: "While video games clearly deserve their hype among Thai teenagers for these reasons, studying is another equally popular hobby."<br>💡 Explanation: Using 'While' and 'equally' creates a stronger contrast and connection, showing how the two hobbies are related but distinct, leading the reader more smoothly from one idea to the next.</p>	3.0	<p>You used good vocabulary related to the topic, including 'vividly' and 'strategic' (even with the small spelling error!). However, there are some recurring grammar patterns that affect clarity, especially with verb forms.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Many teenagers all have their hobbies to help them relaxed."<br>✨ Correction: "Many teenagers all have hobbies to help them relax."<br>💡 Explanation: In English, after 'help someone', we usually use the base form of the verb ('relax'), not the past participle ('relaxed'). This is a common word form issue for Thai learners. We also do not need to use "their" to indicate posssession.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "Thai teenagers loves to relive their stress by playing games..."<br>✨ Correction: "Thai teenagers love to relive their stress by playing games..."<br>💡 Explanation: In English, verbs change their form depending on the subject. For plural subjects like 'teenagers', we use 'love'. In Thai, verbs do not change for plurals, which is why this can be a challenge.</p><p>❌ Problem: You wrote: "This is one of the major reasons why video games has deserve its hype on Thai teenagers."<br>✨ Correction: "This is one of the major reasons why video games deserves their hype."<br>💡 Explanation: The auxiliary verb 'has' needs to be followed by a past participle (e.g., 'deserved'), or the main verb 'deserve' should be in the correct present simple form for a plural subject ('deserve' for 'video games' if it's the subject) or singular ('deserves' if 'video games' is treated as a singular concept, which seems to be the case here). In English, 'has' followed by a bare infinitive like 'deserve' is incorrect, and the simplest fix here is to change 'has deserve' to 'deserves'.</p><p>🎯 YOUR ACTION PLAN<br>1. Complete all parts of writing tasks and develop each point fully.<br>2. Ensure that dependent clauses are properly connected to main clauses to avoid fragments.<br>3. Practice using a wider variety of linking words and phrases for better cohesion.<br>4. Review verb forms, especially after 'help' and for subject-verb agreement.</p>	\N	\N	2025-08-30
28763	2025-12-14 09:33:33.68524+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. There was no anyone outside the house. The city look like abandon there wasn't any living thing here, So I must to find that what happen last night. I went to city center and that made me founded a group of people there. When I went near them. That make me Know that there are scienetis. But that moment they Know that I am here, So them make my come to safety zone. After I know what happen. I am very shock that last night there was acid rain that make every	103	9.0	Hello Best! 👋<br><br>This is a very intriguing start to a mystery story! 🕵️‍♂️ I really liked how you built the atmosphere of an abandoned city and the scary discovery of acid rain. You successfully created a sense of danger and curiosity right from the beginning. <br><br>I have a few tips to help you take your storytelling to the next level! 📋<br>1. <b>The Ending!</b> ✍️ Your story stopped right in the middle of a sentence! Make sure to manage your time so you can give your story a proper ending.<br>2. <b>Grammar Check!</b> 🛠️ Watch out for verb forms after 'make' or 'must'. For example, 'must to find' should be 'must <b>find</b>'.<br>3. <b>Structure!</b> 📝 Try to group your ideas into paragraphs to make the story easier for the reader to follow.	A2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	2.0	You made a great start by using the given sentence perfectly! 🌟 The ideas of an empty city and acid rain are very creative and fit the 'mystery' theme well.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Complete the Mission!</b> 🏁 The story ends very abruptly at 'make every...'. The reader is left hanging! Always try to write a conclusion, even if it's short, so we know what happens to the character.</li><li><b>Explain the 'Why'!</b> ❓ You mentioned 'scientists' and a 'safety zone'. Adding a little more detail about *why* they were there would make the story even more interesting.</li>	3.0	You set a spooky and mysterious tone effectively! 👻 The description of the city as 'abandon' (abandoned) and 'no living thing' really helped the reader picture the scene.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Emotional Connection!</b> 💓 You said 'I am very shock', but showing *how* the character felt (e.g., 'My hands were shaking', 'I couldn't breathe') makes the story more exciting than just saying the emotion.</li><li><b>Clarity!</b> 💡 Some sentences were a bit hard to follow, like 'that made me founded'. keeping your sentences simple and clear helps the reader stay in the story.</li>	2.0	You used some good linking words like 'So', 'When', 'But', and 'After' to move the story forward in time. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 The whole story is one long block of text. Try to start a new paragraph when the scene changes—for example, one paragraph for waking up, one for finding the scientists, and one for the explanation.</li><li><b>Flow!</b> 🌊 Some of your sentences feel a bit disconnected. Using words like 'Suddenly' or 'However' can help connect your exciting events more smoothly.</li>	2.0	You used some good specific vocabulary like 'city center', 'safety zone', and 'acid rain'! 🌧️<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you polish your grammar:<br><li><b>Verb Patterns!</b> 🛠️ After 'make' and 'must', we use the base verb without 'to'. So 'must to find' -> 'must <b>find</b>' and 'make me founded' -> 'made me <b>find</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Forms!</b> 🔄 'The city look like abandon' should be 'The city looked <b>abandoned</b>' (adjective).</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Scienetis' should be '<b>scientists</b>'.</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ You mostly used past tense well, but watch out for consistent forms: 'make me know' -> 'made me <b>know</b>'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
