rder for the target reader to stay engaged. The thesis statement could also be more clearly articulated.	2.0	You attempt to organize your text into paragraphs, with an introduction, a body, and a conclusion. You use some basic linking words. However, the coherence could be improved by using a wider variety of linking words and cohesive devices to connect sentences and ideas more smoothly. For instance, the transition from "Do to sometimes people don't care there neighbors, but they also bring gifts" is awkward and disrupts the flow. Paragraphing could also be more distinct to separate different aspects of your argument.	2.0	You use everyday vocabulary, generally appropriately. You use simple grammatical forms. However, there are frequent errors with spelling, subject-verb agreement, and sentence structure. These errors are noticeable and occasionally impede communication, making it difficult to fully understand your intended meaning in some parts of the essay.	\N	\N	2025-07-13
