he correct English prepositions for common phrases.<br><br><b>Problem:</b> There are some spelling mistakes that make the text harder to read, such as "instragram" and "Becuase".<br><b>Correction:</b> "Instagram", "Because"<br><b>Explanation:</b> Always double-check your spelling, as correct spelling helps your writing look professional and makes it easier for the reader to understand.<br><br><b>Problem:</b> You sometimes miss articles (a/an/the) or use the wrong form of a word, for example: "They spent a lot of money to send we to get knowlage at school."<br><b>Correction:</b> "They spent a lot of money to send us to gain knowledge at school."<br><b>Explanation:</b> Thai doesn't use articles like 'a', 'an', or 'the', which can make them tricky in English. Also, be careful with word forms (e.g., noun vs. verb vs. adjective).	\N	\N	2025-08-21
