tail! 🌟 Your explanation of why online shopping is preferred, and the specific benefits of your Airpods (even for mood!) were very well-articulated. Your content is highly relevant and engaging.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Online Security!</b> 🔒 You mentioned you 'don't need to go to store or talke with people'. While convenient, could you briefly acknowledge any potential downsides of online shopping (e.g., delivery issues, returns) to present a balanced view?</li><li><b>Airpod Model!</b> 🎧 You mentioned 'Airpod 4'. Is there a specific feature of this model that makes it superior to others?</li>	4.0	Your tone is personal and conversational, yet also persuasive, particularly when discussing the advantages of online shopping. 🗣️ You connect well with the reader by sharing your personal experiences.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Vary Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ While your sentences are clear, experimenting with slightly more complex or varied structures could add sophistication to your writing.</li>	5.0	Your article has an excellent logical structure, moving smoothly from general shopping preferences to a specific best purchase and then offering concluding advice. 🧱 Your use of linking words like 'such as', 'And', and 'As a result' is very effective.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Nothing!</b> 🌟 Your organization is clear and effective. Keep up the great work!</li>	3.0	You use a wide range of relevant vocabulary, including terms like 'promotions', 'coupons', 'unpackaging', 'satisfying', 'worth', and 'situation'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Prises' -> '<b>prices</b>', 'talke' -> '<b>talk</b>', 'unpackaging' -> '<b>unpacking</b>'.</li><li><b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ 'It's has a lot' -> 'it <b>has</b> a lot'. 'Wait the package arrive' -> 'wait <b>for</b> the package to arrive'. 'You are enjoy with it' -> 'you <b>enjoy</b> it'.</li><li><b>Punctuation!</b> 🛑 'Messy in my bag my pocket' needs a comma: 'messy in my bag, my pocket'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
28984	2025-12-14 09:36:24.34571+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. A tiny yellow bear wearing a mini red shirt. The tiny bear say I'm pooh what's your name? I say my name is christofer robin, Pooh say I think I remember you, you are my old friend. I say I know but I don't have work and family to take care. Pooh say okay.. then I will go, as I look back Pooh is dissapear I panick and found Pooh' friends. I ask Where is Pooh?. Pooh and his friend say something is here, Pls help us , As look it no one there then I just realize it just me so I pretend to fight air. At the end I sit with pooh on the banch I look at him Pooh im sorry for letting you behide. Pooh say it okay... I wake up Im with pooh But Im late for work. I ran to my office and did the presentation well. After that I always have time for my family and my old friend. I bring my daughter to play with them. We live happy ever after. c the old friend is pooh and his friends)	199	13.0	Hello Platwo! 👋<br><br>This is such a sweet and imaginative story about Winnie the Pooh and Christopher Robin! 🍯 I loved the playful dialogue and the heartwarming message about making time for old friends and family. The dream sequence and the lesson learned were beautifully conveyed!<br><br>I have a few tips to help you make your writing even more charming! 📋<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 Watch out for words like 'dissapear' (disappear), 'behide' (behind), and 'christofer' (Christopher).<br>2. <b>Punctuation for Dialogue!</b> 💬 When writing dialogue, remember to use quotation marks and start each new speaker's words on a new line.<br>3. <b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ Since this is a story about something that happened, try to consistently use past tense verbs (e.g., 'Pooh <b>said</b>' instead of 'Pooh say').	B1	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You crafted a very relevant and heartwarming narrative, beautifully blending the world of Winnie the Pooh with real-life lessons about balancing work and family. 🌟 The content is creative and emotionally resonant.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Clarify the "Pretend" Part!</b> ❓ When you said 'I pretend to fight air', could you briefly explain why? Was it to hide from Pooh's friends, or to avoid looking silly?</li><li><b>The Reunion!</b> 🍯 The moment you sit with Pooh on the bench is lovely. Could you add a small detail about what you and Pooh talked about, or a shared memory?</li>	3.0	You successfully conveyed a nostalgic and comforting tone, making the reader feel the warmth of old friendships. 💖 The dialogue, though informally presented, effectively captured the essence of Pooh's character.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Dialogue Formatting!</b> 💬 Proper punctuation and new lines for each speaker would greatly enhance the readability and professionalism of your dialogue.</li>	3.0	Your story has a clear chronological progression, moving from the initial dream encounter to the real-life application of the lesson learned. 🧱 Your use of linking words like 'then', 'as I look back', and 'after that' helps guide the reader.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 📝 While the story is short, breaking it into paragraphs (e.g., one for the initial encounter, one for the panic, one for the reunion, one for the real-life lesson) would improve readability.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Some sentences are very long and contain multiple ideas. Breaking these into shorter, more focused sentences would make your story easier to follow.</li>	2.0	You used simple, clear vocabulary that suited the whimsical nature of the story. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Belive' -> '<b>believe</b>', 'dissapear' -> '<b>disappear</b>', 'behide' -> '<b>behind</b>', 'christofer' -> '<b>Christopher</b>'.</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'Say' -> '<b>said</b>' (many times). 'I'm with pooh' -> 'I <b>was</b> with Pooh'.</li><li><b>Possessives!</b> 📝 'Pooh' friends' -> 'Pooh<b>'s</b> friends'.</li><li><b>Punctuation!</b> 🛑 Many sentences run together without proper punctuation. Use full stops (.) to separate your thoughts.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
29079	2025-12-14 15:54:59.757949+00	2026	Term 2 Midterms 2025-6	From Ikkyu,<br><br><br>Hi,<br><br>Wow! I'm also very exciting for camping this weekend. So after I've read your text, I think we should take a train on Saturday morning and thanks for your dad of that. And I don't think we should just only cook sausages, we would hungry before another meal. I suggest you to prepare any eggs or some pork or beef, it would make us feel full before another meal. And we need to bring blankets, lots of clothes and I would bring my own some hoodies, I think you should prepare it as well. So, I'll see you in The Train Station this Saturday morning.<br><br><br>See you soon, Alex	112	15.0	Hello Ikkyu! 👋<br><br>You wrote a very friendly email! "Wow! I'm also very exciting" sets a great mood right away (even with the small grammar slip!). ⚡ Identifying that you might get hungry with just sausages was smart.<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>Adjectives!</b> 🎨 "I am exciting" -> "I am <b>excited</b>".<br>2. <b>Verbs!</b> ⚙️ "suggest you to prepare" -> "suggest <b>that you</b> prepare".<br>3. <b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 "thanks for your dad" -> "thanks <b>to</b> your dad".\n	B1+	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You answered fully! ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Details!</b> 💭 Suggesting "pork or beef" is good, maybe add "for a BBQ" to make the picture clearer!</li>\n	4.0	Your tone was perfect for a friend. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Flow!</b> 🌊 "and thanks for your dad of that" - this interrupted the flow a bit. Maybe put it in a separate sentence: "Please thank your dad for the offer!"</li>\n	3.0	You used paragraphs effectively. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linking!</b> 🔗 You used "And" a lot to start sentences. Try "Also," "Plus," or "In addition,".</li>\n	3.0	Good vocabulary like "hoodies"! 👏<br><br>Watch these errors:<br><li><b>Excited/Exciting!</b> 😲 "I'm exciting" means YOU are fun. "I'm <b>excited</b>" means you are happy.</li><li><b>Modals!</b> 🔮 "we would hungry" -> "we would <b>be</b> hungry" or "get hungry".</li>\n	\N	\N	2025-12-14
34043	2026-02-23 14:12:47.817065+00	2026	Question 2 (Article)	In my area there have some places that young people can have an exercise or do sports there but not many. In my area there have parks, hall to organise some activities such as aerobic. The area that allow young people to create activities it's not many but if they want to do sports my area would great for them. There ave gyms, badminton field and also with the soccer field so it's very great choice for them to do sports near here.\n\nAbsolutely, young people should do sports or outdoor activity regularly for their health and someone have very great talent they can start career by sports. Not only that young people will have meet people and can get along with society. Every school in Thailand supporting this young people health, their have P.E class and health education. Health is the most important thing in life.	158	14.0	Hi Kathi! 🌟 You did a fantastic job answering all the questions in the prompt and sharing your thoughtful ideas about sports in Thailand! 💪 My main 'homework' for you is to work on 'gluing' your paragraphs together so your article feels like one smooth story instead of separate answers. You have some great ideas, and I'd love to see them flow more naturally in your next piece! 🚀 All the best, Ed	B1	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	It was wonderful to see how you listed specific facilities like 'gyms, badminton field and also with the soccer field', which really helped me visualize your neighborhood! 🌟 This detailed description ensures the reader is fully informed about the sports options available to young people in your area. 📝	3.0	Your point that 'someone have very great talent they can start career by sports' was a really insightful addition. 🚀 However, the article feels a bit like a list of answers to the prompt rather than a smooth story that flows together. 📓 For your next article, try to imagine you are telling a friend all these things together so the ideas feel more connected! 💡	3.0	I see that you used 'Not only that' to transition between different points, which is a good start. 🧩 However, because you answer each question from the prompt one by one, the article feels a bit disjointed. Try to use more 'linking words' like 'Furthermore' or 'As a result' to glue your paragraphs together and make the whole article feel like one big idea! 🌈	3.0	When you wrote 'In my area there have parks', I could understand your meaning perfectly, although using 'there are' is the standard way to show something exists. ✨ This type of error with 'there have' happens a few times, so my tip is to practice using 'There is/are' when you are describing what can be found in a place. ✍️	\N	\N	2026-02-23
29031	2025-07-24 15:32:06.58681+00	2026	A Place I Love	A place I love is Pattaya which is located around the central south of Thailand. I'm really fonded of this place because of the memories I've made while I was staying there. Pattaya is greatly known for its sandy beach and vivid night life. Furthermore, it's also incredibly popular among tourists who visited Thailand. It's a place that you need to experience yourself at least once.<br><br><br>There are several reasons why Pattaya is packed with tourists almost everyday, and why I personally think that it deserves the hype. Firstly, Pattaya has a great mix of city and nature all together. It's a seaside filled with loads of people enjoying must-do activities, such as skiing, swimming or maybe even go on boat tours. Although it may seem not so relaxing, then I recommend enjoying the sunset at dawn. I have been admiring the scenery ever since, and never got bored of it. Next, the night life is something you can't miss. People never sleeps at night in Pattaya, since they'd be going to the night market to buy the local fresh seafood or they'd be at the bar district that is filled with people everyday. I've been to both of the districts, and I'm sure that you'll regret not visiting both of them.<br><br><br>All in all, Pattaya is a unique and an incredible place to visit during anytime' of the year, especially New Years, since they are extremely precise with the celebration. I've loved going to this place since I was young. Which is why you 'can't miss out.	258	14.0	Overall, Racing, you wrote an interesting article about Pattaya. You provided good details about why it's a popular place. To make your writing even better, try to focus more on your personal feelings and experiences when describing "a place you love." Also, pay close attention to little grammar points like subject-verb agreement and word choice, and make sure your punctuation is just right. Keep up the great work!	B2	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	Part 1	4.0	Racing did a good job of introducing Pattaya as a place they love and supported it with relevant details like the beach, nightlife, and tourist popularity. Racing also included reasons why they personally like it, such as the mix of city and nature, and specific activities. However, sometimes the essay reads more like a general description of Pattaya for tourists rather than a deep, personal reflection on *why* Racing loves it so much, beyond just the memories.\n\nExample: "Pattaya is greatly known for its sandy beach and vivid night life. Furthermore, it's also incredibly popular among tourists who visited Thailand."\nProblem: This sentence describes Pattaya from a general tourist perspective, not necessarily from a personal one about why *you* love it.\nHow to fix it: You could add more personal feelings or specific experiences that show your love. For example, instead of just saying it's popular among tourists, you might say, "I love seeing how happy the tourists are in Pattaya; their excitement makes the place even more special to me."\n\nExample: "There are several reasons why Pattaya is packed with tourists almost everyday, and why I personally think that it deserves the hype."\nProblem: Again, this sounds like you are trying to convince a general reader about Pattaya's worth, rather than sharing your personal connection and feelings that make it *a place you love*.\nHow to fix it: You could rephrase this to be more about your personal reasons. For example, "I think Pattaya deserves its popularity, and for me, it's special because of [your personal reason]."	3.0	The essay communicates straightforward ideas and generally holds the reader's attention. Racing uses an appropriate style for an article, trying to engage the reader with phrases like "It's a place that you need to experience yourself at least once" and "I'm sure that you'll regret not visiting both of them." However, the essay doesn't consistently communicate more complex personal feelings or reflections effectively, often leaning more towards a descriptive, informative tone for a general audience rather than a deeply personal one about "a place I love."\n\nExample: "It's a place that you need to experience yourself at least once."\nProblem: This is a common phrase used to recommend a place to others, but it doesn't clearly show your personal feelings or connection to the place.\nHow to fix it: You could phrase it to show your personal feeling more directly. For example, "It's a place that I feel everyone should experience at least once, because it holds so many special memories for me."\n\nExample: "People never sleeps at night in Pattaya, since they'd be going to the night market to buy the local fresh seafood or they'd be at the bar district that is filled with people everyday."\nProblem: This sentence clearly communicates information, but it doesn't really try to get the reader to feel your personal excitement or connection to the nightlife.\nHow to fix it: You could add a personal touch to make it more engaging. For example, "The nightlife is something you can't miss; I love how the energy of the city never sleeps, whether people are enjoying fresh seafood at the market or the lively atmosphere in the bar district."	4.0	The essay is generally well-organised with a clear introduction, body paragraphs that discuss different aspects of Pattaya, and a conclusion. Racing uses a variety of linking words and phrases such as "Furthermore," "Firstly," "Next," and "All in all" to connect ideas. The flow is generally logical and easy to follow.\n\nExample: "Although it may seem not so relaxing, then I recommend enjoying the sunset at dawn. I have been admiring the scenery ever since, and never got bored of it."\nProblem: The word "then" here isn't quite right. It makes the sentence a little confusing.\nHow to fix it: You could remove "then" or use a different linking word. For example, "Although it may seem not so relaxing, I recommend enjoying the sunset at dawn." or "However, if you're looking for relaxation, I recommend enjoying the sunset at dawn."\n\nExample: "All in all, Pattaya is a unique and an incredible place to visit during anytime' of the year, especially New Years, since they are extremely precise with the celebration. I've loved going to this place since I was young. Which is why you 'can't miss out."\nProblem: The punctuation is a little off with the apostrophe in "anytime'" and "Which is why" starts a new sentence without proper connection.\nHow to fix it: You could remove the apostrophe from "anytime" and connect the last two sentences more smoothly. For example, "All in all, Pattaya is a unique and incredible place to visit any time of the year, especially New Years, since they are extremely precise with the celebration; I've loved going to this place since I was young, which is why you can't miss out."	3.0	Racing uses a range of everyday vocabulary appropriately, such as "sandy beach," "vivid nightlife," "packed with tourists," "must-do activities," and "fresh seafood." There is also an attempt at some more varied vocabulary like "fonded of" and "deserves the hype," though "fonded of" is not a correct word. The essay uses a range of simple and some complex grammatical forms with a good degree of control. There are occasional errors, but they generally do not impede communication.\n\nExample: "I'm really fonded of this place because of the memories I've made while I was staying there."\nProblem: "Fonded of" is not the correct word. The correct phrase is "fond of."\nHow to fix it: You should say, "I'm really fond of this place..."\n\nExample: "People never sleeps at night in Pattaya, since they'd be going to the night market to buy the local fresh seafood or they'd be at the bar district that is filled with people everyday."\nProblem: "People" is a plural noun, so the verb should be "sleep," not "sleeps." Also, "everyday" should be "every day" when referring to "each day."\nHow to fix it: You should say, "People never sleep at night in Pattaya, since they'd be going to the night market to buy the local fresh seafood or they'd be at the bar district that is filled with people every day."\n\nExample: "I've been to both of the districts, and I'm sure that you'll regret not visiting both of them."\nProblem: While understandable, this sentence is a little strong and could be phrased more smoothly.\nHow to fix it: You could say, "I've been to both districts, and I'm sure you'll be glad you visited them." or "I've visited both districts, and I highly recommend experiencing them."	\N	\N	2025-07-24
