33952	2025-12-14 09:36:22.75323+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. His name was Kevin, who was the middle age with the carrer was scienctist, and his favourite hobby were discover about the mythery object and play football. Kevin would have trip with 2 friend on this weekend, Australia. The main of trip was to find out the true of dangerous that these object on sky can make make it.  After that, they arrived to the airport but it late for 40 minutes. The 2 of friend took a picture during flying that it gone now but Kevin didn't mention about this. He told to them, where was a correct direction that this object fly it, and his feel was want to ate some food right now because they didn't eat any before arrive. The next day them drove each own car to carry a speacial things for these project.  Then, they arrived it and rest in living room that the place, where they would work on it. Kevin shouted it loud and point finger on sky , which he said "everyone look on sky". After that everyone shocked but it didn't long because them recogniszed that we have a project. The 2 of freind take a long thing that have a sharp for have a test.  Finally, They have a result of test and it wasn't dangerouse for people. It was very safe for worldwide. Kevin and friends can find out and safe life all the world.	248	10.0	Hello Ken! 👋<br><br>This is a very ambitious and complex story about a scientist, Kevin, and his friends discovering a mysterious object in the sky! 🔭 I liked the idea of them traveling to Australia and doing a project to find out if it was dangerous. You have a lot of creative ideas here!<br><br>I have a few tips to help make your scientific adventure clearer! 📋<br>1. <b>Clarity!</b> 💡 The plot is quite confusing. Try to simplify the main events and ensure the reader can follow Kevin's journey.<br>2. <b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ Watch out for phrases like 'the carrer was scienctist' (should be 'career <b>as a scientist</b>').<br>3. <b>Conciseness!</b> 🗣️ Some sentences are very long and convoluted. Break them down into shorter, more direct statements.	A2+	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	4.0	You crafted a very imaginative plot about a team of scientists investigating a mysterious object from space. 🌟 The core idea of a global safety mission is very strong.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Connect to Prompt!</b> ❓ The initial 'couldn't believe my eyes' moment feels disconnected from the main story about Kevin. Try to integrate it more directly into his discovery of the mysterious object.</li><li><b>Simplify the Project!</b> 🔭 The description of the project is a bit hard to follow ('take a long thing that have a sharp'). Clearly explain what they are doing to test the object.</li>	2.0	You have a very complex story, but at times the meaning is obscured due to grammatical errors and unclear phrasing. 🧩<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Focus on Clear Communication!</b> 💡 Before writing, try to outline your story to ensure each event logically leads to the next. This will help the reader follow your exciting ideas.</li><li><b>Dialogue Clarity!</b> 🗣️ 'Kevin shouted it loud and point finger on sky, which he said "everyone look on sky"'. This can be simplified to 'Kevin shouted loudly, pointing at the sky, "Everyone, look on the sky!"'</li>	2.0	You used some linking words like 'After that', 'The next day', and 'Then' to connect your ideas. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Logical Progression!</b> ➡️ Some events jump around a bit. For example, Kevin's hobby (football) seems unrelated to the main plot. Ensure all details contribute to the central story.</li><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 🧱 Breaking your text into shorter paragraphs would help organize your complex ideas and make them easier to digest.</li>	2.0	You attempted ambitious vocabulary like 'career', 'mystery', and 'recognize' (even if misspelled). 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Carrer' -> '<b>career</b>', 'mythery' -> '<b>mystery</b>', 'recogniszed' -> '<b>recognized</b>', 'dangerouse' -> '<b>dangerous</b>'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'The carrer was scienctist' -> 'whose career <b>was that of a scientist</b>'. 'His feel was want to ate' -> 'he <b>felt</b> like he wanted to <b>eat</b>'.</li><li><b>Infinitives!</b> 🛠️ 'Want to ate' -> 'want to <b>eat</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Take a long thing that have a sharp' is unclear. What *is* that thing?</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
