ting could benefit from stronger transitions between sentences and more varied sentence structures. For example, try using transition words or phrases such as "Furthermore," "In addition," or "However" to create a smoother flow. Also, try to vary your sentence structure; for instance, avoid starting multiple sentences in a row with the word "I."	3.0	While you use a reasonable range of vocabulary, the numerous grammatical and sentence structure errors significantly impact the clarity and quality of your writing. Examples include errors such as "it make us to know" (which should be "it makes us know"), "the humpback whale sing like" (which needs restructuring), "the male whale only sing but the female are not sing" (which also needs restructuring), "humpback whale use to communicate," and "like I want to heard them song." To improve, it is essential to focus on mastering basic grammar rules and sentence construction. Proofreading and seeking feedback from a teacher or language partner will be highly beneficial. Also, avoid overly informal language; for instance, avoid using phrases like "super cool" in academic writing.	\N	\N	2025-07-11
