f being a "lamp lose in huge chaos." To improve, ensure your language is consistently clear; there are moments where the phrasing is a little unclear (e.g., "how struggle it is to fitting in").	2.5	Your text is generally well organised and coherent, following a chronological order of your experience. You used some linking words and phrases to connect your ideas, such as "When I first," "and of course," "Still," and "But at the end." This helps the reader follow your story. To improve, you could enhance the coherence by using a wider variety of cohesive devices and ensuring smoother transitions between sentences.	2.0	You used everyday vocabulary to describe your feelings and the situation, such as "nervous," "society," "struggle," and "friends." There is some appropriate use of vocabulary related to your experience. You used a range of simple grammatical forms with a good degree of control. However, there are noticeable errors with verb forms ("fitting in" instead of "fit in"), articles ("A lots" instead of "A lot"), and sentence structure ("It was like a lamp lose in huge chaos"). While these errors are present, the meaning can still generally be determined. To improve, focus on accuracy with verb forms and articles.	\N	\N	2025-07-13
