!</li><li><b>Comparison!</b> ⚖️ You mentioned stores have discounts in June/December. Adding a specific example of something you bought then would strengthen your point.</li>	3.0	You have a nice, personal tone that fits a school magazine well! 🗣️ 'I'm the one who likes to shop...' connects well with the reader.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Hook the Reader!</b> 🎣 Start with a question like 'Do you hate walking around crowded malls?' to grab attention immediately.</li><li><b>Closing!</b> 🔚 Add a short wrapping-up sentence at the end, like 'So, for me, online shopping is the clear winner!'</li>	4.0	You effectively separated your two main points into two paragraphs. 🧱 This made your article very easy to read.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linkers!</b> 🔗 You use 'But' and 'because' a lot. Try using 'However', 'Furthermore', or 'On the other hand' to make your writing sound more advanced.</li>	3.0	Good use of vocabulary like 'platform', 'discount', and 'scrolling'! 📱<br><br>Here are some fixes:<br><li><b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ 'Have platform online' -> '<b>There are</b> online platforms'.</li><li><b>Infinitive Verbs!</b> 🔄 'I like to shopping' -> 'I like to <b>shop</b>'.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ 'It's a lot more than other months' -> 'The discounts are much <b>bigger</b> than in other months'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Shop in online' -> 'Shop <b>online</b>' (no 'in').</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
