 the next. Also, paying attention to some grammar points will really help your ideas shine! You have a great understanding of the topic, so keep practicing these fundamental areas.	B1+	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	Part 1	4.0	Kaohom L, you have effectively addressed the task by describing Chiang Rai as a place you love and providing several reasons for this, covering nature, architecture, food (Kao Soi), and art (Baan Dum museum). You clearly convey why the mix of city and nature, along with the kind people, makes it special to you. The target reader is generally well-informed. To achieve a score of 5, you could develop some points further with more specific examples or sensory details, ensuring all content is fully elaborated to fully inform the target reader.	2.0	You attempt to use the conventions of an essay with a clear introduction and conclusion. You communicate straightforward ideas, and while your enthusiasm for Chiang Rai is clear, the overall effectiveness in holding the target reader's attention is hampered by the numerous language errors. The use of phrases like \\"trust me this is so delicious\\" is slightly informal for an essay, and combined with the intrusive spelling mistakes, it affects the overall communicative impact. To improve to a 5, you should consistently use conventions of an essay, maintaining a more formal and objective tone, and communicate both straightforward and complex ideas in a way that is consistently engaging and appropriate for the task, with minimal distracting errors.	3.0	Your essay is generally well organised with a clear opening, body, and conclusion. You use some linking words like \\"Another thing that make me,\\" \\"Fristly,\\" \\"Also,\\" \\"However,\\" and \\"There are several reason why I love this city.\\" However, there are some sentences that feel a bit disconnected within paragraphs, and the overall flow could be smoother. For example, the transition between discussing food/art and then nature within the second paragraph could be more fluid. To achieve a score of 5, you should use a wider variety of cohesive devices and organisational patterns more consistently to ensure the text is highly coherent and easy to follow throughout.	2.0	You use everyday vocabulary generally appropriately, relevant to the topic of travel and places (e.g., \\"traditional,\\" \\"nature,\\" \\"relax,\\" \\"signature food,\\" \\"delicious,\\" \\"fantastic,\\" \\"museum,\\" \\"mountains,\\" \\"friendly people\\"). You use simple grammatical forms with a good degree of control. However, errors are noticeable and often impede communication, particularly due to frequent and intrusive spelling mistakes. Specific examples include: \\"it a city\\" (should be \\"it is a city\\"), \\"algritechtures\\" (architecture, repeated), \\"fristly\\" (firstly), \\"recomend\\" (recommend), \\"coco nut\\" (coconut), \\"which is call\\" (which is called), \\"I was really impress\\" (I was really impressed), \\"it not just city\\" (it is not just a city), \\"suround\\" (surrounded), \\"Every times\\" (Every time), \\"possitive\\" (positive), \\"sooting\\" (soothing), and \\"thrue\\" (through\\"). These spelling errors, along with other grammatical inaccuracies, make the text harder to understand at times. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to demonstrate a higher level of grammatical control and accuracy, including very few, if any, spelling errors, and use a wider range of vocabulary with greater precision.	\N	\N	2025-07-22
