ced and concluded your essay. To improve, focus on your spelling and grammar, especially subject-verb agreement and article usage. Also, try to use a wider range of vocabulary to avoid repetition.	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	Part 2	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-08-12
28863	2025-07-23 15:00:49.43265+00	2026	A Place I Love	The place that I love, called 'Salem'. Salem is one of the town in USA, which is unique because of it's history. People called it 'The town of witch hunt'. This town located next to the Attlantic Sea.<br><br><br>Let me explain more cleary for the reason that makes me love it. Salem is a charming town for it's beautiful nature. For examples the beautiful sea veiw, when I first saw it I'm feeling relax and calm. The forest and mountain veiw also! It was green everywhere, soothing waterfalls these things made me feel fresh. They reminded me that I choosed the right place to relax with my family that summer.<br><br><br>In conclusion, Salem is a charming town because of it's beautiful nature that attrach travellers to come to this town. It not just famous for it's beautiful nature, but it is famous for it's unqiue history too. Today Salem town is one of the best town in USA now	159	11.0	Namo T, you wrote about Salem and explained why you love it by talking about its history and beautiful nature. You shared how the sea, forest, and waterfalls made you feel relaxed. You did a good job of introducing the town and giving reasons. To make your writing even better, you can focus on making your sentences connect more smoothly and correcting some mistakes in spelling, punctuation, and grammar so your message is always very clear. Keep practicing, and you'll improve a lot!	B1+	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	Part 1	3.0	Namo T, you introduced Salem as a place you love, mentioning its unique history and natural beauty. You gave examples like the sea view and waterfalls, explaining how they made you feel relaxed. You included the required points about the town and your feelings. However, the connection between the "witch hunt" history and *why* you love the place could be stronger. The essay mostly focuses on the nature aspect.\n\n*   Example: You wrote, "Salem is one of the town in USA, which is unique because of it's history. People called it 'The town of witch hunt'."\n    Problem: You mention the unique history, but you don't really explain *how* this history contributes to your love for the town. It feels like a separate fact rather than a reason for your affection.\n    How to fix it: You could expand on this by saying how the history makes the town feel, for example, "Salem is unique because of its fascinating history, often called 'The town of witch hunt.' This past gives the town a mysterious and interesting atmosphere that I really love to explore." This directly links the history to your feelings.\n\n*   Example: You wrote, "In conclusion, Salem is a charming town because of it's beautiful nature that attrach travellers to come to this town. It not just famous for it's beautiful nature, but it is famous for it's unqiue history too. Today Salem town is one of the best town in USA now"\n    Problem: Your conclusion brings together nature and history, but the last sentence "Today Salem town is one of the best town in USA now" feels like a sudden, general statement that isn't fully supported by what you wrote before.\n    How to fix it: Make sure your conclusion summarizes your main points and connects back to your personal love for the place. You could say, "In conclusion, Salem's charming natural beauty, combined with its fascinating and unique history, makes it a truly special place that continues to attract visitors. It's a town I love because it offers both peace in nature and a captivating glimpse into the past."	3.0	You tried to write an article for a travel website, and you communicated straightforward ideas about Salem. You made an effort to hold the reader's attention by describing its beauty. However, some parts felt a bit simple or direct for an article, and the overall impression could be more engaging for a wider audience.\n\n*   Example: You wrote, "Let me explain more cleary for the reason that makes me love it."\n    Problem: This sentence is very direct and conversational, almost like you are speaking to the reader. It's a bit too informal for an article.\n    How to fix it: You can start this paragraph in a more descriptive way that doesn't sound like you are talking directly to the reader. For example, "Allow me to share the specific reasons that make Salem so special to me." or "My love for Salem stems from its captivating natural beauty."\n\n*   Example: You wrote, "For examples the beautiful sea veiw, when I first saw it I'm feeling relax and calm. The forest and mountain veiw also!"\n    Problem: The phrasing "For examples" is incorrect, and "I'm feeling relax and calm" is a simple structure. "The forest and mountain veiw also!" feels a bit like an afterthought.\n    How to fix it: Use more precise language and combine ideas smoothly. For example, "For instance, the stunning sea view immediately made me feel relaxed and calm when I first saw it. The lush green forests and majestic mountain views also offered a sense of refreshing tranquility." This sounds more natural and descriptive.	3.0	Your essay is well-organized with a clear introduction, body, and conclusion, which helps the reader follow your ideas. You used some basic linking words, but you could use a wider range of words and phrases to connect your sentences and paragraphs more smoothly, making the flow of ideas more natural.\n\n*   Example: You wrote, "This town located next to the Attlantic Sea. Let me explain more cleary for the reason that makes me love it."\n    Problem: The transition from the location of the town to explaining why you love it is a bit abrupt.\n    How to fix it: You could create a smoother link between these two ideas. For example, "This town is located next to the Atlantic Sea, and its coastal position is just one of the reasons that contribute to my deep affection for it."\n\n*   Example: You wrote, "The forest and mountain veiw also! It was green everywhere, soothing waterfalls these things made me feel fresh."\n    Problem: The connection between "The forest and mountain view also!" and the following sentence is not very smooth. "These things" is a bit vague.\n    How to fix it: You could combine these thoughts with clearer transitions. For example, "Beyond the sea, the forest and mountain views are equally breathtaking. The vibrant greenery and soothing waterfalls truly made me feel refreshed and connected to nature."	2.0	You used everyday vocabulary, and your main message about Salem was understandable. However, there were many noticeable errors in spelling, punctuation, and grammar, which sometimes made your meaning unclear or difficult to read.\n\n*   Spelling:\n    Example: "it's history," "cleary," "veiw," "attrach," "unqiue," "Attlantic"\n    Problem: Words like "its" (possessive, no apostrophe), "clearly," "view," "attract," "unique," and "Atlantic" are misspelled.\n    How to fix it: Carefully proofread your writing for spelling errors. Use a dictionary or a spell checker to help you. Remember that "it's" means "it is," while "its" shows possession.\n\n*   Grammar - Subject-Verb Agreement and Tense:\n    Example: "This town **located** next to the Attlantic Sea." and "I'm **feeling** relax and calm."\n    Problem: "Located" needs a "was" or "is" before it (e.g., "This town *is located*"). "I'm feeling" is continuous, but "I felt" or "I feel" might be more natural depending on if it's a current or past feeling. "Relax" should be an adjective "relaxed."\n    How to fix it: Pay close attention to verb forms and tenses. For example, "This town *is located* next to the Atlantic Sea." and "when I first saw it, I *felt relaxed* and calm."\n\n*   Punctuation and Capitalization:\n    Example: "The place that I love, called 'Salem'." and "The forest and mountain veiw also!"\n    Problem: The comma after "love" is not needed. The exclamation mark after "also!" is too informal for an article, and "forest" and "mountain" don't need to be capitalized.\n    How to fix it: Use commas only when necessary. Use periods at the end of most sentences in an article. Only capitalize proper nouns (like "Salem" and "USA") and the first word of a sentence.	\N	\N	2025-07-23
28758	2025-12-01 12:47:07.087453+00	2026	Creative Writing	Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it. In the beginning, Sam is a person in the middle class, he has a normal life, who works for a company.<br><br><br>One day, while he was working, he discovered that he typed slower than others, because its been 20 minutes he still on the half of the first paragraph. Although other people fully finished the first paragraph.<br><br><br>After he arrived home, he suddenly had a idea that could improve his typing, then that night he decided to built an Invention called "The Flash Keyboard" which would let him type everything that he thinking in his head, just by he press the button.<br><br><br>The next day, he brought it to work.<br><br><br>At the office, when he start to working, he press the button quickly. The Flash Keyboard worked really well at first during the work.<br><br><br>Therefore its been only 30 minutes, He could not stop typing. The keyboard began to warmer and warmer! At the end its finally exploded. In the end of that day, he had the most traumatizing moment ever that he will never forget it till he die.	191	15.0	Hello Mymind, 👋<br><br>This is a very relatable story! We've all wished we could type faster. I liked how the invention worked *too* well and caused a disaster. The escalating heat and the explosion made for a great climax!<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing even further. 📋<br><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🔄 After 'decided to', use the base verb. 'Decided to <b>build</b>' (not built).</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 Watch out for 'traumatizing' (you got it right!) but check simple words like 'till' (until).</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🎨 'Began to warmer' should be 'began to <b>get</b> warmer'.</li>	B1+	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	5.0	All content is relevant. The story follows the prompt and resolves the conflict ('keyboard began to warmer... exploded'), and correctly begins with the required sentence: 'Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it.'.	4.0	The narrative is simple but clear ('Sam is a person in the middle class') and easy to follow, holding the reader's attention effectively. To improve, ensure linking words are used with precision to clearly convey causal relationships.	3.0	The text is connected using basic linking words ('In the beginning', 'One day', 'Therefore'). 'Therefore' is used incorrectly in place of 'However' or 'After'. To improve, review the correct usage of linking words to ensure logical connections between ideas.	3.0	Everyday vocabulary is used. Grammatical forms are simple ('decided to built', 'he press', 'he thinking'). Errors are noticeable but meaning is clear. To improve, focus on using correct verb forms (e.g., base form after 'to') and consistent past tense for narrative.	\N	\N	2025-12-01
28997	2025-12-01 12:47:07.087453+00	2026	Creative Writing	Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it. Sam, who was a brilliant kid and introverted, lives in America. His family was not rich but also not poor, and he is just ten years old. <br><br><br>After he pressed the button, suddenly, a lot of robot have come out of nowhere. Fly around the city in the sky. After that, a robot with a massive size but looks not complete yet, walk forward his apartment. Then, start to destroy the building, cars, and start to kill people like they are insect. At first, Sam didn't know what is happening because he can't heard the noise but it's on the news so he walked out of his apartment when he saw that gigantic robot. I feel really upset and he was stun. Because it is his old robot and it is his buddy, when he was six years old. He can't complete it therefore, he got bullied by his friends, and his family didn't even protected him. Instead, they all against him. So he give up and threw away all his invention and become more concentrate about school. But stepped out in front of the robot. He decided to confront it. He was really scared but he have no choice. when it walks toward to me, he shout “we have been buddy for many years, can't you remember?” the robot didn't stop walking to him. But, even walk faster. Sam think that he will die today but he didn't regret to have that robot, a kind and talktive one, as his buddy. <br><br><br>When it is in front of him, it stop. It said “In glad to meet you again, buddy”. when Sam heard the robot voice, he cried. The rain was raining 2 hours ago, but now, it stops. After they talked to each other, they decided to recover the city together. Then Sam announce everyone to live in this town with us. At first, they refused. But when the time past, many robot become kind and understand human, no one disagree anymore. So they all live together happily ever after.	351	17.0	Hello Grace, 👋<br><br>This is a wonderfully imaginative and heartwarming story! I particularly enjoyed the unique twist of the 'scary robot' turning out to be Sam's old childhood friend. The emotional depth and action scenes kept me captivated!<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing even further. 📋<br><li><b>Tense Consistency!</b> ⏳ Practice keeping your verbs in the same tense, usually past tense for narratives.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> 🤝 Double-check that your subjects and verbs match correctly (e.g., 'he' with 'shouted', not 'shout').</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Connect sentence fragments to make your ideas flow more smoothly.</li>	B2	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	5.0	You told a complete and engaging story that fully addresses the prompt, with a strong resolution! 🌟 The 'buddy' relationship between Sam and the robot added a lovely, touching dimension.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Clarify Motivation!</b> 🤖 It would be interesting to know *why* the robot initially started destroying things. Was it confused, or acting under a misconception?</li><li><b>Enhance Reactions!</b> 😲 When the robot speaks, describe Sam's immediate reaction. Was he surprised, relieved, scared? Show us his emotions!</li>	4.0	You skillfully communicated a strong sense of atmosphere and action when describing the robot attack! 🏙️ The image of 'robots destroying the building, cars' is very clear and powerful.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Narrative Voice!</b> 🔄 Maintain a consistent narrative perspective. Shifting from 'I feel really upset' to 'he was stun' can be a little confusing for the reader.</li><li><b>Sentence Clarity!</b> 👓 While your language is evocative, ensure every sentence conveys its meaning with utmost clarity, especially phrases like 'The rain was raining 2 hours ago, but now, it stops' in context.</li>	5.0	Your story is well-organised, using clear paragraph breaks to separate the exposition, rising action, and resolution! 📚 Linking words like 'At first', 'After that', and 'So' effectively guide the reader through the narrative. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Connect Fragments!</b> 🧩 Some phrases, like 'Fly around the city in the sky', are quite descriptive but could be integrated into a full sentence to enhance flow and coherence.</li><li><b>Stronger Connections!</b> ➡️ Phrases like 'But stepped out' would benefit from a clear subject to ensure seamless transitions between actions.</li>	3.0	You made a good effort using complex sentences and appropriate vocabulary such as 'massive', 'confront', and 'introverted'! 👏<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Tense Consistency is Key!</b> ⏳ This is an area to focus on. You frequently switch between past and present tenses ('walks', 'lives', 'is' should be 'walked', 'lived', 'was'). Consistent past tense is crucial for storytelling.</li><li><b>Correct Modals!</b> 🛠️ After modal verbs like 'can't', use the base form of the verb. So, 'can't heard' should be 'couldn't <b>hear</b>'.</li><li><b>Adjective/Verb Forms!</b> 🎨 'He was stun' should be 'he was <b>stunned</b>' (an adjective) and 'didn't even protected' should be 'didn't even <b>protect</b>' (base verb after 'didn't').</li><li><b>Preposition Precision!</b> 📍 Instead of 'Walk forward his apartment', use 'walked <b>towards</b> his apartment' for better accuracy.</li><li><b>Avoid Repetition!</b> ✍️ While 'brilliant kid' and 'buddy' are good, try to find synonyms or rephrase sometimes to keep the vocabulary fresh.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-01
33168	2025-12-01 12:47:07.087453+00	2026	Creative Writing	Sam finished his invention and pressed the button to start it. Sam, who was very friendly, liked to craft new inventions and his latest project was a machine which helped people to fly, even though a lot of people bullied him, but he did not stop & he worked on the project all day.<br><br><br>He wanted to test it then he put it on and pressed the first button, another one and the last one. Therefore his invention is now fully completed, by his surprise he started to fly, he never felt so alive like this since he was young, however he was going to hit the planet because he cannot controlled the direction, as he become more and more closer to the planes, he used all his strenght to change the direction and fortunelly he has dodge the plane, but the invention is slowly running out of fuel, finally he fell into the water, luckily no one was hurt and his invention became viral across the internet.<br><br><br>The next day the biggest innovation company saw his potential and decided to hire him, he accepted quickly and finnished his machine. He help thousand of people fly across the contry and won the noble prize. Belive in yourself don't let anyone block your way.	213	16.0	Hello Rome, 👋<br><br>This is an inspiring success story! I liked how Sam didn't give up despite being bullied. The flying sequence was very exciting, and ending with a Nobel Prize was a great touch. 'Believe in yourself' is a wonderful message.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing even further. 📋<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 Watch out for 'fortunelly' (fortunately) and 'strenght' (strength).</li><li><b>Comparatives!</b> 📏 We say 'closer', not 'more closer'.</li><li><b>Modals!</b> 🛠️ After 'cannot', use the base verb. 'Cannot <b>control</b>'.</li>	B1+	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	5.0	You told a complete story with a clear beginning, climax, and resolution. 🌟 The conflict with the plane added good tension.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Clarify the Action!</b> ✈️ You said he was going to 'hit the planet' - I think you meant 'plane'? A tiny spelling change makes a big difference!</li><li><b>Show the Innovation!</b> 🔧 What did the machine look like? Wings? A jetpack? Describing it helps us see it.</li>	4.0	Your story held my attention, especially during the flight test. 🛫 The message of perseverance was communicated well.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Length!</b> 📏 Some of your sentences are very long with many commas. Try breaking them into shorter sentences for more impact.</li><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The ending jumps quickly to 'The next day'. Maybe show him landing and people cheering first?</li>	4.0	You organised your story well into paragraphs. 📚 Linking words like 'Therefore', 'however', and 'finally' guided the reader perfectly. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Run-on Sentences!</b> 🏃‍♂️ Your second paragraph is one giant sentence! Put a full stop after 'fully completed' and 'young'.</li><li><b>Transitions!</b> ➡️ 'Therefore his invention' - 'So' might be a smoother choice here.</li>	3.0	You used some good words like 'potential', 'accepted', and 'viral'. 👏<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Contry' -> 'country'. 'Finnished' -> 'finished'. 'Botton' -> 'button'.</li><li><b>Comparatives!</b> ⚖️ 'More and more closer' -> 'closer and closer'.</li><li><b>Modals!</b> 🛠️ 'Cannot controlled' -> 'cannot <b>control</b>'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Help him everything' -> 'help him <b>with</b> everything'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-01
28763	2025-08-28 14:07:51.568907+00	2026	Free time Activities	In human life can have stress from works, study or exam. In Thailand, where is teenagers have to use more than half of their time in one day for study because Thailand education systion are very differre, such as mine life that 89 days left. I will have exam that it can change my life in m 4-6. So I make me to study science and math very hard, and i think that have study hard for this exam same like me. In free time two of the most computers activities that I think Thai teenages do are playing games and Successful activities and sulfing internet.<br><br><br>One of successful activites thai Thai teenages do in their free time is playing computer games. There have many computer games that we plays, such as Valorant, Roblox and ROV. which are eazy to play. It famous by eazy to downlode, eazy to play and can play with friend. So this make teenages relax from study with their friends.<br><br><br>A Second successfal activities is sulfing internet, such as IG, Fackbook and Tiktok. This can make relax by chating or watching video but it can make effect in	193	7.0	<b>📝 Dear Best</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 193 words and achieved A2+. You clearly named two free-time activities and gave reasons why teenagers enjoy them, which shows you understood the task and audience.<br><br>	A2+	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	3.0	You named two relevant activities (playing computer games; surfing the internet) and gave basic reasons why teenagers enjoy them. However your explanations are short and the essay ends before the conclusion, so the reader is not fully informed.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Develop each activity with one clear reason plus a short example (for instance, one specific game or one type of video).<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "In free time two of the most computers activities that I think Thai teenages do are playing games and Successful activities and sulfing internet."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In my free time, two of the most popular activities among Thai teenagers are playing computer games and surfing the internet because they are easy to access and help students relax."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved sentence is clearer: it uses correct word order, correct plural/singular forms and gives a brief reason which helps the reader understand why these activities are popular.<br><br>	1.0	The frequent very simple errors and unclear phrasing make it difficult for a reader to follow your ideas consistently.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Aim for clear, full sentences and avoid short fragments; keep a neutral formal tone for an essay (no text-message abbreviations).<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "I will have exam that it can change my life in m 4-6."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "I will have an important exam in M.4–6 that could affect my future, so I am studying science and maths very hard."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved sentence is grammatically complete and more formal. It makes the purpose of the sentence clear and fits the essay tone expected in school assessments.<br><br>	2.0	You used paragraphing, but the essay does not meet the required four-paragraph structure and does not have a clear concluding paragraph. Topic sentences are weak or missing at the start of body paragraphs.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Use four paragraphs: (1) introduction with a clear thesis sentence, (2–3) two body paragraphs each starting with a clear topic sentence, (4) conclusion that restates the thesis and main supporting points.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> The essay ends with an unfinished sentence: "but it can make effect in"<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In conclusion, playing games and surfing the internet are common ways for Thai teenagers to relax after studying, but it is important to use them in moderation to avoid negative effects."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This concluding sentence restates the thesis and summarises the supporting ideas, giving the reader a clear ending and improving cohesion.<br><br>	1.0	You show some useful vocabulary (names of games and apps), but very frequent spelling and grammar errors make the text hard to read. The essay also lacks the relative clauses and passive structures expected at higher levels. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "There have many computer games that we plays, such as Valorant, Roblox and ROV."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are many computer games that we play, such as Valorant, Roblox and ROV."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai verbs are not changed for person or number, so Thai learners often add or miss verb endings in English (subject–verb agreement). In English we say "we play" (not "we plays") and use "there are" for plural subjects. (Pattern reference: learner difficulty with verb agreement and plural marking.)<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "A Second successfal activities is sulfing internet, such as IG, Fackbook and Tiktok."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "A second successful activity is surfing the internet, such as Instagram, Facebook and TikTok."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai has no articles and different plural rules, so learners often use "a" with plural nouns or write incorrect plural/singular forms. Also spelling and word formation (e.g., "sulfing" → "surfing", "Fackbook" → "Facebook") need attention. (Pattern reference: articles and plural/word-form interference.)<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "It famous by eazy to downlode, eazy to play and can play with friend."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "They are famous because they are easy to download, easy to play, and can be played with friends."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai allows long clauses and often does not mark auxiliaries or passive forms the same way as English. This can lead to missing verbs/auxiliaries and run-on or fragmented sentences in English. Practise using full clauses (subject + verb) and correct passive/intransitive patterns. (Pattern reference: run-on clauses and word-form/auxiliary omission.)<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Every day this week: correct and rewrite 5 sentences from your essay focusing on verb agreement, article use, and correct plural/singular forms (use a notebook).<br>2. Spelling drill: choose 10 commonly-misspelt words from this essay (e.g., system, different, surfing, successful, Facebook, download, easy, teenage, friends, play) and write each word 5 times with its correct sentence.<br>3. Weekly writing practice: write one 140–160 word essay following the 4-paragraph plan; include at least one relative clause and one passive sentence. Ask a teacher to check for the three error types above and correct them.<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-28
28806	2025-08-28 13:48:25.47889+00	2026	Free time Activities	Do you want to know? What's activities Thai teenagers do in a free time. Narrowing to Thailand, thai teens was really sophisticated in feelling. In they family were have a difference activities to do in free time.<br><br><br>Nowadays, Thai teenagers play a lot of computer games when they have a free time. Example is Valorant, GTA, Five M and Roblox. It's have another famous game more than these too. In my opinion I think teenagers like to play a computer games, which is a FPS games, except Valorant. Because it really funny you can call team when you play. But they have allowance too.<br><br><br>Next, fantastic activities are sports. Thai teens have fun and laugh when they play sports with their friends. In every sports have a rules and it help teens to be conformist in real life.<br><br><br>In conclusion	140	10.0	<b>📝 Dear Nut</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Free time Activities'. You wrote 140 words and achieved B1. You clearly named two free-time activities (computer games and sports) and gave reasons for each, which shows you understood the task.<br><br>	B1+	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	4.0	You clearly identify two relevant activities (computer games and sports) and give simple reasons for each, so the reader understands your choices.  <br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Develop each activity with one specific example or detail to make your ideas more convincing.  <br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "In they family were have a difference activities to do in free time."  <br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In their families, teenagers take part in different activities in their free time, such as playing games together or exercising in the park."  <br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved sentence is clearer because it uses correct subject reference ("their families"), correct verb forms ("take part in"), and gives concrete examples, which helps the reader understand exactly what kinds of activities you mean.<br><br>	3.0	You communicate straightforward ideas and attempt an essay style, but register and clarity vary across the essay.  <br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Use clear academic/essay phrasing in the introduction and avoid short, fragmented questions as opening lines.  <br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "Do you want to know? What's activities Thai teenagers do in a free time."  <br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "This essay explains what activities Thai teenagers do in their free time and why they enjoy them."  <br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved version matches an essay register and clearly states the purpose; it avoids informal question openings and helps the reader know what to expect next.<br><br>	2.0	You have paragraph breaks, and each body paragraph is about one activity, which is good. However the introduction lacks a clear thesis and the conclusion is incomplete, so the whole essay does not feel finished.  <br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> End the introduction with one clear thesis sentence that states the two activities you will discuss; ensure the conclusion restates the thesis and summarizes the reasons.  <br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> The introduction does not end in a clear thesis (e.g., the ideas are vague and not signposted).  <br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In this essay I will discuss two popular free-time activities among Thai teenagers—playing computer games and taking part in sports—and explain why many choose them."  <br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This model thesis sentence tells the reader exactly what the essay will cover and links directly to the two body paragraphs, creating clear organisation and flow.<br><br>	1.0	You have one clear accurate sentence, but there are many errors with articles, verb forms, plural/singular agreement, and word choice. The main challenges are with forming correct noun phrases and verb agreement compared with Thai patterns.<br><br>\n\n❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "What's activities Thai teenagers do in a free time."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "What activities do Thai teenagers do in their free time?"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai learners often transfer Thai word order into English. In English, questions need the auxiliary verb "do" and the plural noun does not use "a". This matches the common Thai→English interference pattern of incorrect question structure and article/number usage.<br><br>\n\n❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Narrowing to Thailand, thai teens was really sophisticated in feelling."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Focusing on Thailand, Thai teenagers are often sophisticated in their feelings."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This shows errors in subject-verb agreement and spelling. Thai does not mark verb tense/agreement the same way as English, so learners sometimes use the wrong verb form ("was" instead of "are") and misspell words ("feelling" → "feeling").<br><br>\n\n❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "In they family were have a difference activities to do in free time."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "In their families, there are different activities to do in free time."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai does not use articles and plural markers like English, so learners often use wrong pronouns ("they" vs "their"), incorrect verb constructions ("were have"), and wrong use of "a" with plural nouns. This maps to the common Thai interference pattern for articles and plural marking.<br><br>\n\n❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "It's have another famous game more than these too."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are other famous games besides these."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The student used "It's have" (wrong subject and verb). Thai often omits auxiliary verbs or uses different subjects, causing incorrect English auxiliaries and subject-verb forms.<br><br>\n\n❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "like to play a computer games, which is a FPS games, except Valorant." <br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "like to play computer games, such as FPS games, except Valorant." <br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> English does not use "a" with plural "games" and needs consistent number agreement. Thai L1 speakers sometimes misunderstand singular/plural marking and article use.<br><br>\n\n❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Because it really funny you can call team when you play."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Because it is really fun; you can call a team when you play."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This contains a missing verb ("is") and the wrong adjective form ("funny" vs "fun"). Thai learners often translate adjectives directly and may omit the verb "to be," reflecting Thai sentence patterns where a copula can be different or optional.<br><br>\n\n❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "In every sports have a rules and it help teens to be conformist in real life."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "In every sport there are rules, and they help teenagers to become more disciplined in real life." <br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> This shows errors in countability ("sports" vs "sport"), subject-verb agreement ("have" vs "there are") and word choice ("conformist" is not the correct collocation). Thai influence often causes mismatches in plurality and verb forms.<br><br>\n\n<b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Focus practice on articles and plural forms: write 10 short sentences describing activities and check each noun for correct article/plural use. (10 minutes daily for 5 days)<br>2. Practice subject-verb agreement and auxiliaries: transform 10 simple statements into questions (e.g., "They play games." → "Do they play games?") and check with a grammar key. (15 minutes, three times this week)<br>3. Edit your essay: rewrite the introduction and conclusion using the model sentences above; then underline every verb and noun to check agreement and article use. (One full revision session)<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-28
