orks for alot of people"<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In conclusion, while many activities can help you relax, going to the beach and hanging out with friends are two popular choices that offer unique ways to unwind for many people."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Your conclusion should summarize your main body points, not introduce new ones. This helps the reader follow your argument from beginning to end, making your essay more cohesive.<br><br>	3.0	You communicated your ideas clearly, but focusing on a more formal academic style will help you hold your reader's attention more effectively.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Practice using a formal and academic register appropriate for an essay, avoiding language that is more suited for informal conversation.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "alot of tourist says that sitting at the beach enjoying the weather can help you feel calm and relaxed."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Many tourists state that sitting at the beach, enjoying the weather, can help them feel calm and relaxed."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English academic writing, it’s important to use more formal phrasing like 'many tourists state' instead of the more casual 'alot of tourist says,' which is closer to spoken Thai or informal English. This makes your writing sound more authoritative and appropriate for an essay.<br><br>	3.0	Your essay is clearly divided into paragraphs, which helps to separate your main ideas.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Strengthen the connections between your sentences and paragraphs using more varied linking words and clear topic sentences at the start of each body paragraph.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your second paragraph starts abruptly with 'One famous activity people like to do is going to the beach.'<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "One popular free time activity is going to the beach. This offers a fantastic way for people to relax and enjoy themselves, especially due to its calming atmosphere and opportunities for social interaction."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A clear topic sentence like this tells the reader exactly what the paragraph will be about and how it connects to your overall thesis, creating better flow and structure in your essay.<br><br>	3.0	You use everyday vocabulary appropriately, and your meaning is generally clear despite some errors. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Free time is really important because it help us relax and have fun."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time is really important because it helps us relax and have fun."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, verbs do not change form depending on the subject. However, in English, for 'he/she/it' and singular nouns, you must add an '-s' to the verb in the present simple tense.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "There are 2 activity people like to do when they have free time..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are 2 activities people like to do when they have free time..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, when you refer to more than one countable noun, you need to add '-s' or '-es' to make it plural. Thai does not have direct plural markers like English, which can lead to this type of error.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: ". it is one of the activity people do to relax..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "It is one of the activities people do to relax..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, every new sentence must begin with a capital letter. This is a common point to remember for clear writing, and will also help you to correct the plural form of 'activity'.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Review and practice subject-verb agreement rules, paying close attention to verbs that follow 'it', 'he', 'she', and singular nouns.<br>2. Focus on using a more formal and academic tone in your writing, especially in essays, by avoiding casual expressions and conversational phrasing.<br>3. Experiment with using relative clauses (e.g., 'who,' 'which,' 'that') to combine sentences and add detail, and try to incorporate passive structures (e.g., 'is done by') to vary your sentence construction.<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-27
