ment.	2.0	The text attempts to create an organizational structure using numbered paragraphs, but these are not used effectively to develop different ideas in a clear and coherent way. The essay is also not divided into the five paragraphs as instructed, which impacts the flow of ideas and overall coherence. There is a limited use of basic linking words, and the structure does not help the reader to follow the intended essay structure.	2.0	Preaw, you use everyday vocabulary such as "favorite place," "popular place," "capital city," and "street foods." However, there are noticeable errors in your language use, particularly with grammar and sentence structure. For example, "Tokyo at Japan" should be "Tokyo in Japan," "At tokyo has a lot of tourists" is grammatically incorrect, "tourists attraction that very famous" is also awkward, "People in Tokyo, are friendly" has an unnecessary comma, and "Them give good advice" should be "They give good advice." These errors, combined with the lack of paragraphing, impede communication to some extent.	\N	\N	2025-07-11
