ul beaches. Make sure to spend your time with friends or family there in your summer vacation. I hope you would enjoy the recommended places that I have told you. Get your keys and let's go	395	11.0	Gut-Jung, you've shared a lot of enthusiasm for Huahin and its various attractions, making it clear why you love this place. To improve your writing, you should work on organizing your essay into more focused paragraphs and using more formal language. Also, paying attention to grammar and spelling will help to make your writing clearer and more professional.	B1+	Writing	Term 1 Midterm	FIRST	Part 1	3.0	Gut-Jung, you have provided a good amount of detail about Huahin, mentioning its location, beaches, waterparks (Santorini and Black Mountain), and Plearnwan farm. You also included personal reasons, such as your family visits and your mother's connection to the place. However, the essay is longer than the ideal word count of 140-190, and some of the details, such as the explanation of \\"Plearnwan,\\" could be more directly linked to *why* you love the place. To achieve a score of 5, you would need to ensure that all content is relevant and supports the main idea, providing more specific details about *your* personal experiences and feelings related to these places, and keeping within the recommended word count.	2.0	You attempt to use the conventions of an essay with an introduction and conclusion. However, the tone is often informal, using phrases like \\"There's bunch of activitys,\\" \\"I'm in the carnival festival,\\" \\"used to went,\\" and \\"Get your keys and let's go\\". The inconsistent register and conversational style detract from the overall effectiveness of communicating ideas in a formal essay. To improve to a 5, you should maintain a consistent, more academic register throughout and communicate ideas with greater precision and sophistication.	3.0	You have organised the essay with an introduction, a description of various attractions, personal reasons, and a c