s.\n\n❌ Weakness: You wrote: "Free time is essential thing that all teenagers want to have it. When we have free time it like a heaven."\n\n✨ Improved: "Free time is a vital component of a teenager's life, offering a cherished escape from daily routines."\n\n💡 Explanation: The improved sentence uses more formal and precise language suitable for an essay and avoids conversational phrasing.\n\n	3.0	💬 COMMUNICATIVE ACHIEVEMENT: 3/5\nYou communicate your ideas clearly, but the overall tone of your essay is a bit too informal for a B2 level essay.\n\n👉 To Improve: Work on maintaining a consistently formal and academic tone throughout your essay. Avoid informal expressions and contractions.\n\n❌ Weakness: You wrote: "But it sad because Thai teenagers don't have a lot free time."\n\n✨ Improved: "However, it is unfortunate that Thai teenagers often have limited free time."\n\n💡 Explanation: The original sentence is quite conversational. The improved sentence uses more formal vocabulary and phrasing, which is better for an essay. In Thai, it is common to use simpler sentence structures, but in English academic writing, a more complex and formal structure is expected.\n\n	3.0	📋 ORGANISATION: 3/5\nYou used paragraphs to separate your ideas, which is good. However, your introduction doesn't clearly state a thesis, and you are missing a concluding paragraph.\n\n👉 To Improve: Plan your essay with a clear introduction that presents your main argument (thesis statement), body paragraphs with topic sentences that support the thesis, and a strong conclusion.\n\n❌ Weakness: Your introduction did not clearly state your main ideas, and you did not have a concluding paragraph.\n\n✨ Improved: "This essay will explore two popular free time activities among Thai teenagers: watching funny videos and playing video games, examining their appeal and benefits."\n\n💡 Explanation: A clear introductory sentence like this tells the reader exactly what the essay will be about, making your organization much stronger. It helps to guide the reader through your arguments.\n\n	2.0	🔤 LANGUAGE: 2/5\nYou use a good range of everyday vocabulary. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules, especially articles and verb forms.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Free time is essential thing that all teenagers want to have it."\n\n✨ Correction: "Free time is an essential thing that all teenagers want to have."\n\n💡 Explanation: In English, we use articles like "a" or "an" before singular countable nouns, even if they are modified by an adjective. In Thai, there are no direct equivalents for articles, so learners often omit them in English.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "When we have free time it like a heaven."\n\n✨ Correction: "When we have free time, it is like a heaven."\n\n💡 Explanation: This error involves a missing verb "is". In Thai, the verb "to be" is often implied and can be omitted in certain contexts, but in English, a subject must always have a verb.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "when you watch funny video and you laughing your brain will dopamine released."\n\n✨ Correction: "When you watch funny videos and you're laughing, your brain will release dopamine."\n\n💡 Explanation: This sentence has a few issues. "You laughing" should be "you're laughing" (present continuous) or "you laugh" (present simple). Also, "dopamine released" is missing a verb; "will release dopamine" is correct for a future action. Thai language structure can sometimes lead to direct translations that miss these essential English grammatical components.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "TikTok, which is a platform about short video, is have a lot influencer who make funny video or people like to share funny story or funny situation."\n\n✨ Correction: "TikTok, which is a platform for short videos, has a lot of influencers who make funny videos or people who like to share funny stories or funny situations."\n\n💡 Explanation: "About short video" should be "for short videos" (preposition and plural). "Is have" should be "has" (subject-verb agreement). "A lot influencer" should be "a lot of influencers" (missing "of" and plural noun). Thai speakers sometimes omit prepositions and plural markers due to differences in grammatical structure.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "When I fell stress play game it make me comfortable."\n\n✨ Correction: "When I feel stressed and play games, it makes me comfortable."\n\n💡 Explanation: "Fell" is the past tense of "feel"; "feel" (present tense) is needed here. "Play game" should be "play games" (plural) and potentially connected with "and". "It make me" should be "it makes me" (subject-verb agreement). Thai verbs do not change form for tense or agreement as much as English verbs do.\n\n	\N	\N	2025-08-28
