le, you wrote, "When I first stepped there It feels like a time stopped machine every stucture or rider there looks completely unrallistic, without thinking much I ran all the way to a roller coaster. Overall it was very fun and an awesome memorable moment". You could break this into shorter sentences to make it clearer: "When I first stepped there, it felt like a time machine had stopped. Every structure and ride looked completely unreal. Without thinking much, I ran all the way to a roller coaster. Overall, it was a very fun and memorable moment." The second paragraph was also very long and contained many different ideas. It would have been better to divide these ideas into separate paragraphs, espcially as you wrote so many words.	2.0	You used a good range of everyday words related to travel and entertainment. You also used different tenses to talk about your past trip and general facts about Korea. However, there are many small errors with spelling, punctuation, and sentence structure that make it hard to read at times. For example, you wrote, "Soeul Korea is located in the centre of Korea, And are known for it's traditional things for example, modern structures, clothing and many other things." It would be better to write, "Seoul, Korea, is located in the center of Korea and is known for its traditional things, such as its modern structures, clothing, and many other things." Another example is "My trip all got canded because of the upcoring examination." This should be "My trip was cancelled because of the upcoming examination." Also, pay attention to capitalization, as you wrote "Come to think" when it should be "come to think" and "k-pop" when it should be "K-pop".	\N	\N	2025-07-23
