ou use simple grammatical forms, but errors are present. To improve, focus on practicing sentence construction to reduce grammatical errors.	\N	\N	2025-07-13
29045	2025-08-29 09:26:19.213963+00	2026	Free time Activities	Nowadays, Thai teens always on thier phone, but in my childhood we used to do lots of things. Before heading to childhood memory I want to show the importance of "Free time activities for teens especially in Thailand". Back then when the smart phone came out we didn't care much so, we used that free time without phone to do some activities.<br><br><br>Firstly, when it comes to free time activities For Thai teens, mostly for boys we used to played soccer. A lot of time when the san almost set we would play soccer outside with friends. It's popular especially for boys because it's fun and make us stronger, back then we all want to make it to pro.<br><br><br>lastly, chess. Chess, one of the most boring games for teens these days, it was one of the activities that I did when I was 10 until now. It's not really popular because for some people it's too hard or boring, but it make us to use our brain to predict the opponent's.<br><br><br>In conclusion, nowadays parents make their kids to do some activities in their free time to avoid being to much on the phone, which is one of the most teens problems we've seen. There are tons of interesting activities to cure your boredom - instead of being on the phone all days so, why don't you try something new to make your life better.	236	13.0	Well done: you chose two different activities (soccer and chess) and used personal examples that make the essay engaging. You wrote 236 words and achieved B2.	B2	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	4.0	You identify two activities (soccer and chess) and give reasons for each, so the reader is informed. However, the introduction does not finish with a clear thesis that names both activities, and some reasons are short or repeated.\n👉 To Improve: End the introduction with a clear thesis naming both activities and add one specific detail or example for each activity.\n❌ Weakness: "Back then when the smart phone came out we didn't care much so, we used that free time without phone to do some activities."\n✨ Improved: "Back then, before smartphones became common, I spent my free time playing soccer with friends and learning chess at home because these activities kept me active and helped me think more carefully."\n💡 Explanation: A clear thesis listing both activities helps the reader know what to expect. Developing each activity with a detail (when/where/with whom) makes your reasons stronger.	3.0	Your tone is mostly appropriate for an essay but sometimes slips into conversational language, which weakens the formal/neutral register expected in a First exam.\n👉 To Improve: Keep a steady semi-formal tone and avoid fragments or very colloquial phrases.\n❌ Weakness: "lastly, chess. Chess, one of the most boring games for teens these days..."\n✨ Improved: "Finally, chess, which many teens find boring, is an activity I have enjoyed since I was ten because it trains concentration and planning."\n💡 Explanation: A consistent essay register (not too chatty) helps the examiner follow and respect your argument.	3.0	You used four paragraphs, which meets the form requirement. But the introduction lacks a clear thesis, the chess paragraph begins weakly, and topic sentences should link more clearly to the thesis.\n👉 To Improve: Make the introduction end with a thesis that names both activities; start each body paragraph with a clear topic sentence; begin the conclusion with a transition and restate the thesis and main reasons.\n❌ Weakness: Intro ends without explicit thesis; second body begins: "lastly, chess."\n✨ Improved intro ending: "In this essay I will describe two free-time activities I enjoy—playing soccer and playing chess—and explain why I chose them."\n✨ Improved topic sentence for chess paragraph: "Another activity I enjoy is chess, because it improves my thinking and planning skills."\n💡 Explanation: Clear topic sentences and a concluding restatement make your essay easier to follow and show good essay organisation.	3.0	You use everyday vocabulary well, but there are recurring grammar, spelling and form errors that affect clarity. Also, the task asked for relative clauses and passive structures; these are largely missing. Below are the three most urgent language problems with Thai-specific explanations and corrections.\n\n1) Problem (quote): "Nowadays, Thai teens always on thier phone,"\nWhy (Thai interference): Thai often omits the verb "to be" and does not mark plural with -s. Learners commonly transfer this pattern into English and omit "are" or the plural -s. Spelling errors (thier) are also frequent because English letter order differs from Thai sound mapping.\nCorrection: "Nowadays, Thai teens are always on their phones."\n\n2) Problem (quote): "we used to played soccer."\nWhy (Thai interference): Thai verbs don't change form for tense in the same way as English. After "used to" English requires the base verb, but Thai learners often add past -ed, producing incorrect verb forms.\nCorrection: "we used to play soccer."\n\n3) Problem (quote): "it make us to use our brain to predict the opponent's."\nWhy (Thai interference): Thai does not mark subject–verb agreement in the same way, and infinitive/particle usage differs. This causes errors with verb agreement (make → makes), unnecessary "to" before a base verb, and incorrect possessive/plural forms.\nCorrection: "it makes us use our brains to predict our opponents' moves."\n\nNotes on required structures:\n- Relative clauses: I did not find clear relative clauses (which/that/who) used to add information. Try adding one or two (e.g., "a game that improves concentration").\n- Passive structures: No passive sentences were used. At B2, include 1–2 passive forms where natural (e.g., "many activities are organised by schools").	\N	\N	2025-08-29
29031	2025-12-14 09:35:16.814612+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. The sky faded into a pitched black color and nearby lamp posts flickered then they soon blacked out. I panicked in fear as I try to pry the window to open. The children's spirits watched intently as I fail to escape. Their eyes that were filled with anger 'turned into joy, soon they all chant my name as if I was the devil. My limbs froze in terror then I came up with a perfect plan. I quickly put on my animatronic suit that were stained with the children's blood. "How the tables have turned!" I exclaimed my victory by scaring the children's spirits with the thing I had finished them off with. They all stared at me as I manically laughed. Suddenly, the suit felt suffocating since it hadn't been worn in years. I gagged as the metal sliced through me and started crushing my bones. I screamed in agony unable to bare the pain. The spirits all watched me slowly die in satisfaction. How ironic it is that I'd die by my own creation. I accepted that this was the consequence I had to faced as a murderer. My fate was set in stone, the children spirits faded away, leaving me to suffer in the dark. I can only promise myself one thing was that "I'll always come back."	232	17.0	Hello Racing! 👋<br><br>Wow, this is an incredibly dark and gripping horror story! 😈 The imagery of the children's spirits and the animatronic suit is very powerful and unique. You created a strong sense of dread and a chilling twist of fate. It's clear you have a talent for genre writing.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you make this terrifying tale even more impactful! 📋<br>1. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 📝 Your entire story is one long block of text. Breaking it into paragraphs (e.g., one for the initial panic, one for the plan, one for the suit turning, one for the ending) would dramatically improve readability and dramatic effect.<br>2. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Bare the pain' should be '<b>bear</b> the pain'.<br>3. <b>Tense Consistency!</b> 🛠️ 'Had to faced' should be 'had to <b>face</b>'.	B2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You crafted a highly original and disturbing story that fully embraced the horror genre. 🌟 The internal monologue and the vivid descriptions of the animatronic suit were very effective. All content was relevant and contributed to the unsettling narrative.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>The Suit's Description!</b> 🎭 You mentioned it was 'stained with the children's blood'. Adding a small detail about its appearance (e.g., 'rusty', 'broken', 'gnarled') would make it even more gruesome.</li><li><b>The Children's Spirits!</b> 👻 What did they look like? Were they transparent, glowing, or did they have empty eyes?</li>	5.0	You successfully conveyed a chilling, cynical, and ultimately ironic narrative voice. 💀 The shift in power dynamics from hunter to hunted was very well-managed.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing with Punctuation!</b> 🛑 The story reads very breathlessly because of the lack of paragraph breaks. Strategic breaks would allow the reader to absorb the horror and tension more effectively.</li>	3.0	Your story follows a clear chronological sequence of events, from initial panic to the ironic demise. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing is CRITICAL!</b> 🧱 This is the single biggest area for improvement. Splitting your long text into logical paragraphs would dramatically enhance readability, dramatic effect, and overall structure.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Some sentences are very long and contain multiple ideas. Breaking these into shorter, distinct sentences would make your story easier to follow and increase the impact of key moments.</li>	4.0	You used strong and evocative vocabulary like 'flickered', 'manically', 'suffocating', 'crushing', 'agony', 'ironic', 'consequence', and 'murderer'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Homophones!</b> 📝 'Bare the pain' -> '<b>bear</b> the pain'.</li><li><b>Tense!</b> ⏳ 'Had to faced' -> 'had to <b>face</b>'.</li><li><b>Punctuation in Dialogue!</b> 💬 'I exclaimed my victory by scaring the children's spirits with the thing I had finished them off with.' needs a comma before the speech: '"How the tables have turned!" I exclaimed my victory...'</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
