 improve your writing. You have also used the transition word "First of all" which is good, but be mindful of repeating transition words too often.	\N	Writing	Formative	PET	Part 2	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-08-13
33957	2025-08-28 21:49:10.84523+00	2026	Free time Activities	Everybody likes free time because it's enjoyable and useful. Even in Thailand, people like to have relax activities for their free time. Education in Thailand makes Thai teens feel stressed because they need to study about 7-8 hours and have many home work. So they need to have good activities to do. The best free time activities are playing games and doing exercises.<br><br><br>The best activity for Thai teenagers is playing games. Most of adults are thinking that games are giving bad habits to teenagers, but playing games is very good activity. Games can help and practice our English skill and manage our time. Playing game is enjoyable for teenagers and other gens. Game are popular in Thailand because it's easy to access and Thailand is supporting Esports.<br><br><br>Beside playing games, doing exercises is good example of free time activity. Exercises are good for everyone especially teenagers. Exercises can reduced stressed and also make our body stronger. Thailand is supporting sport like football, badminton and swimming. Exercises also help us manage our time by making plan. Teenagers are stressed from study, so they can doing exercises to reduce their stressed.<br><br><br>In conclusion, Thai teens love to have free time because they are stressed from study. Exercises and games can reduced our stressed but you can also have other activities to do.	221	14.0	You've clearly identified two activities and explained their benefits.	B2	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	5.0	📝 CONTENT: 5/5\nYou have fully addressed all parts of the prompt, identifying two free time activities, explaining what they are, and why they are chosen. All content is relevant to the task and the target reader is fully informed.	3.0	💬 COMMUNICATIVE ACHIEVEMENT: 3/5\nYou communicate straightforward ideas, but the tone is a bit too informal for a B2 essay, which should generally aim for a more neutral and academic style.\n\n👉 To Improve: Try to use a more formal and neutral tone for academic essays.\n\n❌ Weakness: You wrote: "Most of adults are thinking that games are giving bad habits to teenagers, but playing games is very good activity."\n\n✨ Improved: "While many adults believe that games promote bad habits in teenagers, playing games can be a very beneficial activity."\n\n💡 Explanation: The improved version uses more formal vocabulary ("While many adults believe" instead of "Most of adults are thinking") and a more balanced tone suitable for an essay.	3.0	📋 ORGANISATION: 3/5\nYou have used paragraphs effectively and presented a clear thesis statement in your introduction. To improve, focus on using a wider variety of linking words and cohesive devices to make your essay flow even more smoothly between sentences and paragraphs.\n\n👉 To Improve: Focus on using a wider variety of linking words and cohesive devices to make your essay flow even more smoothly between sentences and paragraphs.\n\n❌ Weakness: Some sentences within your paragraphs could be more explicitly linked to show their connection. For example: "Playing game is enjoyable for teenagers and other gens. Game are popular in Thailand because it's easy to access and Thailand is supporting Esports."\n\n✨ Improved: "Playing games is enjoyable for teenagers and other generations. Furthermore, games are popular in Thailand because they are easy to access, and the country actively supports Esports."\n\n💡 Explanation: Using linking words like 'furthermore' helps to show the relationship between ideas and makes your argument more cohesive and sophisticated.	3.0	🔤 LANGUAGE: 3/5\nYou use a good range of everyday vocabulary appropriately. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules, particularly verb forms and articles.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Even in Thailand, people like to have relax activities for their free time."\n\n✨ Correction: "Even in Thailand, people like to have relaxed activities for their free time."\n\n💡 Explanation: In English, we use the past participle ("relaxed") as an adjective to describe the activities (e.g., a "relaxed" person, "relaxed" atmosphere). In Thai, adjectives can sometimes be formed directly from verbs without changing their form to indicate past participle.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Games can help and practice our English skill and manage our time."\n\n✨ Correction: "Games can help us practice our English skills and manage our time."\n\n💡 Explanation: In English, "practice" is a verb that needs an object (e.g., "practice a skill"). Also, "skill" should be plural if you are referring to multiple aspects of English ability. In Thai, the concept of a "skill" might not always require the plural -s ending.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Exercises can reduced stressed and also make our body stronger."\n\n✨ Correction: "Exercises can reduce stress and also make our bodies stronger."\n\n💡 Explanation: After a modal verb like "can," the main verb must be in its base form ("reduce"). Also, "stressed" is an adjective; the noun form "stress" should be used here. "Our body" should be plural to refer to people in general. Thai grammar often uses adjectives where English requires a noun, and verb conjugations after auxiliary verbs are less strict.\n\n🎯 YOUR ACTION PLAN\n\n1. Review and understand the use of adjectives ending in -ed (e.g., "relaxed") versus -ing (e.g., "relaxing") to describe things.\n2. Practice using the base form of verbs after modal verbs like "can," "will," and "should."\n3. Focus on differentiating between nouns (e.g., "stress") and adjectives (e.g., "stressed") and using them correctly in sentences.	\N	\N	2025-08-28
