n error areas I noticed are (1) verb forms and subject–verb agreement, (2) article/determiner and pronoun use, and (3) spelling and sentence punctuation, and these are the best places to focus your practice 😊. For example, your sentence “Pets are ours bestfriends” should be “Pets are our best friends.” Fix: change “ours” to “our” and write “best friends” as two words. Another: “it heal self when we get a bad thing today” — better: “they make us feel better when we have a bad day.” Here you need plural pronouns and a clearer verb phrase. Also “they were wating you” should be “they are waiting for you.” For articles and determiners, “There are 3 pet I recomment which are dog, cat and hamster” → “There are three pets I recommend: a dog, a cat and a hamster.” For spelling and forms, “recomment” → “recommend,” “somtimes” → “sometimes,” “makesure” → “make sure.” Concrete steps: (1) every time you write, underline the subject and verb and check they agree; (2) use a short checklist for common words (a/an/the, my/your/our) and check them before you finish; (3) read each sentence aloud and pause at each punctuation mark — if the pause feels wrong, rewrite the sentence shorter. Thai learners often find English articles, verb endings and spelling difficult because those features do not exist in the same way in Thai, so focused practice on these three points will help quickly.	\N	\N	2025-09-14
