ge (e.g., "full of diverse cultures, cuisines, religions, fashion and people"). However, the abrupt ending and some grammatical inaccuracies prevent the essay from fully achieving its communicative purpose.	2.0	The text shows an attempt at organization with distinct paragraphs, which is good. You use a general introduction and then move into describing the place and activities. However, the essay is incomplete, and the required five-paragraph structure is not fully realized, especially the "WHAT MAKES IT SPECIAL" and "CONCLUSION" sections. There are also some spelling errors (e.g., "cuisenes," "religeons," "diffrent," "veiw," "posibally," "tourrist") that detract from the overall readability and coherence. The consistent errors in spelling affect the overall flow.	2.0	Anu, you use a range of everyday vocabulary to describe Bangkok, such as "delicious food," "diverse cultures," and "unique street foods." You also attempt more sophisticated phrasing like "the city with the longest name in the world." However, there are numerous spelling errors throughout the essay (e.g., "cuisenes," "religeons," "diffrent," "veiw," "posibally," "tourrist," "adap"), and some grammatical inaccuracies (e.g., "Also is the capital," "Bangkok, where there is great hospitality, is actually very hot"). While the meaning can generally be understood, these errors are noticeable and sometimes impede communication. To improve, focus on accuracy in spelling and grammar.	\N	\N	2025-07-11
