perience. You communicated straightforward ideas about your different interests and how they lead to feeling like you don't fit in. The example of the conversation about music helps to hold the reader's attention.	3.0	Your essay is generally well organised and coherent. You used linking words like "Firstly" and "secondly" to introduce your reasons. You also used "so" to connect your ideas and explain the consequences of your different interests.	3.0	You used a range of everyday vocabulary to describe your interests and feelings, such as "basketball," "rap lover," and "unusual music taste." You also attempted more complex vocabulary. You used a range of simple and some complex grammatical forms with a good degree of control. While there are some errors ("reason for that" instead of "reasons for that," "I walking" instead of "I was walking," and use of inappropriate vocabulary) errors do not impede communication	\N	\N	2025-07-13
