eat opening question to grab the reader's attention! 🤩 'Do you love to read examine manga?' is a classic way to start an article.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Natural Phrasing!</b> 💬 The phrase 'examine manga' isn't quite right in English. You probably mean 'detective manga' or 'mystery manga.'</li><li><b>Ending with a Punch!</b> 👊 Your ending 'I want to find the criminal before Conan . . .' is a good thought, but try to finish with a full sentence to make it feel complete.</li>	3.0	Your article is connected and easy to follow! 🌊 You used 'But' and 'In my opinion' to show different sides of your argument.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Variety of Links!</b> 🔗 Instead of just using 'and' or 'but,' try phrases like 'On the other hand' or 'In addition' to show more advanced control.</li><li><b>Structure!</b> 🏗️ Your second paragraph is a bit short. You could combine your thoughts about the tricks criminals use with your opinion on reading habits to make the flow smoother.</li>	2.0	You communicated your ideas clearly, but there are some grammar and spelling points to work on. 🛠️<br><br>Here are some corrections:<br><li><b>Adjectives for feelings!</b> 🎭 You wrote 'It's make me relaxing.' We use '-ed' for our feelings. Correction: 'It <b>makes</b> me feel <b>relaxed</b>.'</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> ✏️ 'Crimenal' should be <b>criminal</b>.</li><li><b>Common Phrases!</b> 🗣️ 'As a same time' should be '<b>at the same time</b>'.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'how that crimenal use trick' should be 'how that criminal <b>uses tricks</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🔍 Instead of 'examine manga,' try <b>'detective manga'</b> or <b>'mystery stories.'</b></li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
