ing words carefully helps your essay sound polished and convincing. ✍️	3.0	Your essay is structured quite clearly, Kaohom L, with good use of paragraphs for each new idea. That’s a really important step! You also used some helpful phrases like 'The first thing is' and 'Besides' to introduce new sections. To make your writing flow even more smoothly, think about how each paragraph connects to the one before it and to your main argument. Sometimes, repeating phrases like 'in this age' can make the writing feel a little repetitive. You could try using synonyms or slightly different sentence structures to keep your reader engaged. For example, instead of repeating 'in this age,' you could say 'during adolescence' or 'at this stage of life.' This helps your ideas link together more elegantly. ✨	2.0	It's clear you have a good range of everyday words, which is brilliant! However, there are a few areas in grammar that we can work on to make your writing much clearer and more precise. For example, sometimes your verbs don't quite match your subjects, like saying 'friends are the most effect' instead of 'friends have the most effect.' Also, words like 'they' can sometimes be confused with 'their' or 'them,' so we need to be careful with those possessive pronouns—for instance, 'their friends' not 'they friends.' Finally, do a quick check for spelling, like 'Nowaday' (should be 'Nowadays') or 'preature' (should be 'pressure'). Many Thai learners sometimes face similar challenges with subject-verb agreement and pronoun usage because the rules in English can be quite different from Thai. With a bit of practice, you’ll master these! Keep trying to use more complex sentences, and with careful checking, your grammar will become much stronger. 💪	\N	\N	2025-09-12
