34059	2025-08-29 15:07:52.941075+00	2026	Free time Activities	Free time activities is make people feel relaxed and reduce stress. Although everyone have a different kinds of activities depend of each personalities and environments. In particular, Thai teenagers also have many activities to do in their free times. The most popular free time activities for teens in Thailand is playing sports and doing handmade.<br><br><br>The most popular free time activities in Thailand is playing sports, which is also supports health and body. Thai teenagers usually playing sports for their connection. It help teenagers to find a good friends thoulgh sport team works. In particular some people can able to become a profesional athlete and make their career jobs even better.<br><br><br>Beside playing sports, handmade activities is the one that very interesting. Handmade activities, which can be both relaxing and creative fullfilling. This include origami, painting, drawing and crafting. Handmade also make you unlock the new skills and stay claim. In Thailand handmade, is the very famous activities for teenagers nowadays. People like to spend time with lovers and friend or family and do handmade to giving to the person that you love and respect.<br><br><br>To summerise, both of these activities is a tiny kind of free time activities in Thailand. Teenagers also use the free time to find their hobbys or made their future better than before.	201	12.0	You did a good job identifying some popular free time activities in Thailand!	B2	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	3.0	You identified two free time activities, but you didn't explain why YOU (the author) chose them, which was part of the task. Also, your conclusion was too short and didn't fully develop your ideas. This means the reader isn't fully informed.👉 To Improve: Make sure to answer all parts of the question, especially when it asks for your personal reasons or choices. Always write a full conclusion that summarizes your main points.❌ Weakness: "The essay ends abruptly without a conclusion or full development of the points."✨ Improved: "To truly unwind, Thai teenagers often turn to digital entertainment. Playing computer games with friends, for instance, not only offers a fun escape but also strengthens their social bonds and communication skills, helping them build empathy rather than becoming isolated."💡 Explanation: Completing the essay and developing your ideas fully ensures the reader gets all the information they need and a clear understanding of your points.	3.0	You used an appropriate tone for an article, but sometimes your language changed from being more formal to less formal. This can make it confusing for the reader about who you are writing for.👉 To Improve: Try to keep your language style (register) consistent. Decide if you want to write for a general audience (more formal) or friends (more informal) and stick to that style throughout.❌ Weakness: "Hey guys, let me tell you about this awesome place" followed by more formal language.✨ Improved: "Salem offers visitors a fascinating glimpse into American history through its well-preserved architecture and informative museum exhibits."💡 Explanation: Keeping a consistent formal tone helps establish credibility and makes your writing more professional for a general audience.	3.0	You organized your ideas into paragraphs, which is great for helping the reader follow your points. However, the connections between your ideas could be clearer if you used more different linking words. Your conclusion was also very brief.👉 To Improve: Use a wider variety of linking words and phrases (like "furthermore," "however," "as a result") to show how your ideas are connected. Make sure your conclusion restates your main points and thesis more clearly.❌ Weakness: Using "and" repeatedly to connect ideas instead of showing specific relationships.✨ Improved: "While Salem is famous for its witch trial history, it also offers excellent seafood restaurants; therefore, visitors can enjoy both historical education and culinary experiences."💡 Explanation: Using specific linking words like "while" and "therefore" helps show the relationship between ideas more clearly and makes your writing flow better.	3.0	You used good vocabulary related to the topic, but there are several recurring grammar errors that affect clarity, especially with subject-verb agreement and plural forms.❌ Problem: You wrote: "Free time activities is make people feel relaxed..."✨ Correction: "Free time activities make people feel relaxed..."💡 Explanation: In Thai, verbs don't change form for plural subjects, but in English, the verb 'to be' and other verbs must agree with a plural subject (activities - make, not is make). This is a common challenge for Thai learners.❌ Problem: You wrote: "...everyone have a different kinds of activities..."✨ Correction: "...everyone enjoys different kinds of activities..."💡 Explanation: In English, "everyone" is a singular pronoun and takes a singular verb ("enjoys"). Also, "kinds" is plural, so it doesn't take the singular article "a" – you should use "different kinds" or "a different kind." Thai grammar doesn't distinguish singular/plural in this way, which often causes this type of error.❌ Problem: You wrote: "...find a good friends thoulgh sport team works."✨ Correction: "...find good friends through sports teams."💡 Explanation: "Friends" is plural, so you don't need the article "a". Also, "through" is the correct spelling for 'by means of'. In Thai, there isn't a direct equivalent for English articles, leading to their common omission or misuse.❌ Problem: You wrote: "This include origami, painting, drawing and crafting."✨ Correction: "This includes origami, painting, drawing and crafting."💡 Explanation: "This" is a singular subject, so the verb "include" needs an 's' at the end to agree with it in the present simple tense. This is another example of subject-verb agreement which is not present in Thai.🎯 YOUR ACTION PLAN1. Complete all parts of writing tasks, especially personal elements, and develop each point fully.2. Maintain a consistent register (formal or informal) throughout your writing.3. Practice using a wider variety of linking words and phrases to connect ideas.4. Review subject-verb agreement rules for present tense and plural nouns.	\N	\N	2025-08-29
