ntence ends a bit abruptly with 'to playing toge'. Make sure you finish your words (together) and your thoughts!</li>	3.0	You communicated your ideas clearly enough that I understood your love for <i>Sakura Lovely</i>. 🤩 Using 'Firstly' and 'Secondly' helped me follow your points.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Tone!</b> 🗣️ An article should feel like you are talking to the reader. Instead of just listing facts, try to ask the reader a question, like 'Have you ever read a manga?'</li><li><b>Be more descriptive!</b> 🎨 When you describe the festival in Japan, tell us one thing they did there to make the story come alive!</li>	3.0	The text is connected and has a clear beginning, middle, and end. 🌊 You used linking words like 'Firstly', 'Secondly', and 'For example' to organize your thoughts.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Logical Flow!</b> 🔄 You used 'Finally' to describe the book's relationship, but then you continued with 'For example' and a new point about social media. 'Finally' should usually introduce your very last point or a conclusion.</li><li><b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 Try to start a new paragraph when you switch from talking about 'why reading is good' to 'the story of the manga'.</li>	2.0	You used good vocabulary like 'relationship', 'information', and 'social media'. 👏 However, there are several grammar mistakes that make it a bit difficult to read at times.<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you:<br><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'I am think it interesting' should be '<b>I think it is interesting</b>'.</li><li><b>Negatives!</b> 🚫 'make your brain don't have to' should be '<b>makes your brain not have to</b>' or '<b>means your brain doesn't have to</b>'.</li><li><b>Possessives!</b> 🧑‍🤝‍🧑 'Sakura and his boyfriend' -> If Sakura is a girl, it should be '<b>her</b> boyfriend'.</li><li><b>Articles and Be-verbs!</b> 🔍 'The manga a romantic story is called' -> '<b>The manga, which is a romantic story, is called...</b>'</li><li><b>Infinitives!</b> 🏃 'time to playing' should be '<b>time to play</b>'.</li><li><b>Social Media Comparison!</b> 📱 'Read more book is make your free more than to allway on social media' -> '<b>Reading books makes you feel more free than always being on social media.</b>'</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
