 or vocabulary!</li>	4.0	You communicated your ideas clearly and held my interest with the story about your friend! 🤩 Using a personal anecdote is a great technique for an article.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Article Style!</b> 📰 Articles usually have a catchy title and an engaging introduction. You started right away with your favorite book. Try starting with a question like: 'Do you love gaming and reading? Then I have the perfect story for you!'</li><li><b>Tone Consistency!</b> 💬 Your tone is friendly, which is perfect. Just be careful with phrases like 'In my view; I think' which is a bit repetitive. You can just say 'In my view,' or 'I think...'.</li>	3.0	Your article is well-structured with clear linking words like 'Firstly' and 'Secondly'. 🌊 This makes it very easy to follow your argument.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Punctuation Flow!</b> 🛑 Avoid using a semicolon after 'In my view'. A comma is much better: 'In my view, I think...'. Also, check the comma in 'Minecraft comic, is an online comic'. We don't need a comma between the subject and the verb!</li><li><b>Sentence Variety!</b> 🔗 Try to combine some of your shorter sentences. Instead of 'So, he bought it again, but this time...', you could try 'However, when he bought it again, he found it less exciting.'</li>	3.0	You used some great descriptive words like 'classic' and 'fantasy'! 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you polish your English:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> ✏️ 'Commic' should be spelled '<b>comic</b>'. You spelled it correctly later, so just be careful with consistency!</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'An one time read' -> '<b>A</b> one-time read'. We use 'a' because 'one' starts with a 'w' sound.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'He already know' -> 'He already <b>knows</b>'. Remember the 's' for he/she/it in the present tense!</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 💡 Instead of 'fantasy game as a comic', you could say 'a <b>comic version</b> of a fantasy game' or 'a comic <b>based on</b> a fantasy game'.</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
