tands exactly why you find this story inspirational.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Article Style!</b> 📰 Articles usually need a catchy title at the top to grab the reader's attention.</li><li><b>Engage the reader!</b> 💬 You can ask a question like, 'Have you ever heard of Beethoven?' to make the text feel more like a magazine article and less like a school report.</li>	3.0	Your writing is easy to follow and the story progresses logically from his talent to his hearing loss. 🌊<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Punctuation and Flow!</b> 🔗 You have a floating phrase 'inspirational story' in the middle of your text. Make sure every phrase is part of a complete sentence.</li><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 📑 Even in a short article, using a new paragraph when you switch from describing the book to giving your personal opinion helps the reader stay organized.</li>	3.0	You used some great vocabulary like 'refused to give up' and 'limitation'! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you polish your English:<br><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ Use 'an' before vowel sounds: 'It's <b>an</b> inspiration book'.</li><li><b>Uncountable Nouns!</b> 🎼 'Music' is usually uncountable, so we don't say 'a music'. Try: 'He was composing <b>music</b>'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> ✏️ Watch out for double letters: 'composingg' should be '<b>composing</b>'.</li><li><b>Comparatives!</b> ⚖️ When comparing two things, use 'than': 'stronger <b>than</b> any limitation' (not 'that').</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ 'inspirational story In my opinion, This story is really great...' could be fixed to: '<b>This is an inspirational story. In my opinion, it is great...</b>'.</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
