erstands that you find these books 'funny' and a good cure for boredom.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Engage the Reader!</b> 🤝 Articles usually talk to the reader. You could ask a question like, 'Have you ever felt bored and didn't know what to do?'</li><li><b>Tone!</b> 🎭 You used the word 'funny', but Harry Potter is often 'exciting' or 'adventurous' too. Using more descriptive words helps the reader understand the story better.</li>	3.0	Your text is easy to follow because you used some basic linking words like 'because' and 'like'. 🌊<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Starters!</b> 🛠️ Several sentences start with 'I think' or 'It'. Try to vary this. For example: 'In my opinion,' or 'Additionally, these books...'</li><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 📑 You started a new paragraph well, but try to make sure each paragraph has one clear main idea. The first could be about what you read, and the second about why reading is important.</li>	2.0	You used some good everyday vocabulary like 'fantasy', 'magic', and 'bored'. 👏 However, there are several grammar mistakes that you should watch out for.<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you improve:<br><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'this books is' should be '<b>these books are</b>'. Remember: 'this' is for one, 'these' is for many!</li><li><b>Possession!</b> ✍️ 'its have a many seasons' should be '<b>they have many parts</b>'. </li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🔍 'is a Harry Potter books' -> '<b>are the Harry Potter books</b>'.</li><li><b>Common Phrases!</b> 🗣️ 'a lots of time' should be '<b>a lot of time</b>' or '<b>lots of time</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 📖 Instead of 'seasons', use '<b>books</b>', '<b>volumes</b>', or '<b>series</b>' when talking about literature.</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
