ge clearly.<br><br>	2.0	You started with an introduction and a main idea (thesis), which is a good step! However, the essay didn't follow a clear four-paragraph structure. The second body paragraph started with "The final activity" which was a bit confusing, and there was no concluding paragraph. Making sure each paragraph has a clear purpose and using correct linking words will help your essay flow better.<br><br>	1.0	You used a good range of everyday vocabulary, but the main challenges are with a few key grammar rules and sentence structure.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Freetime make people feel more in control when, face with work, everone needs free time for themself and here in Thailand teens has to work hard to be successful so They needs a lots of free time To feel in control When face with a difficult task, here's are the thing that help them to calm down."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time makes people feel more in control. Everyone needs free time for themselves, especially here in Thailand, where teens have to work hard to be successful. Therefore, they need a lot of free time to feel in control when faced with a difficult task. Here are some things that help them calm down."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, we need to use 'makes' with 'freetime' (singular subject-verb agreement). Also, 'everyone' is singular, so it should be 'needs.' Thai often doesn't distinguish between singular and plural verbs as clearly as English, and it also uses longer sentences without clear conjunctions, leading to run-on sentences in English.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "The first activity here is doodlling stuff on they notebooks, doodlling stuff on the notebooks is nice way and well know Things to do when stress, Many teens do this on They free time to let they mind calm down by doodlling they creativity on to the notebook. let's creativity flow out of they mind."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "The first activity here is doodling in their notebooks. Doodling in notebooks is a nice and well-known way to relieve stress. Many teens do this in their free time to calm their minds by doodling their creative thoughts onto the notebook. This lets their creativity flow from their minds."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> We need to use 'their' (possessive adjective) instead of 'they' (subject pronoun). Also, the phrase 'a nice way' requires the article 'a'. Thai doesn't always use articles or possessive pronouns in the same way, which can lead to these errors.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "The final activity that Teens in Thai and all over is world do in They freetime is playing game, which the way game can calm"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "The final activity that teens in Thailand and all over the world do in their free time is playing games. Playing games is a way to calm..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> 'Teens' should not be capitalized unless it's at the start of a sentence.  'The world' needs the definite article 'the', and 'games' should be plural. Again, 'they' should be 'their'. Thai often uses general nouns without explicit pluralization or articles, which translates to common errors in English.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. **Review Subject-Verb Agreement:** Practice making sure your verbs match your subjects (e.g., "Freetime *makes*", "everyone *needs*", "teens *have*").<br>2. **Use Articles Correctly:** Pay attention to 'a', 'an', and 'the' before nouns. Think about whether you are talking about something specific or general.<br>3. **Structure Your Essay:** Plan your paragraphs (introduction, body paragraphs, conclusion) before you write. Ensure each body paragraph fully develops one main idea.<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-27
