our essay began with a general overview, but due to its incompleteness, it was unable to fully communicate its purpose to the reader.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Ensure your writing effectively holds the reader's attention by developing all your points and maintaining a clear purpose throughout the entire essay.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> "beside play game, doing a exercise"<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Besides playing games, engaging in regular exercise is another free-time activity that greatly benefits teenagers, offering a different kind of relaxation and positive impact."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Developing your ideas with full sentences and clear explanations helps the reader follow your argument and fully understand your message, rather than leaving them with an unfinished thought.	1.0	You attempted to use paragraphs to structure your ideas. However, the essay is incomplete, preventing a clear overall organisation.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Plan your essay to ensure it has a clear introduction with a thesis statement, well-developed body paragraphs with topic sentences, and a concluding paragraph that summarises your main points.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your essay was not completed, so it did not have the required four paragraphs, including a proper introduction, two body paragraphs, and a conclusion.<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In conclusion, free time activities like online gaming and exercise provide essential balance to a busy student's life, offering both mental and physical benefits."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A well-structured conclusion brings your essay to a satisfying close, reinforcing your main ideas and leaving a lasting impression on the reader, which is crucial for overall coherence.	2.0	You used some everyday vocabulary and simple sentences effectively. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "In Thailand, we're don't have much free time."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "In Thailand, we don't have much free time."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, we usually use only one auxiliary verb for negation. Thai doesn't have such contractions or complex auxiliary structures, so it's important to use either 'we are not' or 'we do not' but not combine them.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Absolutley all teenager will full of energy if they have some free time."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Absolutely all teenagers will be full of energy if they have some free time."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, when you refer to 'all' or 'many' of something, the noun that follows needs to be plural (e.g., 'teenagers', 'students', 'books'). Thai does not typically add a plural ending like '-s' to nouns, which can lead to this error.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "doing a exercise"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "doing an exercise"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, we use 'an' before words that start with a vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u) and 'a' before words that starts with a consonant sound. Thai does not have articles like 'a' or 'an', so choosing the correct one can be tricky.<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Complete the next essay task fully, ensuring you address all parts of the prompt.<br>2. Practice using plural '-s' endings correctly on nouns, especially after words like 'all', 'many', and numbers.<br>3. Review the rules for using 'a' and 'an' with different words and practice identifying vowel sounds.<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-28
