'amazing' are good examples of this. However, there are some grammatical points that we can work on to make your writing even clearer and more accurate. For instance, when you wrote 'The school was organized something,' it would be more natural to say 'The school had organised something' or 'The school was organising something.' Also, phrases like 'Me and my friend walked' are very common in spoken English, but in writing, it's better to say 'My friend and I walked.' This small change makes a big difference in formal writing. Additionally, do remember to double-check your spelling, as 'loughed' should be 'laughed.' These kinds of errors are very common for Thai learners, as sometimes the way words are pronounced doesn't always translate directly to how they are spelled or how sentence structures work in English. Practising subject-verb agreement and pronoun usage will really strengthen your writing. Keep an eye on these details, and your language control will surely improve. ✨	\N	\N	2025-09-23
