 and the not-so-good things about having pets! 👍 For example, you mentioned how pets can help with stress and mental health, which is a really important advantage. You also thought about the downsides, like when pets misbehave, which shows you're thinking carefully about the topic. To get an even higher score, remember to give specific examples for *each* point you make. Instead of just saying pets 'ruin couch, sofa eat,' you could write, 'for example, some dogs might chew on furniture, or cats might scratch the sofa, which can be expensive to repair.' Adding these small details helps your reader understand your points much better and makes your article more convincing!	2.0	You've made an effort to write an article that shares your opinions, which is exactly what the task asked for! However, sometimes the way your ideas are presented makes it a little difficult for the reader to fully grasp your message, which is really important for an article in an international magazine for teenagers. For example, your opening sentence 'Pets & cat, dogs, hamster is a conom pets' could be clearer and more engaging to grab the reader's attention right away. Think about using a strong opening statement or a question to draw your audience in, like 'Have you ever wondered why we love our pets so much?' 🤔 To improve here, try to use more varied sentence structures and make sure your main point in each section is really easy for your reader to follow from start to finish.	3.0	You have a good structure for your article, Platwo, as you move from introducing pets to discussing their benefits and then some challenges. You also use some linking words like 'But I would say' to transition between ideas, which is a great start! To make your writing even more organised and flow smoothly, try to use clear paragraph breaks for each new main idea. For example, you could have one paragraph introducing pets and your general opinion, another dedicated to all the advantages, and a third for the disadvantages. 📝 This way, your reader can easily follow the journey of your thoughts without getting lost. Using more varied linking words such as 'Firstly,' 'In addition,' 'On the other hand,' or 'To conclude' can also really help your ideas connect together beautifully!	1.0	Platwo, you're using everyday words to talk about a topic you care about, which is fantastic! However, there are quite a few grammatical errors and choices of words that make your sentences hard to understand sometimes. This means your reader has to work a bit harder to get your message, and it might even impede the meaning occasionally. For example:<br><br>1. Your sentence 'Pets & cat, dogs, hamster **is** a **conom** pets' has a few things we can fix. 'Is' should be 'are' because you're talking about more than one type of animal (cats, dogs, hamsters). Also, 'conom' should be 'common.' So, it should be: 'Cats, dogs, and hamsters **are common** pets.' Remember, for many nouns, we add an 's' to make them plural, like 'pet' becomes 'pets.'<br>2. Another example is 'Pet might be bad when **their** are having animal **spirt** for example dog ruining couch, sofa eat.' Here, 'their' should be 'they' because you're talking about the animals themselves. 'Spirt' should be 'spirit' or, more likely, 'instinct' or 'temperament' in this context. And 'sofa eat' should be 'eating things.' A clearer sentence would be: 'Pets might be challenging when **they** are acting on their animal **instincts**, for example, a dog **ruining** the couch or **eating** the sofa.'<br>3. Also, the sentence 'Nowa days people having less pets' is missing a verb. It should be 'Nowadays, people **are having** fewer pets.' Keep an eye out for these small words like 'are' and 'is' and make sure they match the number of nouns you're talking about!<br><br>Many Thai learners sometimes find articles (`a`, `an`, `the`) and plural forms tricky because these concepts work differently or don't exist in the same way in Thai. Practising these small grammatical points will make a big difference in how clearly you communicate your ideas! Keep a list of these common errors and try to check for them when you review your writing. You're making progress, and focusing on these areas will really help your English get stronger. 💪	\N	\N	2025-09-22
