el a bit simple. Try to vary your expressions. Instead of 'that's why', you could use 'For this reason' or 'Consequently'.</li><li><b>Show your Passion!</b> 🤩 Use stronger words to show you like reading, such as 'fascinating' or 'essential' instead of just 'good'.</li>	3.0	Your text is connected and easy to follow. 🌊 You used linking words like 'So' and 'Because' to show the reasons for your opinions.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Fragments!</b> 🔗 Avoid starting a sentence with 'Because' in formal writing. For example, 'I like to read because it makes me relax' is better than starting a new sentence with 'Because'.</li><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 📑 Your text is a bit like a list of points. Try to group your thoughts into two clear paragraphs: one about your favorite books and one about why reading is healthy for everyone.</li>	2.0	You used some good B1 phrases like 'strongly agree' and 'stressful'! 👏 However, while your meaning is clear, there are **no error-free sentences** in the text due to small mistakes in grammar and word choice.<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you:<br><li><b>Adjectives!</b> 🛠️ 'make me feel relax' -> 'make me feel <b>relaxed</b>'. 'I got stressfull' -> 'I feel <b>stressed</b>'.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'it make me' -> 'it <b>makes</b> me'. Always add the 's' for 'it/he/she' in the present tense.</li><li><b>Articles and Plurals!</b> 📚 'book is great activity for our' -> '<b>Reading books is a</b> great activity for <b>us</b>'.</li><li><b>Passive Voice!</b> 👮 'had create by police' -> '<b>was created</b> by the police'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'alot' -> '<b>a lot</b>' (this should always be two words).</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
