thing about the newest models.'</li>	3.0	Your text is divided into two clear sections, which helps the reader follow your points. 🌊 You also used 'In my view' to introduce your opinion, which is excellent.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Punctuation Flow!</b> 🛠️ Be careful with full stops. You wrote 'In my view. I think...'. This should be connected with a comma: '<b>In my view, I think...</b>'.</li><li><b>Avoid Fragments!</b> 🔗 You started a sentence with 'Which'. Instead of making it a new sentence, connect it to the previous one: '...imagine the pictures, <b>which</b> is good for the brain.'</li>	3.0	You used some nice vocabulary like 'engaging' and 'relax'! 👏 Your meaning was always clear.<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you improve:<br><li><b>Tense Consistency!</b> 🛠️ You used 'There were', but since you are describing comics you read now, use the present tense: 'There <b>are</b> spec details'.</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 💡 Remember to use 'the' for specific things. Instead of 'good for brain', use 'good for <b>the</b> brain'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Brandnew' should be written as two words: '<b>brand new</b>'.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🔗 Try to use more 'because' or 'and' to join your short sentences together into longer, more complex ones.</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
