nd Logic!</b> 💡 In your first sentence, 'Are you provocative movies?' doesn't quite make sense. You probably meant 'Do you like provocative movies?' or 'Are you looking for...'. Make sure your opening clearly relates to the reader.</li><li><b>Purpose!</b> 💬 Since this is for a magazine, try to explain <i>why</i> other people should read/watch your recommendation more clearly.</li>	4.0	Your article is well-organised with clear paragraphing, and I liked how you used your name and interests to personalize the article. 🌊<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linking Ideas!</b> 🔗 Use more connectors like 'Furthermore' or 'On the other hand' to connect your thoughts.</li>	2.0	You used some interesting vocabulary like 'bustling' and 'renowned'! 👏 However, there are some grammar points to work on:<br><br><li><b>Vocabulary Choice!</b> 🛠️ You used 'provocative', which usually describes something that makes people angry. A better word for an exciting action movie might be 'thrilling' or 'intense'.</li><li><b>Verb Patterns!</b> 📝 You wrote 'Prize... is very like this action movie.' To express a hobby, say '<b>really likes</b>' or '<b>is very fond of</b>'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> ✏️ 'Re-nowned' should be one word: <b>renowned</b>.</li><li><b>Articles and Nouns!</b> 📍 'is a example case' should be 'is <b>an</b> example' or 'is a <b>good</b> example'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 💬 'telling about' -> 'The movie <b>is about</b> school bullying' or 'The movie <b>tells a story</b> about...'.</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
