ou mentioned different genres at the end (romance, dark fantasy). You could briefly say which one <i>Rapunzel</i> belongs to!</li>	3.0	You used the conventions of an article well by starting with a question to grab the reader's attention! 🤩 The tone is friendly and personal.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Descriptive Language!</b> 🎨 Instead of saying 'many episodes', you could say 'an exciting series' or 'many chapters' to sound more like a book reviewer.</li><li><b>Clarify the Plot!</b> 📝 When describing <i>Rapunzel</i>, ensure the connection between the girl and the witch is clear so a reader who doesn't know the story can follow along.</li>	3.0	The text is connected and follows a logical order. 🌊 You moved from manga to books and then to your general opinion on reading.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Transitions!</b> 🔗 The jump from <i>Demon Slayer</i> to <i>Rapunzel</i> is very sudden. You could use a linking phrase like 'In addition to manga, I also love classic stories' to bridge the two ideas.</li><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 📋 Try to start a new paragraph for each main idea. You started the second paragraph well, but make sure the first part isn't too crowded with different topics.</li>	2.0	You used some good vocabulary like 'fantasy comedy' and 'difficult situation'. 👏<br><br>Here are some corrections to help you improve:<br><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'Demon slyer have' should be 'Demon Slayer <b>has</b>'. 'This manga show' should be 'This manga <b>shows</b>'.</li><li><b>Plurals!</b> 📚 'a lot of book' should be 'a lot of <b>books</b>'.</li><li><b>Punctuation and Capitalization!</b> 📍 Keep an eye on your capital letters for titles: 'Demon <b>Slayer</b>'. Also, check your sentences: 'I think it's good to read a lot of book. because...' should be one sentence: '...a lot of books <b>because</b> you'll know...'</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'read a Manga' is usually just 'read manga' (uncountable) or 'read a manga series'.</li><li><b>Passive Voice/Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'The most I like forever wrote by' -> 'The story I like <b>the most is Rapunzel, written by</b> the Brothers Grimm.'</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
