ve you ever cracked open...') is a brilliant way to engage the reader of an article. Your tone is very professional.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Target Audience!</b> 👥 While your vocabulary is impressive, remember that a B1 article is usually for a general magazine. Phrases like 'polemical novel' are very advanced; make sure the rest of your article stays accessible to your readers.</li><li><b>Narrative Completion!</b> 🛠️ Because the text stops suddenly, the reader is left confused. Always check that your final paragraph provides a clear ending.</li>	2.0	The first two paragraphs flow beautifully! 🌊 You move from a general hook to the specific details of the book very logically.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Avoid Fragments!</b> 🧩 The sentence 'Interspersed with graphic confessions...' is a fragment—it isn't a complete sentence because it isn't attached to a main clause.</li><li><b>Cohesion at the end!</b> 🔗 The final paragraph becomes a bit list-like ('Bateman's a successful wallstreet businessman... he wears designer'). Try to use linking words like 'Moreover' or 'Not only does he...' to keep the flow smooth.</li>	5.0	Your vocabulary is outstanding! 👏 Words like 'relentless vortex', 'satirical', and 'fixation' are excellent.<br><br>Here are a few corrections to help you polish your work:<br><li><b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ 'Throughout his first person narrating' should be 'Throughout his <b>first-person narration</b>'.</li><li><b>Punctuation!</b> 📍 In the phrase 'status symbols, designer labels and Huey Lewis albums', it's better to add a comma before 'and' or ensure the list feels complete.</li><li><b>Spelling/Capitalization!</b> 💡 'wallstreet' should be two words and capitalized: '<b>Wall Street</b>'.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ 'sadistically, curated consumer perfection' is a bit confusing on its own. It needs a subject and a verb, for example: 'The novel depicts a <b>sadistically curated</b> world of consumer perfection.'</li>	\N	\N	2026-02-05
