s your desire to help poor people when you grow up. However, the task asked for \\"A Place I Love\\" and while you talk a lot about your experiences there, some parts, like the extended reflection on helping the poor, while heartfelt, move slightly away from fully focusing on the \\"place\\" itself and might be considered a minor irrelevance. To achieve a score of 5, you need to ensure all content is strictly relevant to the task and fully informs the reader about the chosen place. For example, you could have elaborated more on specific natural features or activities directly related to the \\"beautiful\\" countryside.	1.0	You use the conventions of a general description to communicate your ideas. Your intention to express your love for China and your family is clear. However, the text's structure significantly hinders the communication of these ideas. For example, the entire essay is presented as one long block of text, which makes it very difficult for the reader to follow your various points and holds their attention minimally. To improve and score higher, you need to use clear paragraphs and appropriate sentence structure to guide the reader through your thoughts. For example, you could have started a new paragraph when you moved from talking about your initial feelings to describing Guangzhou, or when you shifted from talking about your cousin to your reflections on helping people.	1.0	You have a very basic sense of organisation in that you start by introducing the place and end with a concluding thought. However, your text is not organised into paragraphs well enough, which makes it very difficult to read and follow the flow of your ideas. You introduce many different topics (visiting grandparents, the beauty of nature, missing them, Guangzhou, your cousin, learning difficult things, motorcycles, helping the poor) without any clear breaks or transitions between them. To score higher, you need to use paragraphs to group related ideas together. For example, you could have a paragraph about your initial feelings for the place, another about the specific details of Guangzhou, another about your family and activities, and a final one about the deeper impact the place has had on you. Using linking words and phrases more effectively between sentences and paragraphs would also greatly improve coherence. For example, instead of just starting a new thought, you could use phrases like \\"First, I want to tell you about...\\" or \\"In addition to this...\\" or \\"Finally, this place also taught me...\\"	2.0	You use a range of everyday vocabulary related to your topic, such as \\"holiday,\\" \\"countryside,\\" \\"beautiful,\\" \\"yummy food,\\" and \\"grandma/grandpa.\\" You also use simple grammatical forms with some degree of control. For example, you often correctly use \\"I love,\\" \\"I miss,\\" and \\"they have.\\" However, there are many noticeable errors in grammar, spelling, and word choice that sometimes make it difficult to determine the exact meaning. For example, you wrote \\"Every love it because my mother she is a chiness\\" instead of \\"I love it because my mother is Chinese,\\" or \\"Every time when i has finish the holidag\\" instead of \\"Every time when I finish the holiday ...\\" Another example is \\"Every i will see the mountain\\" instead of \\"Every day I will see the mountains.\\" These errors, along with a tendency to overuse certain simple words like \\"very\\" and \\"every,\\" reduce communication at times. To achieve a score of 5, you need to use a wider range of vocabulary more appropriately and demonstrate greater control over both simple and complex grammatical forms, with errors being only occasional and not impeding communication.	\N	\N	2025-07-23
35239	2025-09-13 10:45:24.617429+00	2026	Term 1 Exam Question 1	Teenagers are easily influenced. Some are influenced by their parents and some are influenced by their friends. When it comes to fashion, studying and music, I find myself being more influenced by my friends. It's to my belief that since we're closer in age, my friends have a better understanding of me.<br><br><br>When it comes to fashion, my friends definetely have a huge influence on me. They keep me updated on what's viral and treydy at the moment. I find that wearing viral and trendy clothes help you fit in better with other people. Whereas my parents, they wear styles of clothings which aren't as popular and to my liking.<br><br><br>Secondly, when it's about studying. I also find myself being more influenced by my friends, rather than my parents. My friends have a better understanding of this, since we're in the same boat. They give me better advice and there fore we both improve together academically. Whereas my parents don't know what challenges I have to face. So they don't understand me as much academically.<br><br><br>Finally, when it comes to music preferences. My friends have a major impact on the music that I listen to. Since I'm around them all the time I often pick up on the music that they listen to. I also find that it's better to have the same music preferences than not. Since me and my friends love karaoke, if we didn't have the same music preferences it would be hard to find a song we'd all like.<br><br><br>In conclusion, when it comes to fashion, studying and music. I find that my friends have a better influence on me rather than my parents. Although a parents influence is important, I find that my friends have a 'greater' impact on me. I believe this is because we're closer in age which makes them more relatable.	313	14.0	Your essay demonstrates a good understanding of the topic, and it's evident that you've put considerable effort into it. 👍 To truly elevate your writing, paying closer attention to your sentence structure, especially in your paragraph transitions, will be highly beneficial. With continued dedication, you'll find yourself excelling in essay writing.	B2	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	Part 2	4.0	You have successfully addressed all key aspects of the task and provided a clear response regarding the influence of friends versus parents. The inclusion of relevant examples pertaining to clothing, studying, and music is commendable. To achieve a higher score, consider refining your expression to enhance conciseness, particularly within the constraints of a timed examination. It's worth noting that some Thai students occasionally find it challenging to directly address the prompt; however, you have managed this effectively, which is a notable strength.	3.0	Your essay effectively conveys the intended message with clarity, which is a significant accomplishment. 👍 The register is largely appropriate for an academic essay; however, there are instances where the language leans towards informality. For example, the phrase "What's viral and trendy at the moment" is more suited to casual conversation than formal writing. In such contexts, opting for a more formal expression, such as "What is currently popular," would be preferable. To further refine your communicative achievement, maintain a consistent level of formality throughout the essay. Remember that academic writing typically avoids slang and overly casual expressions. The effective use of formal language is important here.	4.0	The structure of your essay is logical and facilitates ease of comprehension. The presence of an introduction, well-developed body paragraphs, and a conclusion aligns with the conventions of academic writing. 👏 Furthermore, the strategic use of linking words enhances the cohesion of your ideas and contributes to the overall flow of the essay. For instance, transitions such as "secondly" and "in conclusion" guide the reader through your argument. One area for potential improvement lies in strengthening your topic sentences to create smoother transitions between paragraphs. Instead of starting a paragraph with "When it comes to fashion," you could write something like, "Regarding personal style, my friends exert more influence over my choices than my parents." This clearly introduces the paragraph's main idea and links it back to the overall essay question. Think about how the new paragraph connects to the one before it and explicitly state that connection. Thai learners are sometimes too concise, and forget to create effective topic sentences.	3.0	Your command of language is generally proficient, and your arguments are readily understandable. Nonetheless, there are specific areas that merit attention. Firstly, exercise caution with spelling, as inaccuracies such as "definetely" for "definitely" and "there fore" as two words can detract from the overall impression. 🤔 Secondly, be mindful of sentence fragments. For example, "Finally, when it comes to music preferences" is a subordinate clause which needs a main clause to complete the meaning. You have made this mistake several times in your essay -- you should have written: "Finally, when it comes to music preferences, my friends have far more influence on my taste than my parents." Addressing these linguistic nuances will significantly bolster the strength and polish of your writing. Sentence fragments are a common error amongst Thai students. Correct these errors, and your writing will be much stronger.	\N	\N	2025-09-13
