houghtful and sophisticated story! I was impressed by your confident use of advanced vocabulary like 'alter-ego', 'facade', and 'demeanor' to explore a complex theme of identity and self-acceptance. Your narrative is very engaging!<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing even further. 📋<br><li><b>Proofreading Precision!</b> 🧐 Even strong writers can catch small slips with a careful review.</li><li><b>Consistent Verb Forms!</b> 🔄 Pay close attention to verb agreement, especially with modal verbs.</li><li><b>Sentence Crafting!</b> ✍️ Refine your sentence structure to ensure every phrase is clear and complete.</li>	B2	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	5.0	You crafted an excellent narrative arc, taking Sam from initial excitement to profound self-realization and acceptance! 🌟 The internal conflict of 'his machine was slowly erasing his old-self' was vividly portrayed.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Show, Don't Just Tell!</b> 🧠 Instead of just stating Sam 'couldn't answer any question', show us! What did he do? Did he hesitate, or just stare blankly?</li><li><b>Resolution Clarity!</b> 🏁 The final sentence, 'He knew that some people appreciate for no. matter. Who he may be.', is powerful but could be rephrased for greater impact.</li>	5.0	Your writing style is highly engaging and mature, effectively capturing the reader's attention with its thoughtful exploration of Sam's journey! 🤩 The description of a 'rushing sensation' effectively sets the stage for the story's development.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The transition from Sam's popularity to his failing in class could benefit from a smoother connection. Consider what might have happened *before* his grades dropped.</li><li><b>Voice Consistency!</b> 🗣️ While your voice is generally strong, ensure phrases like 'It was no either' are always clear and idiomatic.</li>	5.0	Your story is very well structured and coherent! 🏗️ The paragraph breaks you implemented effectively separate the different stages of Sam's internal and external journey. Your use of linking words like 'Nevertheless' and 'However' is highly effective. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Internal Sentence Linking!</b> ➡️ Some sentences, like 'Despite his habit of studying aheand', could be more seamlessly integrated into the preceding sentence for better flow.</li><li><b>Clearer Transitions!</b> 🌊 Review transitions between ideas within paragraphs to ensure maximum fluidity. For example, 'It was no either' could be 'It was a choice between'.</li>	5.0	Your vocabulary is truly impressive, featuring words like 'charismatic', 'shenanigans', and 'demeanor'! You show a strong command of language. 👏<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Spelling Precision!</b> 📝 Proofread carefully for minor spelling errors such as 'preformance' (performance), 'aheand' (ahead), and 'eruptly' (abruptly).</li><li><b>Modal Verb Usage!</b> 🛠️ Remember that after modal verbs like 'couldn't', you should use the base form of the verb, so 'couldn't brought' should be 'couldn't <b>bring</b>'.</li><li><b>Gerunds vs. Infinitives!</b> 🔄 Phrases like 'nor understanding' often work better when matched with the preceding verb form, e.g., 'answer... nor <b>understand</b>'.</li><li><b>Sentence Completeness!</b> 🧩 Watch for fragments. 'That was dishonest himself' could be made clearer with 'which was dishonest to himself'.</li><li><b>Word Economy!</b> 🎨 Phrases like 'whole entire' can sometimes be simplified to just 'entire' for stronger impact.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-01
