est thing for teenager."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In Thailand, many teenagers enjoy various free time activities, but I believe video games and board games offer the most engaging and social experiences. These activities not only provide relaxation but also enhance social connections."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Starting with a clearer thesis that outlines your specific choices and their benefits immediately informs the reader about what your essay will cover and why, making your content more impactful.<br><br>	3.0	You generally use the conventions of an essay with an introduction, body, and conclusion to communicate your ideas. However, the tone is sometimes inconsistent, and some phrasing is informal for an essay, impacting its overall clarity and formality.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Maintain a consistent academic or semi-formal register throughout your essay. Avoid overly casual language and ensure complete, clear sentences.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> You wrote: "The one that I always play with my friends is Taco game. It very fun and hurt at the same time."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "The board game I particularly enjoy playing with my friends is the Taco game; it is both exciting and involves quick, sometimes painful, physical reactions."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In academic writing, it's important to use complete sentences and maintain a consistent, more formal tone. Avoiding slang or overly conversational phrases helps your essay sound more mature and convincing. The "hurt" part needed a clearer, more formal explanation.<br><br>	3.0	Your essay is structured with clear paragraphs for the introduction, body, and conclusion, and you use topic sentences and a transition in your conclusion. This shows a good understanding of essay structure. To improve, focus on making your ideas flow more smoothly within and between paragraphs.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Strengthen the coherence within and between your paragraphs using a wider variety of cohesive devices and ensure your concluding paragraph fully summarises your points.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> You wrote: "In short, Free time activities are those make teenager not very stress and relax. An excellent activity for me is Taco gam. These activites can make our social better by talk to each other play with other and make friends for your new experence. Find your own activities for your health not to stress."<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "In short, free time activities such as video games and board games are valuable for teenagers. They offer relaxation from stress and significantly improve social skills by encouraging interaction and the formation of new friendships. I believe finding suitable activities is essential for overall well-being and personal growth."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A strong conclusion summarises your main points clearly and concisely, reinforcing your thesis without introducing new ideas. Using a variety of sentence structures and linking words ensures smooth flow and enhances overall coherence, making your final thoughts more impactful.<br><br>	2.0	Your writing shows a good effort to express your ideas, and you have made a major improvement from previous writing, which is excellent! The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules, especially plural nouns, verb forms, and consistency in capitalization.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "All teenager have their own free time activities."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "All teenagers have their own free time activities."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Thai nouns do not change form for plural. In English, when you refer to more than one, you usually add an '-s' to the noun.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "It very fun and hurt at the same time."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "It is very fun and hurts at the same time."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, the verb 'to be' (is/am/are) is often omitted, but in English, you almost always need a verb to connect the subject ('It') to its description ('very fun'). Also, remember subject-verb agreement: 'It' (singular) needs 'hurts' (singular verb form).<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Video game have many type like roblox, valorant and hay day."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "There are many types of video games like Roblox, Valorant, and Hay Day."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> You used 'Video game' (singular) with 'have' (plural verb form). In English, the verb must agree with the subject: a singular subject takes a singular verb ('has'), and a plural subject takes a plural verb ('have'). Also, 'type' should be plural because you list 'many' of them, and game titles are proper nouns, so they need to be capitalized. Also, use there is/there are instead of "it have". <br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "An important thing how to play thoses game most funniest is play with your friends."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "An important thing about how to play those games in the fun you have playing with your friends."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The word 'funniest' is already a superlative (meaning 'most fun'). You don't need 'most' before it. For longer adjectives or adverbs, you would use 'most' (e.g., 'most interesting'), but for short ones, you add '-est'. Also, ensure you use the correct demonstrative pronoun: 'those' for plural, not 'thoses'.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Free time activities for Teens in Thailand is the best thing for teenager."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Free time activities for teens in Thailand are the best thing for teenagers."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In English, you generally only capitalise the first word of a sentence and proper nouns (like 'Thailand'). Common nouns like 'teens' and 'activities' are usually lowercase unless they are part of a title or at the beginning of a sentence. Also, remember subject-verb agreement: 'activities' (plural) requires 'are' (plural verb form).<br><br>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Review rules for plural nouns and practice adding '-s' or '-es' correctly to nouns.<br>2. Work on identifying when the verb "to be" (is/am/are) is needed in sentences, especially when describing things or people.<br>3. Pay close attention to subject-verb agreement to ensure your verbs match your subjects (e.g., singular subject with singular verb, plural subject with plural verb).<br>4. Use a spell checker regularly to catch common spelling errors and pay attention to proper noun capitalization.<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-28
