 (or 'are', 'am') for a complete sentence. Also, remember to use "an" before a word that starts with a vowel sound like "activity."<br><b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Free time is a very important things."<br><b>Correction:</b> "Free time is a very important thing."<br><b>Explanation:</b> 👉 In English, when you use "a" before a noun, the noun must be singular. Also, Thai often doesn't mark plurals in the same way, so be careful with adding '-s' to nouns that should be singular.<br><b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "But thai student they don't have too much free time."<br><b>Correction:</b> "But Thai students don't have too much free time."<br><b>Explanation:</b> 👉 Nationalities like 'Thai' and country names like 'Thailand' always start with a capital letter in English. Also, consider if you are talking about "students" in general (plural) or a "student" (singular).<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-25
