Among the many ways teenagers spend their free time, I find playing online games and immersing myself in a good book to be the most engaging and beneficial activities."\n💡 Explanation: This improved sentence clearly states the two activities AND explains your personal reasons for choosing them ("most engaging and beneficial"), which directly answers the prompt.	3.0	You tried to write like an article, which is good, but sometimes your language changed from formal to informal. This can make it hard for the reader to understand who you are writing for. Your introduction didn't grab the reader's attention well, and your conclusion felt a bit sudden.\n👉 To Improve: Try to keep your writing style (register) the same throughout your essay. Make your introduction interesting and your conclusion feel complete.\n❌ Weakness: The essay sometimes uses very casual language, but other parts are more formal.\n✨ Improved: "This article will explore two popular pastimes among Thai teenagers, examining the reasons behind their widespread appeal and personal significance."\n💡 Explanation: Using a consistent formal tone, like in this improved sentence, helps maintain a professional and clear register suitable for an article, guiding the reader more effectively.	3.0	You put your ideas into paragraphs, which helps the reader follow along. However, the connections between your ideas could be clearer. Your introduction didn't have a strong main idea (thesis statement), and your body paragraphs didn't start with clear topic sentences that linked back to a main idea.\n👉 To Improve: Start your essay with a clear thesis statement in the introduction. Make sure each body paragraph begins with a topic sentence that supports your main idea, and use more varied linking words to connect your sentences and paragraphs smoothly.\n❌ Weakness: Your first paragraph lists activities but doesn't clearly state what your essay will argue or explain.\n✨ Improved: "Free time activities are incredibly important for teenagers, providing opportunities for relaxation and personal growth. In this essay, I will discuss two popular choices among Thai youth: online gaming and reading, highlighting their appeal and the benefits they offer."\n💡 Explanation: This introduction clearly states the main purpose of the essay (thesis) and introduces the two topics, giving the reader a roadmap for what to expect.	3.0	You used good words about the topic, but there were a few grammar mistakes that made some sentences unclear. You also needed to use relative clauses and passive structures, which were not present.\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Every teenagers have free time activities and each teens have own style of free time activities."\n✨ Correction: "Every teenager enjoys free time activities, and each teen has their own style of free time activities."\n💡 Explanation: In English, words like 'every' and 'each' need a singular noun (teenager, teen) and a singular verb (has). Thai grammar doesn't always show singular or plural in the same way, which is a common difference.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Nowadays many teens prefer to playing games..."\n✨ Correction: "Nowadays many teens prefer to play games..."\n💡 Explanation: After 'prefer to', we usually use the base form of the verb (play), not the -ing form (playing). This is a common error in verb forms for Thai speakers.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "...it give us to imagine with story, relaxtion, and feel calm."\n✨ Correction: "...it gives us the ability to imagine the story, develop relaxation, and and feel calm."\n💡 Explanation: The verb 'give' needs an '-s' for 'it' in the present simple tense (subject-verb agreement). Also, 'relaxtion' is misspelled, and 'imagine with story' could be more natural. Thai often uses more flexible word forms.\n\n❌ Problem: You wrote: "Beside looking at playing games, reading is the popular style."\n✨ Correction: "Besides playing games, reading is another popular activity."\n💡 Explanation: 'Besides' (with an 's') is used to mean 'in addition to'. Also, the phrase 'looking at' is not needed here, and 'another' helps to show it's a second option. Thai can sometimes have more direct phrasing which doesn't always translate perfectly to English.\n\n🎯 YOUR ACTION PLAN\n1. Complete all parts of writing tasks and develop each point fully\n2. Maintain consistent formal register throughout your writing\n3. Practice using different linking words to connect ideas\n4. Review subject-verb agreement rules for present tense	\N	\N	2025-08-29
33953	2025-08-29 15:19:40.460509+00	2026	Free time Activities	As we know that teens like us are study really stress, so that why free time activity is very important for teens. Esspecially, in Thailand most of teenagers do they hobby in their freetime to relax. Two of the most popular activity are playing games and listening to music.One of the most popular actity in Thailand is playing games. It is the activity that you can join with your friends and playing together such as the game that you can play in the same server which is Roblox.Besides playing games, listening to music is another activity that can make people feel soothing or some music make people feel uplifting, especially if we listen to the music that very melodious people will feel more relaxing after they have to encouter with works and stress.To sum up, free time activity for teens is very important because it can help them to communicate with others and feel relaxing, so if they don't stress they concentration will be better.	165	12.0	You did a good job of identifying two relevant free time activities and using some interesting vocabulary!	B2	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	3.0	You identified two free time activities and explained what they are, which is great. However, you didn't fully explain why you chose these activities or why they are important to you personally. The essay feels a little incomplete because of this.👉 To Improve: Make sure to fully address all parts of the question, especially explaining your personal connection or reasons for choosing the activities.❌ Weakness: The essay doesn't clearly state *why* you chose these specific activities or *why* they are important to you.✨ Improved: "I chose playing games and listening to music because they are not only popular but also personally help me relax and connect with friends after a busy week of studying."💡 Explanation: Adding a clear reason for your choices helps the reader understand your perspective and makes your essay more complete and personal.	3.0	You used an appropriate tone for an article for the most part, but sometimes the language felt a bit too informal for a B2 essay. For example, "As we know that teens like us are study really stress" is a bit casual. A B2 article should maintain a more consistent and slightly more formal register to appeal to a general audience.👉 To Improve: Try to keep a consistent, slightly more formal tone throughout your article. Avoid overly casual phrases that might sound like spoken language.❌ Weakness: You wrote: "As we know that teens like us are study really stress, so that why free time activity is very important for teens."✨ Improved: "It is widely acknowledged that teenagers often experience significant academic pressure, which highlights the importance of engaging in free time activities."💡 Explanation: Using more formal language like "It is widely acknowledged" and "significant academic pressure" creates a more appropriate and consistent tone for an essay at this level, making it sound more professional for a general audience.	3.0	You did a good job of organizing your ideas into paragraphs, which helps the reader follow your main points. However, the introduction needs a clearer thesis statement, and some of your body paragraphs could start with stronger topic sentences. Also, you could use a wider variety of linking words to make your ideas flow more smoothly between sentences and paragraphs.👉 To Improve: Start your introduction with a clear thesis statement. Ensure your body paragraphs begin with strong topic sentences that clearly relate to your main argument. Use a wider range of linking words and phrases to connect your ideas.❌ Weakness: The introductory paragraph doesn't have a clear thesis statement, and transitions between some sentences are basic.✨ Improved: "The demanding nature of academic life for teenagers today necessitates engaging in beneficial free-time activities. Among the most popular and effective are playing games and listening to music, both of which offer unique ways to unwind and develop important skills."💡 Explanation: This improved introduction clearly states the main argument (thesis) and introduces the two activities, giving the essay a stronger sense of direction from the beginning. Using more varied linking words will also help your essay flow more smoothly.	3.0	You used some good vocabulary related to the topic, such as "melodious," "soothing," and "uplifting," which is excellent! However, there are several recurring grammar and spelling errors that affect the clarity of your message.❌ Problem: You wrote: "As we know that teens like us are study really stress"✨ Correction: "As we know that teens like us are really stressed by studying" or "As we know that teens like us are really stressed by their studies"💡 Explanation: In English, "stress" is often a noun or a verb meaning to put pressure on someone. To describe a person feeling overwhelmed, we use the adjective "stressed." Also, in Thai, you might say "study stress" directly, but in English, we need to adapt the structure to show that studying causes the stress. This is a common challenge for Thai learners when transitioning from direct translation.❌ Problem: You wrote: "most of teenagers do they hobby"✨ Correction: "most teenagers do their hobbies" or "most of the teenagers do their hobbies"💡 Explanation: After "most of," you should use "the" if you are referring to a specific group, or simply "most teenagers" for a general statement. Also, "they" is a pronoun, and "their" is the possessive adjective needed before "hobby." Thai doesn't have the same distinction between "they" and "their," which can lead to this kind of error for Thai learners.❌ Problem: You wrote: "One of the most popular actity in Thailand"✨ Correction: "One of the most popular activities in Thailand"💡 Explanation: "Activity" needs to be plural ("activities") after "one of the most popular." Also, "actity" is a spelling mistake for "activity." Thai words don't typically change for plurals in the same way English nouns do, which can make it challenging to remember the "-ies" ending for plural nouns in English.❌ Problem: You wrote: "after they have to encouter with works and stress"✨ Correction: "after they have to encounter work and stress" or "after they encounter work and stress"💡 Explanation: "Encounter" is often used directly with its object (e.g., "encounter a problem") without "with." Also, "works" in this context should be "work" (uncountable). "Encouter" is a spelling mistake. Thai might use a phrase that translates more literally to "encounter with work," but in English, "encounter work" is more natural.	\N	\N	2025-08-29
34080	2025-09-20 19:27:25.992464+00	2026	Term 1 Exam Question 2	In Thailand, there are many people having pet in they house. Althought, they house is not very big but they can give them a good life.<br><br><br>In my opinion, I think having pet is a good thing because pet can help you in many way. For example, when you fell sad or bad you can go to play with them. Your pet always play with you and make you fell better. Such as, when I fell bad I will go to play with my pet which is a dog called Jack. I fell better and relax with I play with Jack. Pet also can save you. Them always run to you at the first time when you are dangerous. For example, when someone try to hit me my dog will go to hit them first.<br><br><br>In conclusion, I think having pet is a good thing. Pet can help you do many thing and pet always honest to you. I think we should having pet in our house. And if you love your pet, your pet will love you more.	177	10.0	Hello ThatThat! You've made a great start to your article about pets, sharing your lovely personal experiences and showing real enthusiasm for the topic. Keep up the good work! The most important area to focus on is making sure you cover all parts of the essay question, especially discussing both the good and not-so-good aspects of having pets. With a little more practice in planning your arguments, your writing will become even more persuasive and complete!<br><br>📋 Action Plan:<br>• ✅ Before you start writing, make a quick plan or a 'mind map' of all the things the question asks you to include, like advantages AND disadvantages.<br>• ✅ Read your writing aloud to yourself after you finish; this often helps you catch small grammar mistakes like missing 's' or incorrect verb forms.<br>• ✅ Pay close attention to pronouns like 'they' and 'them' to make sure they clearly refer to the right people or things.	B1+	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	Part 2	2.0	You shared your opinion clearly and gave lovely examples of how pets help us feel better, even talking about your dog, Jack! 💖 This made your article feel very personal and engaging. To get a higher score, it's really important to answer *all* parts of the question. The task asked for both the good things (advantages) and the trickier parts (disadvantages) of having pets. Next time, try to think of at least two difficulties, like how pets need a lot of looking after or can be expensive, and add a paragraph about those. For instance, you could write, "However, having a pet also means big responsibilities. You need to feed them every day and take them to the vet when they are sick." This would show you can see both sides!	3.0	You did a good job of structuring your article with an introduction, main points, and a conclusion, which makes it easy to follow your ideas. 😊 Using phrases like "In my opinion" and "In conclusion" helps the reader understand your flow. For an article in an online magazine for teenagers, it's great to grab the reader's attention right away! You could start with a catchy title, like "My Furry Best Friend: The Pros and Cons of Pet Ownership," or an interesting question in your first paragraph, such as "Do you ever wonder what life would be like with a wagging tail or a purring companion by your side?" Adding these elements would make your article more appealing and engaging for your target audience.	3.0	Your article is clearly organised, and I can see how you've tried to link your ideas using words like "For example" and "Such as." This makes your writing easy to understand. 👍 Your use of paragraphs helps to separate your thoughts nicely. To improve your organisation, you could try to introduce each paragraph with a slightly stronger topic sentence that tells the reader what that paragraph will be about. For example, instead of starting with "In my opinion, I think having pet is a good thing...", you could begin with a sentence like "I truly believe that having a pet brings immense joy and numerous benefits into our lives." Also, consider using a wider variety of linking words to show different relationships between your ideas, such as 'furthermore' to add more advantages, or 'however' to introduce disadvantages.	2.0	You used a good amount of everyday vocabulary to talk about pets, which is appropriate for the topic! 🐶 Words like 'play', 'sad', 'relax', and 'dangerous' are clear and get your message across. One important thing to work on is making sure your verbs agree with your subjects, and using the correct pronouns. For example, you wrote "they house" instead of "their house," "pet is a good thing because pet can help you" instead of "pets are a good thing because they can help you," and "Them always run to you" instead of "They always run to you." In English, if you're talking about more than one pet, you need to use 'pets' (plural) and 'they' or 'them'. Thai speakers sometimes omit plural markers or struggle with subject-verb agreement because Thai grammar doesn't always require these changes. A good habit is to reread sentences and ask yourself: "Is it one thing or many? Does my verb match?" For instance, if you write "My dog *runs*", it's one dog. If you write "My dogs *run*", it's many dogs. Another area to focus on is using the correct form of verbs. You wrote "when you fell sad or bad" instead of "when you *feel* sad or bad" and "make you fell better" instead of "make you *feel* better." You also said "we should having pet" instead of "we should *have* pets." English verbs change depending on tense (past, present, future) and after modal verbs like 'should'. Remember, after 'should', 'can', 'will', we always use the base form of the verb (e.g., should *have*, can *help*). Sometimes, a slightly different word can make your meaning clearer. You wrote "pet always honest to you." While the meaning is understandable, 'loyal' or 'faithful' are more common and precise words to describe a pet's devotion. For example, "Pets are always loyal to you." Keep building your vocabulary so you have more words at your fingertips to choose from. 😊	\N	\N	2025-09-20
