cle shows a good control over language, using a range of everyday vocabulary accurately and even attempting some sophisticated sentence structures! Phrases like "Pets are able to sense our emotion waves or they can notice from our changed behavior... which can help you feel more relaxed and calmer" demonstrate your ability to construct multi-clause sentences effectively. That's a real talent! 🚀 To refine your language further, pay close attention to word forms and common collocations. For example, instead of "Emotional supporting," the correct term is "emotional support." Similarly, "time arrangement" is better expressed as "time management" or "arranging your time." You also said "socializing skill" when "socializing skills" is more appropriate. Sometimes in Thai, nouns can be used in a very flexible way, often without needing a plural form or a different adjective/noun form like in English. This can lead to minor errors in English where a specific noun form (like 'support' or 'management') or plural 's' is required. A good tip is to read your work aloud; sometimes, your ears will catch what your eyes miss! Also, try to use a wider range of vocabulary for repeated concepts to avoid overuse of certain words. These small adjustments will make your writing even more polished and natural.	\N	\N	2025-09-22
