val," "pick me up," and "snacks and water." This is a solid foundation. You also showed good control over simple sentence structures. However, there were some small language points that could be refined to make your writing more precise and natural. For example, you wrote "sending me email corey" when it should be "sending me *an* email, Corey." Also, "I'd enjoy to watch movie" could be improved to "I'd enjoy *watching a movie*." There was also a slightly informal phrase "if we wanna build a robot" and a question that was a little unclear "or we are too lazy?". Paying attention to these smaller grammatical details, such as using articles ("a," "an," "the") correctly and choosing the right verb forms (like using a gerund after "enjoy"), will really help your English sound more polished. Many Thai learners sometimes miss these smaller grammatical elements, so don't worry, it's a common area for improvement. Keep practising, and you'll see a great improvement. 👍	\N	\N	2025-09-16
