st a pets but let me say something that's really real," you could try something like, "It's easy to think of them as 'just pets,' but let me share some real truths about pet ownership." This helps your message come across more clearly and keeps your audience hooked.	2.0	You've correctly used paragraphs to separate your ideas, which is an important step in organising an article! You also use some basic linking words like "Lastly" and "Finally" to show movement through your points. To make your writing even clearer and more connected, try to use a greater variety of linking words and phrases. For example, when you move from one disadvantage to another, you could use phrases like "Furthermore," "In addition to this," or "Another point to consider is..." This helps your reader follow your arguments more easily. Right now, some of your paragraphs feel a little disconnected, so focusing on these linking phrases will help your article feel more coherent and flow together naturally.	1.0	You've used everyday vocabulary appropriately to discuss the topic of pets, and the meaning of your text can usually be understood, which is a good foundation! However, there are quite a few noticeable errors in grammar, spelling, and word choice that can sometimes make your ideas a little difficult to follow. For instance, in your first sentence, "I positive that having pets is really effect our life," it should be "I **am positive** that having pets **really affects** our life." Also, words like "conquensens" should be "consequences," "thier" should be "their," and "hampter" should be "hamster." Many Thai learners sometimes struggle with subject-verb agreement (e.g., "pets is" instead of "pets are") and word forms (like using "effect" as a verb when "affect" is needed). Also, some of your sentences are quite long without enough punctuation, which makes them hard to read. For example, "People usually have pets for thier mental health assistance or service but you still need to think about the cost to own them you might need to pay over one hundred thousand dollar, you need to takes everything about them as your responsibilitys thier health, thier mental health, thier food/water and it's really expensive and cost alot of money." Try breaking these into shorter sentences with more full stops and commas to make your points clearer and easier for the reader to understand. Keep practicing these basics, and your writing will become much more accurate!	\N	\N	2025-09-22
