because," which help connect your sentences. To improve your score in organisation, consider using more varied linking words and phrases to create an even smoother flow between your ideas. For instance, you could use phrases like "First of all," "In addition," or "Finally" to guide your reader through the different aspects of the festival. Also, breaking your article into separate paragraphs for different ideas (like one for when it takes place, one for what happens, and one for what you like about it) can make your writing much clearer and more pleasing to read. Think of each paragraph as a mini-story about a single idea. ✍️	3.0	You've used everyday vocabulary quite well to describe the festival, Kati, and your use of simple grammatical forms is generally controlled. However, there are a few areas where you could focus on improving accuracy to make your writing even clearer. For example, you wrote "many festival" where it should be "many festivals" (remember to add 's' for plural nouns). Another common area for improvement is word order and exact phrasing, such as "the most festival that my family usually celebrate that is Loykratong festival" could be more naturally expressed as "the festival that my family celebrates the most is Loy Krathong." Also, "my mom original hometo" should be "my mom's original hometown" to show possession and correct the spelling. Many Thai learners sometimes omit plural endings or struggle with articles and prepositions because these work differently in Thai. By paying close attention to these small details, your language control will significantly improve, making your writing more precise and polished. Don't worry, these are common learning points, and with practice, you will master them. 💡	\N	\N	2025-09-23
