34059	2025-08-14 13:59:24.517571+00	2026	Thai Food	Food is represent all cultures. Although each culture develop their food by following each environment. In particular, street food is the most accessible kind of food for all generation. Especially Thai street food, which has the top delicious food in the world. Three of the most famous Thai street food are Mhoo Satay, Khao Jee, grilled pork neck with sticky rice.<br><br><br>One of the representative Thai street food is Mhoo Satay. A simple meal featuring a pork shoulder in bite-sized pieces and lemon grass. In addition, some reipe will add the coconut milk to make the taste more sweet. Mhoo Satay is very general breakfast for Thai workers because it's a common street food and easy to find out.<br><br><br>Beside Mhoo Satay, Khao Jee also very symbolic of Thailand, which is a stick rice coast in an egg. In addition, golden mountain sauce and pepper. Khao Jee is strongly show the Thai culture. In northeastern, which is call "Isan", people often offered Khao Jee to monks during Boon Khao Jee festival. This festival are inspired by a story of Buddha. They believe that it's a way of offering food to ancester spirit. Khao Jee also became a beloved comfort food, enjoyed by people of all ages.<br><br><br>Finally, grilled pork neck with sticky rice is a Thai street food that you shouldn't miss, which is a pork neck marinating and grilling with soy sauce, palm sugar and various spices. It's a very stable cuisin in Thailand. In particular, people appreciated for its taste and texture that reflects the Thai culture. Grilled pork neck had been known as "Kor Moo Yang" in Thailand. It's often serve with spicy dipping sauce, which call "Jaew". That's why its became a popular cusine for traveller around the world.<br><br><br>Overall, food is really represent all cultures in the world involve these three beloved comfort food in Thailand, which is Mhoo Satay Khao Jee and grilled pork neck with sticky rice. However, food represent more than just culture, it also represent traditional society and history.	338	\N	Your essay on Thai street food is well-organized and presents clear ideas about different dishes. You have successfully included cultural aspects, especially in your discussion of Khao Jee, and your use of relative clauses and passive structures adds some variety to your writing. To improve, focus on correcting consistent grammatical errors related to subject-verb agreement and verb forms, and be careful with your spelling.	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	Part 2	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-08-14
35239	2025-07-11 03:35:03.959777+00	2026	My Special Place	There are many wonderful places all over the world, but my absolute favourite has to be Rome. Rome, a large city in central Italy, is within the Lazio region. It's a beautiful Italian city with lots of history. Rome is a great ancient European city with so much history, like the Roman empire for instance. On top of that, it also has many historical buildings like the colloseum, which was a place where gladiator fights used to be held. Rome is so dear to me and I'll always have a special place in my heart for it. I've met some of the best people ever in Rome. Some of which I'm still in contact with. Almost everyone I met there was super nice and friendly. Unlike some other countries I've visited. In addition Rome, has so many beautiful ancient building and artifacts around every corner. For instance the St. Peters cathedral, truly a wonderful place. It was so beautiful, I was truly astonished by the architecture. The amount of details they had on the walls and ceiling was truly astonishing. On top of that Rome has so many activities you can do. Such as going to the colloseum, the leaning tower of pisa or going to churches and cathedrals like I did. It's truly a beautiful sight to see. Rome also has many wonderful restaraunts with authentic Italian cuisine you could go eat at. So, in conclusion, I'd have to say with no hesitation that Rome is my absolute favourite city. Theres so many things you can do. I couldn't have asked for a better holiday.	241	15.0	Ana, you've written a good essay about Rome, highlighting its history, people, and attractions. To improve, focus on eliminating the capitalization errors and adding more specific details and sensory descriptions to make your writing more vivid.	B2+	Writing	CA	FIRST	Part 2	4.0	The content is relevant, and the target reader is well informed. You describe Rome's history, attractions, and personal significance to you. To achieve a 5, you could add more specific details and sensory descriptions to bring Rome to life for the reader. For example, instead of saying "beautiful Italian cuisine," describe a specific dish you ate – *perhaps "cacio e pepe," its simple but rich flavors coating your tongue as you sat in a sun-drenched piazza* - and what made it so delicious.	4.0	You have communicated straightforward ideas effectively. The register is appropriate, and the tone is enthusiastic and personal. To achieve a 5, you could use more sophisticated rhetorical devices to further engage the reader and make your writing more memorable. For example, you could use: * Metaphor: "Rome is a living museum, its streets whispering tales of emperors and artists." * Hyperbole: "The beauty of the Sistine Chapel could steal your breath away for eternity." * Rhetorical Questions: "Can you imagine a more inspiring place to wander and discover?"	4.0	The text is well organized and coherent, with a clear introduction, body paragraphs, and conclusion. You also use appositives effectively. To achieve a 5, you could use a wider variety of cohesive devices and organizational patterns to create a more sophisticated and nuanced structure. For example: * Varied Transition Words: Instead of always using "In addition" or "On top of that," try using "Furthermore," "Moreover," "Conversely," "Despite this," or "Subsequently." * Complex Relationships Between Paragraphs: Instead of just listing reasons, create more complex connections between your paragraphs. For example, you could use one paragraph to present a general idea, then use the next paragraph to provide a specific example or counter-argument.	3.0	Ana, the range of vocabulary and grammatical structures is generally good, but there are some noticeable errors, including capitalization errors ("St. Peters cathedral"), spelling errors ("colloseum" should be "Colosseum," "restaraunts" should be "restaurants", "Theres" should be "There's") and a comma splice ("In addition Rome, has so many beautiful ancient building"). To achieve a 5, you need to demonstrate greater control and flexibility in your use of language, with fewer errors and a wider range of sophisticated vocabulary and grammatical structures.	\N	\N	2025-07-11
