ry. You created a strong atmosphere of revenge and tragedy. The plot twist involving the family was quite shocking! Your narrative voice is very distinct.<br><br>I have a few tips to help you polish your writing even further. 📋<br><li><b>Possessives!</b> 🐾 Watch out for 'it's' vs 'its'. 'It's' means 'it is'. For possession, use 'its'.</li><li><b>Verb Agreement!</b> 🤝 'He will earns' should be 'he will <b>earn</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🎨 'Loose-middle aged' is a bit unusual. Maybe just 'middle-aged'?</li>	B2	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	5.0	All content is relevant. The story is dark but follows a strong narrative arc ('Sam caught his wife cheating', 'This is my vengence').	5.0	The text communicates complex emotions and ideas effectively ('he's not hasty, he waited'). The dramatic tone holds the reader's attention.	5.0	The text is well organised and coherent. Cohesive devices are used effectively ('Therefore', 'As a result', 'Even though', 'Finally').	4.0	A range of vocabulary is used ('barricade', 'confessed', 'vengeance', 'chaotic'). Grammatical forms are varied, though there are some subject-verb agreement errors ('he will earns') and possessive pronoun issues ('it's son'). To improve, ensure consistent subject-verb agreement and correct use of possessive pronouns (its vs it's).	\N	\N	2025-12-01
