er 'to', use the base verb. 'Tried to <b>press</b>', not 'tried to pressed'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 A quick check can fix words like 'mistery' (mystery) and 'dissapeard' (disappeared).</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'It was worked' should be 'it <b>worked</b>'.</li>	B1+	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	5.0	All content is relevant. The story is clear and the reader is informed about the 'Imagination box' and its effects ('his neighbor's jewery too').	4.0	The story holds the reader's attention. The mystery element is handled well ('glitter was so beautiful'). To improve, ensure greater clarity in character motivations and reactions to events.	4.0	The text is generally well organised using a variety of linkers ('One day', 'After', 'but', 'So'). To improve, ensure consistency in paragraph breaks, making sure each new idea starts a new paragraph.	3.0	Everyday vocabulary is used appropriately ('mystery', 'gorgeous', 'shocked'). Grammatical forms are generally simple but controlled, with some errors ('intelligentness' is a slip, 'tried to pressed', 'it was worked', 'dissapeard', 'shutted'). To improve, focus on correcting verb forms after 'to' and irregular verbs.	\N	\N	2025-12-01
