</b> 🎬 When Sam is looking for the machine parts, instead of just saying 'after a long search 7 days he found', describe some of his struggles or discoveries during that time.</li><li><b>Deepen Emotions!</b> 😨 How did Sam *feel* when the 'dino suer' was chasing him? Was he terrified, exhausted, determined? Adding these feelings makes the reader connect more.</li>	4.0	Your narrative effectively holds the reader's attention with its action-packed plot! 🦖 The description of the 'dino suer with big sharp tooth trying to cruch him' is vivid and creates excitement.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Vary Sentence Starts!</b> 🔄 While you effectively communicate the action, try starting sentences in different ways to make your writing more dynamic and less repetitive.</li><li><b>Clarify Connections!</b> 🌊 The quick shift from the chase to finding parts could be smoother. How did he escape or lose the dinosaur before finding the pieces?</li>	4.0	You used some effective linking words to guide the reader through the sequence of events, such as 'However', 'As a result', and 'Finally'. This helps to create a coherent story structure. 🔗<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 🧱 Breaking your long text into shorter paragraphs would make it easier for the reader to follow the different stages of Sam's adventure, for example, a new paragraph for the dinosaur chase.</li><li><b>Internal Cohesion!</b> ➡️ Focus on how sentences within a paragraph connect. Ensure a smooth transition of ideas from one sentence to the next.</li>	2.0	You used some adventurous vocabulary like 'inventor', 'creatures', and 'scattered'. That's a great start! 👏<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Past Tense Mastery!</b> ⏳ Many verbs in your story are not consistently in the past tense. For example, 'he travel' should be 'he <b>travelled</b>', and 'he end up' should be 'he <b>ended up</b>'.</li><li><b>Correct Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ After 'to', we use the base form of the verb. So 'tried to went' should be 'tried to <b>go</