ses like 'At first', 'A little while later', and 'Little did he know' to guide the reader through the events smoothy.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraph Balance!</b> ⚖️ Your paragraphs are well-structured, but the second one is quite long. You could have started a new paragraph when the chip malfunctioned to emphasize the panic.</li><li><b>Sentence Variety!</b> 🎼 Try to vary the length of your sentences even more to control the tension—short, punchy sentences work great for action scenes!</li>	5.0	Your vocabulary is outstanding! 👏 Words like 'ecstatic', 'revolutionary', 'malfunctioned', and 'shell-shocked' really elevated your writing.<br><br>Here are a few tiny tweaks for perfection:<br><li><b>Missing Words!</b> 🔍 In the sentence 'people truly thought of him', you missed the word 'what' -> '<b>what</b> people truly thought of him'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Squeling' should be spelled '<b>squealing</b>'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🔄 'Learnt how to love his ability' is good, but 'Learned to <b>accept</b> his ability' might fit the context of hearing thoughts a bit better.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'Voices started coming in' is great. Just be careful with complex sentences to ensure the subject and verb always match perfectly.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-02
