ce the prizes helps to guide the reader through your different points. 📝 However, each paragraph feels a little bit like an answer to a list of questions rather than a smooth, connected message. To help your writing flow even better, try using more 'internal' connectors between and within your paragraphs, like 'Regarding the judges...' or 'As for the prizes...', to make the flow even more natural. 🌟	2.0	When you wrote 'I'm not agree' and 'some of student', I could still understand your meaning, but these grammar slips are like speed bumps that make the reader slow down. 🧐 Using 'I don't agree' and 'some students' would make your writing feel much more natural. My tip for you is to practice the difference between 'I am' and 'I do' and to check that your plural words (like 'students') are correct to help your ideas shine! 📚	\N	\N	2026-02-23
