d the prompt perfectly with a very creative story! 🧙‍♂️ The plot progression from waking up to joining a party is clear and satisfying.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Focus on the Narrative!</b> 🎬 The comment about the 'isekai plot' breaks the immersion slightly. Try to show his surprise through his actions instead of telling the reader it's a genre trope.</li><li><b>Character Detail!</b> 👤 You introduced Kei and Aden quickly at the end. Giving them a bit more description earlier or slowing down their introduction would make the ending feel less rushed.</li>	5.0	Your story is very engaging and fun to read! 🤩 The dialogue at the end really brings the characters to life.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Tone Consistency!</b> 🎼 The shift from narrative description to internal monologue ('On my god...') is a bit jarring. Try to weave thoughts in more naturally.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Some sentences are a bit long and complex. Breaking them down can make the action clearer.</li>	4.0	Your paragraphing is excellent! 🧱 You clearly separated the different stages of the story, which made it very easy to follow.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Smoother Transitions!</b> 🔗 You used 'Suddenly' and 'After', which are good. Try adding words like 'Meanwhile' or 'Consequently' to show how events are connected.</li>	3.0	You used some great fantasy vocabulary like 'guild', 'mage', 'brewer', and 'haphazardly'! 👏<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Irregular Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Shut' is irregular—the past tense is just '<b>shut</b>', not 'shutted'.</li><li><b>Adjectives vs. Nouns!</b> 🔄 'The placed seems difference' -> 'The place seemed <b>different</b>'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Haird' -> '<b>haired</b>', 'Help full' -> '<b>helpful</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'The party need three people' -> 'The party <b>needs</b>' or '<b>needed</b>'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
28783	2026-02-23 09:16:38.227972+00	2026	Question 1	Hi, Mrs Hallam\n\nI strongly believe. That was a good idea to have a school talent competition\n\nI think that talent competition could be for students of all ages. Because the teachers need to know that his students have any talent or not. If not they can teach his students like how to start or what the students need to knew.\n\nI strongly agree because the competition would be perfect if some students parents judge it. That made this show better.\n\nI thought that we should have a really big prizes because all of students have practice before show on stage. that they have more powerful to do this things.\n\nThank, Mrs Hallam	113	14.0	Hi Kao! 🌟 You did a fantastic job responding to all of Mrs Hallam's questions, and your word count was perfect. Your enthusiasm for the talent show really shines through, and I can tell you care about all the students participating. The most important 'homework' for your next piece is to focus on sentence connections—try to avoid starting sentences with 'Because' and see if you can join those ideas to the sentence before. All the best, Ed	B1	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	Part 2	5.0	It was great to see that you included all the points Mrs Hallam asked for, especially when you explained that the 'talent competition could be for students of all ages'. This ensures the teacher is fully informed about your opinions, which makes your response very successful. For your next task, try to give a specific example of a prize to make your final suggestion even more detailed!	3.0	Your choice of 'I strongly agree' really helps to show an enthusiastic and polite tone, which is perfect for an email to a teacher. This clear expression of your opinion helps the reader understand your position immediately, though some of the phrasing feels a bit like a list of separate points. To improve, try using more conversational phrases like 'Regarding the judges...' to link your ideas more naturally.	3.0	I see that 