o improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 Even in a short text, try to have one paragraph for your preference and one for your best purchase.</li><li><b>Punctuation!</b> 🛑 Use full stops to end sentences. It helps the reader breathe!</li>	2.0	You used some basic words well, like 'stock' and 'decide'. 📚<br><br>Here are some corrections:<br><li><b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Want to ate' -> 'Want to <b>eat</b>'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🔄 'That why's I love' -> 'That's <b>why</b> I love'.</li><li><b>Grammar!</b> ⚙️ 'If i about to buy' -> 'If I am <b>about</b> to buy'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'In the online' -> '<b>Online</b>' (no 'in the').</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
31545	2025-12-14 09:33:34.543949+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. Before that, I was an ordinary person, is lived in remote city, Waked up from a bad dream. I go to do my routine like every day, but something strange. I heard the noise from nowhere. I didn't care it because it not essential for me.<br><br>Intially, The wind is too heavy, it make my window open. I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes. It was a massive monster out side my apartment. I was shocked, my heart race and feel like butterfly in my stomach.<br><br>Subsequently, a giant monster saw me and moved forward to me. I find the place to hide, but it was too late. A monster destroy my apartment. I fail from second floor. It was hurt but I don't feel anything because it form adrenaline.<br><br>Nevertheless, I about to died but I was rescued by my friends. I escaped from that monster and become a normal.<br><br>This even make me to with this book.	174	12.0	Hello Mew! 👋<br><br>This was a very intense and action-packed story! 🦖 The image of a giant monster attacking your apartment is terrifying. You did a good job describing the sequence of events from the noise to the attack.<br><br>I have a few tips to help clarify your story! 📋<br>1. <b>The Ending!</b> ❓ The last sentence 'make me to with this book' is a bit confusing. Make sure to double-check your ending so the reader knows exactly what happened.<br>2. <b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ Watch your past tenses! 'I fail' should be 'I <b>fell</b>'.<br>3. <b>Vocabulary!</b> 🗣️ Try to learn more specific words for feelings. Instead of just 'shocked', maybe 'paralyzed with fear'?	B1	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	3.0	You followed the story prompt well! 🌟 The transition from a normal day to a monster attack was clear.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Clarify the Ending!</b> 🏁 Did you write a book about the event? Or did the event make you stronger? Rewriting the final sentence to be clearer is key.</li><li><b>Explain the 'Adrenaline'!</b> 💓 You mentioned you didn't feel pain because of adrenaline. That's a great detail! describing *how* that felt (e.g., 'my body felt numb') would be even better.</li>	3.0	You kept the action moving, which is good! 🏃‍♂️<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Emotional Depth!</b> 🎭 You said 'I was shocked', but trying to describe the physical feeling (shaking hands, racing heart) makes the reader feel it too.</li><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The rescue happened very quickly. Slowing down that moment to explain *how* your friends saved you would add more excitement.</li>	4.0	You used excellent sequencing words like 'Initially', 'Subsequently', and 'Nevertheless'. 🌟 This gave your story a very clear structure.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linking Variety!</b> 🔄 While those words are good, they are quite formal. In a story, words like 'Suddenly', 'Moments later', or 'Just then' often sound more natural.</li>	2.0	You tried some complex sentences, which is great effort! 💪<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'Is lived' -> '<b>lived</b>', 'I fail' -> 'I <b>fell</b>', 'Waked up' -> '<b>Woke</b> up'.</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Intially' -> '<b>Initially</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'It not essential' -> 'It wasn't <b>important</b>'.</li><li><b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ 'I didn't care it' -> 'I didn't care <b>about</b> it'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
