33957	2025-12-14 09:33:35.428931+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of window and couldn't believe my eyes. I was tried from a work because my manager gave me many works to do, but I realized that the next was my birthday.<br><br>After a work, I went to the cake shop to buy my birthday cake. I saw a strange cake, which sold for only 10$, was on top by smile clown. It looked scary but it's cheap, so I bought it.<br><br>I went back to my room and took a shower. After that, I opened the windows and I saw that many people were in front of my condominium and I saw a clown that looked like my cake. I felt stressed and looked my door. After a few minute, my door had knocked by someone.<br><br>I didn't know how to do next and I was embarrassing. I decided to open the door slowly with a nervous feeling.<br><br>The man in front of the door surprised me. He showed that I bought a special cake which was making by a famous influencer called Mr. Shan. I was surprised and they gave me 10000 $. I was happy with that.	192	15.0	Hello Peptine! 👋<br><br>What a fantastic plot twist! 🎁 I went from feeling scared for you (scary clown!) to feeling happy (prize money!). You did a great job manipulating the reader's emotions. The 'strange cake' was a very creative clue.<br><br>I have a few tips to make it perfect! 📋<br>1. <b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ Don't forget 'the'. 'I looked out of window' -> 'out of <b>the</b> window'.<br>2. <b>Passive Voice!</b> 🛠️ When describing who made the cake, say 'made by', not 'making by'.<br>3. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'I was embarrassing' means *you* were embarrassing people! You meant 'I was <b>embarrassed</b>'.	B1+	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	4.0	You created a very engaging story with a satisfying surprise ending. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>The Door Scene!</b> 🚪 You said you 'looked my door'. Did you lock it? Peek through it? clarifying this action would build more suspense.</li>	4.0	You held my attention really well! I wanted to know what the clown would do. 🤡<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Emotional Reaction!</b> 💓 When you got the $10,000, tell us more! Did you jump for joy? Did you faint? 'I was happy' is a bit too calm for such a big prize!</li>	4.0	Your paragraphing is excellent. 🧱 You clearly separated the work, the shop, the home, and the ending.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Linkers!</b> 🔗 You rely on 'After...' a lot. Try using 'Later', 'Then', or 'Consequently' to mix it up.</li>	3.0	You used good vocabulary like 'condominium', 'influencer', and 'stressed'. 🏢<br><br>Here are some corrections:<br><li><b>Adjectives!</b> 🔄 'I was embarrassing' -> 'I was <b>embarrassed</b>'.</li><li><b>Passive Voice!</b> 🛠️ 'Making by' -> '<b>Made</b> by', 'Had knocked by' -> '<b>Was</b> knocked on by'.</li><li><b>Verbs!</b> ⏳ 'Looked my door' -> '<b>Locked</b> my door' (I assume!).</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
