hop (online vs. in-store) would complete the task.	B2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You thoroughly explored the significance of your pillow as the 'best thing I ever bought', providing rich context about your emotional journey. 🌟 Your content is highly relevant and well-developed.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Explicitly Address Shopping Habits!</b> 🛒 While you implied the pillow was bought, briefly stating whether you prefer online or in-store shopping (even just one sentence) would ensure full task coverage.</li><li><b>Clarify Dense Phrases!</b> 💡 Phrases like 'emotions my emotional control were considerably worse' could be rephrased for smoother reading, e.g., 'my emotional control was considerably worse'.</li>	4.0	Your writing has a mature and reflective tone, drawing the reader into your personal narrative. 🧠 You successfully convey the emotional depth and personal growth.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing and Flow!</b> 🌊 Some complex ideas are presented in very long sentences. Breaking these into shorter, more direct sentences would improve overall flow and impact.</li>	4.0	Your narrative follows a clear and logical progression: problem, solution, acquisition, and reflection. 🧱 This makes your story easy to follow.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Visual Paragraph Breaks!</b> 📝 While your ideas are grouped logically, adding more distinct paragraph breaks would enhance readability, especially for longer sections of text.</li><li><b>Transition Variety!</b> 🔗 While 'soon after' and 'later on' are good, try to vary your transitional phrases (e.g., 'consequently', 'meanwhile', 'however') to make the flow even more seamless.</li>	4.0	You use an impressive range of ambitious vocabulary, such as 'notably', 'considerably', 'unpleasant', 'hesitation', 'gratification', and 'extensively'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Decipline' -> '<b>discipline</b>', 'slove' -> '<b>solve</b>', 'meanful' -> '<b>meaningful</b>', 'fufill' -> '<b>fulfill</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice/Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'By given me a viable option Got sent...' -> 'by <b>giving</b> me a viable option: <b>get</b> sent...'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'Started to saved' -> 'started to <b>save</b>'.</li><li><b>Subject-Verb Agreement!</b> ⚙️ 'It all started when I was young. I had a problem with emotions my emotional control were considerably worse' -> 'It all started when I was young. I had a problem with emotions; my emotional control <b>was</b> considerably worse'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
