it have dark eyes? A small detail could make it much scarier.</li><li><b>Teacher's Reaction!</b> 👩‍🏫 You told the teacher you were going to the toilet. What was the teacher's reaction? Did they look suspicious?</li>	3.0	You successfully built a sense of unease and horror, especially with the ghost's words, "come~ with~ me~". 😱<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Show, Don't Tell!</b> 🎬 Instead of saying 'it was really creepy', describe *why* it was creepy. What specific sights or sounds contributed to that feeling?</li><li><b>Vary Your Language!</b> 🗣️ Try to avoid repetition. For instance, instead of 'I saw a courp on the floor... I told the teacher that I would go to toilet to saw a courp', use a pronoun or rephrase.</li>	4.0	Your story has a clear chronological progression, from the school rumors to the classroom incident and the dream ending. 🧱 Your paragraph breaks are generally effective.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Dialogue Formatting!</b> 💬 When a character speaks, it's best practice to put their speech on a new line and enclose it in quotation marks. This makes dialogue much easier to read.</li>	3.0	You used everyday vocabulary, along with some horror-related terms like 'creepy' and 'balcony'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Courp' -> '<b>corpse</b>', 'screemved' -> '<b>screamed</b>', 'dreamming' -> '<b>dreaming</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Did at this building' -> '<b>died</b> in this building'.</li><li><b>Past Tense!</b> ⏳ 'I look out' -> 'I <b>looked</b> out'. 'I was the student' -> 'I <b>am a</b> student'.</li><li><b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ 'Saw a courp' (the first time) -> '<b>see</b> a corpse' (when thinking about going to the toilet).</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
28858	2025-12-14 09:36:23.074573+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out of the window and couldn't believe my eyes, Sam a handsome kid who loves to play basketball. Sam has a dream to become the best basketball player in the world. Sam mother didn't want him to play basketball and focus on studying. But his dad kept support him and train him.  One day sam was playing games in his house but suddenly he heard a man sound outside his house calling his name he looked out of the window and couldn't believe his eyes the coach from his dream team that he always wanted to meet is there. He quickly go up to him. The coach said that he had watched his game play in youtube and saw potential in his and he decided to come and invite him to the team. He was so confused and happy at the same time about the youtube the coach watched.  when he went inside. He asked his dad about the youtube. and found out that it was his dad who made the youtube and trust him and supported him all the time.  Finally he learned that always keep P trying and you will achieve his dream.	197	16.0	Hello Gunner! 👋<br><br>This is such a heartwarming and inspiring story about chasing your dreams! 🏀 I loved the twist about your supportive dad secretly being behind the YouTube channel and inviting the coach. It's a fantastic message about perseverance and trust. Keep that dream alive!<br><br>I have a few tips to help you make your story even more impactful! 📋<br>1. <b>Apostrophes!</b> 📝 'Sam mother' should be 'Sam<b>'s</b> mother' (possessive).<br>2. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Keep P trying' is a bit unclear. Did you mean 'keep <b>on</b> trying' or 'keep <b>persevering</b>'?<br>3. <b>Clarity of Dialogue!</b> 💬 Make sure to use quotation marks for direct speech (e.g., when the coach speaks).	B1+	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You created a very relevant and emotionally resonant story about a young basketball player's journey. 🌟 The build-up of Sam's dream and his dad's secret support was excellently handled.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>The Coach's Words!</b> 💬 The coach saw 'potential in his'. What specific potential did he see? Describing that would add more depth to Sam's talent.</li><li><b>Sam's Game Play!</b> ⛹️‍♂️ You mentioned the coach watched 'his game play in youtube'. Briefly describing one exciting move Sam made in his game would make the coach's interest more tangible.</li>	4.0	You successfully conveyed an inspirational tone, highlighting the importance of dreams and family support. 💖 The repetition of 'couldn't believe his eyes' at key moments was effective in building excitement.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Dialogue Punctuation!</b> 💬 Using quotation marks around direct speech makes it much clearer who is saying what.</li>	4.0	Your story has a clear narrative arc: the dream, the struggle, the opportunity, and the revelation. 🧱 Your use of linking words like 'One day', 'suddenly', and 'Finally' helps guide the reader.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 📝 While you use some paragraph breaks, consider breaking the longer paragraph when the coach speaks, to give that important moment more emphasis.</li>	3.0	You used good vocabulary like 'potential', 'support', 'invite', and 'achieve'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Possessives!</b> 📝 'Sam mother' -> 'Sam<b>'s</b> mother'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'Kept support him' -> 'kept <b>supporting</b> him'. 'He quickly go up' -> 'He quickly <b>went</b> up'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Made the youtube' -> '<b>created the YouTube channel</b>'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🔄 'Always keep P trying' -> 'always keep <b>on trying</b>'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
34931	2025-09-16 21:45:26.729885+00	2026	Term 1 Email	Dear Corey,<br><br><br>Thanks for organizing a tickets for the science festival for me.<br><br><br>I'd be pleasure, if you can pick me up at my home. Because my parents won't have a time to take me to the science festival. They probably working on Saturday.<br><br><br>I think build a robot should be more interesting, because I don't really like Dinosaurs, so it would be boring. Build a robot seem fun and we can learn for our science project in the next term.<br><br><br>I think we should bring a camera to take a pictures and selfie to collect the amazing moments. And don't worry, I'll bring a pocket for sure.<br><br><br>Goodbye,<br><br><br>Frame	104	13.0	Hi Frame! It was lovely to read your email to Corey. You did a really good job of responding to all of his questions and making your preferences clear. To make your writing even clearer and more natural, you could focus on making sure your sentences are grammatically correct. Keep practicing, and you will see wonderful progress. 📋 Here are three steps you can take to improve your writing:<br>✔️ Check verb forms carefully to ensure they match the subject and tense of your sentences.<br>✔️ Pay close attention to articles (a, an, the) when you use nouns.<br>✔️ Practice using common phrases for expressing feelings and opinions so they sound more natural.	B1	Writing	Term 1 Finals	PET	Part 2	3.0	You've done well to include most of the important information Corey needed to know for the science festival. For example, it was great that you clearly told Corey you'd prefer to be picked up and gave a good reason why your parents couldn't take you. You also made it clear you'd rather build a robot than watch a film, and explained why the film sounded a bit boring to you. Suggesting a camera was a clever idea too, and you said why you wanted to bring it. However, to get an even better score, try to make your excitement about the tickets more obvious at the beginning. Also, when Corey asked about "pocket money," it seems you thought he meant "a pocket" instead. This minor misunderstanding meant you didn't quite address that point fully. Thai learners sometimes make these small slips when a word has a similar sound or form to another.	5.0	Your email to Corey was very well-structured and easy to follow. You started with a friendly "Dear Corey" and ended with a clear "Goodbye, Frame," which is exactly what we expect in an email to a friend. 🥳 You also did a fantastic job of organising your thoughts into different paragraphs, which makes your message very clear and helps the reader understand all your ideas without any trouble. This shows you know how to write an email that keeps the reader engaged and gets your message across effectively.	3.0	Your email was generally well-organised and coherent, with your ideas presented in a sensible order. You used some basic linking words, like "Because" and "so," which helped to connect your sentences and make the text flow. This is a good start. To improve, try to use a wider variety of linking words and phrases. For instance, instead of just "Because," you could use "since" or "as a result" to show different connections between your ideas. Thinking about how one sentence leads to the next will help you explore more ways to link your thoughts smoothly. Thai learners often focus on getting their main points across, and sometimes forget to add these small words that really help the reader follow their train of thought.	2.0	You used everyday vocabulary quite well, and I could generally understand what you wanted to say, which is excellent. However, there were a few noticeable grammatical errors that, while not completely stopping communication, did make some sentences a little less clear. For example, you wrote "organizing a tickets" instead of "organising the tickets," and "I'd be pleasure" should be "I'd be pleased" or "it would be a pleasure." Also, "won't have a time" should be "won't have time," and "They probably working" should be "They are probably working." To improve, try to pay close attention to articles like "a," "an," and "the," and make sure your verbs are in the correct tense and form. For instance, after "I think," you usually need a full sentence, like "I think **that building** a robot would be more interesting." Thai learners sometimes struggle with articles and verb agreement because these grammatical features work differently, or are not as prominent, in Thai.	\N	\N	2025-09-16
28841	2025-12-14 09:36:23.749581+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M2A Part 2	I looked out the window and couldn't believe my eyes. I saw a dragon standing calmly in my garden! Its icy blue eyes were staring me like it was waiting for me a long time already. I blinked so many times but the large dragon was still there no matter what.  Out of curiosity, I walked out from my house and slowly approached the dragon yet cautiously. The dragon quickly back away and lowly growled at me like it was scared of me. So I also stepped back so it didn't suddenly attack me. However I saw that its right wing was bleeding for some reasons. The dragon seemed to be in so much pain that I couldn't help but decided to help it.  Then I went back into my house to the first aid bag. After I had grabbed my first aid bag, I immediately headed to the injured dragon and carefully healed its wing with things inside my first aid bag then wrapped its wound with a bandage! Although the dragon seemed to be cautious at first, it later cooperated with me when I promised to heal its wound.  "You are a very kind person human" The voice suddenly came out from the dragon's mouth. I was so surprised that the dragon could talk but it later explained to me that this was just a trial and it didn't really hurt, just pretended to be. After that the dragon grabbed on my shirt collar with its mouth carefully and placed me down on its back. "As a thank for you a very kind-hearted human I will let you ride me to see the sky for once" and prepared to take off.  The dragon spreaded its beautiful wings widely before everything would turn black. In the end I woke up on my bed and it turned out it all was just a dream! I was a little bit disappointed for waking up before getting to see the sky but it was very inspiring that I immediately wrote what I remembered on my notebook so I could use this for my next novel idea after being burn out for a long time as a famous writer.	366	20.0	Hello Ie Ie! 👋<br><br>This is an absolutely breathtaking and imaginative story! 🐉 Your dragon encounter, from its icy blue eyes to the thrilling flight, was incredibly vivid. The twist about using the memory for your next novel was brilliant and very meta! You have a true gift for storytelling!<br><br>I have a few tiny tips to help you perfect this masterpiece! 📋<br>1. <b>Spelling!</b> 📝 Watch out for 'spreaded' (spread) and 'burn out' (burnout).<br>2. <b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Staring me' should be 'staring <b>at</b> me'.<br>3. <b>Refine Dialogue!</b> 💬 Your dragon dialogue is strong, but ensure you punctuate it clearly.	B2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You crafted an exceptionally relevant and richly detailed narrative, exceeding expectations for the prompt! 🌟 The emotional arc of healing the dragon, the magical flight, and the meta-narrative twist of it being a dream for a writer's novel idea were all perfectly executed. All content contributed significantly to the story's depth and enjoyment.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Dragon's Pain!</b> 💔 You said the dragon 'seemed to be in so much pain'. Describing *how* it showed its pain (e.g., whimpering, labored breathing) would heighten the reader's empathy.</li><li><b>Writer's Block!</b> ✍️ You mentioned 'being burn out'. Briefly explaining *what kind* of novel you write or what caused the burnout would add even more depth to your character as a writer.</li>	5.0	This is an outstanding piece of engaging and sophisticated narrative writing! 🤩 You skillfully use descriptive language, emotional cues, and a clever plot device to captivate the reader. The dialogue with the dragon is particularly effective.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Show, Don't Tell!</b> 🎬 You excelled at this! Continue to focus on describing actions and sensory details rather than just stating emotions (e.g., 'icy blue eyes were staring me').</li>	5.0	Your story is exceptionally well-organized, with clear paragraph breaks that logically guide the reader through each stage of the encounter. 🧱 Your use of linking words like 'Out of curiosity', 'Although', and 'In the end' creates a seamless flow.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Nothing!</b> 🌟 Your organization is superb. This story demonstrates excellent structural control.</li>	5.0	You display an excellent command of language, using a wide range of sophisticated vocabulary such as 'calmly', 'cautiously', 'cooperated', 'kind-hearted', 'inspiring', and 'burnout'. 📚 Your use of complex sentences is highly effective.<br><br>Here are a few minor polishes:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Spreaded' -> '<b>spread</b>'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Staring me' -> 'staring <b>at</b> me'. 'Thank for you' -> 'thank <b>you for being</b> a very kind-hearted human'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'Couldn't help but decided to help it' -> 'couldn't help but <b>decide</b> to help it'.</li><li><b>Capitalization!</b> 🅰️ 'I saw a dragon standing calmly in my garden! Its icy blue eyes were staring me like it was waiting for me a long time already. I blinked so many times but the large dragon was still there no matter what. Out of curiosity, I walked out from my house and slowly approached the dragon yet cautiously.' -> 'I saw a dragon standing calmly in my garden! Its icy blue eyes were staring at me like it had been waiting for a long time. I blinked many times, but the large dragon was still there. Out of curiosity, I walked out of my house and slowly but cautiously approached the dragon.'</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
