 a very relatable plot about a belief in aliens and a disappointing prank. 🌟 The contrast between your character's belief and the reality of the prank was well-conveyed.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Bully's Motivation!</b> 🤔 Why did the bully target you specifically? Was it because of your belief in aliens? A small detail could add more depth to this aspect of the story.</li><li><b>The 'Joyful' Part!</b> 🎢 You mentioned being 'scared and joyful at the same time' about the UFO. What was the source of that joy? Was it the validation of your belief?</li>	3.0	You successfully conveyed the emotional journey of a high-schooler facing both belief and bullying. 💬<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Vary Emotional Expression!</b> 🎭 You repeated 'couldn't belive my eyes'. Try using synonyms or different phrases to express surprise or disbelief.</li>	4.0	Your story has a clear chronological progression, moving from your initial belief to the sightings and the eventual prank reveal. 🧱 Your paragraph breaks are generally effective.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Boundaries!</b> 🛑 Ensure that each sentence is a complete thought, especially when connecting multiple ideas.</li><li><b>Linking Words!</b> 🔗 While you use words like 'One day' and 'After', try to incorporate more varied transitions (e.g., 'however', 'consequently', 'despite this') to create a smoother flow.</li>	3.0	You used everyday vocabulary related to school, bullying, and space, like 'high-schooler', 'bullied', 'strange', and 'UFO'. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Belive' -> '<b>believe</b>' (multiple times), 'continved' -> '<b>continued</b>', 'pronked' -> '<b>pranked</b>', 'shater' -> '<b>shattered</b>', 'happyness' -> '<b>happiness</b>', 'humorus' -> '<b>humorous</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'I get bullied' -> 'I <b>got</b> bullied'. 'Was about to went' -> 'was about to <b>go</b>'.</li><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'Humorus my face look' -> 'how humorous my face <b>looked</b>'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
33953	2026-02-23 09:59:15.665585+00	2026	Question 1	Dear Mrs Hallam,\n\nA school talent competition is very good idea because it make a space for all students to show they talent and it will make them be confident and proud of them self.\n\nI think the talent show could be for students of all ages to let them show their abilities for everyone who want not just for students over 15 only.\n\nI agree that we can let some parents judge the competition but I think we also have to let the students do the vote because this is a talent show for students so we have to let them vote.\n\nTo sumup, I think the winners of this competition should receive a certificate and some exclusive merchaindise.\n\nThank you\n\nSalila Lookasemsukwong	124	15.0	Hi Kaohom L! You’ve done a wonderful job responding to all of Mrs Hallam's questions, and your suggestion about letting students vote was very thoughtful. Your vocabulary is quite sophisticated for this level, especially with words like 'merchandise' and 'confident.' My main 'homework' for you is to focus on your 'subject-verb agreement' (like 'it makes' or 'everyone wants') to ensure your grammar is as strong as your great ideas. All the best, Ed	B1	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	Part 2	5.0	It was great to see how you included 'all students to show they talent' as a reason for supporting the show, as this provides the teacher with a very clear justification for your opinion. By answering every part of Mrs Hallam's email—including the age range, the judges, and the prizes—you have ensured the reader is fully informed and can move forward with the planning. To keep this high standard, continue to provide a specific 'why' for every suggestion you make, just as you did here! 🌟	4.0	Your choice of 'I agree that we can let some parents judge' really helps maintain a polite and respectful tone suitable for writing to a teacher. 🚀 To reach the top level, try to make the transition between your opinions feel a bit more like a natural conversation and less like a sequential list of responses to the prompt. 🌟	3.0	I see that you used clear paragraphs for each new topic, which acts like a helpful roadmap for your reader! 📝 However, each paragraph feels a little bit like an answer to a list of questions rather than a smooth, connected message. To help your writing flow even better next time, try using more 'internal' connectors between and within your paragraphs, like 'Additionally' or 'Furthermore', to make the flow even more natural. 🌟	3.0	When you wrote 'exclusive merchaindise', you showed a really impressive vocabulary range that goes beyond basic B1 levels. However, small slips in grammar like 'it make' instead of 'it makes' or 'they talent' instead of 'their talent' act as little speed bumps that slow the reader down slightly. For your next piece, try to have a quick 'grammar check' at the end specifically for subject-verb agreement and possessive pronouns to make your writing even smoother!	\N	\N	2026-02-23
