ection with the reader. 🚀	3.0	I see that you included a new paragraph for each point, starting with clear markers like 'In my opinion' and 'I disagree', which acts like a map for the reader. This logical structure helps the reader follow your arguments one by one without getting lost in the text. One way to level up is to use 'linkers' like 'Additionally' or 'Finally' to connect these paragraphs so the email feels like one continuous, flowing conversation. 📝	3.0	When you wrote 'students are have their own ability', I could understand your meaning, but the extra 'are' makes the sentence feel a bit 'bumpy' for the reader. Using two verbs together like this is a common hurdle, and removing the 'are' would give the sentence a much stronger heartbeat. My tip for next time is to double-check your sentences for 'double verbs'—usually, you only need the main action verb to make your point clearly! ✨	\N	\N	2026-02-23
