y, for an article, consider a slightly more structured approach with an introduction and conclusion that frames your narrative.</li>	3.0	Your story follows a clear chronological progression from your childhood dream to finally owning Sam. ⏳<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphing!</b> 🧱 The entire text is a single block. Breaking it into paragraphs (e.g., one for your childhood dream, one for your parents' decision, one for meeting Sam) would greatly enhance readability.</li><li><b>Sentence Structure!</b> 🏗️ Some sentences are quite long and combine many ideas. Breaking these into shorter, more focused sentences would make your story easier to follow.</li>	2.0	You used clear, simple vocabulary that effectively conveys your message. 📚<br><br>Here are a few corrections:<br><li><b>Phrasing!</b> 🗣️ 'I very love to do' -> 'I <b>really</b> love to do' or 'I <b>really</b> love <b>doing</b>'.</li><li><b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ 'My class is on monday' -> 'my class <b>was</b> on Monday'. 'It been 4 year' -> 'it <b>has been</b> 4 years'. 'Can bought' -> 'can <b>buy</b>'.</li><li><b>Articles!</b> 🅰️ 'It baby horse' -> 'it<b>'s a</b> baby horse'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
