28835	2025-12-14 15:56:27.895231+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M3A Task 1	From : Tatar<br><br>Hi, I'm enjoying either that we are going camping this weekend. I want to gain some new experience which I never do that.<br><br>From my perspective, I advice you for take the train on Saturday morning because it doesn't waste of time anyway.<br><br>In addition, your dad can be exhausted for the long journey. I don't want to worry about this situation.<br><br>I strongly don't agree with you because sausages may make you fat easily if you eat it a lot.<br><br>I suggest you to make some vegetables or fruits because it is healthy. In the end, I suggest you to bring a huge teddy bear for huging every night.<br><br>See you soon, Alex.	117	15.0	Hello Tatar! 👋<br><br>Great job on your email! I liked your thoughtful advice about taking the train and bringing a teddy bear - that was a sweet detail! 🧸 Your ideas were very clear.<br><br>Here are 3 tips for next time: 📋<br>1. <b>Relax your tone!</b> 🗣️ "From my perspective" is a bit too formal for a friend. Try "I think..." instead!<br>2. <b>Word Choice!</b> 📚 "Huging" should be "hugging".<br>3. <b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ "Advice you for take" -> "Advise you <b>to</b> take".\n	B1+	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You answered all the questions well! ✅<br><br>✅ <b>Travel:</b> Good reasons for the train (dad's energy).<br>✅ <b>Food:</b> Healthy suggestions (fruit/veg).<br>✅ <b>Warmth:</b> A teddy bear is a unique idea!<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Explain "Why"!</b> 💭 You said sausages "make you fat". Maybe simply say they are "unhealthy" to be softer.</li>\n	3.0	You communicated your ideas clearly. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Register!</b> ⚖️ You used formal phrases like "In addition" and "From my perspective". In an email to a friend like Alex, it's better to be casual! Use "Also," or "And,".</li>\n	4.0	Your email was very well organised with clear paragraphs. 📝 It was easy to follow your points.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Sentence Flow!</b> 🌊 Try shorter sentences to keep the energy high for a camping trip email.</li>\n	3.0	Good use of words like "exhausted" and "healthy"! 👏<br><br>Watch out for these errors:<br><li><b>Verbs!</b> ⚙️ "waste of time" -> "waste time".</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 "advise you <b>to</b> take" (not "for take").</li><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 "huging" -> "hu<b>gg</b>ing".</li>\n	\N	\N	2025-12-14
34080	2025-12-14 15:56:28.72135+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M3A Task 1	Me too! I really want to go now and I think it will be very interesting. I think we can take the train on Saturday morning. Because the train is large and faster than car and I think we can go by ourself so your dad can go to work or having his free time. I disagree about that you said we just cook sausages. Because I think we can do something that harder such as hamburger. And finally we can take more clothes so it will be warm at night.	91	13.0	Hi ThatThat! 👋<br><br>Nice email! I liked your point that taking the train lets Alex's dad go to work or have free time - very thoughtful of you! 🤔<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 Your email is one big block. Split it up!<br>2. <b>Grammar!</b> 🛠️ "go by ourself" -> "go by <b>ourselves</b>".<br>3. <b>Linking!</b> 🔗 You used "Because" a lot. Try "Since" or "As" sometimes.\n	B1	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You included all the necessary information. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Details!</b> 💭 "Something that harder such as hamburger" - Good idea! Doing something difficult can be fun.</li>\n	3.0	Your tone was nice and friendly. 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Flow!</b> 🌊 Using "And" and "Because" at the start of every sentence makes it sound a bit repetitive. Try putting them in the middle of sentences.</li>\n	2.0	To get a higher score, you MUST use paragraphs! 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Structure!</b> 🏗️ Hit 'Enter' twice after talking about the car, and again after talking about food. It makes it much easier to read.</li>\n	3.0	You expressed your ideas clearly! 👏<br><br>Fix these errors:<br><li><b>Reflexive Pronouns!</b> 🪞 "ourself" -> "our<b>selves</b>" (plural).</li><li><b>Comparatives!</b> 📏 "something that harder" -> "something <b>harder</b>" (no 'that').</li>\n	\N	\N	2025-12-14
34014	2025-12-14 15:56:28.473881+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M3A Task 1	From : Lookpear Subject : Camping Trip<br><br>Dear, Alex<br><br>I am so excited about our camping trip this weekend too! We are going to have the most wonderful time ever! I prefer to take the train on Saturday morning, Can we meet in front of the train station? For the food option, sausages are great but I need something that is exciting to cook and eat. Maybe we should cook some hamburger. I think we should bring some sweaters and leggings to keep us warm too<br><br>See you soon, Alex.	90	17.0	Hi Lookpear! 👋<br><br>Wow, what an energetic email! "Most wonderful time ever!" - I love that positivity! 🌟 Your suggestion to cook hamburgers because sausages aren't "exciting" was a great point.<br><br>Here are 3 tips to be even better: 📋<br>1. <b>Punctuation!</b> 🛑 "Saturday morning, Can we..." -> The comma should be a full stop or question mark.<br>2. <b>Linking!</b> 🔗 Try connecting your ideas with "since" or "although".<br>3. <b>Details!</b> 💭 "Exciting to cook" - great phrase!\n	B2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	All points covered perfectly! ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Meeting Point!</b> 📍 You asked "Can we meet...?". That's a great addition! It makes the email feel real.</li>\n	4.0	You sounded exactly like a friend writing to a friend. Perfect tone! 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Flow!</b> 🌊 Your sentences are good, but try varying the length. Some short, some long.</li>\n	4.0	Your email flowed logically from one point to the next. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Paragraphs!</b> 🧱 Ensure you have a clear blank line between the travel section and the food section.</li>\n	4.0	Great words like "leggings" and "option"! 👏<br><br>A tiny fix:<br><li><b>Punctuation!</b> 🖋️ "Saturday morning, Can we" -> "Saturday morning. Can we". New sentences start with capitals, so they need a full stop before them!</li>\n	\N	\N	2025-12-14
35239	2026-02-23 10:48:48.923725+00	2026	Question 1	Dear Ms. Hallam,\n\nI think organizing a school talent competition is a fantastic idea! It's a great way for students to show off their skills.\n\nFirst of all, I don't think there should be an age restrictment. I think it's wonderful to see everyone come together and show their talents. Not just people over 15.\n\nRegarding the judges, I definitely think we should get professiond experts that know the craft to pick the winners. Since parents can be biased towards their children.\n\nAnd finally, I think the winners should receive a cash prize or a scholarship instead of a trophy. Since it can be more beneficial to them than a one-time celebration.\n\nFrom,\n\nAna Semjang	115	19.0	Hi Ana! 🌟 Your email was a joy to read! You gave very thoughtful reasons for your opinions, and your vocabulary is truly impressive. My main 'homework' for you is to practice connecting your ideas together into full sentences. For example, instead of using 'Since' to start a new sentence, try to join it to the previous one with a comma. Keep up the amazing work, you have a natural talent for writing! 🚀 All the best, Ed	B2	Writing	Term 2 Finals	PET	Part 2	5.0	Your suggestion that 'the winners should receive a cash prize or a scholarship' was excellent because you didn't just name a prize, you explained why it would be better than a trophy. This tells the reader exactly what you think and provides a clear justification, which makes your response very helpful. For your next piece, try to keep this habit of explaining the 'why' behind every suggestion you make!	5.0	Starting your email with 'I think organizing a school talent competition is a fantastic idea!' immediately creates a warm and supportive tone. This kind of enthusiastic opening is perfect for an email to a teacher because it shows you are engaged with their project. You’ve struck a great balance between being polite and being friendly, so keep using that natural voice in your future