29076	2025-12-14 15:56:29.099422+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M3A Task 1	Hi Alex,<br><br>I am also very happy and I can't wait to see your there. From my perspective, we should take the train on Saturday morning. I don't want to disturb your father. Moreover, it's not very expensive. On the campfire, I think we should cook somethings more than sausages so it would be healthier. Finally when we prepare to sleep, I think sleeping bags are a good choice for both of us. We should also bring some snacks and drinks to make sure that there will be somethings to eat when we're hungry at night. I suggest you to bring some hot coffee or maybe somethings which are hot so we'll not be very cold.<br><br>See you soon, Jane.	120	19.0	Hi Kris! 👋<br><br>Excellent work! This is a very strong email. You used phrases like "From my perspective" and "moreover" which are quite advanced, but you kept a friendly feeling. 🌟 Your idea to bring hot coffee was very cozy! ☕<br><br>Here are 3 tips to reach perfection: 📋<br>1. <b>Uncountables!</b> 🚫 "somethings" -> "something" (never add 's'!).<br>2. <b>Verbs!</b> 🛠️ "suggest you to bring" -> "suggest <b>that you</b> bring".<br>3. <b>Flow!</b> 🌊 Your writing flows beautifully!\n	B2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You developed every point fully. ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Logic!</b> 💭 bringing hot coffee is a great tip for staying warm!</li>\n	5.0	Your tone is natural and confident (B2 level!). 🤩<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Slight formality!</b> ⚖️ "From my perspective" is a bit formal. "In my opinion" or "I think" is more natural for a friend.</li>\n	5.0	Perfect structure. You used "Moreover" and "Finally" effectively. 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>None!</b> 🌟 Your organisation is spot on.</li>\n	4.0	High-level vocabulary! 👏<br><br>One main rule to remember:<br><li><b>Something!</b> 1️⃣ "Something" is part of a group called 'indefinite pronouns' (anything, everything, nothing). They <b>never</b> take an 's'. It is always "something", even if you mean many things!</li>\n	\N	\N	2025-12-14
28859	2025-12-14 15:56:29.021387+00	2026	Term 2 Midterm M3A Task 1	Dear Alex<br><br>I very exciting to see you this weekend. We weren't hang out together for long time. I am so happy that we are going camping this weekend too! So, I prefer to let you dad drive us to campsite because we can get some advice for this trip and also we can take a break for a while. We can buy some burgers or some drinks.<br><br>I think sausages it must not make us full. I think we should cook noodles. It very simple and tasty. If we make a campfire outside it too hard for us. How about the sleep bag for camp I think this is a good idea, what do you think?<br><br>See you at the campsite Alex, bye!<br><br>from. Prize .	127	16.0	Hello Prize! 👋<br><br>What a fun email! You sound so interactive - asking "what do you think?" makes it feel like a real conversation. 🗣️ Good idea about the noodles too - simple and tasty!<br><br>Here are 3 tips for you: 📋<br>1. <b>Verb Tenses!</b> ⏳ "I very exciting" -> "I <b>am</b> very excited".<br>2. <b>Negatives!</b> ⛔ "it must not make us full" -> "it <b>won't</b> make us full".<br>3. <b>Pronouns!</b> 👤 "let you dad" -> "let <b>your</b> dad".\n	B1+	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	You answered everything nicely! ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Clarity!</b> 💭 You asked "How about the sleep bag... what do you think?". This implied you wanted to bring it, which counts as a suggestion. Good job!</li>\n	4.0	Your interactive tone is your biggest strength. Keep asking questions! 🌟<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Grammar checks!</b> 🔍 "We weren't hang out" -> "We <b>haven't hung</b> out". This is a bit complex, but "haven't seen each other" is easier!</li>\n	4.0	Smooth transitions between paragraphs! 📝<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Punctuation!</b> 🖋️ "from. Prize ." -> "From Prize". No full stops needed there!</li>\n	3.0	"Tasty" and "simple" are great adjectives here! 👏<br><br>Watch these errors:<br><li><b>Adjectives!</b> 🎨 "I very exciting" -> "I am very <b>excited</b>".</li><li><b>Modals!</b> 🔮 "must not" implies prohibition (forbidden). "Won't" is better for prediction.</li>\n	\N	\N	2025-12-14
28716	2025-09-12 13:41:11.787854+00	2026	Term 1 Exam Question 1	Most teenagers often make a major affect to another teenagers more than their own parents. Nowadays, most teenagers are often spend times with their friends more than their parents because how easily that their own parents often misunderstood of what have the teenagers have said and might easily argue with each other so, their most safest comfort zone for them are their teenager especially their friends so, the more emotional attachment they get, the more risk of them getting persuaded by their own friends. Here are some of the most choices that teenager often listen to each other instead of listen to their own parents which are, clothes and fashion, studying and mental healthress.<br><br><br>Start of with clothes and fashion, which one of the most major problem between teenagers and parents, some of the parent often tell their kids to always wear needly clothes on the other hand, teenager often said that to wear an appropriate clothes base on environment or the situation for example going on a beach. You don't have to wear shirt, socks all the time but instead you should wear a swimsuit or even or can a bikini. With that according to that sentence, it significantly make mostly of the teenager to wear what actually want not just obeying their parents instruction.<br><br><br>Following up with studying, Mostly teenager are often influence by their family of what they need to study but some of them decided to follow their friends path and go along with them, with that type of action it often came with a bigger affect or consequences to the teenagers themself, these type of dilema are often happend during highschool to university by choosing their faculty. Some of them choose the perfect path for them to improve which is a good thing but on the other hand some of the teenager also often choose the wrong-path by just only following their friends.<br><br><br>Warping up with a mental health, as you may know mental health became one of the	337	11.0	Overall, Aunna, you've done a good job of tackling an interesting and relevant topic for teenagers. There are some excellent ideas in your writing, and you clearly have a point of view on whether friends or parents have more influence. To help your writing become even clearer and more persuasive, we'll focus on making sure your ideas flow smoothly and that your grammar and word choices are as precise as possible. Keep up the great effort, as improving these areas will truly help your thoughts stand out!	B1+	Writing	Term 1 Finals	FIRST	Part 2	3.0	You've made a really solid start by addressing the question about who influences teenagers more – friends or parents – and you've included "clothes and fashion" and "studying" as the prompt asked. You even thought of your own idea, "mental healthress," which is fantastic! That shows you're thinking deeply about the topic. To get a higher score, like a 5, try to expand on your points more fully. For example, when you talk about clothes, you could explain *why* friends' opinions are more persuasive than parents' instructions, giving specific examples of situations and peer pressure, not just different types of clothing. Sometimes, the end of your essay felt a little rushed, so ensure all your ideas are fully developed and explained, giving the reader a complete picture of your thoughts.	3.0	You've tried to write in a formal style, which is exactly what's needed for an essay like this, and you've definitely aimed to inform the reader about your perspective. That's a great approach! However, sometimes the way you've expressed your ideas makes the essay feel a little less formal or clear. For instance, phrases like "Start of with" could be replaced with more academic alternatives such as "Firstly," or "To begin with." To really impress and achieve a score of 5, focus on consistently using language that is precise and appropriate for an academic audience throughout your entire essay. This will help your arguments come across with greater authority and clarity, making your point of view even more impactful.	3.0	You've done a good job of breaking your essay into paragraphs, which helps organise your thoughts. It's clear that you're trying to guide the reader through your ideas point by point, which is important for any essay. However, some of your linking words, like "Start of with" and "Warping up with," while they show an effort to connect ideas, could be a little more varied and formal for an essay. For example, instead of "Warping up with," you might use "Finally," or "In conclusion." Sometimes, the connections between your sentences felt a little abrupt, which can make the essay a bit harder to follow. Thai learners sometimes focus more on the individual ideas and less on how those ideas are linked together, which can make the writing feel a bit disjointed. Practising a wider range of cohesive devices will help your essay flow much more smoothly and logically.	2.0	Your essay contains some interesting vocabulary, and you're attempting to use complex sentence structures, which is commendable. However, there are quite a few grammar and word choice mistakes that make it difficult for the reader to understand your message clearly at times. For example, you repeatedly use "affect" when you mean "effect," and phrases like "mental healthress" are not standard English. Another key area for improvement is subject-verb agreement; for instance, "teenager often said" should be "teenagers often said" or "a teenager often said" depending on whether you're talking about one teenager or many. Thai learners sometimes struggle with these grammatical agreements because the structures are different in Thai, where verbs don't change based on the subject's number. Focusing on these fundamental areas will make a big difference to the clarity and accuracy of your writing. For instance, double-check that your verbs match your subjects, and try to use a dictionary to confirm the correct word when you're unsure, especially for words that sound similar but have different meanings.	\N	\N	2025-09-12
