r your invention! ✅<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Pacing!</b> ⏱️ The invention and its success happen quite quickly. You could expand on the challenges of building it or the excitement of testing it.</li>	4.0	Your paragraphing is good, clearly separating the problem, the solution, and the result. 🧱 This makes your story easy to follow.<br><br>To improve:<br><li><b>Connecting Ideas!</b> 🔗 You used 'So' and 'And finally'. Try to add more varied linking words like 'As a result', 'Consequently', or 'Afterwards' to create a smoother flow.</li>	3.0	You used good vocabulary like 'invention' and 'prototype' (even if misspelled). 📚<br><br>Here are some corrections:<br><li><b>Spelling!</b> 📝 'Desing' -> '<b>Design</b>', 'buit' -> '<b>built</b>', 'atmosfear' -> '<b>atmosphere</b>', 'literly' -> '<b>literally</b>', 'ture' -> '<b>true</b>'.</li><li><b>Word Choice!</b> 🗣️ 'Couldn't wanted to live' -> '<b>didn't want to live</b>'.</li><li><b>Verb Forms!</b> 🛠️ 'I feel' (past tense) -> 'I <b>felt</b>'.</li><li><b>Prepositions!</b> 📍 'Cold air for the sky' -> 'cold air <b>from</b> the sky'.</li>	\N	\N	2025-12-14
