n she arrived at the theater acted like a bridge that brought the tension of the traffic jam to a happy conclusion. This logical connection helps the reader follow the timeline of the date without getting lost. For your next piece, try using a few more 'sequencing' words like 'Meanwhile' or 'A few minutes later' to make the movement between different scenes feel even smoother.	3.0	When you wrote 'makes she feels confident', the grammar gets a little tangled because the verb 'makes' usually needs an object like 'her' followed by the base verb 'feel'. This small slip acts like a tiny speed bump in an otherwise lovely sentence about her outfit. A great rule to remember is that after 'make/makes', we use the person (her) and then the simple action (feel) without adding an 's' at the end.	\N	\N	2026-02-23
