34289	2025-08-17 10:04:20.947411+00	2026	Thai Food	Food is an essential need for all people. Although, most people don't eat more food. People should eat more food, it was really important things to do. One successful type of popular food is street food, which is easy to eat and delicious. The three most important or the best greatest in street food are Som Tum, Lamb and Tom yum.<br><br><br>A first really amazing street food in Thailand is Tom Tum, which is a kind of a spicy papaya salad. Ingredients of Som Tum is lime, fish sauce, chili, papaya, crab and a small shrimp. A taste and flavor of papaya salad are really spicy and salt. Although Som Tum are spicy, but people still eat them because it's was really delicious.<br><br><br>Example, yesterday I ate Som Tum with my family and we're ordered many type of street food. There are many people in the cities, who eat street food like Som Tum. And here is a way to make Som Tum. First, put a garlic and chilies in a motor and pound it until them crushed and add fish sauce, lime, sugar and papaya salad. Mix everything together and you will got a delicious Som Tum.<br><br><br>Besides Som Tum, Tom Yum is also one of the best street foods in Thailand. It has a spicy and sour taste, and many people are enjoy eating with some rice or noodles. Ingredients of 1 stalk of lemongrass and cut into pieces, 3 slices of galangal, 3-5 lime leaves, 2-3 thai chilies, 4 mushrooms or more, 1 table spoon of lime, 1 teaspoon of chili paste. Here is a way to make Tom Yum, boil water with lemongrass, lime leaves, galangal add fish sauce, lime, and chili.<br><br><br>A third famous street food is Laab. Laab is a popular thai dish. It's made from pork, lime, fish sauce, chili, and toasted rice powder. The taste is spicy, sour and a little salty. People usually eat with sticky rice and a fresh vegetables.<br><br><br>In conclusion, street food is a delicious and easy thai dish. You don't need many ingredients and it doesn't take along time to make and very easty to eat it. Most people are really loves it	356	\N	Overall, you have written a clear essay about Thai street food, covering three different dishes. You have a good understanding of the structure of an essay, with an introduction, body paragraphs, and a conclusion. Your writing is easy to follow, and you use some good vocabulary. To improve, you need to work on your grammar, especially with verb forms and subject-verb agreement. Also, remember to include comments on the cultural value of the food, as this was a key part of the task.	\N	Writing	Formative	FIRST	Part 2	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	2025-08-17
29031	2026-02-23 13:32:08.183797+00	2026	Question 3 (Story)	Lois smiled as she put the tickets in her pocket and walked out of her house. She walked her way to the nearest train station and quickly got on when it arrived. As the time passed, she finally reached the newly opened museum. Her eyes wandered around until she met her friend, Evan. They exchanged glances and smiles. "I can't wait! Thank you for the tickets!" she said sincerely. He nodded and they both headed into the huge building.\n\nBoth of their faces lit up brightly. The museum was filled with all sorts of taxidermy of animals and ancient fossils. "Look at that lion, Lois. It looks eerily real, doesn't it?" Evan exclaimed with a wide grin. "We should check it out!" She firmly grabbed his wrist and ran to the showcase. As they both admire it, the lights suddenly flickered.\n\nWhen the lights turned back on, the taxidermy disappeared. "Where did it go?" she asked before she heard a distinct roar from behind. Evan took her hand and ran for the exit before the lights flickered again. This time it was back to where it was before. They both let out a sigh of relief, not until it flickered again. "Where can it be now?" Lois turned around to be met with a Lion staring into her eyes.	224	20.0	Hi Racing! 🌟 I was absolutely gripped by your story—you have a wonderful talent for building suspense and using very descriptive language like 'eerily real.' Your vocabulary is excellent! My main advice for your next writing task is to keep an eye on your word count; while your story was fantastic, practicing how to tell a great tale in fewer words will help you stay sharp for the exam. All the best, Ed	B2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	Your story began perfectly with 'Lois smiled as she put the tickets in her pocket and walked out of her house,' and you did a wonderful job of building a complete narrative with a clear beginning, middle, and a very exciting ending. This keeps the reader fully informed and invested in Lois's adventure at the museum. For your next piece, try to stay closer to the 100-word target to help you manage your time effectively during a real exam.	5.0	Including dialogue such as '“Look at that lion, Lois. It looks eerily real, doesn't it?”' was a brilliant choice because it makes the characters feel alive and pulls the reader right into the scene. This creates an engaging, suspenseful atmosphere that is exactly what a good story needs. To take this even further, you could describe a physical reaction, like Lois's heart racing, to make the reader feel her fear even more.	5.0	I see that you used 'When the lights turned back on' to signal a shift in the action, which acts like a clear road map for the reader to follow the sequence of events. This logical flow makes the spooky disappearance of the lion very easy to visualize and follow. You might try using a few more short, punchy sentences during the scary parts to make the pace feel even faster and more exciting.	5.0	Your choice of words like 'taxidermy' and 'eerily real' really shows off a sophisticated vocabulary that is well above the average level. When you wrote 'As they both admire it,' the switch to the present tense felt a little bit like a skip in a record because the rest of the story is in the past. Try to keep all your verbs in the past tense, like 'admired,' to keep the 'heartbeat' of your story consistent.	\N	\N	2026-02-23
33896	2025-08-22 12:28:36.162678+00	2026	Social Issue	In my view, mobile phones should be allowed to be used in the classroom. Firstly, it helps students discover things to do work easily. According to students, teachers usually give work for students to work online. They can search anything that they want to know on internet. The books have less information than online. students should look for the information online to make them work easily. Secondly, some class has allowed the students to use thier phones in the freetime. So, they can play game with thier friends or listening the music alone. It makes students are happier when they are at school and make the class unserious. The final reason that supports my opinion is that it helps student have less stress. In Thailand, students are study hardly. So, they often have more stress. According to the students, they always wear the headphones and turn on the music on the phone when they are getting stressed. For these three reasons, I feel that mobile phones should be allowed to use in the classroom to make the students feel happier and have less stress when they are at the school.	190	16.0	<b>📝 Dear Kati</b><br>Here is your writing feedback for 'Social Issue'. You wrote 190 words and achieved B1+. You presented your ideas clearly and structured your paragraph very well, making it easy to understand.<br><br>	B1+	Writing	CA	PET	Part 2	5.0	[Single sentence performance summary]All aspects of the prompt were fully addressed, including a clear opinion, three distinct supporting ideas, and relevant evidence for each.<br><b>Strength:</b> You clearly state your opinion at the beginning and end of your paragraph, and you use good topic sentences for each supporting idea, such as "Firstly, it helps students discover things to do work easily."	3.0	[Single sentence performance summary]You generally use the correct style for an academic paragraph to share your ideas, but sometimes the tone is a little too informal for this type of writing.<br><b>Problem:</b> You used a slightly informal phrase in your paragraph: "It makes students are happier when they are at school and make the class unserious."<br><b>Correction:</b> "This makes students happier when they are at school and can make the class feel less formal."<br><b>Explanation:</b> In academic writing, we aim for a more formal and objective tone. Also, "unserious" is not a common word to describe a class; "less formal" or "more relaxed" would be better.	5.0	[Single sentence performance summary]Your paragraph is very well-organised and easy to follow. You use linking words effectively to connect your ideas.<br><b>Strength:</b> You use clear linking words like "Firstly," "Secondly," and "The final reason" to introduce each of your main points, which makes your paragraph very logical and easy to read.	3.0	[Single sentence performance summary]You use a good range of everyday words and try to use more complex sentences with some success, but you have some errors in spelling and basic grammar.<br><b>Problem:</b> There were several spelling errors in your writing, for example: "thier phones" and "freetime".<br><b>Correction:</b> "their phones" and "free time".<br><b>Explanation:</b> In English, some common words are often misspelled, and compound nouns like "free time" are usually written as two separate words. Thai students sometimes misspell these due to direct translation or phonetics.	\N	\N	2025-08-22
29045	2026-02-23 13:32:08.183797+00	2026	Question 3 (Story)	Lois smiled as she put the tickets in her pocket and walked out of her house. Not long after that the uber's finally arrived, she quickly get into the seat at the back of the driver, she was heading to the cinema near her school. Lois, cute five-feet five-inches tall with with her black-leather bag and pink hoodie, is going on a date with excitement. When the uber's arrived at the cinema, she quickly handed a one-hundred dollar bill to her driver and stormed out of the car and slowly walk to Aerion, blond six-feet tall with tattoo behind his neck, he is also a captain of shool basket ball team and Aerion is the boy who's Lois going to cinema with. From eleven AM to six PM, things go really well they have already kissed and Aerion decided to drive to her home to meets her parents but before they could arrive something happened. "Lois! Lois! Lois!" her mom shouted, Lois was just dreaming about her crush but in reality Aerion doesn't even know her.	188	16.0	Hi In-Sun! I really enjoyed the 'dream' twist you added to your story—it was a very creative way to use the prompt! Your descriptions made Lois and Aerion feel like real people. My main 'homework' for you is to focus on 'tense consistency'; try to pick one tense (usually the past for stories) and stick with it throughout the whole piece. This will make your writing much smoother. All the best, Ed	B1+	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	It was great to see how you used the required starting sentence to jump straight into a vivid scene. Your choice to end with 'Lois was just dreaming about her crush' was a clever way to wrap up the narrative, ensuring the reader is fully informed and entertained by the 'twist' ending. For your next story, try to keep the word count closer to the 100-word mark to practice being even more concise with your storytelling! 🌟	4.0	The way you included specific details like the 'black-leather bag and pink hoodie' really helped to paint a clear picture of the characters in my mind. These descriptive choices hold the reader's attention well because they make the world feel real. To reach a 5, try to ensure your tone stays consistent; for example, 'stormed out' is very dramatic, so make sure the reason for the character's speed matches that level of emotion! 🚀	4.0	I see that you used time-based phrases like 'Not long after that' and 'From eleven AM to six PM' to move the story forward logically. This helps the reader follow the timeline of the date without getting lost. To make your organization even stronger, try using a new paragraph when the 'reality' hits at the end, as this visual break acts like a signal to the reader that the scene has changed. 📝	3.0	Your use of descriptive vocabulary like 'stormed out' and 'crush' shows a wonderful range of expression. However, when you wrote 'she quickly get' and 'slowly walk', the mix of present and past tenses made the story's timeline feel a bit bumpy. A great tip is to check that all your verbs are in the past tense (like 'got' and 'walked') if your story starts in the past, as this keeps the 'heartbeat' of your writing steady and professional. 🛠️	\N	\N	2026-02-23
