urate as possible by always including a verb before an adjective—for example, 'She was really interested' instead of 'She really interested'. 🚀	3.0	When you wrote 'So she head to a concert quickly', you used a helpful transition to move the action from her house to the venue. However, because the whole story is written as one single paragraph, it can be a bit harder for the reader to see the different stages of the adventure. Next time, try to use separate paragraphs for the beginning, middle, and end to act like a clear map for your reader! 🗺️	3.0	I see that you included some great vocabulary like 'passionate' and 'meaning', which shows you are comfortable using descriptive B1-level words. While your meaning is always clear, phrases like 'she's spend a lot of time listen' show that you are still working on your past tense forms and verb patterns. A great tip for your 'homework' is to remember that after the verb 'spend', we usually use the '-ing' form, such as 'spending time listening'. 📝	\N	\N	2026-02-23
