t doesn't fully achieve its communicative purpose of presenting a well-rounded discussion of your chosen activities.<br><br>	2.0	Your introduction is clear, and you started the first body paragraph well with a topic sentence. However, the essay is incomplete, lacking a fully developed second body paragraph and a conclusion. This significantly affects the overall coherence and flow of your writing.<br>👉 <b>To reach a 5/5:</b> Focus on ensuring your essay has a complete structure with all paragraphs fully developed. Remember to start body paragraphs with clear topic sentences and include a strong concluding paragraph that summarizes your main points.<br><br>	3.0	You use good everyday vocabulary and are trying to use more complex sentences, which is great! The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules and spelling.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "making these activities are seen as very important things foward them."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "making these activities are seen as very important things for them."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Always double-check your spelling, especially for common words. Sometimes in Thai, we don't focus as much on precise spelling in every context, but in English, it's very important. A small spelling error can sometimes change the meaning of your sentence.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "Besides playing games, there are travelling too which is as famous as the frist one."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "Besides playing games, there is also travelling, which is as famous as the first one."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> When talking about a general activity like 'travelling' (a gerund), it's treated as a singular noun in English, so we use 'there is' instead of 'there are'. Also, be careful with letter order in English words; 'frist' should be 'first'.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "However free time activities help them a lot..."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "However, free time activities help them a lot..."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In 