es are team sports and creative hobbies. Team sports like basketball help teenagers build friendships, while creative hobbies like painting allow self-expression."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> The improved version directly answers the question by naming specific activities and explaining their benefits, rather than focusing on why teenagers can't do activities.	2.0	Your writing shows you understand academic topics, but needs to stay focused on the task.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Keep your writing focused on the exact question being asked throughout the entire essay.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Writing about parental pressure instead of free time activities<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> Stay focused on describing and explaining the two chosen free time activities in each paragraph<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> Academic writing requires staying precisely on topic. When the question asks about free time activities, every paragraph should develop that specific theme.	2.0	You used paragraph breaks well to separate your ideas.<br>👉 <b>To Improve:</b> Create a clear thesis statement and use topic sentences that connect to your main argument.<br>❌ <b>Weakness:</b> Your introduction doesn't clearly state what two activities you will discuss<br>✨ <b>Improved:</b> "Free time activities are essential for teenagers' development, with team sports and creative hobbies being particularly valuable for building social skills and self-expression."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> A clear thesis statement tells the reader exactly what your essay will be about and helps you stay organized throughout your writing.	2.0	You used some good vocabulary like "investment" correctly. The main challenges are with a few key grammar rules.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "I think freetime is the most important for kid and teenagers."<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "I think free time is very important for children and teenagers."<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, compound words like "freetime" are common, but in English we write "free time" as two separate words. Also, we need to use plural forms: "children" ("kids" is too informal) not "kid" when talking about groups.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "they parents give a lot of pressure to them"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "their parents give them a lot of pressure"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, the same word "they" can be used for possession, but in English we need to use "their" for possessive form. This is a common challenge for Thai learners.<br><br>❌ <b>Problem:</b> You wrote: "That make teenagers get stress"<br>✨ <b>Correction:</b> "That makes teenagers feel stressed"<br>👉 <b>Explanation:</b> In Thai, subject-verb agreement is different. In English, "that" (singular) needs "makes" (singular verb), not "make." Also, we say "feel stressed" rather than "get stress."<br><br><b>📚 YOUR ACTION PLAN</b><br>1. Practice identifying the exact question requirements before writing - underline key words like "two activities" and "explain why"<br>2. Work on subject-verb agreement with singular/plural nouns<br>3. Study possessive pronouns (my/your/his/her/our/their) and when to use them<br><br>	\N	\N	2025-08-28
33169	2026-02-23 13:32:08.183797+00	2026	Question 2 (Article)	Sport is one of the best activities you can do to stay healthy and strong. It is for everyone. Do any kind of sport or exercise once a week can keep you away from doctors, which is one of the several reasons of why we should exercise and play sports.\n\nIn my hometown, there's a park for people to run and play football together. They also have a play ground for kids. But when I moved to Bangkok, I rarely see them around in my area. There's not enough sports activities for people in my area, which left me with nothing to do at the weekends.\n\nFirst year in my school, at that time I was very fat because I don't exercise enough. This make me run slowly and get tired easily. Untill when I start playing sports with my friends. Playing sports not only make you healthy, it also teach you team work and sportmanship. So for young people, do sport and exercise are important and beneficial for yourself.	178	19.0	Hi Milan! 🌟 You've written a very engaging article that really captures the reader's interest with your personal story and honest reflections. Your range of vocabulary and your ability to use complex sentences with 'which' are very impressive! My main 'homework' for your next piece is to watch out for subject-verb agreement (like saying 'this makes' instead of 'this make') and to practice using 'ing' forms when you start a sentence with an activity. You're doing a fantastic job! 🚀 All the best, Ed.	B2	Writing	Term 2 Midterm	PET	Part 1	5.0	When you wrote 'But when I moved to Bangkok, I rarely see them around in my area', you perfectly contrasted two different locations to answer if there are enough activities. This gives the reader a clear picture of your current situation and makes your article feel very authentic. Try to keep using these personal comparisons in future articles to add depth and personality to your writing.	5.0	It was great to see you share a personal story by writing 'First year in my school, at that time I was very fat because I don't exercise enough'. By being honest about your own journey, you build a strong connection with your readers and make your arguments about health much more persuasive. To make it even better, you could add a catchy title at the start to grab the reader's attention immediately.	5.0	Your use of the word 'which' in sentences like 'which left me with nothing to do at the weekends' acts like a strong bridge between your ideas. This helps the reader follow your logic effortlessly because the result of the lack of activities is directly connected to your feelings. One small tip: you could use more specific sequencing words like 'Firstly' or 'In addition' to make your different reasons for exercising stand out even more clearly.	4.0	I see that you used some sophisticated vocabulary like 'sportsmanship' and 'beneficial', which really shows off your high-level word bank. However, when you wrote 'Do any kind of sport... can keep', it makes the sentence feel a bit unstable because the subject of your sentence needs to be an action. Using a gerund like 'Doing' instead of 'Do' at the start of a sentence will make your grammar much smoother and more professional.	\N	\N	2026-02-23
