onnection to the place. While you could still expand on some points to reach a score of 5, the essay is generally comprehensive and informative.	3.0	You have generally used the conventions of the task to communicate straightforward ideas. The writing is mostly clear, and you have attempted to engage the reader by describing the attractions of Huahin. To improve to a score of 5, you could use more descriptive and vivid language to hold the reader's attention more effectively. Ensure that your tone and register are consistent throughout the essay.	3.0	You have organized your essay into paragraphs, and the ideas generally follow a logical sequence, moving from a general introduction to specific details about the city and your personal connection to it. You've also used some cohesive devices. To reach a higher score of 5, you should aim for more sophisticated linking words and cohesive devices to improve the flow and coherence of the essay. For instance, using transitions like "Furthermore," "Moreover," or "In addition" could help connect your ideas more smoothly.	2.0	Gut-Jung, your essay contains several errors in grammar and spelling that sometimes impede communication. Examples include "most favorite" instead of "favorite," "locate" instead of "located," "in between of" instead of "between," "There's many things" instead of "There are many things," "There's beach" instead of "There is a beach," "bonana boat" instead of "banana boat," "borned" instead of "born," "seafoods" instead of "seafood," and "absolutly" instead of "absolutely." There are also missed opportunities to use relative clauses to combine sentences and make your writing more sophisticated. To improve to a score of 5, you need to significantly improve the accuracy of your language and demonstrate a wider range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.	\N	\N	2025-07-11
